FamilyTree.person({"id":"ackermans_joanna","name":"Joanna Ackermans","dates":"d. 27 Dec 1877 Alsemberg","confidence":"doc","surname":"Ackermans","family":"ackermans","sex":"f","died":"27 Dec 1877 Alsemberg","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"swaelens_egidius","name":"Egidius Swaelens"}],"source":"Civil marriage acts for the Bossin/Swaelens/Vrebos family of Kraainem, 1884-1901 (harvested corpus, July 2026); Marriage act nr. 3 — Joannes Baptista Julianus Swaelens x Ludovica Bossin, Kraainem, 25 February 1884 (register image); Marriage banns nrs. 7 and 8 — Joannes Baptista Julianus Swaelens x Ludovica Bossin, Alsemberg, 10 and 17 February 1884 (register image)","note":"Named as mother of the groom, already dead, in her son [[swaelens_joannes_1858]]'s marriage act —\nKraainem, 25 February 1884 — which gives her death as **Alsemberg, 27 December 1877**.\nThat is a second, checkable fact alongside the bare parent-name pair, and it is what lifts\nthis parentage above a name coincidence: a dead mother's exact place and date, six years\nbefore the wedding, is not the kind of detail an act invents.\n\n**UPGRADED TO `doc` (2026-07-27) — no longer single-source.** The Kraainem act's own\nregister image was read, confirming this exactly. Independently, and before that act\nexisted, the **Alsemberg marriage banns** (nrs. 7 and 8, 10 and 17 February 1884) — a\ndifferent commune, register series and clerk — name the same pair, **Egidius Swaelens x\nJoanna Ackermans, overleden**. Her identity is not corroborated a second time as to the\ndeath date itself (the banns omit it), but the parent pairing is: two unconnected\nregisters, not one act alone.\n\nFRONTIER: her marriage to [[swaelens_egidius]], and her own birth."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"adriaenssens_joanna_1761","name":"Joanna Adriaenssens","dates":"1761 – 1833","confidence":"sup","surname":"Adriaenssens","family":"adriaenssens","born":"1761","order":"1761","died":"1833","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"bundervoet_philippus_1756","name":"Philippus Jacobus Bundervoet","detail":"m. 1784"}],"source":"Fauconier / Bauwens \"Bundervoet–Vermeulen\" parenteel"});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bisschop_francine","name":"Francine Bisschop","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bisschop","family":"bisschop","sex":"f","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"bundervoet_marcel_1933","name":"Marcel Henri Bundervoet"}],"source":"Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust memorial card — Marcel Bundervoet, d. Oostende 20 November 2015","note":"Second partner of [[bundervoet_marcel_1933]]. The Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust memorial-card\nindex names both his partners — her and a Van Iseghem ([[vaniseghem_rosette]]) — which is what\nindependently confirmed the two marriages the family had reported.\n\n`sup`: the index is a transcription of the card, and nobody here has read the card\nitself. No dates, no marriage date, no children recorded. His three children\nare [[vaniseghem_rosette]]'s."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"blomme_josephus","name":"Josephus Blomme","dates":"","confidence":"doc","surname":"Blomme","family":"blomme","line":"de-keyser","spouses":[{"id":"meseure_mathilde","name":"Mathilde Sophia Meseure"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 9 — Petrus Augustus Blomme x Louisa Maria Bocklandt, Stene, 1 March 1924 (register image)","note":"Father of [[blomme_petrus_1884]]. Named in his son's Stene marriage act of 1 March 1924 —\nregister image read directly — as *zonder beroep* (no occupation), living at Oostende,\npresent in person and consenting to the marriage. The act gives no birth or death date\nfor him."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"blomme_petrus_1884","name":"Petrus Augustus Blomme","dates":"b. 23 Jan 1884 Stene","confidence":"doc","surname":"Blomme","family":"blomme","sex":"m","born":"23 Jan 1884 Stene","order":"1884-01-23","occupation":"werkman","line":"de-keyser","father":"blomme_josephus","mother":"meseure_mathilde","spouses":[{"id":"bocklandt_louise_1877","name":"Louise Marie Bocklandt","detail":"m. Stene, 1 Mar 1924"}],"source":"Memorial-card record — Louisa-Maria Bocklandt, d. Oostende 15 July 1946; Marriage act nr. 9 — Petrus Augustus Blomme x Louisa Maria Bocklandt, Stene, 1 March 1924 (register image)","note":"Second husband of [[bocklandt_louise_1877]], who had divorced [[dekeyser_edouard_1876]] on 14 November\n1922. The Familiekunde Westkust memorial-card record ([[S17]]) first named him as her\npartner, at her death on 15 July 1946 — she died a Blomme.\n\nFOUND (2026-07-26), replacing the FRONTIER this record used to carry. Their own marriage\nact — Stene, 1 March 1924, akte nr. 9, register image read directly\n([[fs-stene-1924-marriage-blomme-bocklandt]]). He is *werkman*, living at Stene and born\nthere **23 January 1884**, major son of **Josephus Blomme**, *zonder beroep*, living at\nOostende and present in person, consenting to the marriage; and of **Mathilde Sophia\nMeseure**, dead at Oostende **21 July 1922**. Both parents are given their own record here\nfor the first time: [[blomme_josephus]] and [[meseure_mathilde]].\n\nHe is a step-relation, not blood: no line of descent in this tree runs through him."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bocklandt_alphonsus","name":"Alphonsus Bocklandt","dates":"d. 26 Oct 1892 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bocklandt","family":"bocklandt","died":"26 Oct 1892 Oostende","line":"de-keyser","father":"bocklandt_edouard_1839","mother":"vanbergen_marielouise_1842","source":"Death act nr. 712 — Alphonsus Bocklandt, Oostende, 26 October 1892","note":"Son of [[bocklandt_edouard_1839]] and [[vanbergen_marielouise_1842]] — a previously unrecorded sibling of\n[[bocklandt_louise_1877]]. His death act — Oostende nr. 712, 26 October 1892\n([[agatha-oostende-1892-death-alphonsus-bocklandt]]) — names his father and mother and\nstates he was born at Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen), but gives no age, so no birth date is\nrecorded here. AGATHA serves this act only as an \"analyse van akte\" (index transcription),\nnot the register image, hence `sup`."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bocklandt_antonius_1805","name":"Antonius Dominicus Bocklandt","dates":"1805 – 1883","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bocklandt","family":"bocklandt","born":"1805","order":"1805","died":"1883","line":"de-keyser","father":"bocklandt_daniel_1768","mother":"vanpuyenbroeck_philippa_1778","spouses":[{"id":"ichau_isabella_1803","name":"Isabella Livia Ichau","detail":"m. 1838"}],"source":"wete1998 (Erik Bekaert) — Hamme (O-Vl) specialist; Rijksarchief AGATHA — Belgian State Archives search robot","note":"Paternal grandfather of Louise Bocklandt. Married Isabella Livia Ichau in 1838. Of the Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen / Waasland) Bocklandt family."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bocklandt_caesar_1867","name":"Caesar Antonius Bocklandt","dates":"b. 2 Jul 1867 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bocklandt","family":"bocklandt","sex":"m","born":"2 Jul 1867 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)","order":"1867-07-02","occupation":"koordedraaier (ropemaker)","line":"de-keyser","father":"bocklandt_edouard_1839","mother":"vanbergen_marielouise_1842","spouses":[{"id":"vincke_florence_1869","name":"Florence Amelie Vincke","detail":"m. Diksmuide, 11 Feb 1893"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 40 — Caesar Antonius Bocklandt x Florence Amelie Vincke, Diksmuide, 11 February 1893","note":"Son of [[bocklandt_edouard_1839]] and [[vanbergen_marielouise_1842]], and [[bocklandt_louise_1877]]'s brother.\nHis marriage act — Diksmuide nr. 40, 11 February 1893\n([[agatha-diksmuide-1893-marriage-bocklandt-vincke]]) — names him born at Hamme 2 July\n1867, *koordedraaier* (ropemaker — his father's own trade under a different word), resident\nat Oostende, son of Eduard Bocklandt (53, *koordedraaier*) and the already-deceased Maria\nLouisa Vanbergen. He married **Florence Amelie Vincke** (b. Diksmuide 22 Apr 1869,\n*kantwerkster*), daughter of [[vincke_lucien_1840]] and [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]] of Diksmuide — now\nher own record, [[vincke_florence_1869]]. AGATHA serves this act only as an \"analyse van akte\"\n(index transcription), not the register image, hence `sup`.\n\nRESOLVED (research-log §64). This act was previously flagged as a frontier: the bride's\nparents shared full names with this tree's existing [[vincke_lucien_1840]] x [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]]\n(parents of [[vincke_emma_1880]], Van Iseghem line), but the act alone named them by name only —\none identifier, not the two a graft needs — and Florence Amelie had no record of her own to\ngraft onto. With her own record now written, a province-wide sweep of the Diksmuide birth\nindex found no rival couple of that name, so the link stands: this marriage joins the Van\nIseghem and De Keyser/Bocklandt branches of this tree (objective 3)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bocklandt_daniel_1768","name":"Daniel Bocklandt","dates":"1768 – 1837","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bocklandt","family":"bocklandt","born":"1768","order":"1768","died":"1837","line":"de-keyser","spouses":[{"id":"vanpuyenbroeck_philippa_1778","name":"Philippa Van Puyenbroeck","detail":"m. 1801"}],"source":"wete1998 (Erik Bekaert) — Hamme (O-Vl) specialist","note":"FRONTIER (top of the Bocklandt line in the wete1998 tree) — paternal great-grandfather of Louise Bocklandt. Married Philippa Van Puyenbroeck in 1801. Of Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen). His own parents are not recorded in the tree; the Hamme O-Vl parish/civil registers (Rijksarchief AGATHA) are the place to push further."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bocklandt_edouard_1839","name":"Édouard Bocklandt","dates":"1839 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen) – 4 Jul 1907 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bocklandt","family":"bocklandt","born":"1839 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)","order":"1839","died":"4 Jul 1907 Oostende","occupation":"zeeldraaier (ropemaker)","line":"de-keyser","father":"bocklandt_antonius_1805","mother":"ichau_isabella_1803","spouses":[{"id":"vanbergen_marielouise_1842","name":"Maria Louisa Van Bergen"}],"source":"wete1998 (Erik Bekaert) — Hamme (O-Vl) specialist; Death act nr. 417 — Eduardus Bocklandt, Oostende, 4 July 1907; Death act nr. 126 — Ludovicus Bocklandt, Hamme (O-Vl), 9 June 1880 (register image)","note":"Father of Louise Marie Bocklandt (1877, Hamme O-Vl). Born 1839 at Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen);\nmarried Maria Louisa Van Bergen (1842-1888). Died Oostende 4 July 1907.\n\nCITATION REPAIRED (2026-07-26), replacing the §52 downgrade. Two acts now stand behind this\nrecord. His own death act — Oostende nr. 417, 4 July 1907\n([[agatha-oostende-1907-death-eduardus-bocklandt]]) — names his parents **Antonius\nDominicus Bocklandt** and **Isabella Livina Ichau** (both already deceased, place not\nstated), independently of the wete1998 tree that first supplied them, and gives his death\ndate and Hamme birthplace. The act spells her **Isabella Livina**, against this record's\n**Isabella Livia** — a single-letter variant, and with no rival Isabella Ichau anywhere in\nthe record to collide with, so it is read as the same woman; the same note is on\n[[ichau_isabella_1803]]'s own record. The Hamme death act of his young son Ludovicus, 9 June\n1880 — register image read directly ([[fs-hamme-1880-death-ludovicus-bocklandt]]) — puts\nhim at Hamme with Maria Louisa Van Bergen, aged 40 (consistent with the held birth of\n1839), trade *zeeldraaier* (ropemaker).\n\nCONFIDENCE STAYS `sup`, not `doc`. The parent-link fact — his own parentage — rests on the\n1907 death act, and AGATHA serves that act only as an \"analyse van akte\" (a volunteer index\ntranscription); the image itself sits behind an AGATHA login and was not opened. The 1880\nregister image WAS read, but it does not name his own parents, so it cannot carry that\nparticular fact to `doc` on its own.\n\nSix more of his and Maria Louisa's children now have their own records, each sourced to an\nact naming him by name as father: [[bocklandt_paulina_1870]] (m. Oostende 1888),\n[[bocklandt_maria_1874]] (m. Oostende 1892), [[bocklandt_maria_1872]] (m. Oostende 1893),\n[[bocklandt_caesar_1867]] (m. Diksmuide 1893), [[bocklandt_philemondus_1880]] (m. Oostende 1900) and\n[[bocklandt_alphonsus]] (d. Oostende 1892), alongside [[bocklandt_ludovicus_1875]] (d. Hamme\n1880) and [[bocklandt_louise_1877]] herself. Across the four marriage acts of 1888-1900 he is\nconsistently *touwslagersknecht* (a ropemaker's assistant) at Oostende — the same trade as\n*zeeldraaier* at Hamme in 1880, under a different word for it — and his stated age rises\nfrom 50 (1888) to 62 (1900), which fits a birth of 1838-1839 throughout."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bocklandt_louise_1877","name":"Louise Marie Bocklandt","dates":"31 Dec 1877 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen) – 15 Jul 1946 Oostende","confidence":"doc","surname":"Bocklandt","family":"bocklandt","born":"31 Dec 1877 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)","order":"1877-12-31","died":"15 Jul 1946 Oostende","line":"de-keyser","father":"bocklandt_edouard_1839","mother":"vanbergen_marielouise_1842","spouses":[{"id":"dekeyser_edouard_1876","name":"Édouard Dekeyser","detail":"m. 4 May 1901 · divorced 14 Nov 1922 · legitimized their two eldest children"},{"id":"blomme_petrus_1884","name":"Petrus Blomme","detail":"m. Stene, 1 Mar 1924"}],"source":"Memorial-card record — Louisa-Maria Bocklandt, d. Oostende 15 July 1946; wete1998 (Erik Bekaert) — Hamme (O-Vl) specialist; Marriage act nr. 9 — Petrus Augustus Blomme x Louisa Maria Bocklandt, Stene, 1 March 1924 (register image)","note":"Source detail: Stene marriage act nr. 9, 1 March 1924 (FamilySearch register image, read\ndirectly — [[fs-stene-1924-marriage-blomme-bocklandt]]); Familiekunde Westkust memorial\ncard ([[S17]]); Geneanet tree wete1998 (Erik Bekaert, for the ancestors above her parents).\n\nBorn 31 Dec 1877 in Hamme (OOST-VLAANDEREN, Waasland) — the SAME town as her first husband\nÉdouard Dekeyser (both Hamme natives who moved to Oostende). This is the true source of the\nlong 'Hamme' confusion: it was the couple's shared birth-town, not Hamme-Merchtem and not a\nmarriage place. Married Édouard 4 May 1901 (the marriage legitimized their two eldest\nchildren); they DIVORCED on 14 November 1922, by decree of the Rechtbank van eersten aanleg\nte Brugge. Died 1946 Oostende, buried at Stene. Her Bocklandt family is a Hamme (O-Vl) /\nWaasland family documented back to the 1760s (see her parents and the Bocklandt / Van\nBergen ancestors).\n\nSHE REMARRIED (July 2026). A Familiekunde Westkust memorial-card record ([[S17]]) gives her\ndeath as **15 July 1946 at Oostende** — the tree had only the year — with her birthplace\nHamme, and names her partner as **Petrus Blomme**.\n\nNot Édouard. She and [[dekeyser_edouard_1876]] divorced in 1922, and this is the first sign of what\nshe did afterwards: she married again. The chronology is quietly striking — Édouard\nremarried Leontine Schreel at Oostende on 9 May 1946, and Louise died nine weeks later, on\n15 July, a Blomme.\n\nFOUND (2026-07-26), closing the frontier this record used to carry. The Bocklandt–Blomme\nmarriage act itself: Stene, 1 March 1924, akte nr. 9, register image read directly\n([[fs-stene-1924-marriage-blomme-bocklandt]]). She is a *werkvrouw*, born Hamme 31 December\n1877 — exact to the day and to the commune — daughter of Eduardus Bocklandt (d. Oostende\n4 Jul 1907) and Maria Louisa Van Den Bergen (d. Oostende 22 Nov 1888), and the act states in\nfull that she is the *gescheiden echtgenoote* of Eduardus De Keyser, divorced by the\nRechtbank van eersten aanleg te Brugge on 14 November 1922 — dating the divorce this record\nhad only as `~1923`. The groom, [[blomme_petrus_1884]], is given as *werkman*, born Stene 23\nJanuary 1884, son of Josephus Blomme (living, Oostende) and Mathilde Sophia Meseure (d.\nOostende 21 Jul 1922).\n\nA TRAP FOR THE NEXT READER. FamilySearch's own index dates this act **1 May 1924**. The\nregister itself reads *\"den eersten Maart\"* — 1 March — confirmed by the facing act (nr. 8,\n23 February 1924) and by the banns, published Sunday 10 February 1924: neither fits a May\nwedding. The index's own raw month field reads `\"Maand\": \"Maa\"`, which the site auto-expands\nto the English \"May\" instead of the Dutch \"Maart\" — a demonstrable indexing bug, not a\nsecond date to reconcile. The register, not the index, is what is cited here.\n\nRESTORED (2026-07-26) to `doc`. §52 downgraded this record because its only citation was a\nbare `agatha` — no page id, no artifact, no search-log entry, so `doc` could not be checked\nagainst anything. That gap is closed: the citation is now the register image itself\n([[fs-stene-1924-marriage-blomme-bocklandt]], an artifact saved from the FamilySearch\nviewer), and it carries two identifiers independent of the wete1998 tree that first\nsupplied her parents — her birth exact to the day and commune, and the De Keyser\nmarriage-and-divorce, itself independently corroborated by [[dekeyser_edouard_1876]]'s own 1946\nremarriage act, read 22 years later."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bocklandt_ludovicus_1875","name":"Ludovicus Bocklandt","dates":"~1875 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen) – 8 Jun 1880 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)","confidence":"doc","surname":"Bocklandt","family":"bocklandt","born":"~1875 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)","order":"1875","died":"8 Jun 1880 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)","line":"de-keyser","father":"bocklandt_edouard_1839","mother":"vanbergen_marielouise_1842","source":"Death act nr. 126 — Ludovicus Bocklandt, Hamme (O-Vl), 9 June 1880 (register image)","note":"Son of [[bocklandt_edouard_1839]] and [[vanbergen_marielouise_1842]], and [[bocklandt_louise_1877]]'s brother —\nnamed until now only inside his parents' own prose. Died in his parents' house at Hamme,\n8 June 1880, aged about five (so born about 1875); his father Eduardus Bocklandt,\n*zeeldraaier*, declared the death the following morning — Hamme death act nr. 126,\nregister image read directly ([[fs-hamme-1880-death-ludovicus-bocklandt]]).\n\n`doc`, because the register image itself was read and saved as an artifact\n(`data/artifacts/bocklandt-ludovicus-1880-death-hamme.md`), not an index transcription of\nit."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bocklandt_maria_1872","name":"Maria Mathildis Bocklandt","dates":"b. 12 May 1872 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bocklandt","family":"bocklandt","sex":"f","born":"12 May 1872 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)","order":"1872-05-12","occupation":"werkmeid (housemaid)","line":"de-keyser","father":"bocklandt_edouard_1839","mother":"vanbergen_marielouise_1842","source":"Marriage act nr. 11 — Justinus Vincentius Dubuy x Maria Mathildis Bocklandt, Oostende, 21 January 1893","note":"Daughter of [[bocklandt_edouard_1839]] and [[vanbergen_marielouise_1842]], and [[bocklandt_louise_1877]]'s\nsister. Her marriage act — Oostende nr. 11, 21 January 1893\n([[agatha-oostende-1893-marriage-bocklandt-dubuy]]) — names her born at Hamme 12 May 1872,\n*werkmeid*, resident at Oostende, daughter of Eduardus Bocklandt (54, *touwslagersknecht*)\nand the already-deceased Maria Louisa Vanbergen. She married **Justinus Vincentius Dubuy**\n(b. Oostende 29 Dec 1870, *touwslagersknecht* — her own father's trade), son of the\nalready-deceased Justinus Vincentius Lud. Dubuy and of Carolina Reck. AGATHA serves this\nact only as an \"analyse van akte\" (index transcription), not the register image, hence\n`sup`.\n\nThe act itself misdates her mother's death \"22/11/1858\", against every other act's\n\"22 Nov 1888\" — a clerical slip in this one register entry, not a rival date;\n[[vanbergen_marielouise_1842]]'s own record keeps 1888."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bocklandt_maria_1874","name":"Maria Elodia Bocklandt","dates":"b. 9 Mar 1874 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bocklandt","family":"bocklandt","sex":"f","born":"9 Mar 1874 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)","order":"1874-03-09","occupation":"werkmeid (housemaid)","line":"de-keyser","father":"bocklandt_edouard_1839","mother":"vanbergen_marielouise_1842","source":"Marriage act nr. 42 — Fredericus Desiderius Debuf x Maria Elodia Bocklandt, Oostende, 26 March 1892","note":"Daughter of [[bocklandt_edouard_1839]] and [[vanbergen_marielouise_1842]], and [[bocklandt_louise_1877]]'s\nsister. Her marriage act — Oostende nr. 42, 26 March 1892\n([[agatha-oostende-1892-marriage-bocklandt-debuf]]) — names her born at Hamme 9 March\n1874, *werkmeid*, resident at Oostende, daughter of Eduardus Bocklandt (54,\n*touwslagersknecht*) and the already-deceased Maria Ludovica Vanbergen (d. Oostende\n22 Nov 1888). She married **Fredericus Desiderius Debuf** (b. Oostende 28 Sep 1871,\n*matroos bij het zeewezen*), whose own father, Desiderius Joannes Debuf, was lost at sea —\n*\"kwam vermoedelijk op zee om\"* — per an act of bekendheid of 23 February 1892, days before\nthis wedding. AGATHA serves this act only as an \"analyse van akte\" (index transcription),\nnot the register image, hence `sup`.\n\nHer husband very likely stood as informant, \"Fredericus Debuf, 33, matroos bij de\nstaatsmarine\", at the 1903 Oostende death of her niece [[dekeyser_angela]]."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bocklandt_paulina_1870","name":"Paulina Bocklandt","dates":"b. 30 Apr 1870 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bocklandt","family":"bocklandt","sex":"f","born":"30 Apr 1870 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)","order":"1870-04-30","occupation":"werkmeid (housemaid)","line":"de-keyser","father":"bocklandt_edouard_1839","mother":"vanbergen_marielouise_1842","source":"Marriage act nr. 80 — Petrus Dominicus Ketels x Paulina Bocklandt, Oostende, 26 May 1888","note":"Daughter of [[bocklandt_edouard_1839]] and [[vanbergen_marielouise_1842]], and [[bocklandt_louise_1877]]'s\neldest known sister. Her marriage act — Oostende nr. 80, 26 May 1888\n([[agatha-oostende-1888-marriage-bocklandt-ketels]]) — names her born at Hamme 30 April\n1870, *werkmeid*, resident at Oostende, daughter of Eduardus Bocklandt (50,\n*touwslagersknecht*) and Maria Louisa Vanbergen. She married **Petrus Dominicus Ketels**\n(b. Waasmunster 15 Oct 1857, *touwslagersknecht*), whose own father is not named in the act\n(*NN NN*) and whose mother is Maria Louisa Ketels of Waasmunster. AGATHA serves this act\nonly as an \"analyse van akte\" (index transcription), not the register image, hence `sup`.\n\nFRONTIER, not pursued here. Two further AGATHA-indexed Stene acts of 1898 name her as\nmother — a birth, Elisa Ketels (13 Oct 1898, act GEWVL_GEBWVL_00356758, which also repeats\nher own birthplace as Hamme O-Vl), and an infant death, Philemon Ketels (12 Nov 1898, act\nOVWVL_00329163) — so she and Petrus Ketels had at least one more child than this record\nshows. Neither act is registered as a source and neither child has a record here: objective\n2 reaches this generation, but it is not this pass's work."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bocklandt_philemondus_1880","name":"Philemondus Bocklandt","dates":"b. 10 Jun 1880 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bocklandt","family":"bocklandt","sex":"m","born":"10 Jun 1880 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)","order":"1880-06-10","occupation":"touwslagersknecht (ropemaker's assistant)","line":"de-keyser","father":"bocklandt_edouard_1839","mother":"vanbergen_marielouise_1842","source":"Marriage act nr. 100 — Philemondus Bocklandt x Rosalia Cecilia Mewis, Oostende, 12 May 1900","note":"Son of [[bocklandt_edouard_1839]] and [[vanbergen_marielouise_1842]], and [[bocklandt_louise_1877]]'s youngest\nknown brother. His marriage act — Oostende nr. 100, 12 May 1900\n([[agatha-oostende-1900-marriage-bocklandt-mewis]]) — names him born at Hamme 10 June\n1880, *touwslagersknecht*, resident at Oostende, son of Eduardus Bocklandt (62, still\n*touwslagersknecht*) and the already-deceased Maria Louisa Vanbergen. He married **Rosalia\nCecilia Mewis** (b. Oostende 29 Sep 1881, *werkmeid*), daughter of Franciscus Antonius\nMewis and Theresia Lomard of Oostende. AGATHA serves this act only as an \"analyse van akte\"\n(index transcription), not the register image, hence `sup`.\n\nBorn at Hamme just two days after his infant brother [[bocklandt_ludovicus_1875]] died in the\nsame town — 10 June against 8 June 1880. That is close enough to read the marriage act's\nbirthdate with some caution: it is a date recalled twenty years later, not a contemporary\nrecord, and the true gap between the two events may not be quite this narrow."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bogaert_petronilla","name":"Petronilla Bogaert","dates":"1711 – 1792","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bogaert","family":"bogaert","sex":"f","born":"1711","order":"1711","died":"1792","line":"bundervoet","father":"bogaert_petrus","mother":"taedts_maria","spouses":[{"id":"bundervoet_christoffel_1709","name":"Christoffel Bundervoet"}],"source":"Fauconier / Bauwens \"Bundervoet–Vermeulen\" parenteel; Evergem burial register 1792 — Petronella Bogaert, 31 August 1792","note":"Wife of [[bundervoet_christoffel_1709]], and the mother of the line: their son\n[[bundervoet_philippus_1756]] is the direct ancestor of Renée and Léon.\n\n**The Evergem burial register of 1792 supplies almost everything this record used to\nlack.** It held a bare `death: 1792` from the fauconier parenteel and nothing else — no\nbirth, no parents. The register entry gives her burial on **31 August 1792**, a birth year\nof **1711**, and her own parents, [[bogaert_petrus]] and [[taedts_maria]] — a generation\nthe tree did not have at all.\n\nTwo independent identifiers licence the join: the death year 1792, which the held record\nalready carried from a different source, and the husband, named in the register as\nChristophorus Bundervoet.\n\n**The date is the burial, not the death.** The register gives no date of death, so the year\nstands as the fact and the day of burial sits beside it in `raw` rather than being\ncollapsed into a death date the source never stated. The same distinction her\nbrother-in-law's record draws — see [[bundervoet_petrus_1727]], buried at Assenede in 1777.\n\nRead from the FamilySearch index entry, not from the register image, so `sup` throughout.\nReading the image would give the burial in the parish's own words, and might name a\nwidower — which would date [[bundervoet_christoffel_1709]]'s death against the 1786 the\ntree holds."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bogaert_petrus","name":"Petrus Bogaert","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bogaert","family":"bogaert","sex":"m","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"taedts_maria","name":"Maria Taedts"}],"source":"Evergem burial register 1792 — Petronella Bogaert, 31 August 1792","note":"Father of [[bogaert_petronilla]], and through her a direct ancestor of Renée and Léon.\n\nHe exists here on one line of the Evergem burial register of 31 August 1792, which names\nhis daughter's parents as Petrus Bogaert and [[taedts_maria]]. That is all the source\ngives: no date, no place, no occupation, and none of those is guessed here.\n\nA first frontier, and a narrow one: his daughter was born about 1711, so a marriage to\nMaria Taedts should sit in the Evergem registers somewhere before then, and it would give\nboth their origins."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bolle_valerie","name":"Valerie Marie Pharaïlde Bolle","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bolle","family":"bolle","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"vincke_theophil_1866","name":"Theophil Henri Vincke","detail":"m. Diksmuide, 13 Dec 1893"}],"source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Wife of [[vincke_theophil_1866]]. Named on their marriage act — Diksmuide, 13 December 1893,\nact nr. 239 (`rab-bs-huwelijken`) — and again, as his surviving spouse, on his own death\nact — Oostende, 22 April 1922, act nr. 280 (`rab-bs-overlijdens`), where she is written\nBolle Valerie Maria. Index only, not the register image, hence `sup`. Her own birth,\ndeath and parents are not in the reachable pages."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin_anna_1829","name":"Anna Maria Bossin","dates":"b. 3 Nov 1829 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","born":"3 Nov 1829 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1829-11-03","occupation":"dagloonster (day labourer)","line":"thumas","father":"bossin_arnoldus","mother":"deyn_elisabeth","spouses":[{"id":"pardon_franciscus_1830","name":"Françiscus Pardon","detail":"m. Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1 Dec 1853"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 9 — Françiscus Pardon × Anna Maria Bossin, Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1 December 1853","note":"Sister of [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]], and the first of that generation this tree has besides\nhim. Her marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 9, 1 December 1853 (S22) — names her\nparents as [[bossin_arnoldus]] and [[deyn_elisabeth]], exactly as her brother's 1846 act\nnames his, and it is her brother who stands as a witness at her wedding.\n\nShe was of age, born at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe on 3 November 1829 — a date the act gives to\nthe day — living there still, and working as a *dagloonster*. Like almost everyone in the\nact, she declared herself unable to write.\n\nShe married Françiscus Pardon, a servant of Zaventem. Banns were published in both\ncommunes on 20 and 27 November.\n\n`sup` rather than `doc`: this is AGATHA's transcription of the act, complete as it reads,\nand the register image itself is not linked from the page and has not been pulled."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin_antonia_1849","name":"Antonia Bossin","dates":"10 Jan 1849 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe – 7 Nov 1894 Kraainem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","born":"10 Jan 1849 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1849-01-10","died":"7 Nov 1894 Kraainem","line":"thumas","father":"bossin_guilielmus_1824","mother":"peremans_joanna_1824","spouses":[{"id":"thumas_georges_1836","name":"Georges Carolus Josephus Thumas","detail":"m. Kraainem, 20 Jun 1872"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 4 — Franciscus Coenraets × Henrica Thumas, Kraainem, 15 April 1899; Marriage act nr. 3 — Ludovicus Bossin × Maria Isabella Helena Thumas, Kraainem, 10 April 1900; Birth declarations at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe for three children of Guilielmus Bossin x Peremans, 1847-1853; Kraainem marriage act nr. 2, 20 June 1872 — Thumas × Bossin (read on AGATHA); Marriage act — Georges Carolus Josephus Thumas × Antonia Bossin, Kraainem, 20 June 1872","note":"SPELLING CORRECTED (July 2026): *Antonia*, not \"Antoina\". the Kraainem marriage act of 3 February 1902 (akte nr. 2, [[S5]]) names her as the\nbridegroom's mother, which is also what fixes her as the mother of [[thumas_joannes_1876]]. The act\ngives her no dates and no occupation, so none is recorded — her own birth and marriage\nacts are the frontier.\n\nDOCUMENTED (July 2026) by her own marriage act — Kraainem, 20 June 1872 — which names\nher as the bride, born at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, and gives **both her parents**:\nGuilielmus Bossin and Anna Catharina Peremans. The tree already had [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]]\nand [[peremans_joanna_1824]] as her parents on a member tree's word; the act settles it.\n\nHer mother is written *Anna* Catharina Peremans here, where this tree calls her Joanna\nCatharina Jacoba. Both forms are recorded, and neither is preferred without a second act.\n\nACT READ (July 2026). The Kraainem marriage act of 20 June 1872 has now been read on\nAGATHA rather than through an index, and it sharpens this record twice: her birth is\n**10 January 1849** where the tree had only the year, at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe**, and her\ntrade at marriage was *fabriekwerkster*. Her parents are named in the act.\n\nCORROBORATED (2026-07-26) — and she turns out to be a middle child. FamilySearch's index of\nthe Sint-Stevens-Woluwe civil registers (S24) carries her birth declaration as **11 January\n1849**, one day after the birth of 10 January 1849 that her 1872 marriage act gives — the\nordinary gap between a birth and its declaration, and an independent confirmation of a date\nread at the archive. The register writes her forename in the Latin masculine, *Antonius*,\nwhere the act she married under says Antonia.\n\nThe same series gives her two siblings this tree did not have: [[bossin_cornelius_1847]], declared\n13 September 1847, and [[bossin_ludovica_1853]], declared 5 October 1853. Both are recorded at\n`sup`; her own already-documented entry sitting in the middle of the sequence is what makes\nthem safe to add rather than merely plausible.\n\nDEATH DATED (2026-07-26): this record held only the year. **Two of her daughters' marriage\nacts state it exactly** — Kraainem, **7 November 1894** — [[thumas_henrica_1878]]'s of 15 April 1899\n(S27) and [[thumas_maria_1880]]'s of 10 April 1900 (S28), independently, in the field for a dead\nparent. She was forty-five.\n\nThose same acts, with [[thumas_joanna_1873]]'s of 1892, give her three daughters this tree did not\nhave. In 1892 she is alive and keeping house; by 1899 she is a date in her daughters' acts.\n\nDOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.\nNothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the\nevidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own\nDemogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or\nits image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin_arnoldus","name":"Arnoldus Bossin","dates":"d. after 1853","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","died":"after 1853","occupation":"arbeider (labourer)","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"deyn_elisabeth","name":"Elisabeth Deyn"}],"source":"Zaventem marriage act nr. 1, 24 February 1846 — Bossin × Peremans; Marriage act nr. 9 — Françiscus Pardon × Anna Maria Bossin, Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1 December 1853","note":"Father of the groom in his son [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]]'s marriage act — Zaventem, act nr.\n1, 24 February 1846 (S19), read as an image. The act puts him at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe,\nworking as an *arbeider*, present at the wedding and consenting to it. He signed with a\nmark: the act states he could not write.\n\nThe death entry says only that he was alive on the day of the act. He is nowhere given\nan age, so this record carries no birth date — his son was 21, which places him loosely\nin the 1780s or 1790s and no closer than that.\n\nFRONTIER — his own marriage to [[deyn_elisabeth]], which would name his parents, and\nwhich the Sint-Stevens-Woluwe or Zaventem registers should hold for roughly 1815–1824.\nNeither has been searched for him.\n\nACT READ (2026-07-26): named again seven years later, as father of the bride in his\ndaughter [[bossin_anna_1829]]'s marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 9, 1 December 1853\n(S22). Still at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, present and consenting, still unable to write, and\nhis trade written *daglooner* where the 1846 act had said *arbeider*. The two words say the\nsame thing; the record keeps each act's own.\n\nHe is therefore alive on 1 December 1853, and the death bound moves from 1846 to that date.\nHis known children go from one to two.\n\nDOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.\nNothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the\nevidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own\nDemogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or\nits image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin_catharina","name":"Catharina Bossin","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","occupation":"huishoudster (housekeeper)","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"coppens_hendrik","name":"Hendrik Coppens"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 4 — Jan Baptist Coppens × Joanna Catharina Seraphina Thumas, Kraainem, 27 July 1892","note":"Mother of the groom in her son [[coppens_jan_1870]]'s marriage act — Kraainem nr. 4, 27 July 1892\n(S26). A *huishoudster* of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, alive at the wedding.\n\n**Another Bossin of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, and again left unconnected.** [[bossin_antonia_1849]], the bride's\nmother, is a Bossin of the same commune and the same generation. They may well be sisters or\ncousins. The act does not say so, and this project does not graft on a surname and a village.\n\nNo dates: the act gives her none.\n\nFRONTIER: her own marriage or birth act, which would give her parents and settle whether she\nbelongs to Antonia's family."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin_cornelius_1847","name":"Cornelius Bossin","dates":"b. 1847 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","born":"1847 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1847","line":"thumas","father":"bossin_guilielmus_1824","mother":"peremans_joanna_1824","source":"Birth declarations at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe for three children of Guilielmus Bossin x Peremans, 1847-1853","note":"Eldest known child of [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] and [[peremans_joanna_1824]], and an elder brother of\n[[bossin_antonia_1849]]. His birth was declared at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe on **13 September 1847**, eighteen\nmonths after his parents married at Zaventem.\n\nThe birth entry is a `raw` note rather than a date because the index gives the **declaration**,\nnot the birth. They are usually a day or two apart, and this project does not turn one into\nthe other.\n\n`sup`: an index row, no register image read. What makes it safe rather than a guess is the\nsibling in the middle of the same series — his sister's declaration of 11 January 1849 sits\nagainst a birth of 10 January 1849 already read from her marriage act, with the same two\nparents and the same commune (S24).\n\nFRONTIER: his own birth act, for the exact date; and any marriage or death — nothing is known\nof him after 1847."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin_frans_1882","name":"Frans Bossin","dates":"b. 11 Nov 1882 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","sex":"m","born":"11 Nov 1882 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1882-11-11","line":"thumas","father":"bossin_joannes_1834","mother":"wolf_maria_1836","source":"Civil registration acts for the Bossin family of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, Kraainem and Zaventem (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Named as the child in a civil birth act at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 36, 11 Nov 1882**,\n23:00, born at home. **Sex is stated in the act** (\"Man\"), not read off the forename.\n\nThe father, [[bossin_joannes_1834]], self-declares (*aangever*), aged 48, born at\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe, a *herbergier* — an exact match to his own 1834-01-02 birthdate (his\nJanuary birthday had passed). The mother, [[wolf_maria_1836]], is aged 46, born at Brussel, a\n*huishoudster* — an exact match to her own 1836-04-04 birthdate (her April birthday had\npassed). Forty-six is late for a birth but not implausible for a last child.\n\nThe father's trade here, *herbergier* (innkeeper), is the first appearance in this\nfamily's acts of the trade [[wolf_maria_1836]] herself is later recorded keeping in her own\nright after his death — see [[bossin_joannes_1834]] for the fuller occupation history.\n\n`sup`: an act analysis, not the register image. No later act naming him has been found in\nthis pass."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin_guilielmus_1824","name":"Guilielmus Bossin","dates":"1824 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe – 10 Oct 1888 Kraainem","confidence":"doc","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","born":"1824 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1824","died":"10 Oct 1888 Kraainem","occupation":"landbouwer (farmer)","line":"thumas","father":"bossin_arnoldus","mother":"deyn_elisabeth","spouses":[{"id":"peremans_joanna_1824","name":"Joanna Catharina Jacoba Peremans","detail":"m. Zaventem, 24 Feb 1846"}],"source":"Zaventem marriage act nr. 1, 24 February 1846 — Bossin × Peremans; Marriage act nr. 9 — Françiscus Pardon × Anna Maria Bossin, Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1 December 1853; Kraainem marriage act nr. 2, 20 June 1872 — Thumas × Bossin (read on AGATHA); Marriage act — Georges Carolus Josephus Thumas × Antonia Bossin, Kraainem, 20 June 1872; Civil registration acts for the Bossin family of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, Kraainem and Zaventem (harvested corpus, July 2026); Civil marriage acts for the Bossin/Swaelens/Vrebos family of Kraainem, 1884-1901 (harvested corpus, July 2026); Marriage act nr. 3 — Joannes Baptista Julianus Swaelens x Ludovica Bossin, Kraainem, 25 February 1884 (register image); Marriage act nr. 6 — Henricus Bossin x Maria Catharina Guns, Kraainem, 23 November 1887 (register image)","note":"CORROBORATED (July 2026) as a father, by his daughter's Kraainem marriage act of\n20 June 1872, which names the bride's parents as Guilielmus Bossin and Anna Catharina\nPeremans.\n\nACT READ (July 2026): named in his daughter's Kraainem marriage act of 20 June 1872 as\n*landbouwer*, living at Kraainem — an occupation this record did not have.\n\nACT READ (2026-07-26): his own marriage act — Zaventem nr. 1, 24 February 1846 (S19),\nread as an image. He married [[peremans_joanna_1824]] there, and the act states he was **born at\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe**, was **21 years old**, and worked as an *arbeider*. The age puts his\nbirth in 1824 or early 1825, confirming from a civil act the 1824 this record had carried\nfrom a member tree; the birthplace is new, and the *landbouwer* of 1872 was a labourer at\ntwenty-one.\n\nIt also names his parents, [[bossin_arnoldus]] and [[deyn_elisabeth]] of\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe, both present at the wedding, both consenting, and neither able to\nwrite. They are recorded here from this act.\n\nACT READ (2026-07-26): he appears again as a **witness at his sister's wedding** —\n[[bossin_anna_1829]], Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 9, 1 December 1853 (S22). The bride's\nparents are named identically to his own, and he is there in person, so this tree gains\nhis sister and he gains a sibling.\n\n**It also dates him twice over.** He is **29** on 1 December 1853, which places his birth\nbetween December 1823 and December 1824; his own act made him **21** on 24 February 1846,\nwhich places it between February 1824 and February 1825. The two windows overlap only in\n**1824, between late February and early December** — two acts, seven years apart, agreeing\non a year this record had been carrying from a member tree alone.\n\nHis trade moves with him: *arbeider* at twenty-one, *steenslager* at twenty-nine,\n*landbouwer* of Kraainem by 1872. He was living at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, where he was born,\nin 1853.\n\nDOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.\nNothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the\nevidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own\nDemogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or\nits image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step.\n\nA FOURTH CHILD (2026-07-27): [[bossin_joannes_1851]], a birth act at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr.\n19, 15 August 1851 — a son between [[bossin_antonia_1849]] (1849) and [[bossin_ludovica_1853]] (1853). He\nself-declares on that act, aged 27, born Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, a *daglooner*.\n\n**Birth window narrowed again.** Age 27 on 15 August 1851 puts his own birth between 16\nAugust 1823 and 15 August 1824. Crossed against the window this record already carried —\n25 February to 1 December 1824, from the 1846 marriage act and the 1853 witness\nappearance — the overlap narrows to **25 February – 15 August 1824**. The `birth.date`\nfield stays `\"1824\"`: the date grammar's only span form is a year-to-year range\n(`1575..1587`), so a day-precision window cannot be written as the field itself, and a\nplain `\"1824\"` already asserts no more than the year, which both windows agree on. The\nnarrower window is recorded here, in prose, as what the evidence now permits — not as a\nchange to what the field asserts.\n\nHe also appears again as father, self-declaring, aged 29, at [[bossin_ludovica_1853]]'s own\nbirth act (Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 18, 5 October 1853, S33) — a *steenslager* there, same\ntrade as his sister's 1853 witness appearance already gave him. That age falls inside the\nnarrowed window with no conflict.\n\nA FIFTH AND SIXTH CHILD (2026-07-27): [[bossin_henricus_1863]] (b. Kraainem, 1 January 1863)\nand [[bossin_joannes_1866]] (b. Kraainem, 17 March 1866), found from Henricus's own\n1887 Kraainem marriage act and Joannes Franciscus's own 1896 Werchter marriage act\nrespectively — both name this couple as parents directly.\n\n**DEATH DATED TO THE DAY, and corroborated twice independently.** This record held only\nthe year 1888. His daughter [[bossin_ludovica_1853]]'s 1901 Kraainem remarriage act and his\nson [[bossin_joannes_1866]]'s 1896 Werchter marriage act — two different children,\ntwo different registers, five years apart — both give his death as **Kraainem, 10\nOctober 1888**, agreeing to the day. That is what makes the day-level date safe to hold\nrather than a single-source guess, and it now supersedes the bare year.\n\n**UPGRADED BACK TO `doc` (2026-07-27) — two register images, not index rows, were read.**\n[[bossin_ludovica_1853]]'s 1884 Kraainem marriage act and [[bossin_henricus_1863]]'s 1887 Kraainem\nmarriage act were both read as images. Both state him **present in person and\nconsenting** alongside his wife [[peremans_joanna_1824]] — the 1887 act naming both explicitly:\n*\"beiden alhier tegenwoordig en toestemmende.\"* That puts a **hard floor of 23 November\n1887** under the 10 October 1888 death this record already holds, a third, direct\nconfirmation independent of the two children's later acts that first supplied the\nday-level date. This does not reopen §52's downgrade of the AGATHA-only acts, which remain\n`sup`-grade evidence in their own right; it is these two specific, newly-read images that\ncarry the record's overall confidence back to `doc`.\n\n**TWO MORE SONS-IN-LAW, NAMED BUT NOT LINKED — a frontier, not a graft.** Both weddings\nname a brother-in-law of the bride/groom whose own wife is never given: **Petrus\nVanhoudenhoven**, aged 30 in 1884 and 34 in 1887 (b. ~1853), stated *schoonbroeder der\nbruid* at [[bossin_ludovica_1853]]'s wedding and *schoonbroeder des bruidegoms* at\n[[bossin_henricus_1863]]'s — the same man both times, on the arithmetic — and **Egidius\nFranciscus De Hondt**, 26 in 1887 (b. ~1861), stated *schoonbroeder des bruidegoms* at\n[[bossin_henricus_1863]]'s wedding only. Each therefore married a Bossin daughter of this\ncouple who is not yet identified in this tree — a seventh child, or an eighth, neither\nnamed in any register read so far. Recorded here, once, rather than duplicated on every\nchild's own page."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin_guillielmus_1869","name":"Guillielmus Josef Bossin","dates":"b. 30 Sep 1869 Kraainem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","sex":"m","born":"30 Sep 1869 Kraainem","order":"1869-09-30","occupation":"daglooner (day labourer)","line":"thumas","father":"bossin_joannes_1834","mother":"wolf_maria_1836","spouses":[{"name":"Maria Louisa Vanlombeek","detail":"m. Zaventem, 18 Apr 1896"}],"source":"Civil registration acts for the Bossin family of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, Kraainem and Zaventem (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Not found as a birth act in this pass — no Kraainem birth register for 1869 has been\nsearched. He is placed here entirely from his own **marriage act, Zaventem, 18 April\n1896**, which states his birth directly: **1869-09-30, Kraainem**, and gives him as a\n*daglooner*, born and raised, per the residence given, into a family that had moved\nbetween Kraainem and Sint-Stevens-Woluwe (his own residence at marriage is given as\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe). His father is named *Jan Baptiste Bossin*, **deceased\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe, 19 March 1887** — an exact match, to the day, to [[bossin_joannes_1834]]'s\nalready-held death, independently of the same corroboration on [[bossin_jan_1876]]'s\n1897 marriage act. His mother is named *Maria Anna Dewolf*, a *landbouwster*, present and\nconsenting.\n\nA fifth child for [[bossin_joannes_1834]] × [[wolf_maria_1836]], born three years before\n[[bossin_jan_1876]] and at a different commune (Kraainem, not Sint-Stevens-Woluwe) —\nthe family's residence moved between the two at some point in this span, which is noted\nas a fact and not otherwise explained.\n\n`sup`: an act analysis, not the register image, and not itself a birth act — his own\nbirth act has not been located."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin_henricus_1863","name":"Henricus Bossin","dates":"b. 1 Jan 1863 Kraainem","confidence":"doc","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","sex":"m","born":"1 Jan 1863 Kraainem","order":"1863-01-01","occupation":"schaliedekker (roofer)","line":"thumas","father":"bossin_guilielmus_1824","mother":"peremans_joanna_1824","spouses":[{"id":"guns_maria_1864","name":"Maria Catharina Guns","detail":"m. Kraainem, 23 Nov 1887"}],"source":"Civil marriage acts for the Bossin/Swaelens/Vrebos family of Kraainem, 1884-1901 (harvested corpus, July 2026); Marriage act nr. 6 — Henricus Bossin x Maria Catharina Guns, Kraainem, 23 November 1887 (register image); Marriage act nr. 3 — Joannes Baptista Julianus Swaelens x Ludovica Bossin, Kraainem, 25 February 1884 (register image)","note":"A FIFTH CHILD of [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] and [[peremans_joanna_1824]] (2026-07-27), found as a witness\nat his sister [[bossin_ludovica_1853]]'s wedding — Kraainem, 25 February 1884 — aged 21,\nalready a *schaliedekker*. That appearance names no parents; it is his own **marriage\nact**, Kraainem, **23 November 1887** (the act that also brought [[guns_maria_1864]] into the\ntree), that states them directly: **Guillelmus Bossin**, landbouwer, and **Joanna\nCatharina Peremans**, landbouwster, both of Kraainem. It also gives his own birth as\n**Kraainem, 1 January 1863**.\n\n**Two identifiers carry the parent link, not one.** First, the parent names on his own\n1887 act, matching [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] and [[peremans_joanna_1824]] exactly. Second, and\nindependent of the first: [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]]'s death — **Kraainem, 10 October 1888** —\nrecurs identically, to the day, in two further acts for two *different* children five\nyears apart: his sister [[bossin_ludovica_1853]]'s 1901 remarriage and his brother\n[[bossin_joannes_1866]]'s 1896 Werchter marriage. Two unconnected documents\nagreeing to the day is what confirms this is the same Guilielmus Bossin family and not a\nnamesake — a real risk in this commune, since [[bossin_joannes_1834]] already turned out to be an\nentirely different, unconnected Joannes Baptista Bossin two generations earlier.\n\n**Age consistency across five appearances (1884–1902) is a DERIVED check, not an\nindependent identifier.** Against the 1 January 1863 birth: 21 at the 1884 wedding\n(exact), 32 at the 1896 Werchter wedding (one year short of the 33 the date implies), 36\nat a 1900 Kraainem act (one year short of 37), 38 at his sister's 1901 remarriage (exact),\n39 at a 1902 Kraainem act (exact). Two of five a year short is ordinary rounding, the same\npattern already accepted on [[bossin_joannes_1834]]'s own age record — it shows one continuous man,\nwhich the parent-name-plus-death-date pair above had already established; it adds no new\nidentifying weight of its own.\n\n**The mother's forename is the already-reconciled variant, not a new dispute.** The 1887\nact calls her *Joanna Catharina Peremans* — closer to [[peremans_joanna_1824]]'s own anchor act\n(*Joanna Catharina Jacoba*) than the *Anna Catharina* several other acts in this family\nuse. It applies the standing reconciliation (peremans.md, joannes_bossin51.md,\nresearch-log §65) and changes nothing.\n\n**UPGRADED TO `doc` (2026-07-27) — BOTH REGISTER IMAGES WERE READ.** His own 1887 Kraainem\nmarriage act confirms his birth directly on the register — **Kraainem, 1 January\n1863** — and states his parents were **both present in person and consenting**: *\"meerderjarigen\nzoon van Guillelmus Bossin en van Joanna Catharina Peremans, gehuwden, landbouwers, wonende\nte Crainhem, beiden alhier tegenwoordig en toestemmende.\"* That is a hard floor: both\nparents were demonstrably alive on 23 November 1887, sharpening what\n[[bossin_guilielmus_1824]]'s own record already treats as his death window. The 1884 Kraainem\nact (his sister [[bossin_ludovica_1853]]'s wedding) states the sibship outright as well,\nindependently of this act: *\"Henricus Bossin, schaliedekker, oud een en twintig jaren,\nwonende te Crainhem, **broeder der bruid**\"* — no longer resting on the arithmetic\ncoincidence of his stated age alone.\n\n**His bride signs a different name from the one the act gives her — recorded, not\nsmoothed over.** [[guns_maria_1864]] is named throughout as *Maria Catharina Guns*, but she signs\nthe register **\"Justine Guns\"**. A roepnaam (call-name) or a formal/informal name pair used\nby the same woman for the same act is self-referential and no threat to identity — there is\nno rival Guns family proposed at Sterrebeek — but it is worth recording exactly as written.\n\n**Three brothers-in-law stand witness, two of them frontiers rather than links.**\n[[swaelens_joannes_1858]], 29, *schrijnwerker*, is stated *schoonbroeder des bruidegoms* — the groom's\nbrother-in-law, and by 1887 resident at **Kraainem** rather than the Alsemberg of his own\n1884 wedding, an exact arithmetic match to his 11 May 1858 birth. The other two are new\nnames, and neither act names a wife for either: **Petrus Vanhoudenhoven**, 34 here (30 at\nthe 1884 wedding, so b. ~1853), and **Egidius Franciscus De Hondt**, 26 (b. ~1861), both of\nKraainem, both stated *schoonbroeder des bruidegoms*. Each therefore married an\nunidentified Bossin daughter — see [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] for that frontier, recorded once\nrather than on every sibling's own page.\n\nFRONTIER: his own civil birth registration (a separate document from this marriage act),\nand any children of this marriage."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin_jan_1876","name":"Jan Philip Bossin","dates":"b. 15 Mar 1876 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","sex":"m","born":"15 Mar 1876 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1876-03-15","occupation":"landbouwer (farmer)","line":"thumas","father":"bossin_joannes_1834","mother":"wolf_maria_1836","spouses":[{"name":"Maria Florentia Verbist","detail":"m. Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 12 Jun 1897"}],"source":"Civil registration acts for the Bossin family of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, Kraainem and Zaventem (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Named as the child in a civil birth act at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 8, 15 Mar 1876**,\n22:00, born at home. **Sex is stated in the act** (\"Man\"), not read off the forename.\n\nThe father, [[bossin_joannes_1834]], self-declares (*aangever*), aged 41, born at\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe, a *landbouwer*, marked *gehuwd*. The mother, [[wolf_maria_1836]], written\nhere *Anna Maria De Wolf*, is aged 39, born at Brussel, a *huishoudster*. Her age is an\nexact match to her 1836-04-04 birthdate (her April birthday not yet due); the father's\nage is a year short of his own 1834-01-02 — ordinary rounding, given the mother's exact\nmatch on the same act.\n\n**Double-attested by his own marriage, which also fixes his father's death.** His\nmarriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 12 June 1897, to Maria Florentia Verbist of\nSterrebeek — restates his birth as 1876-03-15 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe directly, and names his\nfather as *Jan Baptist Bossin*, **deceased Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 19 March 1887** — an exact\nmatch, to the day, to [[bossin_joannes_1834]]'s already-held death. His mother appears again as\n*Anna Maria Dewolf*, aged 62, present and consenting.\n\n`sup`: an act analysis, not the register image."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin_joannes_1834","name":"Joannes Baptista Bossin","dates":"2 Jan 1834 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe – 19 Mar 1887 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","born":"2 Jan 1834 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1834-01-02","died":"19 Mar 1887 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","occupation":"herbergier (innkeeper)","line":"thumas","father":"bossin_judocus","mother":"desmedt_maria","spouses":[{"id":"wolf_maria_1836","name":"Maria Wolf","detail":"m. Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 17 Jun 1858"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 3 — Ludovicus Bossin × Maria Isabella Helena Thumas, Kraainem, 10 April 1900; Civil registration acts for the Bossin family of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, Kraainem and Zaventem (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Father of the groom in his son [[bossin_ludovicus_1879]]'s marriage act — Kraainem nr. 3, 10\nApril 1900 (S28), which gives his death as **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 19 March 1887**. His son was\nseven.\n\n**RESOLVED (2026-07-27) — not [[bossin_antonia_1849]]'s family.** His own marriage act — Sint-Stevens-\nWoluwe nr. 4, **17 June 1858** (S33) — was the open question this record carried: whether\nhe descended from the same Bossins as his son's mother-in-law, [[bossin_antonia_1849]] (Antonia\nBossin, daughter of [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] × [[peremans_joanna_1824]]). It answers no. The act names\nhis own parents as **Judocus Bossin** and **Maria Desmedt**, a dagloonster — a wholly\ndifferent couple from [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] × [[peremans_joanna_1824]]. Same surname, same commune,\ntwo unconnected families a generation apart; that is now settled rather than left as a\nquestion. It also supplies his exact birth for the first time — **2 January 1834,\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe** — and his trade there, *daglooner*, and his bride's exact\nbirth, **4 April 1836, Brussel**, where she is recorded as a *verlaten kind* (abandoned\nchild) — see [[wolf_maria_1836]].\n\n**Five more children (2026-07-27), all from acts naming this couple as the child's\nparents:** [[bossin_joannes_1857]] (b. SSW 1857, unmarried on the act — see the flag\nbelow), [[bossin_philippus_1859]] (b. SSW 1859), [[bossin_jan_1876]] (b. SSW 1876),\n[[bossin_frans_1882]] (b. SSW 1882) and [[bossin_guillielmus_1869]] (b. Kraainem 1869, known only\nfrom his own 1896 marriage act). [[bossin_ludovicus_1879]] was already the only child this\ntree held for this couple; these six make seven.\n\n**The mother's exact age is the identifier that carries all five.** Against the\n1836-04-04 birthdate the 1858 marriage act gives her, her stated age is an *exact* match\nin five separate acts — 21 (1857), 22 (1859), 39 (1876), 46 (1882) and 43 on\n[[bossin_ludovicus_1879]]'s own 1879 birth act — five for five, which is what defeats the\n\"two couples\" reading the seventeen-year gap between the 1859 and 1876 births might\notherwise invite. The father's own age matches exactly in two of those acts and is a year\nshort in two others — ordinary rounding, not a conflict, given the mother's precision on\nthe same documents.\n\n**His own death is restated twice more, independently.** [[bossin_jan_1876]]'s 1897\nmarriage act and [[bossin_guillielmus_1869]]'s 1896 marriage act both give his death as\n**Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 19 March 1887** — an exact match, to the day, to what this record\nalready held from S28. Two of his children's own later marriages, nine years apart,\nindependently agree with each other and with the record.\n\n**His trade moves with him across seven documents, 1857-1887:** *papiermaekersgast* at 24\n(1857) → *daglooner* at his own 1858 marriage and again at 25 (1859) → *landbouwer* at 41\n(1876) and 45 (1879, [[bossin_ludovicus_1879]]'s own birth act) → *herbergier* at 48 (1882),\nthe trade he is still keeping, and the one [[wolf_maria_1836]] continues alone, when he dies in\n1887.\n\n**FLAG, not resolved — a child born before this marriage.** [[bossin_joannes_1857]] was\nborn **28 June 1857**, about eleven months before this couple's marriage on 17 June 1858.\nBoth dates stand as their own acts give them; neither is altered to make them agree. See\nhis own record for the reasoning, which follows the same shape already documented on\n[[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]].\n\nThe mother's surname is spelled across these acts as *Dewolf*, *Wolf*, *De Wolf* and *Anna\nMaria*/*Maria Anna Dewolf* — one woman, several clerks; see [[wolf_maria_1836]].\n\nFRONTIER: [[bossin_judocus]]'s own marriage and death, neither yet searched for."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin_joannes_1851","name":"Joannes Baptista Bossin","dates":"b. 15 Aug 1851 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"doc","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","sex":"m","born":"15 Aug 1851 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1851-08-15","line":"thumas","father":"bossin_guilielmus_1824","mother":"peremans_joanna_1824","source":"Civil registration acts for the Bossin family of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, Kraainem and Zaventem (harvested corpus, July 2026); Civil marriage acts for the Bossin/Swaelens/Vrebos family of Kraainem, 1884-1901 (harvested corpus, July 2026); Marriage act nr. 3 — Joannes Baptista Julianus Swaelens x Ludovica Bossin, Kraainem, 25 February 1884 (register image)","note":"Named as the child in a civil birth act at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 19, 15 Aug 1851**.\n**Sex is stated in the act** (\"Man\"), not read off the forename.\n\nThe father, [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]], self-declares (*aangever*), aged 27, born at\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe, a *daglooner*. The mother, [[peremans_joanna_1824]], is aged 27, born at\nZaventem. Both ages fall inside this couple's already-established 1824 birth years, and\nboth birthplaces match exactly — two independent identifiers on each side.\n\nA fourth sibling: FamilySearch's index (S24) had already found [[bossin_cornelius_1847]]\n(1847), [[bossin_antonia_1849]] (1849) and [[bossin_ludovica_1853]] (1853) for this couple, but not this\nchild, born between the second and third of those. This act closes that gap.\n\n**A namesake, not a relative — do not confuse with [[bossin_joannes_1834]].** This tree already\nholds a *different* Joannes Baptista Bossin, husband of [[wolf_maria_1836]] and father of\n[[bossin_ludovicus_1879]]. The two are not the same man and this act does not connect their\nfamilies: this pass's other finding — [[bossin_joannes_1834]]'s own 1858 marriage act — names *his*\nparents as Judocus Bossin and Maria Desmedt, not [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] and [[peremans_joanna_1824]].\nSame forename, same surname, same small commune, two unrelated men a generation apart in\nthe records. See the note on [[bossin_joannes_1834]] for the act that settles this.\n\n**The mother's forename here is a reconciled variant, not an open question.** The act\ncalls her *Anna Catharina Peremans*, shorter than this tree's *Joanna Catharina Jacoba*.\nThat is not the unresolved Haesaerts-style conflict flagged elsewhere in this family\n(§51/§53/§54): the anchor act that put [[peremans_joanna_1824]] in this tree in the first place — her\nown 1846 marriage act, S19, read as an image — already gives her the full *Joanna\nCatharina Jacoba Peremans*, and her own record already reasons that shorter forms\nelsewhere are a clerk's quotation from memory of that document. This 1851 act repeats an\nalready-reconciled shortening; it does not itself have to do the reconciling, which is\nexactly what distinguishes it from the Haesaerts case, where no document ever settled the\nvariant independently of the disputed act.\n\n**CORROBORATED (2026-07-27), independently of his own birth act for the first time.** He\nstands witness at his sister [[bossin_ludovica_1853]]'s wedding — Kraainem, 25 February 1884 —\ngiven as 32, *pleisteraar*. Age 32 on that date is an exact arithmetic match to the\n1851-08-15 birth this record already holds.\n\n**UPGRADED TO `doc` (2026-07-27) — THE REGISTER IMAGE WAS READ, and it states the\nrelationship outright.** The act's own words, not this tree's inference from a shared\nbirth act: *\"Joannes Baptista Bossin, pleisteraar, oud twee en dertig jaren, wonende te\nCrainhem, **broeder der bruid**\"* — brother of the bride, in the register itself. The\nsibship no longer rests on the arithmetic match to his own 1851 birth act alone."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin_joannes_1857","name":"Joannes Philippus Bossin","dates":"b. 28 Jun 1857 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","sex":"m","born":"28 Jun 1857 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1857-06-28","occupation":"papiermaekersgast (paper-mill hand)","line":"thumas","father":"bossin_joannes_1834","mother":"wolf_maria_1836","spouses":[{"name":"Maria Theresia De Rom","detail":"m. Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 25 May 1907"}],"source":"Civil registration acts for the Bossin family of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, Kraainem and Zaventem (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Named as the child in a civil birth act at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 15, 28 Jun 1857**,\n10:30. **Sex is stated in the act** (\"Man\"), not read off the forename.\n\nThe father, [[bossin_joannes_1834]], self-declares (*vaderlands kind aangever*), aged 24, born at\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe, a *papiermaekersgast*, marked *ongehuwd* (unmarried). The mother,\n[[wolf_maria_1836]], is aged 21, born at Brussel, a *dagloonster*, also marked *ongehuwd*. Her\nage is an exact match to the 1836-04-04 birthdate her own marriage act gives (her April\nbirthday had already passed); the father's age is a year short of the same act's\n1834-01-02 — ordinary rounding, not a conflict, given the mother's exact match on the\nsame document.\n\n**FLAG, not resolved: born before his parents' marriage.** [[bossin_joannes_1834]] and [[wolf_maria_1836]]\nmarried at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe on **17 June 1858** — about eleven months *after* this\nbirth. Both dates stand exactly as their own acts give them; neither is altered to make\nthem agree. Legitimation by a marriage that follows the birth is the obvious reading, and\nthis tree documents the same shape elsewhere ([[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]], flagged for the same\nreason). It is recorded here as an open question, not resolved.\n\n**Double-attested, fifty years on.** His own marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 25 May\n1907, to Maria Theresia De Rom, a widow of Neerijse — restates his birth as 1857-06-28\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe directly, and names his mother as *Maria Dewolf*, aged 71, a match to\n1836-04-04 exact. By 1907 he had lived at Pironchamps (Hainaut) and returned; his trade\nthere is given as *fabriekswerker*.\n\n`sup`: an act analysis, not the register image."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin_joannes_1866","name":"Joannes Franciscus Bossin","dates":"b. 17 Mar 1866 Kraainem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","sex":"m","born":"17 Mar 1866 Kraainem","order":"1866-03-17","occupation":"kuiper (cooper)","line":"thumas","father":"bossin_guilielmus_1824","mother":"peremans_joanna_1824","spouses":[{"id":"verstraeten_maria_1867","name":"Maria Catharina Verstraeten","detail":"m. Werchter, 18 Jan 1896"}],"source":"Civil marriage acts for the Bossin/Swaelens/Vrebos family of Kraainem, 1884-1901 (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"A PROBABLE SIXTH CHILD of [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] and [[peremans_joanna_1824]] (2026-07-27), found\nwhole from his own **marriage act, Werchter, 18 January 1896** — a commune well outside\nthis family's usual Kraainem/Sint-Stevens-Woluwe/Zaventem range, which is why it had not\nsurfaced before. He was resident at Kraainem, born there **17 March 1866**, a *kuiper*.\nHis bride was **Maria Catharina Verstraeten** — see [[verstraeten_maria_1867]].\n\nThe act names his father as **Guilielmus Bossin**, dead **Kraainem, 10 October\n1888**, and his mother as **Joanna Catharina Peremans**, landbouwster of Kraainem — the\ndeath date is an exact, independent, day-level match to the one this family already holds\nfrom his sister [[bossin_ludovica_1853]]'s 1901 remarriage act, five years apart, which is\nwhat anchors this as the same couple rather than a namesake pair.\n\n**Two of the witnesses are this family, standing for him at his own wedding**: his\nbrother [[bossin_henricus_1863]], 32, *schaliedekker*, and his brother-in-law [[swaelens_joannes_1858]],\n36, *schrijnwerker*, both resident Kraainem — the same pattern that put\n[[bossin_joannes_1851]] and [[bossin_henricus_1863]] themselves in the tree, a relative standing\nwitness at a sibling's or in-law's wedding.\n\n`sup`: an index-level AGATHA/Demogen act analysis, no register image read.\n\nFRONTIER: his own birth act, and any children of this marriage."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin_judocus","name":"Judocus Bossin","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"desmedt_maria","name":"Maria Desmedt"}],"source":"Civil registration acts for the Bossin family of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, Kraainem and Zaventem (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Named as father of the groom in his son [[bossin_joannes_1834]]'s marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe\nnr. 4, 17 June 1858 (S33). The act gives him no age, no residence and no trade, and no\nremark of him being present — where his wife [[desmedt_maria]] is recorded as present and\nconsenting on the same act. Nothing is inferred from that silence: it may mean he was\nalready dead by 1858, or simply that the transcription omitted the field.\n\nThis is the first generation this tree has for [[bossin_joannes_1834]], previously top-of-branch on\nhis own record.\n\nFRONTIER: his own marriage to [[desmedt_maria]], and his death, neither yet searched for."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin_karel_1901","name":"Karel Joseph Bossin","dates":"b. 27 Feb 1901 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","sex":"m","born":"27 Feb 1901 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1901-02-27","line":"thumas","father":"bossin_ludovicus_1879","mother":"thumas_maria_1880","source":"Civil registration acts for the Bossin family of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, Kraainem and Zaventem (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Named as the child in a civil birth act at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 7, 27 Feb 1901**,\n08:00, born at home. **Sex is stated in the act** (\"Man\"), not read off the forename.\n\nThe father, [[bossin_ludovicus_1879]], self-declares (*aangever*), aged 21, born at\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe — an exact match to his held birth of 5 December 1879, since his\nDecember birthday had already passed. The mother, [[thumas_maria_1880]], is aged 20, born at\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe — an exact match to her held birth of 18 August 1880, her August\nbirthday not yet due. Two independent identifiers on each side: age-implied birth year\nplus birthplace.\n\n**The father's trade has changed.** This act gives him as a *daglooner* (day labourer),\nwhere his own 1900 marriage act (S28) gave *polijster* (polisher). Both are recorded as\nwhat they are — the trade on the day of this act, and the trade on the day of that one —\nrather than one being preferred and the other silently dropped. A labourer's trade moving\nyear to year is ordinary and not a conflict.\n\n`sup`: an act analysis, not the register image."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin_ludovica_1853","name":"Ludovica Bossin","dates":"b. 5 Oct 1853 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"doc","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","born":"5 Oct 1853 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1853-10-05","line":"thumas","father":"bossin_guilielmus_1824","mother":"peremans_joanna_1824","spouses":[{"id":"swaelens_joannes_1858","name":"Joannes Baptista Julianus Swaelens","detail":"m. Kraainem, 25 Feb 1884"},{"id":"vrebos_petrus_1856","name":"Petrus Vrebos","detail":"m. Kraainem, 30 May 1901"}],"source":"Birth declarations at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe for three children of Guilielmus Bossin x Peremans, 1847-1853; Civil registration acts for the Bossin family of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, Kraainem and Zaventem (harvested corpus, July 2026); Civil marriage acts for the Bossin/Swaelens/Vrebos family of Kraainem, 1884-1901 (harvested corpus, July 2026); Marriage act nr. 3 — Joannes Baptista Julianus Swaelens x Ludovica Bossin, Kraainem, 25 February 1884 (register image); Marriage banns nrs. 7 and 8 — Joannes Baptista Julianus Swaelens x Ludovica Bossin, Alsemberg, 10 and 17 February 1884 (register image)","note":"Younger sister of [[bossin_antonia_1849]], and one of six known children of [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] and\n[[peremans_joanna_1824]] — a fourth, [[bossin_joannes_1851]] (b. 1851), a fifth, [[bossin_henricus_1863]] (b.\n1863), and a sixth, [[bossin_joannes_1866]] (b. 1866), were all found in the same\npass that day-dated this birth or the one after it.\n\n**Birth dated to the day (2026-07-27), superseding the declaration-date reading.** A\nseparate civil birth act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 18 (S33) — names her directly as the\nchild, states an \"hour of birth\" of 8:00, and gives its own registration date\n(*SourceDate*) as the same day, 5 October 1853. Across this corpus, a Geboorte act's\nEventDate and its SourceDate ordinarily differ by one or two days — a child registered a\nday or two after the birth — which is what made the earlier FamilySearch declaration date\n(S24) read as \"probably a day late,\" on the same reasoning already applied to her sister\n[[bossin_antonia_1849]]'s birth. Here, uniquely, the two dates coincide: an hour is stated, the role is\n*Kind* rather than a declarant, and there is no registration lag to allow for. That\ninternal evidence — same-day EventDate and SourceDate, plus a stated hour of birth — is\nwhy this act is read as giving the birth itself rather than a declaration a day behind it,\nand the field now carries **1853-10-05** as a day-level date rather than a year with a\n`raw` declaration note.\n\nA FamilySearch declaration index (S24) named her parents as *Guilielmus Bossin* and\n*Joanna Maria Peremans* against an entry it read as \"marriage, 17 February 1884,\nAlsemberg\" — a fourth spelling of her mother's forename, after the *Joanna Catharina\nJacoba* of her mother's own act, the *Anna Catharina* of her sister's 1872 act, and the\n*Anna Catharina* of these birth declarations. **That reading is now known to be the second\npublication of the marriage banns, not the marriage — see below**; it was S24 correctly\ntranscribing an index row and this record misreading what kind of act the row was.\n\n**Her own marriage act, read in full (2026-07-27) — Kraainem, 25 February 1884.** It\nrestates her birth exactly as held here, **5 October 1853, Sint-Stevens-Woluwe**, and\nnames her parents as **Guillelmus Bossin**, landbouwer, and **Anna Catharina Peremans**,\nlandbouwster, both of Kraainem — a further, independent match to [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]]\nand [[peremans_joanna_1824]], with the mother's forename in the already-reconciled shortened form\n(see peremans.md, joannes_bossin51.md, research-log §65).\n\n**THE REGISTER IMAGE WAS READ (2026-07-27), and the 17-vs-25 February discrepancy is\nSETTLED.** The Kraainem marriage act states outright that the banns were published \"op de\nZondagen tienden en zeventienden Februari laatstleden\" — Sundays the 10th and 17th of\nFebruary — at Kraainem and Alsemberg. A second, independent register confirms it: the\n**Alsemberg banns register itself**, read as an image, carries acts nrs. 7 and 8, each\nprinted **AKTE VAN HUWELIJKSAFKONDIGING**, dated Sunday 10 February (\"voor de eerste maal\nafgekondigd\") and Sunday 17 February (\"voor de tweede maal afgekondigd\") 1884. **S24 was\nnever wrong about the 17th — it correctly read the second banns publication; what was\nmissing was the fact that a banns publication and a marriage are two different acts.**\nThe marriage itself is **25 February 1884, Kraainem**, now the value in this record's\nfrontmatter, matching [[swaelens_joannes_1858]]'s record field for field as the data model requires.\nThe banns dates are kept here, in prose, as what they actually are, not discarded.\n\nConfidence is raised to `doc`: both this marriage and the discrepancy that had kept it at\n`sup` now rest on two independently read register images, not an index row.\n\n**The witnesses, all named by relationship in the act's own words.** [[swaelens_franciscus]],\n24, is stated *broeder des bruidegoms* — the groom's brother. [[bossin_joannes_1851]], 32, and\n[[bossin_henricus_1863]], 21, are both stated *broeder der bruid* — her own brothers, no longer\nresting on inference from their own separate acts alone. **Petrus Vanhoudenhoven**, 30, is\nstated *schoonbroeder der bruid* — her brother-in-law, meaning a Bossin sister not yet\nidentified in this tree married him; see [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] for that frontier, which a\nsecond, independent act in 1887 repeats.\n\n**A REMARRIAGE (2026-07-27) — Petrus Vrebos, Kraainem, 30 May 1901.** Not previously in\nthe tree. By then a widow — [[swaelens_joannes_1858]] had died at Kraainem on 7 October 1898, named in\nthis act as her deceased \"vorige partner\" — she married **[[vrebos_petrus_1856]]**, himself a\nwidower. Her own birth is restated exactly, **5 October 1853, Sint-Stevens-Woluwe**, an\nexact day-level match confirming this is the same woman. Her father is named **Guillelmus\nBossin, dead 10 October 1888, Kraainem** — sharpening [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]]'s held death\nfrom a bare year to a day, now corroborated a second time independently by\n[[bossin_joannes_1866]]'s own 1896 marriage act — and her mother **Anna Catharina\nPeremans**, the already-reconciled shortened form.\n\nFRONTIER: the 1901 remarriage register image (the 1884 marriage's image is now read), and\nany children of either marriage."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin_ludovicus_1879","name":"Ludovicus Bossin","dates":"b. 5 Dec 1879 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","sex":"m","born":"5 Dec 1879 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1879-12-05","occupation":"polijster (polisher)","line":"thumas","father":"bossin_joannes_1834","mother":"wolf_maria_1836","spouses":[{"id":"thumas_maria_1880","name":"Maria Isabella Helena Thumas","detail":"m. Kraainem, 10 Apr 1900"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 3 — Ludovicus Bossin × Maria Isabella Helena Thumas, Kraainem, 10 April 1900; Civil registration acts for the Bossin family of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, Kraainem and Zaventem (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Married [[thumas_maria_1880]] at Kraainem on **10 April 1900** (act nr. 3, S28). Born at\n**Sint-Stevens-Woluwe on 5 December 1879**, a *polijster*, son of [[bossin_joannes_1834]] — dead since\n1887 — and [[wolf_maria_1836]], who kept an inn there.\n\n**RESOLVED (2026-07-27) — the shared surname is not a shared family.** This record used\nto leave open whether he shared blood, not just a surname, with his bride's mother\n[[bossin_antonia_1849]] (Antonia Bossin of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe). His father [[bossin_joannes_1834]]'s own 1858\nmarriage act now names *his* parents — Judocus Bossin and Maria Desmedt — a different\ncouple from Antonia's parents, [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] and [[peremans_joanna_1824]]. The two Bossin\nfamilies are not connected by this line. The witnesses at this 1900 wedding — two more\nBossins, hoveniers of Zaventem and Kraainem — remain unexplained by this finding; a small\ncommune can still hold more than one unconnected Bossin family, and no claim is made about\nthem here.\n\n**Note the id.** He is not [[bossin_ludovica_1853]], Antonia's sister born 1853; the two ids differ\nby a single letter and the people differ by a generation and a sex. This one carries his birth\nyear for exactly that reason.\n\n**A first known son (2026-07-27):** [[bossin_karel_1901]], born Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 27\nFebruary 1901. That birth act gives him, self-declaring at 21, as a *daglooner* — where\nhis own 1900 marriage act (S28) gives *polijster*. Both trades are kept on their own\nrecords; a labourer's trade moving within a year is not a conflict.\n\nHis own birth is independently corroborated by a further act, the Sint-Stevens-Woluwe\nregister entry his parents' ages are checked against on [[bossin_joannes_1834]] and [[wolf_maria_1836]]'s\nrecords (S33): his father aged 45, *landbouwer*, and his mother aged 43, both matching\ntheir marriage-act birthdates exactly."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bossin_philippus_1859","name":"Philippus Amandus Bossin","dates":"b. 22 Mar 1859 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","sex":"m","born":"22 Mar 1859 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1859-03-22","occupation":"daglooner (day labourer)","line":"thumas","father":"bossin_joannes_1834","mother":"wolf_maria_1836","source":"Civil registration acts for the Bossin family of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, Kraainem and Zaventem (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Named as the child in a civil birth act at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 9, 22 Mar 1859**,\n03:30. **Sex is stated in the act** (\"Man\"), not read off the forename.\n\nThe father, [[bossin_joannes_1834]], self-declares (*aangever*), aged 25, born at\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe, a *daglooner* — an exact match to the 1834-01-02 birthdate his own\n1858 marriage act gives (his January birthday had passed). The mother, [[wolf_maria_1836]], is\naged 22, born at Brussel — an exact match to her own 1836-04-04 birthdate (her April\nbirthday not yet due).\n\n**Both parents are marked *ongehuwd* (unmarried) on this act**, despite their marriage at\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe on 17 June 1858, nine months earlier. This reads as a transcription\nanomaly rather than a rival couple: every other identifier — both exact ages, both\nbirthplaces, both forenames and surnames — agrees precisely with [[bossin_joannes_1834]] and\n[[wolf_maria_1836]], and no second couple sharing both names and both birthdates to the year\nis a plausible alternative. It is recorded rather than smoothed over.\n\n**Later seen as a witness.** As *Amandus Bossin*, 48, *landbouwer*, he stands witness at\nhis brother [[bossin_joannes_1857]]'s 1907 wedding — an age consistent with this birth.\n\n`sup`: an act analysis, not the register image."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bostin_henricus_1801","name":"Henricus Josephus Bostin","dates":"18 Aug 1801 Koekelare – 17 Jul 1867 Varsenare","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bostin","family":"bostin","born":"18 Aug 1801 Koekelare","order":"1801-08-18","died":"17 Jul 1867 Varsenare","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"id":"perquy_anna_1806","name":"Anna Theresia Perquy","detail":"m. Westkerke, 9 May 1833"}],"source":"stefanieschil; Vrijwilligers RAB","note":"FRONTIER above — father of Henricus Josephus Bostyn (1841). Surname Bostin here, Bostyn in the next generation; same family. His own parents not yet recovered."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bostyn_elodia_1908","name":"Elodia Octavia Bostyn","dates":"1908 – 1997 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bostyn","family":"bostyn","born":"1908","order":"1908","died":"1997 Oostende","occupation":"werkster (labourer)","line":"bundervoet","father":"bostyn_henricus_1869","mother":"cappaert_judith_1879","spouses":[{"id":"bundervoet_alphonsus_1905","name":"Alphonsus Bernardus Bundervoet"}],"source":"Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust memorial card — Alfons Bundervoet, d. Oostende 11 Mar 1980; Geneanet","note":"Source detail: Fauconier tree (Geneanet); Oostende marriage act 334, 1930\n\nMarcel’s mother. Oostende birth act 1013/1908. Her Bostyn/Cappaert family came from the Bruges area (Varsenare, Oostkamp).\n\nCORROBORATED (July 2026) as a wife: she is named as the partner on her husband's\nmemorial-card record ([[bundervoet_alphonsus_1905]], d. Oostende 11 March 1980), which puts the marriage on\nan independent record rather than on family memory alone. The card gives no dates of her\nown."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bostyn_henricus_1841","name":"Henricus Josephus Bostyn","dates":"b. 18 Dec 1841 Varsenare","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bostyn","family":"bostyn","born":"18 Dec 1841 Varsenare","order":"1841-12-18","occupation":"herbergier (innkeeper)","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"bostin_henricus_1801","mother":"perquy_anna_1806","spouses":[{"id":"desmet_mathilde_1841","name":"Mathilde Desmet","detail":"m. Sint-Andries, 11 Sep 1867"}],"source":"stefanieschil","note":"Source detail: 1867 Sint-Andries marriage act (via Geneanet tree stefanieschil)\n\nParents named in his 18 Dec 1841 Varsenare birth act and 1867 Sint-Andries marriage act: Henricus Josephus Bostin (1801–1867) × Anna Theresia Perquy (1806)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bostyn_henricus_1869","name":"Henricus Bostyn","dates":"16 Sep 1869 Varsenare – 11 Nov 1947 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bostyn","family":"bostyn","born":"16 Sep 1869 Varsenare","order":"1869-09-16","died":"11 Nov 1947 Oostende","occupation":"metser (mason)","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"bostyn_henricus_1841","mother":"desmet_mathilde_1841","spouses":[{"id":"cappaert_judith_1879","name":"Judith Marie Cappaert","detail":"m. Oostkamp, 31 Jul 1900"}],"source":"1960dirk (Dirk Teerlinck)","note":"From Varsenare near Bruges; moved to Oostende (died Mariakerkelaan 115). Parents found via the Vynce Lémans (vxnce13) tree — his direct ancestry, sourced to the Rijksarchief."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bouchier_constantin","name":"Constantin Stanislas Bouchier","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bouchier","family":"bouchier","sex":"m","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"bundervoet_coleta_1766","name":"Coleta Bundervoet"}],"source":"Memorie van successie, kantoor Hulst nr. 2027, filed 27 December 1807, Assenede — Colete Bundervoet","note":"Husband of [[bundervoet_coleta_1766]], named in the one line of remark attached to the\nestate-duty declaration filed in her name at Assenede on 27 December 1807: *\"Gehuwd met\nConstantin Stanislas Bouchier.\"*\n\nThe marriage has no date and no place here because the memorie gives neither. It states\nonly that they were married, which is why the `spouses` entry carries no `married` field —\nthe marriage is the fact, the date is not known.\n\n**A French name in a Flemish village, and worth noticing.** Bouchier is not a local\nsurname, and a three-part French given name is unusual at Assenede in the 1790s. The\nAssenede marriage register is the place to look; the act would date the marriage and say\nwhere he came from."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bouckaert_marie_1799","name":"Marie Theresia Bouckaert","dates":"b. 16 Oct 1799 Avekapelle","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bouckaert","family":"bouckaert","born":"16 Oct 1799 Avekapelle","order":"1799-10-16","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"vanalderweireldt_petrus_1803","name":"Petrus Antonius Vanalderweireldt","detail":"m. Diksmuide, 20 Apr 1828"}],"source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Married [[vanalderweireldt_petrus_1803]] at Diksmuide, 20 April 1828, act nr. 76, RAB ID 85443 — the same\nact that restates his parents [[vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780]] × [[wyllie_brigitte_1779]]. Her birth is given\nas 16 October 1799 (24 Vendémiaire VIII, the Republican-calendar conversion checked by\ncomputation) at Avekapelle. Volunteer INDEX/Detail transcription (`rab-bs-huwelijken`),\n`sup`, never `doc`."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"boxoens_maria","name":"Maria Anna Theresia Boxoens","dates":"d. 13 Dec 1767 Woumen","confidence":"sup","surname":"Boxoens","family":"boxoens","died":"13 Dec 1767 Woumen","line":"vanstechelman","spouses":[{"id":"vanstechelman_andreas_1698","name":"Andreas Andries Vanstechelman"}],"source":"stechec (Christian Vanstechelman)","note":"Mother of eight, including Silvester (1740)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"brissinck_silvia","name":"Silvia Rosalia Brissinck","dates":"","confidence":"doc","surname":"Brissinck","family":"brissinck","occupation":"werkvrouw (working woman / labourer)","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"devriendt_ludovicus","name":"Ludovicus Josephus Devriendt"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 258 — Eugenius Alphonsius Devriendt × Octavia Maria Schalandrijn, Oostende, 10 November 1906; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Named as mother of the groom in her son Eugenius's 1906 Oostende marriage act (nr.\n258, S20), read as an image — alive, present and consenting, \"werkvrouw\", living at\nSteene, all three stated directly on the act.\n\nFRONTIER — her own parents, per the vrijwilligersrab Huwelijken index, not read at\nimage level: Joannes Franciskus Brissinck x Theresia Francisca Levecke. No specific\nact reference is held for this pass; it needs the underlying act image read before it\nbecomes a fact (verification pass, 2026-07-26)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bundervoet_alphonsus_1905","name":"Alphonsus Bernardus Bundervoet","dates":"6 Jan 1905 Oostende – 11 Mar 1980 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","born":"6 Jan 1905 Oostende","order":"1905-01-06","died":"11 Mar 1980 Oostende","occupation":"labourer","line":"bundervoet","father":"bundervoet_petrus_1879","mother":"vanstechelman_augusta_1882","spouses":[{"id":"bostyn_elodia_1908","name":"Elodia Octavia Bostyn"}],"source":"Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust memorial card — Alfons Bundervoet, d. Oostende 11 Mar 1980; Spaenhiers heemkring memorial-card index — Alfons Bundervoet, d. Oostende 11 Mar 1980; Geneanet","note":"The first Bundervoet of the line born in Oostende (1905); eldest child of Petrus Franciscus Bundervoet & Augusta Vanstechelman.\n\nCORROBORATED (July 2026), twice over. Two unrelated heemkring collections —\nFamiliekunde Vlaanderen Westkust and Spaenhiers — each hold a memorial-card record\ngiving birth 6 January 1905 at Oostende, death 11 March 1980 at Oostende, and spouse\nElodia Bostyn. Two independent indexes, the same four facts.\n\nStays `sup`: both are transcriptions. The Spaenhiers index publishes as a PDF of card\nlistings rather than card images, so there is still nothing here anyone has read."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bundervoet_annacatharina_1772","name":"Anna Catharina Bundervoet","dates":"b. 1772 Assenede","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","sex":"f","born":"1772 Assenede","order":"1772","line":"bundervoet","father":"bundervoet_petrus_1727","mother":"dedeckere_marie_1731","links":{"father":{"confidence":"asm","note":"born at Assenede in 1772, where this is the only attested Bundervoet household — but no act names her parents","source":"Assenede register entries for the Bundervoet household, 1766-1831"},"mother":{"confidence":"asm","note":"born at Assenede in 1772, where this is the only attested Bundervoet household — but no act names her parents","source":"Assenede register entries for the Bundervoet household, 1766-1831"}},"siblings":[{"id":"bundervoet_christophorus_1755","weak":true,"note":"rests on her Assenede birth in this household's own commune; no act names her parents"},{"id":"bundervoet_coleta_1766","weak":true,"note":"rests on her Assenede birth in this household's own commune; no act names her parents"},{"id":"bundervoet_joanna_1761","weak":true,"note":"rests on her Assenede birth in this household's own commune; no act names her parents"},{"id":"bundervoet_joannis_1751","weak":true,"note":"rests on her Assenede birth in this household's own commune; no act names her parents"},{"id":"bundervoet_joannis_1757","weak":true,"note":"rests on her Assenede birth in this household's own commune; no act names her parents"},{"id":"bundervoet_livina_1760","weak":true,"note":"rests on her Assenede birth in this household's own commune; no act names her parents"},{"id":"bundervoet_livinus_1752","weak":true,"note":"rests on her Assenede birth in this household's own commune; no act names her parents"},{"id":"bundervoet_petronella_1754","weak":true,"note":"rests on her Assenede birth in this household's own commune; no act names her parents"}],"source":"Assenede register entries for the Bundervoet household, 1766-1831","note":"A Bundervoet born at **Assenede in 1772**, from the Assenede register index. She is not in\nthe paulderidder list of [[bundervoet_petrus_1727]]'s eight children, and no act read this\npass names her parents.\n\n**Her parent links are `asm`, deliberately.** What is known is one identifier and a\nsupporting circumstance: the surname, worth 13 bits in this corpus, and the commune, where\nthis is the only Bundervoet household anywhere attested — the father buried there in 1777,\n[[bundervoet_coleta_1766]] born there in 1766, [[bundervoet_petronella_1754]] married there\nin 1781, [[bundervoet_livina_1760]] married there in 1788 and dead there in 1831,\n[[bundervoet_joanna_1761]] dead there in 1825. The rules want two independent identifiers\nfor a parent link and this has one, so the link is drawn as assumed: the scorer cannot see\nit in either direction, and it can never come back as evidence licensing another graft.\n\n**The chronology is the reason to hedge rather than to graft.** The mother\n[[dedeckere_marie_1731]] would have been about 41 in 1772, and the paulderidder list of\nchildren stops at 1766. That is possible and not at all impossible — but it is exactly the\ngap where a niece, or the daughter of a brother not yet in the tree, would sit just as well.\n\n**What would settle it:** her Assenede baptism act, which names both parents outright.\nUnder objective 2 that is a cheap, well-aimed fetch — the same register run that holds\nColeta's 1766 birth."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bundervoet_bernardus_1837","name":"Bernardus Bundervoet","dates":"1837 – 1900 Evergem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","born":"1837","order":"1837","died":"1900 Evergem","occupation":"farmer, innkeeper, shopkeeper","line":"bundervoet","father":"bundervoet_judocus_1794","mother":"roegiers_francisca_1808","spouses":[{"id":"goethals_marie_1842","name":"Marie Eulalie Goethals","detail":"m. 1875"},{"id":"dhooge_rosalia","name":"Rosalia Dhooge","detail":"m. 1881"}],"source":"Geneanet","note":"Widowed in 1879 when his first wife Marie Goethals died — the same year their son Petrus Franciscus was born; he remarried Rosalia Dhooge in 1881. FRONTIER (MyHeritage, July 2026): a record in Belgium, Civil Death Registers 1800-1950 (MyHeritage 21034-1003940) is a death act for him — b. circa 1837, d. 1900 — and it names his father and mother. The values are behind a MyHeritage Data subscription, but as a Belgian civil act the same document should be free via AGATHA or FamilySearch. It would independently test the Judocus x Roegiers parentage recorded here. Member trees also indicate he had more children than the single son Petrus Franciscus we record."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bundervoet_christoffel_1709","name":"Christoffel Bundervoet","dates":"1709 Evergem – 19 Nov 1786 Evergem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","born":"1709 Evergem","order":"1709","died":"19 Nov 1786 Evergem","line":"bundervoet","father":"bundervoet_joannes_1682","mother":"stockman_livina_1688","spouses":[{"id":"bogaert_petronilla","name":"Petronilla Bogaert"}],"source":"paulderidder; glorieuxp","note":"Born 1709, Evergem. Son of Joannes Bundervoet's FIRST marriage, to Livina Stockman (not his second wife De Wilde). Children with Petronilla Bogaert: Guillaume (1731), Joanna Maria (1741), Maria Anna (1746), Philippus Jacobus (1756).\n\n**NOT PROVEN, refused — the Gent \"Oost-Vlaanderen, Gent\" cluster (objective 3, 2026-07-27).**\nThe harvested corpus's own clustering (`coverage.surname_clusters()`) offers this record as\nthe `best_link` for a 16-mention Gent sub-cluster, on the strength of a 1904 Gent marriage\nact naming Emilius Bundervoet's own parents as \"Joannes Bundervoet\" × \"Sophia Livina De\nMoerloose\" — a kin-forename echo of Christoffel's own parents Joannes × Livina Stockman.\n26.5 bits, 1 independent identifier, NOT GRAFTABLE, labelled in `research/labels.jsonl`.\n`link.py` already auto-vetoes this identical act one generation down, against\n[[bundervoet_joannes_1682]] directly, as 144 years too late; the same impossibility applies here, 118\nyears up through Christoffel (b. 1709, d. 1786). This is an independently attested,\nunrelated 20th-century Gent line (Emilius 1872–1943 × Sylvia Nathalia Maria De Rudder, m.\nGent 1904). See research-log §73 for the full six-family breakdown this cluster resolves\ninto; none connects to this record.\n\n**A second frontier, left open rather than graftable.** Christoffel's own son \"Guillaume\n(1731)\" and the same cluster's separate patriarch \"Guillielmus Bundervoet\" share only a\ncommon forename, with no place, spouse or further detail to compare — flagged, not\nupgraded. Guillaume has no person file of his own yet; he exists only as this string, a\ngap the tree still owes him under objective b (every person referenced anywhere gets a\nrecord)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bundervoet_christophorus_1755","name":"Christophorus Bundervoet","dates":"b. 1755","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","sex":"m","born":"1755","order":"1755","line":"bundervoet","father":"bundervoet_petrus_1727","mother":"dedeckere_marie_1731","siblings":[{"id":"bundervoet_annacatharina_1772","weak":true,"note":"rests on her Assenede birth in this household's own commune; no act names her parents"}],"source":"paulderidder","note":"One of the eight children of [[bundervoet_petrus_1727]] and [[dedeckere_marie_1731]]. Their father was\nthe younger brother of [[bundervoet_christoffel_1709]], through whom this tree's line runs, so these eight are\nfirst cousins of [[bundervoet_philippus_1756]]'s generation — blood relatives of Renée and Léon under\nobjective 2.\n\nRecorded from the paulderidder tree's list of the couple's children, which gives the years\nabove and nothing further. No act has been read for Christophorus: a birth act at Evergem\nor Assenede would give the day and the parents in the register's own words."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bundervoet_coleta_1766","name":"Coleta Bundervoet","dates":"1766 Assenede – 1807 Assenede","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","sex":"f","born":"1766 Assenede","order":"1766","died":"1807 Assenede","line":"bundervoet","father":"bundervoet_petrus_1727","mother":"dedeckere_marie_1731","siblings":[{"id":"bundervoet_annacatharina_1772","weak":true,"note":"rests on her Assenede birth in this household's own commune; no act names her parents"}],"spouses":[{"id":"bouchier_constantin","name":"Constantin Stanislas Bouchier"}],"source":"paulderidder; Assenede register entries for the Bundervoet household, 1766-1831; Memorie van successie, kantoor Hulst nr. 2027, filed 27 December 1807, Assenede — Colete Bundervoet","note":"One of the eight children of [[bundervoet_petrus_1727]] and [[dedeckere_marie_1731]]. Their father was\nthe younger brother of [[bundervoet_christoffel_1709]], through whom this tree's line runs, so these eight are\nfirst cousins of [[bundervoet_philippus_1756]]'s generation — blood relatives of Renée and Léon under\nobjective 2.\n\nRecorded first from the paulderidder tree's list of the couple's children, which gave a\nbirth year and a death year and nothing else. **Two Assenede records now stand behind\nboth.** The Assenede register has her birth there in 1766; and a *memorie van successie*\n— an estate-duty declaration, kantoor Hulst nr. 2027 — was filed at Assenede on\n**27 December 1807** in her name, giving her husband as **[[bouchier_constantin]]**.\n\nThree identifiers agree, which is what licences reading the estate as hers: a surname worth\n13 bits with an uncommon forename, the death year 1807 that the held record already\ncarried from a different source, and Assenede, where her father was buried in 1777.\n\n**The estate date is not a death date.** A memorie is filed after a death, so 27 December\n1807 says only that she was dead by then. The year stands as the fact and the filing sits\nin `raw`, the same distinction [[bundervoet_petrus_1727]]'s burial draws.\n\nStill index-level on both — the memorie itself has not been read, and it would give the\ndate of death, an address and what she left."});
