FamilyTree.person({"id":"declerck_victoria_1786","name":"Victoria Declerck","dates":"b. 30 Apr 1786 Klemskerke","confidence":"sup","surname":"Declerck","family":"declerck","born":"30 Apr 1786 Klemskerke","order":"1786-04-30","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"janssen_joannes_1778","name":"Joannes Janssen","detail":"m. Oostende, 17 Nov 1819"}],"source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Mother of [[janssen_josephus_1820]], named on his 1851 marriage act (Oostende act nr. 090) as\n\"DECLERCK Victoria, 64, *werkvrouw*\" — still living. Her own marriage act, Oostende 17\nNovember 1819 (RAB ID 572117), gives her birth as 30/04/1786 at **Klemskerke**, age 33 at\nthe wedding, residence Oostende. The 1820 Oostende birth register, still French at that\ndate, spells her \"Declerck Victoire\".\n\n**A stated conflict, not smoothed over.** A birth of 30/04/1786 makes her 65 at the August\n1851 wedding, but that act's Detail transcription gives her age as 64. This is ordinary\nindex slippage on a self-reported age thirty-two years after the fact, and does not veto\nthe identification, which rests on both spouses' exact-matching birth date and place plus\na second, independent corroboration of the parent names on [[janssen_josephus_1820]]'s own\n1820 birth act.\n\nThree further children with [[janssen_joannes_1778]] at Oostende: [[janssen_petrus_1822]]\n(1822), [[janssen_hermanus_1825]] (1825), [[janssen_clementia_1832]] (1832).\n\nFRONTIER, not pursued. Her own parents, per the 1819 act, are **Declerck Pierre × Pauwels\nJosephe** — both recorded as having died at Klemskerke, no dates given. Rests on that\nsingle index row alone, with no independent document. Left unlinked."});
