FamilyTree.person({"id":"deconninck_jeanne","name":"Jeanne Marie Deconninck","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Deconninck","family":"deconninck","sex":"f","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"joostens_guillaume","name":"Guillaume Joostens"}],"source":"Death act nr. 35 — Marie Catherine Joostens, Grez-Doiceau, 10 June 1857 (read on AGATHA); Death act of Marie Catherine Joostens, Grez-Doiceau, 10 June 1857","note":"Mother of Marie Catharina Joostens (1810–1857) and so a direct ancestor.\n\nNamed alongside her husband in her daughter's Grez-Doiceau death act of 10 June 1857, which\nis the only source read for her. It gives her no dates and no place; none is invented here.\n\nThe surname is Flemish (De Coninck / Deconinck are the commoner spellings) in a\nWalloon-Brabant setting, which is worth noting for the search: the family may have come to\nWoluwe-Saint-Lambert or Grez-Doiceau from Flanders, and the name may be spelled either way\nin the registers.\n\nFRONTIER: the Joostens–Deconninck marriage, and her own parents.\n\nACT READ (July 2026): named as the mother of the deceased in her daughter's 1857\nGrez-Doiceau death act, read at the archive. As with her husband, the act gives her nothing\nbeyond the name.\n\nDOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.\nNothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the\nevidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own\nDemogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or\nits image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"dedeckere_marie_1731","name":"Marie Anna de Deckere","dates":"~1731 – 1809","confidence":"sup","surname":"de Deckere","family":"dedeckere","sex":"f","born":"~1731","order":"1731","died":"1809","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"bundervoet_petrus_1727","name":"Petrus (Pieter) Bundervoet","detail":"m. ~1750"}],"source":"paulderidder","note":"Wife of [[bundervoet_petrus_1727]] and mother of his eight children, so a great-aunt by marriage of\nthis tree's direct line rather than an ancestor of it.\n\nShe outlived him by more than thirty years: he was buried at Assenede in 1777, she died in\n1809. Her own parents are not recorded in the paulderidder tree, and nothing else has been\nread for her."});
