FamilyTree.person({"id":"dekeyser_angela","name":"Angela Luciana Dekeyser","dates":"d. 20 Oct 1903 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Dekeyser","family":"dekeyser","died":"20 Oct 1903 Oostende","line":"de-keyser","father":"dekeyser_edouard_1876","mother":"bocklandt_louise_1877","source":"Death act nr. 828 — Angela Luciana Dekeyser, Oostende, 20 October 1903","note":"Daughter of [[dekeyser_edouard_1876]] and [[bocklandt_louise_1877]] — named until now only inside her\nfather's own prose, and inside a §52 note on her mother's record. Her death act — Oostende\nnr. 828, 20 October 1903 ([[agatha-oostende-1903-death-angela-dekeyser]]) — names Eduardus\nDekeyser, 26, *werkman*, as her father and Louisa Maria Bocklandt, *zonder beroep*, as her\nmother; born and died at Oostende. AGATHA serves this act only as an \"analyse van akte\"\n(index transcription), not the register image, hence `sup`. No age or birth date is given\nin the act, and none is otherwise held.\n\nOne of the two witnesses declaring her death, Fredericus Debuf, 33, *matroos bij de\nstaatsmarine*, is very likely her uncle by marriage — [[bocklandt_maria_1874]]'s husband\nFredericus Desiderius Debuf."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"dekeyser_bertha_1901","name":"Bertha Alida Theresia Dekeyser","dates":"b. 7 Aug 1901 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Dekeyser","family":"dekeyser","sex":"f","born":"7 Aug 1901 Oostende","order":"1901-08-07","line":"de-keyser","father":"dekeyser_edouard_1876","mother":"bocklandt_louise_1877","source":"Geneanet; Ancestry","note":"Source detail: Ancestry / Geneanet West-Vlaanderen civil-registration index (Oostende birth act, 1901; original data Rijksarchief)\n\nA newly-found child of Édouard Dekeyser × Louise Bocklandt — born 7 Aug 1901 Oostende, three months after her parents' 4 May 1901 marriage. Her birth act names both parents (Eduardus de Keyser × Louisa Maria Bocklandt). Sister of Jérôme (1897), Gustavus (1899), Maria (1902) and the two infants Angela Luciana (†1903) and Cesar Mauritius (†1905). Her own later life is not yet traced."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"dekeyser_cosette_1963","name":"Cosette De Keyser","dates":"b. 30 Nov 1963","confidence":"fam","surname":"De Keyser","family":"dekeyser","born":"30 Nov 1963","order":"1963-11-30","line":"de-keyser","father":"dekeyser_roland_1943","mother":"devriendt_hugette_1943","spouses":[{"id":"bundervoet_ronny_1964","name":"Ronny Bundervoet"}],"source":"stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck)","note":"Her sister is Sancha De Keyser (❦ Christophe Develder)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"dekeyser_desiderius","name":"Desiderius De Keyser","dates":"d. before 1946","confidence":"doc","surname":"De Keyser","family":"dekeyser","died":"before 1946","line":"de-keyser","spouses":[{"id":"vandenbroeck_maria","name":"Maria Theresia Van den Broeck"}],"source":"Édouard Dekeyser's 1946 Oostende remarriage act (akte nr. 81); FamilySearch","note":"Source detail: Oostende marriage act nr. 81, 9 May 1946 (FamilySearch, Belgium West Flanders Civil Registration 1582-1950 — image read directly), naming him as father of Eduardus De Keyser\n\nFATHER of Édouard Dekeyser — the long-sought wall, now broken. Named (with his wife) in Édouard's 1946 remarriage act as 'zoon van Desiderius en van Maria Theresia Van den Broeck, beiden overleden'. A Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen) family (his son Mauritius Eduardus married in Hamme in 1912; his son Édouard was born in Hamme in 1876). Both parents were already deceased by 9 May 1946. Their known children (FamilySearch, Oost-Vlaanderen civil registration): Édouard (1876, our line), Mauritius Eduardus (1892, m. Marie Henriette Neus, Hamme 1912), Augustinus (†1883 as an infant), Frederiens Carolus, and Leontinus Josephus de Keyser. His own dates/parents are the new frontier — pursue in the Hamme (O.-Vl.) registers (AGATHA / FamilySearch)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"dekeyser_edouard_1876","name":"Édouard Dekeyser","dates":"12 Nov 1876 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen) – 8 Sep 1951 Oostende","confidence":"doc","surname":"Dekeyser","family":"dekeyser","born":"12 Nov 1876 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)","order":"1876-11-12","died":"8 Sep 1951 Oostende","occupation":"werkman","line":"de-keyser","father":"dekeyser_desiderius","mother":"vandenbroeck_maria","spouses":[{"id":"bocklandt_louise_1877","name":"Louise Marie Bocklandt","detail":"m. 4 May 1901 · divorced 14 Nov 1922 · legitimized their two eldest children"},{"id":"schreel_leontine_1890","name":"Leontine Schreel","detail":"m. Oostende, 9 May 1946"}],"source":"Rijksarchief AGATHA — Belgian State Archives search robot; FamilySearch; Geneanet","note":"Source detail: PRIMARY: Oostende marriage act nr. 81, 9 May 1946 (FamilySearch, Belgium West Flanders Civil Registration 1582-1950 — image read directly). Also Geneanet/AGATHA (children's Oostende acts).\n\nWALL BROKEN (July 2026, FamilySearch). Édouard's own 1946 Oostende remarriage act states in full: 'Eduardus De Keyser, werkman, geboren te Hamme den twaalfden November 1876 ... echtgescheiden van Louisa Maria Bocklandt (divorce decree, Rechtbank van eersten aanleg Brugge, ~1923) ... zoon van Desiderius en van Maria Theresia Van den Broeck, beiden overleden.' Every detail matches (werkman; born 12 Nov 1876; first wife Louisa Maria Bocklandt) — so this is unambiguously our Édouard, and: (1) his PARENTS are Desiderius De Keyser × Maria Theresia Van den Broeck; (2) his BIRTHPLACE is Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen) — the SAME town Louise Bocklandt came from (they were fellow Hamme natives who both moved to Oostende); (3) Édouard and Louise did not stay married — they DIVORCED (decree of the Rechtbank van eersten aanleg te Brugge, 14 November 1922 — dated exactly by Louise's own 1924 remarriage act), and Édouard REMARRIED Leontine Schreel (b. Aartrijke 11 Jan 1890, herself divorced from Benoni Joseph Rossel) in Oostende on 9 May 1946. Children with Louise (Oostende civil acts): Jérôme (1897), Gustavus (1899), Bertha Alida Theresia (1901), Maria (1902), + infants Angela Luciana (†1903) and Cesar Mauritius (b.~1904, †1905). This also finally explains 'Hamme' in the old trees: it was the couple's shared birth-town, Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen) — never Hamme-Merchtem, never a marriage place. NEW FRONTIER: Desiderius De Keyser's and Maria Theresia Van den Broeck's own dates & parents, in the Hamme (O.-Vl.) registers. NAME SPELLING: the family surname is recorded both as 'Dekeyser' (one word — the Oostende line) and 'De Keyser' (two words — his father Desiderius in the 1946 act, and the living generation Roland/Cosette). Same family; each person here keeps the spelling of the record they were found in (historical accuracy over uniformity)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"dekeyser_gustaaf","name":"Gustaaf Dekeyser","dates":"b. 1920–1929 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Dekeyser","family":"dekeyser","born":"1920–1929 Oostende","order":"1920","line":"de-keyser","father":"dekeyser_jerome_1897","mother":"paelinck_leonie_1901","spouses":[{"id":"vandewalle_simonne","name":"Simonne Vandewalle"}],"source":"stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck); The family itself","note":"Source detail: Family memory (Roland’s father). Documentary lead: = Gustavus-Josephus Dekeyser b.1899 (stefpaelinck tree, Oostende), Jerome’s brother — unconfirmed\n\nCONFIRMED placement: Cosette confirms Jerome is Roland’s GRANDFATHER, so Gustaaf is Jerome & Léonie’s son — a younger brother of Albert (1920–1972), born ~1920–1928 in Oostende. (This rules out the earlier idea that he was Jerome’s brother Gustavus-Josephus b.1899.) He & Simonne were in England during WWII, where Roland was born in 1943 (plus a daughter). UNCERTAIN: Shaun wondered whether Gustaaf may have died during the war (perhaps in Belgium or France) — but he’s not sure, so this is only a possibility to check, NOT established. He simply isn’t in Belgian civil indexes for a Gustave Dekeyser born ~1920s Oostende, which fits either a wartime death abroad OR a life lived mostly outside Belgium. Open leads to chase next (they’d resolve his fate either way): (1) Roland’s 1943 birth certificate — England & Wales GRO, Edmonton registration district, Q3/Q4 1943, surname De Keyser/Dekeyser, mother’s maiden name Vandewalle (via FreeBMD/GRO); (2) a UK marriage of Gustaaf × Simonne, 1940–43; (3) UK death indexes for a Gustave De Keyser; (4) if he served, Free Belgian Forces / Brigade Piron rolls; (5) Belgian war-dead databases (bel-memorial.org; De Plate Oostende heemkring) — only relevant IF he died in the war.\n\nCHECKED, AND THE CORPUS DOES NOT HAVE HIM (July 2026). His best candidates score 27 bits\nand are **Josse De Keyser of Aalst, 1809**, **Petrus De Keyser of Aalst, 1840**, and an\nAlphonse De Keyser at Leuven in 1952. The first two are a century out and in the wrong\nprovince; none has a date or place in common with him.\n\nThe score comes from the surname plus a shared forename among children, which for De Keyser\nin Oost-Vlaanderen is close to no information at all. This is a clean negative: the open\nBelgian corpus as harvested so far holds nothing that could be Gustaaf, which is consistent\nwith what his record already suspects — that his adult life, and possibly his death, happened\noutside Belgium.\n\nThe leads that matter are still the English ones listed above."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"dekeyser_gustavusjosephus_1899","name":"Gustavus-Josephus Dekeyser","dates":"b. 19 May 1899 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Dekeyser","family":"dekeyser","sex":"m","born":"19 May 1899 Oostende","order":"1899-05-19","line":"de-keyser","father":"dekeyser_edouard_1876","mother":"bocklandt_louise_1877","source":"stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck)","note":"Source detail: Stef Paelinck (stefpaelinck) tree; Oostende birth 19 May 1899\n\nJerome’s brother (son of Édouard & Louise). Was briefly considered as a candidate for Roland’s father Gustaaf, but the family confirms Jerome — not Édouard — is Roland’s grandfather, so this Gustavus-Josephus is a great-uncle, not the father. No spouse or death recorded in the tree."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"dekeyser_jerome_1897","name":"Jerome Joseph Dekeyser","dates":"14 Jun 1897 Oostende – 1972 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Dekeyser","family":"dekeyser","born":"14 Jun 1897 Oostende","order":"1897-06-14","died":"1972 Oostende","line":"de-keyser","father":"dekeyser_edouard_1876","mother":"bocklandt_louise_1877","spouses":[{"id":"paelinck_leonie_1901","name":"Léonie (Philomena Leonia) Paelinck","detail":"m. Sint-Niklaas, 10 Dec 1919"}],"source":"stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck); Rijksarchief AGATHA — Belgian State Archives search robot","note":"Source detail: Stef Paelinck (stefpaelinck) tree; Oostende Burgerzaken; Rijksarchief AGATHA (Oostende birth act nr. 585, 1897)\n\nCONFIRMED Roland's grandfather (Cosette). Full first names Jérôme Josephus; born Oostende 14 Jun 1897 (birth act nr. 585, Rijksarchief AGATHA). Born before his parents married: he was LEGITIMIZED by their marriage on 4 May 1901 (marginal note 'Gewettigd 4 5 1901' on his birth act). Lived in Oostende (Blauwkasteelstraat 21; later Amsterdamstraat 38). Recorded child: Albert Dekeyser (1920–1972); Gustaaf (Roland's father) is another of their sons. His siblings (children of Édouard × Louise, per AGATHA): Gustavus Josephus (1899, also legitimized 1901), Bertha Alida Theresia (1901), Maria (1902–2002), Angela Luciana (†1903) and Cesar Mauritius (†1905) — the last two died in infancy.\n\nDOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.\nNothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the\nevidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own\nDemogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or\nits image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"dekeyser_maria_1902","name":"Maria Dekeyser","dates":"1902 – 2002 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Dekeyser","family":"dekeyser","sex":"f","born":"1902","order":"1902","died":"2002 Oostende","line":"de-keyser","father":"dekeyser_edouard_1876","mother":"bocklandt_louise_1877","source":"stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck)","note":"Source detail: Stef Paelinck (stefpaelinck) tree; Oostende, 1902–2002"});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"dekeyser_rita","name":"Rita De Keyser","dates":"b. 1940–1949","confidence":"fam","surname":"De Keyser","family":"dekeyser","sex":"f","born":"1940–1949","order":"1940","line":"de-keyser","father":"dekeyser_gustaaf","mother":"vandewalle_simonne","source":"The family itself","note":"Roland's only sister, born in the early-to-mid 1940s — in England if she was born\nalongside him during the family's wartime years there, in Oostende if before or after.\nHer birth record is one of the two routes that would confirm Gustaaf × Simonne as a\ncouple, the other being Roland's own 1943 certificate.\n\nMERGED (July 2026). This record and a second one, `roland_sis`, described the same\nperson: both were daughters of Gustaaf × Simonne, both were \"Roland's sister\", both\nborn in the 1940s. `roland_sis` was written when the family could recall a sister but\nnot her name, and this one after the name came out; nothing ever distinguished them.\nThe family knows of one sister, and Gustaaf's record likewise says one daughter. The\ntwo are now one, with `roland_sis` deleted rather than left as a second copy.\n\nNAME. \"Rita\" is family recollection, held with some confidence but not documented.\n\nSURNAME UNCERTAIN — and deliberately so. Her brother's 1943 Tottenham registration is\nknown to have mangled the Flemish name, and the family does not know how Rita's own\nwas written down. The spelling here is the family's form, not a transcription of any\nrecord: treat \"De Keyser\" as a placeholder until a document settles it. Variants\nalready seen or plausible for an English registrar: Dekeyser, Dekeyster, De Kayser,\nKeyser. Any index search must run across all of them rather than the Flemish form\nalone — the wrong spelling is the likeliest reason such a search comes back empty.\n\nFRONTIER: England & Wales GRO birth index, Edmonton registration district (which\ncovered Tottenham) and its neighbours, 1940–1949, mother's maiden name Vandewalle.\nThe mother's-maiden-name field is the strong discriminator — it survives whatever the\nregistrar did to the surname, and it would tie Simonne to this family at the same time."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"dekeyser_roland_1943","name":"Roland De Keyser","dates":"1943 Tottenham – 2003","confidence":"fam","surname":"De Keyser","family":"dekeyser","born":"1943 Tottenham","order":"1943","died":"2003","line":"de-keyser","father":"dekeyser_gustaaf","mother":"vandewalle_simonne","spouses":[{"id":"devriendt_hugette_1943","name":"Hugette Devriendt"}],"source":"Geneanet; The family itself","note":"Born in Tottenham, London in 1943 while his family were WWII refugees (Tottenham was then in the Edmonton registration district); an English registrar mis-wrote the Flemish name. Buried at Stene, Oostende. His 1943 London birth certificate is the key record to confirm his father Gustaaf and mother Simonne Vandewalle — and, if his father died in the war, Simonne likely returned to Oostende a widow with Roland and his sister.\n\nCHECKED, AND THE CORPUS DOES NOT HAVE HIM (July 2026) — the same Josse De Keyser of Aalst,\n1809, that the scorer offered for his father. He was born at Tottenham in 1943 and died in\n2003, so a Belgian civil-registration corpus was never likely to hold him; the harvest\nconfirms it rather than assuming it.\n\nHis 1943 birth certificate (England & Wales GRO, Edmonton district) remains the record that\nwould confirm both his parents."});
