FamilyTree.person({"id":"demuynck_isabella_1782","name":"Isabella De Muynck","dates":"1782 – 1809","confidence":"sup","surname":"De Muynck","family":"demuynck","sex":"f","born":"1782","order":"1782","died":"1809","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"id":"stroobandt_jacobus_1782","name":"Jacobus Stroobandt"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"First wife of [[stroobandt_jacobus_1782]]. isavdw gives her years as 1782–1809 and\nnothing more — no day, no place, no parents, and no children.\n\nHer death in 1809 is what dates the sequence: Jacobus married\n[[keirsebilck_joanna_1791]] at Oostkamp on 24 July 1810, the year after. Our line runs\nthrough that second marriage, not this one."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"denijs_helena","name":"Helena Denijs","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Denijs","family":"denijs","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"id":"stekelorum_pieter","name":"Pieter Stekelorum"}],"source":"stefanieschil; Death act nr. 27 — Agatha Stekelorum, Roksem, 24 May 1855","note":"FRONTIER above — wife of Pieter Stekelorum; dates not yet recovered.\n\nCITATION REPAIRED (2026-07-26), replacing the §52 downgrade. The same Roksem death act of\nher daughter [[stekelorum_agatha]], 24 May 1855\n([[agatha-roksem-1855-death-agatha-stekelorum]]), names her as mother — the whole of what\nAGATHA holds on her: one act, one mention, no dates of her own. CONFIDENCE STAYS `sup`: an\n\"analyse van akte\" index transcription, not the register image. See [[stekelorum_pieter]]\nfor the uniqueness check against the rest of the surname — the only AGATHA act pairing a\nPieter Stekelorum with a Helena Denijs, against two refuted near-collisions."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"deridder_sophie","name":"Sophie Miranda Deridder","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Deridder","family":"deridder","sex":"f","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"thumas_georges_1843","name":"Georges Joseph Thumas","detail":"m. Grez-Doiceau, 7 Oct 1868"}],"source":"The children of Georges Thumas x Marie Catherine Joostens at Grez-Doiceau, 1835-1868; Netradyle — Grez-Doiceau, actes de mariage (tab_mari.php); Netradyle — Grez-Doiceau, actes de naissance (tab_naiss.php)","note":"Married [[thumas_georges_1843]] at Grez-Doiceau on **7 October 1868**, which makes her\n[[thumas_georges_1836]]'s sister-in-law.\n\nNothing else is held. The index rows that record the banns and the marriage give her name and\nno more — no birth, no parents, no trade — so this record has none rather than a guess at any.\n\nCORROBORATED, SECOND INDEX (2026-07-27): [[netradyle-grez-mariages]] independently\nindexes this marriage, \"row 50, 08/10/1868 THUMAS Georges & DERRIDER Sophie\" — a second,\nunrelated compiler agreeing with S25 that it happened, one day off S25's 7 October (the\nordinary drift documented across this venue). Its marriage detail pages carry no parents,\nages or trade at all, so this can corroborate the event and nothing more.\n\nCANDIDATE PARENTS, NOT PROVEN (2026-07-27): [[netradyle-grez-naissances]] indexes a Sophie\nDeridder born at Grez-Doiceau on **20 May 1844**, daughter of Isidore Deridder and Cordélie\nVictorine Lacourt (married there 2 Dec 1839, other children 1840-1853), aged 24 at an\nOctober 1868 wedding — agreeing on forename, surname (a spelling variant), commune, and an\nage consistent with the marriage. Her middle name **Miranda** appears nowhere in this\nvenue. Nothing ties this child to the 1868 groom, and nothing ever could from this venue\nalone: netradyle's marriage detail pages carry no parents at all, by construction, not\nmerely by omission. Surname + commune is one identifier, and age-consistency is arithmetic\nthat fits any Sophie Deridder of the right cohort. **Isidore Deridder × Cordélie Victorine\nLacourt is recorded here as a named frontier only — no father/mother link is made.**\n\nVENUE CLOSED (2026-07-27) on the act that would settle it: Open Archives holds zero\nHuwelijk or Geboorte acts for Grez-Doiceau at all, so `harvest.py` cannot reach the 1868\nmarriage act by any route. FamilySearch (the exact film and image are already known, from\nS23's own volume) and AGATHA both came back `blocked` this pass — an expired/logged-out\nsession, not a `miss`.\n\nFRONTIER: the marriage act itself, which would give all of it in one page, name her actual\nparents, and is in the same Grez-Doiceau volume as [[S23]], near image 221."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"derudder_joanna_1793","name":"Joanna Theresia Derudder","dates":"b. ~1793 Poperinge","confidence":"sup","surname":"Derudder","family":"derudder","born":"~1793 Poperinge","order":"1793","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"huyghebaert_hubertus_1791","name":"Hubertus Franciscus Huyghebaert","detail":"m. Oudenburg, 29 Apr 1821"}],"source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Mother of [[huyghebaert_appolonia_1830]], named on her 1851 marriage act (Oostende act nr.\n090) as \"DERUDDER Johanna, 59, *zonder beroep*\". Her own marriage act, Oudenburg 29 April\n1821, act nr. 24 (RAB ID 253572), gives age 28 (so b. ~1793), *dienstmeid*, birthplace\n**Poperinge**.\n\nStill living in 1868: [[huyghebaert_appolonia_1830]]'s second marriage act (Oostende act nr.\n106) gives her age as 76 at that date, occupation *zonder beroep*, with no death date\nrecorded — broadly consistent with the ~1793 birth computed from the 1821 act.\n\nTen children with [[huyghebaert_hubertus_1791]] — see his record for the full sibship.\n\nFRONTIER, not pursued. Her own parents, per the 1821 act, are **Derudder Pieter Josephus\n× Vandenbrande Anna Maria** — Pieter Josephus d. Poperinge 09/04/1810; Anna Maria age 69\nand still living in 1821, *werkvrouw*. Rests on that single index row alone, with no\nindependent document — and, unlike the Huyghebaert pair on [[huyghebaert_hubertus_1791]]'s\nrecord, no rival-community check has yet been run against it either. Left unlinked."});
