FamilyTree.person({"id":"dewilde_livina","name":"Livina De Wilde","dates":"d. 1750 Evergem","confidence":"sup","surname":"De Wilde","family":"dewilde","sex":"f","died":"1750 Evergem","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"bundervoet_joannes_1682","name":"Joannes Bundervoet","detail":"m. ~1745"}],"source":"paulderidder; glorieuxp","note":"Joannes Bundervoet's SECOND wife (married ~1745, died 1750) — NOT the mother of\nChristoffel or Pieter; both were by his first wife, Livina Stockman. Several trees\nconfuse the two wives.\n\nGIVEN NAME DISPUTED. This record calls her Livina; the paulderidder tree calls her\n**Joanna de Wilde**, and gives her no dates at all — the 1750 death here comes from\nglorieuxp. Both trees are cited below, and they do not agree, so the name is held\nloosely: \"Livina\" is what this record has always said and is kept for stability, but it\nis not settled. The confusion is easy to see how it started, since the first wife was\nalso a Livina. FRONTIER: the ~1745 Evergem marriage act would name her outright and\nsettle it."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"deyn_elisabeth","name":"Elisabeth Deyn","dates":"d. after 1846","confidence":"sup","surname":"Deyn","family":"deyn","died":"after 1846","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"bossin_arnoldus","name":"Arnoldus Bossin"}],"source":"Zaventem marriage act nr. 1, 24 February 1846 — Bossin × Peremans; Marriage act nr. 9 — Françiscus Pardon × Anna Maria Bossin, Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1 December 1853","note":"Mother of the groom in her son [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]]'s marriage act — Zaventem, act nr.\n1, 24 February 1846 (S19), read as an image. She was present and consenting, and like her\nhusband [[bossin_arnoldus]] she signed with a mark, the act stating she could not write.\n\nThe act gives her no age and no occupation, so this record has neither. The death entry\nrecords only that she was alive on the day.\n\nFRONTIER — her marriage to Arnoldus Bossin, and her surname's spelling. *Deyn* as written\nhere is also found as De(y)n, Deijn and Deyns in Brabant registers, and only her own acts\nwill settle which this family used.\n\nACT READ (2026-07-26): named as mother of the bride in her daughter\n[[bossin_anna_1829]]'s marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 9, 1 December 1853 (S22).\n\n**And named as nothing more than a name.** Where the 1846 act had her present, consenting\nand signing with a mark, the 1853 analysis gives her no residence, no trade and no remark,\nwhile giving her husband all three. That is a difference worth recording and not worth\ninterpreting: an absent field in a transcription may mean she was absent, or dead, or\nsimply that the field was not filled. Her death bound therefore still rests on 1846, and\nnothing is inferred from the silence. The register image would settle it.\n\nDOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.\nNothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the\nevidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own\nDemogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or\nits image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"dhooge_rosalia","name":"Rosalia Dhooge","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Dhooge","family":"dhooge","sex":"f","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"bundervoet_bernardus_1837","name":"Bernardus Bundervoet","detail":"m. 1881"}],"source":"Geneanet","note":"Second wife of [[bundervoet_bernardus_1837]], married 1881 — two years after his first wife\n[[goethals_marie_1842]] died. Nothing else is recorded of her: no dates, no parents, no\nchildren. FRONTIER — the 1881 Evergem marriage act would give all three."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"dutreeuw_eugenia_1808","name":"Eugenia Henrica Dutreeuw","dates":"b. 28 Feb 1808 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Dutreeuw","family":"dutreeuw","born":"28 Feb 1808 Diksmuide","order":"1808-02-28","line":"van-iseghem","father":"dutreeuw_ludovicus_1781","mother":"ellebout_ludovica_1765","spouses":[{"id":"vanalderweireldt_carolus_1808","name":"Carolus Ludovicus Vanalderweireldt","detail":"m. Diksmuide, 4 Jun 1828"}],"source":"bartvanhooren (Bart Vanhooren)","note":"Daughter of Ludovicus Dutreeuw & Ludovica Ellebout; mother of Ludovica Vanalderweireldt (1845)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"dutreeuw_ludovicus_1781","name":"Ludovicus Emanuel Dutreeuw","dates":"b. 9 Nov 1781 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Dutreeuw","family":"dutreeuw","born":"9 Nov 1781 Diksmuide","order":"1781-11-09","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"ellebout_ludovica_1765","name":"Ludovica Prudentia Ellebout","detail":"m. Diksmuide, 27 May 1807"}],"source":"bartvanhooren (Bart Vanhooren)","note":"Son of Nicolas Dutreeuw & Therese Desramont; his wife was about sixteen years his senior."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"elisabeth","name":"Elisabeth NN","dates":"","confidence":"sup","sex":"f","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"bundervoet_livinus_1600","name":"Livinus Bundervoet"}],"source":"paulderidder","note":"First wife of Livinus Bundervoet and mother of Segerius Bundervoet (~1615–1669), so a\ndirect ancestor. Her given name is all that survives: the paulderidder tree records her\nas \"Elisabeth NN\", with no surname, no dates and no parents.\n\nSURNAME NOT KNOWN — and specifically not \"Hovelynck\". Livinus's record here used to\ncall her Elisabeth Hovelynck; the paulderidder tree, which that claim was attributed\nto, gives no surname at all. The surname has been removed rather than carried forward,\nbecause a name that no reachable source states is exactly the kind of detail that\nhardens into fact by being repeated. If another tree does give a surname, it can be\nrestored with that tree cited.\n\nFRONTIER: an Evergem marriage of Livinus Bundervoet in the 1610s would name her in\nfull, and would also settle which of his two marriages came first."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"ellebout_ludovica_1765","name":"Ludovica Prudentia Ellebout","dates":"b. 29 Apr 1765 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Ellebout","family":"ellebout","born":"29 Apr 1765 Diksmuide","order":"1765-04-29","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"dutreeuw_ludovicus_1781","name":"Ludovicus Emanuel Dutreeuw","detail":"m. Diksmuide, 27 May 1807"}],"source":"bartvanhooren (Bart Vanhooren)","note":"Daughter of Ferdinand Ellebout & Catherine Millecam; married at 42 a husband about sixteen years younger."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"elseviers_petronella","name":"Petronella Elseviers","dates":"d. after 1838","confidence":"sup","surname":"Elseviers","family":"elseviers","died":"after 1838","occupation":"landbouwster (farmer)","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"coekelberghs_henricus","name":"Henricus Coekelberghs"}],"source":"Bertem marriage register 1838, act nr. 8, 30 October 1838 — Coekelberghs × Haesaerts (REGISTER IMAGE); Bertem marriage act nr. 8, 30 October 1838 — Coeckelberghs × Haesaerts","note":"Mother of the bridegroom in her son [[coekelberghs_joannes_1809]]'s marriage act — Bertem nr. 8,\n30 October 1838, read as the register image. A *landbouwster* of Berthem, present at the\nwedding and consenting to it in person, and recorded as unable to sign.\n\nThe act gives her no age, so this record carries no birth date, and does not call her\n*wijlen*, so the death entry says only that she was alive on the day.\n\n`sup` for the same reason as her husband [[coekelberghs_henricus]]: the image proves what\nthe act says, not that its groom is this tree's man.\n\nFRONTIER — the surname is the useful thing about her. *Elseviers* is rare enough to be\nsearched on its own, where Coekelberghs and Haesaerts at Bertem are not; it also occurs as\nElsevier, Elzeviers and Elseveers in Brabant registers, and her own marriage or death act\nwould settle which this family used."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"engelsen_victoria_1791","name":"Victoria Eugenia Engelsen","dates":"17 Mar 1791 Oostende – 8 Sep 1849 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Engelsen","family":"engelsen","born":"17 Mar 1791 Oostende","order":"1791-03-17","died":"8 Sep 1849 Oostende","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"vaniseghem_judocus_1787","name":"Judocus Franciscus Van Iseghem","detail":"m. Oostende, 25 Mar 1810"}],"source":"gverdievel (Guy Verdievel)","note":"Widowed in 1832 at 41; she lived another 17 years."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"feyaerts_elisabeth_1878","name":"Elisabeth Leonia Feyaerts","dates":"b. 6 Oct 1878 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Feyaerts","family":"feyaerts","born":"6 Oct 1878 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1878-10-06","occupation":"fabriekwerkster (factory worker)","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"vandenbemden_jan_1880","name":"Jan Van den Bemden","detail":"m. Kraainem, 17 Sep 1900"}],"source":"Marriage act — Joannes (Jan) Vandenbemden × Elisabeth Leonia Feyaerts, Kraainem, 17 September 1900","note":"Named as the bride in her own marriage act, Kraainem, 17 September 1900, to [[vandenbemden_jan_1880]] —\nborn at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 6 October 1878, *fabriekwerkster*. The act names her father as\n**Carolus Feyaerts**, already dead by 1900 (Kraainem, 19 June 1884), and her mother as\n**Petronilla Philomena Decoster**, *huishoudster* of Kraainem — neither yet in this tree.\n\nThe act is held in the harvested corpus and reached through Open Archives:\nhttps://www.openarchieven.nl/abl:4c6b4500-15c3-889f-9fda-ffb9021b817c\n\n`sup`: an indexed act, not the register image. This record carries only what the marriage act\nstates; a person exists here so the marriage is a link rather than a string in someone else's\nnote."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"gautiert_albertus_1784","name":"Albertus Jacobus Gautiert","dates":"6 Mar 1784 Oostende – 8 Sep 1847 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Gautiert","family":"gautiert","born":"6 Mar 1784 Oostende","order":"1784-03-06","died":"8 Sep 1847 Oostende","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"robbe_theresia_1787","name":"Theresia Joanna Monica Robbe","detail":"m. Oostende, 5 May 1813"}],"source":"gverdievel (Guy Verdievel)","note":"Born under Austrian rule, he lived through the French Empire and the Dutch period into independent Belgium; died at 63."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"gautiert_anna_1819","name":"Anna Maria Gautiert","dates":"12 Oct 1819 Oostende – 26 May 1860 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Gautiert","family":"gautiert","born":"12 Oct 1819 Oostende","order":"1819-10-12","died":"26 May 1860 Oostende","line":"van-iseghem","father":"gautiert_albertus_1784","mother":"robbe_theresia_1787","spouses":[{"id":"vaniseghem_joannes_1819","name":"Joannes Josephus Van Iseghem","detail":"m. Oostende, 24 Mar 1847"}],"source":"gverdievel (Guy Verdievel); West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Died at 40, a year before her husband; her son Joannes (1852) was orphaned young.\n\n**RE-CONFIRMED (2026-07-27)** by her son [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]]'s own 1872 marriage act (Oostende,\nact nr. 93, RAB ID 582203), which independently restates her death as 26/05/1860 Oostende\n— an exact match to this record, from a document outside the tree-gverdievel line this\nrecord otherwise rests on alone."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"godts_anna","name":"Anna Amelia Godts","dates":"d. 5 Jan 1875 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Godts","family":"godts","died":"5 Jan 1875 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"coenraets_franciscus","name":"Franciscus Coenraets"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 4 — Franciscus Coenraets × Henrica Thumas, Kraainem, 15 April 1899","note":"Mother of the groom in her son [[coenraets_franciscus_1872]]'s marriage act — Kraainem nr. 4, 15 April\n1899 (S27), which gives her death exactly: **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 5 January 1875**. Her son\nwas two and a half.\n\nThe act gives her no age and no occupation, so this record has neither.\n\nA witness at that wedding is **Franciscus Godts**, 54, a plasterer of Kraainem — her surname,\nher commune's neighbour, and the right age to be her brother. He is named here and not\ngrafted: the act calls him a witness and nothing more.\n\nFRONTIER: her 1875 death act, which would give her age and her parents."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"goes_nn","name":"NN Goes","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Goes","family":"goes","sex":"f","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"huyghebaert_carolus_1823","name":"Carolus Josephus Huyghebaert","detail":"m. Oudenburg, 8 Jun 1846"}],"source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Wife of [[huyghebaert_carolus_1823]], married Oudenburg 8 June 1846, act nr. 59 (RAB 253852).\nOnly her family name is recorded in the index; written the same way as\n[[vandenberghe_nn]] — a name half known is recorded half, never completed."});
