FamilyTree.person({"id":"guns_joannes","name":"Joannes Franciscus Guns","dates":"","confidence":"doc","surname":"Guns","family":"guns","sex":"m","occupation":"landbouwer (farmer)","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"vogels_amelia","name":"Amelia Vogels"}],"source":"Civil marriage acts for the Bossin/Swaelens/Vrebos family of Kraainem, 1884-1901 (harvested corpus, July 2026); Marriage act nr. 6 — Henricus Bossin x Maria Catharina Guns, Kraainem, 23 November 1887 (register image)","note":"Named as father of the bride in his daughter [[guns_maria_1864]]'s marriage act — Kraainem, 23\nNovember 1887 — resident Sterrebeek, *landbouwer*. The act gives him no age and no dates,\nso this record has none.\n\n**UPGRADED TO `doc` (2026-07-27)** — the register image was read, confirming him present\nin person and consenting alongside [[vogels_amelia]], not just an AGATHA/Demogen index row.\n\nFRONTIER: his marriage to [[vogels_amelia]], which the Sterrebeek/Vossem registers should hold\nfor roughly 1855–1864."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"guns_maria_1864","name":"Maria Catharina Guns","dates":"b. 23 Dec 1864 Vossem","confidence":"doc","surname":"Guns","family":"guns","sex":"f","born":"23 Dec 1864 Vossem","order":"1864-12-23","occupation":"dienstmeid (maidservant)","line":"thumas","father":"guns_joannes","mother":"vogels_amelia","spouses":[{"id":"bossin_henricus_1863","name":"Henricus Bossin","detail":"m. Kraainem, 23 Nov 1887"}],"source":"Civil marriage acts for the Bossin/Swaelens/Vrebos family of Kraainem, 1884-1901 (harvested corpus, July 2026); Marriage act nr. 6 — Henricus Bossin x Maria Catharina Guns, Kraainem, 23 November 1887 (register image)","note":"Married [[bossin_henricus_1863]] at **Kraainem on 23 November 1887**. She was resident at\nSterrebeek, born **Vossem, 23 December 1864**, a *dienstmeid*. Her parents are named in\nthe act — **Joannes Franciscus Guns**, landbouwer, and **Amelia Vogels**, landbouwster,\nboth of Sterrebeek — see [[guns_joannes]] and [[vogels_amelia]].\n\n**UPGRADED TO `doc` (2026-07-27) — THE REGISTER IMAGE WAS READ**, confirming every field\nabove exactly, both parents present and consenting. **Recorded, not smoothed over**: she\nsigns the register **\"Justine Guns\"**, not Maria Catharina — a roepnaam or a formal name\nused only by the clerk, self-referential within this one act and no threat to identity;\nthere is no rival Guns family at Sterrebeek being proposed.\n\nFRONTIER: her own birth act at Vossem, and any children of this marriage."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"gunst_angela","name":"Angela Coralia Gunst","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Gunst","family":"gunst","sex":"f","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"vaniseghem_eduardus_1901","name":"Eduardus Van Iseghem","detail":"m. Oostende, 15 Jan 1927"}],"source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Wife of [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1901]]. Named as the marrying party on their marriage act — Oostende\nnr. 10, 15 January 1927 (vrijwilligersrab Huwelijken index, `rab-bs-huwelijken`) — the\nwhole of what is held on her: no birth date, place or parents are given in the reachable\npages. Index only, not the register image, hence `sup`."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"haesaerts_anna_1810","name":"Anna Haesaerts","dates":"24 Oct 1810 Bertem – 8 Jan 1880 Bertem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Haesaerts","family":"haesaerts","born":"24 Oct 1810 Bertem","order":"1810-10-24","died":"8 Jan 1880 Bertem","occupation":"landbouwster (farmer)","line":"thumas","father":"haesaerts_joannes","mother":"vandenbroeck_elisabeth","spouses":[{"id":"coekelberghs_joannes_1809","name":"Joannes Baptista Coekelberghs"}],"source":"Bertem marriage register 1838, act nr. 8, 30 October 1838 — Coekelberghs × Haesaerts (REGISTER IMAGE); Bertem marriage act nr. 8, 30 October 1838 — Coeckelberghs × Haesaerts; Sint-Stevens-Woluwe marriage act nr. 6, 24 April 1873 — Van den Bemden × Coekelberghs; Kraainem marriage act nr. 16, 6 November 1903 — Van Esch × Coekelberghs, her remarriage","note":"Mother of the bride in her daughter [[coekelberghs_maria_1848]]'s marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe\nnr. 6, 24 April 1873. A *landbouwster* of Bertem, present and consenting, and like her\nhusband [[coekelberghs_joannes_1809]] recorded as unable to write or sign.\n\nNamed again in the same daughter's 1903 Kraainem remarriage act, which gives her death:\nBertem, 8 January 1880 — ten months before her husband, and both of them nine years dead\nwhen their son-in-law died at Kraainem.\n\nThe act gives her no age, so this record carries no birth date.\n\n`sup`: AGATHA act analyses, not the register images.\n\nFRONTIER — **her forename is unstable across the acts, and it is not settled here.** The\n1838 Bertem marriage, the 1853 birth, the 1873 marriage and the 1903 marriage all write\nher *Anna Haesaerts* plain; two 1867 acts write *Anna Maria Haesaerts*; an 1858 birth\nwrites *Anna Catharina Haesaerts*. One husband, one commune, one occupation and an\nunbroken run of children from 1839 to 1858 make one woman written three ways much the\nlikeliest reading — but it is a reading, not a fact, and the records are deliberately\n**not merged** on it. Only the register images, or her own death act at Bertem in January\n1880, will settle which forename she was baptised with.\n\nGRAFTED (2026-07-26) — her own marriage act, **Bertem nr. 8, 30 October 1838, read as the\nregister image** (`fs-bertem-1838-marriage-register-nr8`). It gives her birth, **Bertem\n24 October 1810** — where this record had none — and her parents [[haesaerts_joannes]] and\n[[vandenbroeck_elisabeth]], both *landbouwers* of Berthem, both present and consenting in\nperson, and both, like her, unable to sign. The image corrects two of AGATHA's spellings:\n*Joannes Baptista* Haesaerts, not *Baptist*, and *van den Broeck* in three words.\n\n**On the forename, the act settles less than it looks.** She is written plain **Anna**\nthree times — twice in the display hand opening her half of the act, and again in the\noperative sentence — with no second forename and no gap where one was dropped. So *Anna*\nis what she was called at her own wedding. It is not what she was baptised: a birth act\nwould say that, and the 1838 act reports her birth rather than proving it. *Anna Maria*\n(two 1867 acts) and *Anna Catharina* (an 1858 birth) therefore stay **unreconciled and\nunmerged**, exactly as before. Her Bertem birth of 24 October 1810 is now a dated, single\ntarget instead of a range, and that is the test.\n\n`sup`, not `doc`, for the same reason as [[coekelberghs_joannes_1809]]: the image proves the 1838\nact, not that its bride is [[coekelberghs_maria_1848]]'s mother, and that bridge is two AGATHA\ntranscriptions."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"haesaerts_joannes","name":"Joannes Baptista Haesaerts","dates":"d. after 1838","confidence":"sup","surname":"Haesaerts","family":"haesaerts","died":"after 1838","occupation":"landbouwer (farmer)","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"vandenbroeck_elisabeth","name":"Elisabeth van den Broeck"}],"source":"Bertem marriage register 1838, act nr. 8, 30 October 1838 — Coekelberghs × Haesaerts (REGISTER IMAGE); Bertem marriage act nr. 8, 30 October 1838 — Coeckelberghs × Haesaerts","note":"Father of the bride in his daughter [[haesaerts_anna_1810]]'s marriage act — Bertem nr. 8,\n30 October 1838, read as the register image. A *landbouwer* of Berthem, present and\nconsenting in person, and recorded as unable to sign.\n\nThe image corrects AGATHA's transcription of his name: the ink reads **Joannes Baptista**,\nnot *Joannes Baptist*.\n\nHe is not called *wijlen* and is given no age, so this record carries no birth date and the\ndeath entry says only that he was alive on the day.\n\n`sup`, not `doc`: see [[coekelberghs_henricus]] for why an image-read act still yields a\n`sup` person record here.\n\nFRONTIER — his own marriage to [[vandenbroeck_elisabeth]], which the Bertem registers should\nhold for roughly 1800–1810. The film is **DGS 004471767** (*Huwelijken 1796–1832*),\nunindexed and bound in blocks by record type."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"huenaerts_anna","name":"Anna Catharina Huenaerts","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Huenaerts","family":"huenaerts","sex":"f","occupation":"arbeidster (labourer)","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"vangindertaelen_joannes","name":"Joannes Franciscus Van Gindertaelen"}],"source":"Marriage act — Joannes Baptista Peremans x Joanna Catharina Van Gindertaelen, Zaventem, 21 August 1848","note":"Named in her daughter [[vangindertaelen_joanna_1825]]'s marriage act — Zaventem, 21 August 1848\n(S34) — as *arbeidster* of Zaventem, present and consenting. The act gives her no age and\nno dates, so this record has none.\n\nFRONTIER: her marriage to [[vangindertaelen_joannes]], which the Zaventem registers should\nhold for roughly 1815–1825."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"huyghebaert_adelaide_1829","name":"Adelaide Rosalie Huyghebaert","dates":"b. 4 Mar 1829 Oudenburg","confidence":"sup","surname":"Huyghebaert","family":"huyghebaert","born":"4 Mar 1829 Oudenburg","order":"1829-03-04","line":"van-iseghem","father":"huyghebaert_hubertus_1791","mother":"derudder_joanna_1793","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Oudenburg birth index, act nr. 24, 4 March 1829 — one of the two births that bracket\n[[huyghebaert_appolonia_1830]]'s own missing birth act, eighteen months before her."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"huyghebaert_adelia_1826","name":"Adelia Juliana Huyghebaert","dates":"b. 13 Jul 1826 Oudenburg","confidence":"sup","surname":"Huyghebaert","family":"huyghebaert","born":"13 Jul 1826 Oudenburg","order":"1826-07-13","line":"van-iseghem","father":"huyghebaert_hubertus_1791","mother":"derudder_joanna_1793","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Oudenburg birth index, act nr. 54, 13 July 1826."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"huyghebaert_appolonia_1830","name":"Appolonia Joanna Huyghebaert","dates":"26 Sep 1830 Oudenburg – 27 Jan 1895 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Huyghebaert","family":"huyghebaert","born":"26 Sep 1830 Oudenburg","order":"1830-09-26","died":"27 Jan 1895 Oostende","line":"van-iseghem","father":"huyghebaert_hubertus_1791","mother":"derudder_joanna_1793","spouses":[{"id":"janssen_josephus_1820","name":"Josephus Joannes Janssen","detail":"m. Oostende, 28 Aug 1851"},{"id":"pieren_leopoldus_1839","name":"Leopoldus Franciscus Pieren","detail":"m. Oostende, 27 Oct 1868"}],"source":"gverdievel (Guy Verdievel); West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Born in Oudenburg; widowed in 1866 and remarried two years later.\n\nHer own marriage act — Oostende, 28 August 1851, act nr. 090 (RAB ID 574198) — names her\nparents for the first time on any civil-registration document: [[huyghebaert_hubertus_1791]]\n(*schoenmaker*, then living) and [[derudder_joanna_1793]] (59, *zonder beroep*). The spelling\nthere, \"Apollonia Johanna\", is not a discrepancy against this record's \"Appolonia Joanna\":\n`data/forenames.json` folds `apollonia~appolonia` and `joanna~johanna`.\n\n**A second marriage, found without looking for it.** Widowed 26 July 1866, she remarried\n[[pieren_leopoldus_1839]] at Oostende on 27 October 1868 (act nr. 106, RAB ID 580783), civil\nstatus \"weduwe\". The act's \"Previous Partners\" table names her first husband exactly —\n\"JANSSEN | Josephus Joannes | Oostende | 26/07/1866\" — corroborating\n[[janssen_josephus_1820]]'s death date and place **from a civil act**, where until now it had\nrested only on tree-gverdievel. Note for a future search: her 1895 death may be\nregistered under **Pieren**, not Huyghebaert or Janssen.\n\n**Her own birth act was not found.** Scope: both spellings (Huyghebaert 2,668 rows,\nHuygebaert 740), province-wide, all years; Oudenburg 1828–1833 read row by row. Oudenburg\n1830 retains only one Huyghebaert row (nr. 96, 26/12/1830) — this reads as an\n**untranscribed batch, not a contradiction**: her siblings bracket the slot exactly —\n[[huyghebaert_adelaide_1829]] (04/03/1829, nr. 24) and [[huyghebaert_marie_1832]]\n(04/03/1832, nr. 20), an 18-month cadence with a gap precisely where 26/09/1830 falls.\n\nNine siblings, all children of [[huyghebaert_hubertus_1791]] × [[derudder_joanna_1793]] at\nOudenburg — see his record for the full list."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"huyghebaert_augustinus_1824","name":"Augustinus Desiderius Huyghebaert","dates":"b. 12 May 1824 Oudenburg","confidence":"sup","surname":"Huyghebaert","family":"huyghebaert","born":"12 May 1824 Oudenburg","order":"1824-05-12","line":"van-iseghem","father":"huyghebaert_hubertus_1791","mother":"derudder_joanna_1793","spouses":[{"id":"vantyghem_nn","name":"NN Vantyghem","detail":"m. Zandvoorde, 23 Nov 1859"}],"source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Oudenburg birth index, act nr. 34, 12 May 1824. Married Zandvoorde 23 November 1859, act\nnr. 62 (RAB 361339), to a bride whose surname alone is recorded, Vantyghem."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"huyghebaert_carolus_1822","name":"Carolus Josephus Huyghebaert","dates":"b. 13 Mar 1822 Oudenburg","confidence":"sup","surname":"Huyghebaert","family":"huyghebaert","born":"13 Mar 1822 Oudenburg","order":"1822-03-13","line":"van-iseghem","father":"huyghebaert_hubertus_1791","mother":"derudder_joanna_1793","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Oudenburg birth index, act nr. 11, 13 March 1822. Ten months later the same forename pair\nis registered again to the same parents ([[huyghebaert_carolus_1823]]) — the ordinary sign of\na name reused after an infant death, though no death act for this child has itself been\nfound."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"huyghebaert_carolus_1823","name":"Carolus Josephus Huyghebaert","dates":"b. 1 Feb 1823 Oudenburg","confidence":"sup","surname":"Huyghebaert","family":"huyghebaert","born":"1 Feb 1823 Oudenburg","order":"1823-02-01","line":"van-iseghem","father":"huyghebaert_hubertus_1791","mother":"derudder_joanna_1793","spouses":[{"id":"goes_nn","name":"NN Goes","detail":"m. Oudenburg, 8 Jun 1846"}],"source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Oudenburg birth index, act nr. 12, 1 February 1823 — the same forename pair as\n[[huyghebaert_carolus_1822]], born ten months earlier, most likely reused after that child's\ninfant death. Married Oudenburg 8 June 1846, act nr. 59 (RAB 253852), to a bride whose\nsurname alone is recorded, Goes."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"huyghebaert_hubertus_1791","name":"Hubertus Franciscus Huyghebaert","dates":"~1791 Oudenburg – 15 Mar 1857 Oudenburg","confidence":"sup","surname":"Huyghebaert","family":"huyghebaert","born":"~1791 Oudenburg","order":"1791","died":"15 Mar 1857 Oudenburg","occupation":"schoenmaker (shoemaker)","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"derudder_joanna_1793","name":"Joanna Theresia Derudder","detail":"m. Oudenburg, 29 Apr 1821"}],"source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Father of [[huyghebaert_appolonia_1830]], named on her 1851 marriage act (Oostende act nr.\n090) as \"HUYGHEBAERT Hubertus, *schoenmaker*, living\". His own marriage act, Oudenburg 29\nApril 1821, act nr. 24 (RAB ID 253572, microfilm 1358641, remark \"SCAN 122 GSU\"), gives\nage 30 (so b. ~1791), *schoenmaker*, residence Oudenburg.\n\nHis daughter [[huyghebaert_appolonia_1830]]'s 1868 remarriage act (Oostende act nr. 106)\nindependently gives his death: **15 March 1857, Oudenburg** — read off the \"Decease Date\nFather\" / \"Location of Decease Father\" fields on the bride's side of the same act already\naccepted for corroborating her first husband's death.\n\nTen children with [[derudder_joanna_1793]] at Oudenburg, all sup from the RAB birth index:\n[[huyghebaert_carolus_1822]] (13/03/1822, apparently died in infancy — see\n[[huyghebaert_carolus_1823]]), [[huyghebaert_carolus_1823]] (the name reused, 01/02/1823, m.\nOudenburg 1846 [[goes_nn]]), [[huyghebaert_augustinus_1824]] (12/05/1824, m. Zandvoorde 1859\n[[vantyghem_nn]]), [[huyghebaert_adelia_1826]] (13/07/1826), [[huyghebaert_petrus_1827]]\n(05/08/1827), [[huyghebaert_adelaide_1829]] (04/03/1829), [[huyghebaert_appolonia_1830]]\n(26/09/1830 — own birth act not found, see her record), [[huyghebaert_marie_1832]]\n(04/03/1832), [[huyghebaert_magdalena_1834]] (21/06/1834) and [[huyghebaert_petrus_1837]]\n(19/02/1837).\n\n**FRONTIER, refused despite being right there.** His own parents, per the 1821 act, are\n**Ferdinandus Huyghebaert × Anna Theresia Termote** — Ferdinandus d. Oudenburg 06/07/1803\n(17 Messidor XI), Anna Theresia d. Oudenburg 05/05/1804 (15 Floréal XII); both\nrepublican-calendar dates convert correctly to their Gregorian equivalents. **Not\nlinked**: this identical name pair recurs as parents in at least four other West-Flemish\ncommunes (Eernegem, Leffinge, Westkerke, Oostkerke-bij-Damme) — exactly the\nsurname-and-region trap CLAUDE.md rule 1 exists for, and this single 1821 index row is\nthe only document naming them for *this* family. The document that would settle it: the\nDetail page of **Oudenburg 1806, RAB 253462** — same name pair as parents, a different\nchild — which could not be pulled this pass. Re-openable there, or at the register image."});
