FamilyTree.person({"id":"janssen_hermanie_1853","name":"Hermanie Ludovica Janssen","dates":"5 Jul 1853 Oostende – 13 Nov 1926 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Janssen","family":"janssen","born":"5 Jul 1853 Oostende","order":"1853-07-05","died":"13 Nov 1926 Oostende","line":"van-iseghem","father":"janssen_josephus_1820","mother":"huyghebaert_appolonia_1830","spouses":[{"id":"vaniseghem_joannes_1852","name":"Joannes Van Iseghem","detail":"m. Oostende, 23 Aug 1872"}],"source":"gverdievel (Guy Verdievel); West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; Marriage act nr. 212 — Eduardus Ludovicus Rudolphus Vanyseghem x Emma Celesta Vincke, Oostende, 28 September 1907 (register image)","note":"Married at 19; lived her whole life in Oostende, reaching 73.\n\nHer own birth act — Oostende, 5 July 1853, act nr. 238, RAB ID 1458582 — confirms her\nfather/mother links, until now sourced from a single Geneanet tree (tree-gverdievel)\nalone: both parents are named in full, \"JANSSEN Josephus Joannes x HUYGHEBAERT Appolonia\nJoanna\", matching this record exactly. What changed is not the fact but its basis: a\ncivil-act index, independent of that member tree, now stands behind it.\n\n**HER OWN DEATH ACT (2026-07-27)** — Oostende, 13 November 1926, act nr. 611, RAB ID\n2201502 — gives Birth Date 05/07/1853, matching her held birth to the day, and names her\npartner \"VANISEGHEM Joannes\", matching [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] exactly. Both her parents are\nrestated in full, agreeing with her own birth act above.\n\n**A THIRD, INDEPENDENT PRIMARY SOURCE FOR THE SAME LINK (2026-07-27), DOC-GRADE.** Her son\n[[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]]'s own 1907 marriage act, read as a register image\n([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]],\n`data/artifacts/vaniseghem-vincke-1907-marriage-oostende.md`), names her present and\nconsenting, *\"zonder beroep\"*. A different register from both her own birth and death\nacts, 26 years before the latter — a third, wholly independent primary attestation of the\n[[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] × [[janssen_hermanie_1853]] → [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] link. This record's own vital\ndates remain index-only, so confidence stays `sup`.\n\n**EIGHT CHILDREN with [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] — see his record for the full sibship, the\nidentifier that grounds it (a province-wide sweep found nine different men recorded\nidentically as \"Joannes Vaniseghem\", so the parent PAIR, not the father's name alone, is\nwhat carries this), the two unnamed infant deaths that are not counted among the eight,\nand the narrowed negative on an unrecorded daughter.** Filtering the birth index by her\nown surname independently returns the identical eight RAB IDs found from her husband's\nside — no rival couple, no ninth child."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"janssen_hermanus_1825","name":"Hermanus Edouardus Janssen","dates":"b. 14 Aug 1825 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Janssen","family":"janssen","born":"14 Aug 1825 Oostende","order":"1825-08-14","line":"van-iseghem","father":"janssen_joannes_1778","mother":"declerck_victoria_1786","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Oostende birth index, act nr. 223, 14 August 1825 (RAB ID 625496). A plausible namesake\nfor his brother [[janssen_josephus_1820]]'s own daughter Hermania Ludovica\n([[janssen_hermanie_1853]], b. 1853) — noted, not asserted as more than a naming echo."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"janssen_joannes_1778","name":"Joannes Janssen","dates":"11 Apr 1778 Moersum (D.) – before 1851 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Janssen","family":"janssen","born":"11 Apr 1778 Moersum (D.)","order":"1778-04-11","died":"before 1851 Oostende","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"declerck_victoria_1786","name":"Victoria Declerck","detail":"m. Oostende, 17 Nov 1819"}],"source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Father of [[janssen_josephus_1820]], named on his son's 1851 marriage act (Oostende, act nr.\n090) as \"JANSSEN Joannes, deceased at Oostende\" — no date given, only that he had already\ndied by 1851. His own marriage act, Oostende 17 November 1819 (RAB ID 572117, microfilm\n1358564, remark \"SCAN 812 GSU\"), gives the fuller record: b. 11/04/1778 **Moersum\n(Deutschland)** — Germany — age 41, *zeeman* (seaman), residence not stated. The 1820\nOostende birth register, still kept in French at that date, spells him \"Jean Janssen\" —\nthe same man, a register-language difference rather than two people; the 1851 act, in\nDutch, gives \"Joannes\".\n\nThree further children with [[declerck_victoria_1786]] at Oostende: [[janssen_petrus_1822]]\n(1822), [[janssen_hermanus_1825]] (1825), [[janssen_clementia_1832]] (1832), besides\n[[janssen_josephus_1820]] himself (1820).\n\nFRONTIER, not pursued. His own parents, per the 1819 act, are **Jean Janssen × Karckman\nCatherine** — both recorded only as having died at an unknown place (\"Onbekend\"), no\ndates given. Rests on that single index row alone, with no independent document. Left\nunlinked."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"janssen_josephus_1820","name":"Josephus Joannes Janssen","dates":"11 Aug 1820 Oostende – 26 Jul 1866 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Janssen","family":"janssen","born":"11 Aug 1820 Oostende","order":"1820-08-11","died":"26 Jul 1866 Oostende","line":"van-iseghem","father":"janssen_joannes_1778","mother":"declerck_victoria_1786","spouses":[{"id":"huyghebaert_appolonia_1830","name":"Appolonia Joanna Huyghebaert","detail":"m. Oostende, 28 Aug 1851"}],"source":"gverdievel (Guy Verdievel); West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Died at only 45; father of [[janssen_hermanie_1853]], who married into the Van Iseghem line,\nand of nine other children (below).\n\nHis own marriage act — Oostende, 28 August 1851, act nr. 090 (RAB ID 574198, microfilm\n1358587, FamilySearch waypoint QZ9J-PQZ) — names his parents for the first time on any\ncivil-registration document: [[janssen_joannes_1778]] (deceased at Oostende by 1851) and\n[[declerck_victoria_1786]] (64, *werkvrouw*). Both spouses' birth date and place match this\nrecord's pre-existing (tree-gverdievel) values exactly.\n\n**Independently corroborated by his own birth act**, Oostende 11 August 1820, act nr.\n303, RAB ID 623503 (FamilySearch waypoint QZ9J-P7S) — \"JANSSEN Joseph Jean, F: JANSSEN\nJean, M: DECLERCK Victoire\", French register forms. **Checked explicitly against the\nduplicate-id trap**: 623503 is not 574198 — a different register (geboorten vs\nhuwelijken), a different RAB ID, a different FamilySearch waypoint and film, so this is a\nsecond, independent transcription rather than the same index row counted twice. Rival\ncheck: of 315 Janssen rows in the province-wide birth index, exactly four have a Declerck\nmother, and all four name this identical couple (children born 1820, 1822, 1825, 1832) —\nno rival family anywhere in the sweep.\n\nThree siblings at Oostende, same parents: [[janssen_petrus_1822]] (24/11/1822, nr. 392),\n[[janssen_hermanus_1825]] (14/08/1825, nr. 223), [[janssen_clementia_1832]] (30/03/1832).\n\nTen children with [[huyghebaert_appolonia_1830]] at Oostende, all sup from the RAB birth\nindex: [[janssen_pharaildis_1852]] (06/04/1852, nr. 127), [[janssen_hermanie_1853]] (05/07/1853,\nnr. 238), [[janssen_augustus_1855]] (04/12/1855, nr. 472), [[janssen_paulus_1857]] (17/09/1857,\nnr. 417), [[janssen_maria_1858]] (26/12/1858, nr. 531), [[janssen_victorina_1860]]\n(21/02/1860, nr. 93), [[janssen_florentina_1861]] (24/04/1861, nr. 158),\n[[janssen_carolus_1862]] (13/06/1862, nr. 228), [[janssen_seraphinus_1864]] (14/09/1864, nr.\n394) and [[janssen_josephus_1866]] (11/08/1866, nr. 348) — this last **posthumous**, born\nsixteen days after his father's death on 26 July 1866.\n\nFamilySearch's ark (3:1:QZ9J-PQZ) and film 001358587 both returned HTTP 403\nunauthenticated this pass — a one-request retry once a session exists, not a miss (the\nmaterial was never reached).\n\n**RE-CONFIRMED A SECOND TIME (2026-07-27)**, independently of the 1868 Pieren remarriage\nact above: [[janssen_hermanie_1853]]'s own 1872 marriage act (Oostende, act nr. 93, RAB ID\n582203) also restates his death as 26/07/1866 Oostende — a third document, wholly\nseparate register and volunteer batch, agreeing to the day."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"janssen_josephus_1866","name":"Josephus Amandus Janssen","dates":"b. 11 Aug 1866 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Janssen","family":"janssen","born":"11 Aug 1866 Oostende","order":"1866-08-11","line":"van-iseghem","father":"janssen_josephus_1820","mother":"huyghebaert_appolonia_1830","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Oostende birth index, act nr. 348, 11 August 1866 (RAB ID 1458584) — youngest of ten\nchildren, and **posthumous**: born sixteen days after his father [[janssen_josephus_1820]]'s\ndeath on 26 July 1866. The arithmetic was checked (26 July to 11 August is sixteen days),\nconsistent with a birth already carried to term when the father died."});
