FamilyTree.person({"id":"langes_elisabeth","name":"Elisabeth Agatha Langes","dates":"d. after 1873","confidence":"sup","surname":"Langes","family":"langes","died":"after 1873","occupation":"landbouwster (farmer)","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"vandenbemden_jan","name":"Jan Baptist Van den Bemden"}],"source":"Sint-Stevens-Woluwe marriage act nr. 6, 24 April 1873 — Van den Bemden × Coekelberghs","note":"Mother of the groom in her son [[vandenbemden_henricus_1849]]'s marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 6,\n24 April 1873. A *landbouwster* of Everberg, present at the wedding and consenting to it,\nand recorded as unable to write.\n\nEverberg is where her son was born, in August 1849, so the family was still there\ntwenty-four years later.\n\n**She is a correction, not only an addition.** [[vandenbemden_henricus_1849]]'s record carried, as an\nunverified Geneanet claim, a mother named *Agatha Langa*. The act names her **Elisabeth\nAgatha** and spells the surname **Langes**. The forename was incomplete and the surname\nwas wrong; both are now as the act has them, and the Geneanet reading is retired.\n\nThe act gives her no age, so this record carries no birth date. The death entry records\nonly that she was alive on the day.\n\n`sup`: an AGATHA act analysis, not the register image.\n\nFRONTIER — the spelling is worth pinning before it is searched on. *Langes* as written here\nalso occurs as Lange, Langhe and Langens in Brabant registers, and the Geneanet reading\n*Langa* is a fourth. Her own marriage or her death act at Everberg would settle it, and a\nsurname that rare is one of the few that can be searched on its own."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"leclercq_marie_1710","name":"Marie Jacqueline Leclercq","dates":"30 Oct 1710 Grez-Doiceau – 14 Apr 1786 Grez-Doiceau","confidence":"sup","surname":"Leclercq","family":"leclercq","born":"30 Oct 1710 Grez-Doiceau","order":"1710-10-30","died":"14 Apr 1786 Grez-Doiceau","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"thumas_jean_1701","name":"Jean Lambert Thumas","detail":"m. Wavre, 23 Feb 1743"}],"source":"Death act nr. 58 — George Thumas, Grez-Doiceau, 20 November 1808 (read on AGATHA); Death act of George Thumas, Grez-Doiceau, 20 November 1808; m2155","note":"CORROBORATED (July 2026) as a mother. Her son Georges's death act (Grez-Doiceau, 20\nNovember 1808) names his mother as *Marie Leclercq*, alongside the father Lambert Thumas —\nwhich puts this couple, and her motherhood of the line's Georges, on a civil act.\n\nSecond wife of Jean Lambert Thumas (m. Wavre 1743) and mother of the line's Georges (1744); the couple had eight children.\n\nACT READ (July 2026): named as *Marie Leclercq of Grez*, mother of the deceased, in her son\nGeorge's 1808 Grez-Doiceau death act, beside the father Lambert Thumas.\n\nDOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.\nNothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the\nevidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own\nDemogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or\nits image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step."});
