FamilyTree.person({"id":"looten_francois_1785","name":"François Joseph Looten","dates":"b. 17 Aug 1785 Rexpoede (Département du Nord, France)","confidence":"sup","surname":"Looten","family":"looten","born":"17 Aug 1785 Rexpoede (Département du Nord, France)","order":"1785-08-17","occupation":"timmerman (carpenter)","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"wyllie_brigitte_1779","name":"Brigitte Josephine Joanna Wyllie","detail":"m. Diksmuide, 25 Jun 1818"}],"source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Second husband of [[wyllie_brigitte_1779]], widow of [[vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780]]. Married her at\nDiksmuide on 25 June 1818, act nr. 82, RAB ID 85255, microfilm 1166237\n(`data/artifacts/looten-wyllie-1818-marriage-diksmuide.md`) — a volunteer INDEX/Detail\ntranscription, `sup`, never `doc`. He was 33, a *timmerman*, born just across the French\nborder at Rexpoede; she was 38, a widow. **This act is what identifies her as this record**,\nnot the name alone — see [[wyllie_brigitte_1779]] for the \"Previous Partners\" row that does the\nwork.\n\nHis own parents are named on the same act but not linked here — a single index row, the\nsame standard applied throughout this pass: Jeremie Jacques Looten, died 20 August 1804 (2\nFructidor XII, the Republican-calendar conversion checked by computation) at Stavele, ×\nAnne Therese Deprez, died 12 April 1792 at Rexpoede.\n\nAt least four children with [[wyllie_brigitte_1779]], found in the same sweep that turned up\nthis marriage, each naming both parents in full as Looten Franciscus Josephus × Wyllie\nBrigitta Josephina: [[looten_catharina]] (died Diksmuide 1823), [[looten_renatus]] (died\nDiksmuide 1825, weeks after his mother), [[looten_ludovica]] (married 1842) and\n[[looten_maria]] (married 1843). No individual act number was read for any of the four — the\ndetail comes from the same summary already gathered while reading the 1818 act — so the\nsibship should be treated as complete only as far as that sweep reached, not as a closed\nlist."});
