FamilyTree.person({"id":"morree_anna","name":"Anna Francisca Morree","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Morree","family":"morree","line":"devriendt","spouses":[{"id":"smessaert_franciscus","name":"Franciscus Leopoldus Smessaert"}],"source":"Marriage act — Franciscus Léopoldus Smessaert × Anna Francisca Morbeé, Brugge, 16 August 1851","note":"STRONG LEAD, NOT GRAFTED (July 2026) — see [[smessaert_franciscus]] for the whole of it. A Brugge\nmarriage act of 1851 gives an Anna Francisca **Morbeé**, daughter of Petrus Josephus Morbeé\nand Joanna De Clerck, marrying a Franciscus Léopoldus Smessaert. The forenames and the\nhusband match; the surname does not.\n\nMorree and Morbeé are a plausible pair to confuse in a nineteenth-century hand — the double\nr and the rb are near-identical in cursive — and this record's spelling comes from a member\ntree, not from an act. That makes the act the better authority in principle, but \"in\nprinciple\" is not evidence, so nothing is changed here. Her son's 1857 Oostende birth act\nwould settle which spelling the registrar used."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"noel_marie_1751","name":"Marie Catherine Noël","dates":"19 Jan 1751 Grez-Doiceau – 2 Aug 1812 Grez-Doiceau","confidence":"sup","surname":"Noël","family":"noel","born":"19 Jan 1751 Grez-Doiceau","order":"1751-01-19","died":"2 Aug 1812 Grez-Doiceau","occupation":"bierverkoopster (beer seller)","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"thumas_georges_1744","name":"Georges Thumas","detail":"m. Grez-Doiceau, 3 Jan 1771"}],"source":"Death act nr. 58 — George Thumas, Grez-Doiceau, 20 November 1808 (read on AGATHA); Death act of George Thumas, Grez-Doiceau, 20 November 1808; Geneanet","note":"CORROBORATED (July 2026) as a wife. Her husband's death act (Grez-Doiceau, 20 November\n1808) names his wife as *Marie Catherine Noël*, which puts the marriage on a civil act\nrather than on a tree. She outlived him by nearly four years.\n\nMarried the carpenter Georges Thumas at Grez-Doiceau in 1771; worked as a beer seller. Daughter of Jean Baptiste Noël × Marie Josephe Derossart.\n\nACT READ (July 2026): named as the partner of the deceased in her husband's 1808\nGrez-Doiceau death act — written **Marie Catherine Noé** there, not Noël. The act puts the\nmarriage beyond the trees; the spelling is recorded as a variant rather than adopted, since\nher own record and this tree's other sources use Noël.\n\nDOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.\nNothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the\nevidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own\nDemogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or\nits image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step."});
