FamilyTree.person({"id":"paelinck_eduardus_1858","name":"Eduardus Franciscus Paelinck","dates":"19 Nov 1858 Belsele – 28 Aug 1912 Sint-Niklaas","confidence":"doc","surname":"Paelinck","family":"paelinck","born":"19 Nov 1858 Belsele","order":"1858-11-19","died":"28 Aug 1912 Sint-Niklaas","occupation":"leurder (itinerant pedlar)","line":"paelinck","father":"paelinck_joannes_1809","mother":"wittock_rosalia_1820","spouses":[{"id":"vanbogaert_maria_1861","name":"Maria Magdalena Van Bogaert (1888)","detail":"m. Sint-Niklaas, 17 Nov 1888"}],"source":"Birth registration nr. 997 — Philomena Leonia Paelinck, Sint-Niklaas, 31 October 1901; Birth act of Philomena Leonia Paelinck, Sint-Niklaas, 31 October 1901; stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck)","note":"An itinerant pedlar (leurder); married the widow Maria Magdalena Van Bogaert in 1888; eight children.\n\nCORROBORATED (July 2026) as a father: he is named in his daughter Léonie's Sint-Niklaas\nbirth act of 31 October 1901, alongside her mother [[vanbogaert_maria_1861]] — putting the couple\nand the parentage on a civil act rather than on a member tree.\n\nCONFIRMED BY A CIVIL RECORD (July 2026): named as the father on his daughter's Sint-Niklaas\nbirth registration of 31 October 1901 ([[S16]]), alongside [[vanbogaert_maria_1861]]. Found on\nFamilySearch after AGATHA had come back empty for the same act.\n\nREGISTER PAGE READ (July 2026), and it corroborates him twice over. In his daughter's act\nof 31 October 1901 he appears not only as the father but as *geboortig te Belsele* — born at\nBelsele — which is the birthplace this record already held from the stefpaelinck tree, said\nback independently by the man himself in front of the registrar. Name and birthplace agreeing\nis what makes this an identification rather than a name match."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"paelinck_jan_1771","name":"Jan Baptist Paelinck","dates":"20 May 1771 Destelbergen – 29 May 1843 Lokeren","confidence":"sup","surname":"Paelinck","family":"paelinck","born":"20 May 1771 Destelbergen","order":"1771-05-20","died":"29 May 1843 Lokeren","occupation":"dagloner (day labourer)","line":"paelinck","father":"paelinck_apolonius_1748","mother":"vanmaele_christina_1747","spouses":[{"id":"vanacker_joanna_1775","name":"Joanna Coleta Van Acker","detail":"m. 1795"}],"source":"stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck)","note":"A day labourer; the family moved from Destelbergen to Lokeren, where he died. His wife was Joanna Coleta Van Acker."});
