FamilyTree.person({"id":"pardon_cornelius_1859","name":"Cornelius Pardon","dates":"b. 5 Sep 1859 Zaventem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Pardon","family":"pardon","born":"5 Sep 1859 Zaventem","order":"1859-09-05","line":"thumas","father":"pardon_franciscus_1830","mother":"bossin_anna_1829","source":"Civil birth acts naming both parents, for couples already in the tree (harvested corpus, July 2026); Three Zaventem marriage acts of Franciscus Pardon's children, 1877–1886 — the batch that gives his death","note":"Named as the child in a civil birth act at **Zaventem, 1859-09-05**, which gives both\nparents — [[pardon_franciscus_1830]] and [[bossin_anna_1829]] — and so places this person in the tree by the act rather than\nby a name. The father, present as *aangever*, is a *papiermakerswerkman* living at Zaventem —\nhis trade at his 1853 marriage was *dienstbode*, so it had already changed by this second child.\n\nThe act is held in the harvested corpus and reached through Open Archives:\nhttps://www.openarchieven.nl/abl:17bb266b-3a29-270a-469d-40e86d230954\n\n**The family's move from Sint-Stevens-Woluwe to Zaventem, between this birth and the two births\nbefore it, is one migrating family and not two couples.** [[pardon_henricus_1854]] (1854) and\n[[pardon_joanna_1856]] (1856) were born at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe; this child (1859) and\n[[pardon_maria_1863]] (1863) at Zaventem. Three of the four — Henricus, Joanna Coleta and Maria\nThérèsia — are double-attested by their own later Zaventem marriage acts, and each of those three\nindependently names the same father, \"Frans/Franciscus/Jan Frans Pardon, deceased Zaventem\n18/07/1874,\" and the same mother, Anna Maria Bossin (`zaventem-pardon-children-marriages-1877-1886`).\nThat carries the identity across the move rather than starting a second family at the new\naddress; this child alone has no later marriage act found in the held corpus, so is\nsingle-attested by the birth act, which is already two independent identifiers (both parents'\nnames and birthplaces) beyond the shared surname.\n\n`sup`: an indexed act, not the register image. **No `sex` is recorded**, because the harvested\nmention carries only the relation role and never a sex, and this project does not read a sex\noff a forename."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"pardon_franciscus_1830","name":"Françiscus Pardon","dates":"16 Feb 1830 Winksele – 18 Jul 1874 Zaventem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Pardon","family":"pardon","born":"16 Feb 1830 Winksele","order":"1830-02-16","died":"18 Jul 1874 Zaventem","occupation":"dienstbode (servant)","line":"thumas","father":"pardon_guilielmus","mother":"pergijsels_maria","spouses":[{"id":"bossin_anna_1829","name":"Anna Maria Bossin","detail":"m. Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1 Dec 1853"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 9 — Françiscus Pardon × Anna Maria Bossin, Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1 December 1853; Three Zaventem marriage acts of Franciscus Pardon's children, 1877–1886 — the batch that gives his death","note":"Married [[bossin_anna_1829]] at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe on 1 December 1853 (act nr. 9, S22),\nso he is [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]]'s brother-in-law.\n\nBorn at Winksele on 16 February 1830, and living at Zaventem by the time he married,\nworking as a *dienstbode*. He brought his National Militia certificate to the wedding —\nthe act says it was attached to the record — and, like his bride and his parents, declared\nhimself unable to write.\n\nNote the spelling: the act writes *Françiscus*, with the cedilla, and that is what this\nrecord follows.\n\n`sup`: AGATHA's transcription, not the register image.\n\nDIED (2026-07-26): **Zaventem, 18 July 1874**, per three of his children's own later marriage\nacts — Joanna Coleta's (Zaventem, 29 January 1877), Henricus's (Zaventem, 18 July 1881) and Maria\nThérèsia's (Zaventem, 15 November 1886) — each independently naming him as their late father with\nthat exact date and place (`zaventem-pardon-children-marriages-1877-1886`). None of the acts this\ntree already held for him states a death directly; it comes from his children's own registers,\nread a generation later.\n\nFour children are recorded: [[pardon_henricus_1854]], [[pardon_joanna_1856]], [[pardon_cornelius_1859]]\nand [[pardon_maria_1863]]. The family's residence moves from Sint-Stevens-Woluwe to Zaventem between\nthe 1856 and 1859 births — one migrating family, not two couples, since the same \"Frans Pardon,\ndeceased Zaventem 18/07/1874\" and the same mother, Anna Maria Bossin, recur across all three later\nmarriage acts, tying the Sint-Stevens-Woluwe-born and the Zaventem-born children to the same\nparents. See [[pardon_cornelius_1859]] for the reasoning in full.\n\nFRONTIER — **Isabella Pardon**, stated in her own Zaventem marriage act (to August Deryck, 21 May\n1890) to have been born at Zaventem on 16 June 1868, daughter of \"Jan Frans Pardon, deceased\nZaventem 18/07/1874\" and Maria Anna Bossin\n(https://www.openarchieven.nl/abl:d81c47c5-c5c5-a339-0df1-03d43a09b42c). Both the father's death\ndate and place and the mother's name match this couple exactly, and her stated birth year would\nmake her a fifth child, younger than [[pardon_maria_1863]]. No birth act naming her has turned up in\nthe held corpus — the date above is what her own marriage act states about her, not a birth\nregistration — so she stays a named frontier and not a record of her own.\n\nFRONTIER — the Winksele births of February 1830 and his parents' own marriage, which would\ncarry [[pardon_guilielmus]] and [[pergijsels_maria]] back a generation."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"pardon_guilielmus","name":"Guilielmus Pardon","dates":"d. after 1853","confidence":"sup","surname":"Pardon","family":"pardon","died":"after 1853","occupation":"daglooner (day labourer)","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"pergijsels_maria","name":"Maria Anna Pergijsels"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 9 — Françiscus Pardon × Anna Maria Bossin, Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1 December 1853","note":"Father of the groom in his son [[pardon_franciscus_1830]]'s marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe\nnr. 9, 1 December 1853 (S22). A *daglooner* of Winksele, present at the wedding and\nconsenting to it, and recorded as unable to write.\n\nThe act gives him no age, so this record carries no birth date. His son was twenty-three,\nwhich places him loosely in the 1790s or early 1800s and no closer.\n\nThe death entry says only that he was alive on the day of the act.\n\nFRONTIER — his marriage to [[pergijsels_maria]], which the Winksele or Herent\nregisters should hold for roughly 1820–1830, and which would name his own parents."});
