FamilyTree.person({"id":"rossel_benoni","name":"Benoni Joseph Rossel","dates":"","confidence":"doc","surname":"Rossel","family":"rossel","sex":"m","line":"de-keyser","spouses":[{"id":"schreel_leontine_1890","name":"Leontine Schreel"}],"source":"FamilySearch","note":"First husband of [[schreel_leontine_1890]]. `doc`, because the evidence is the same document\nthat carries her: [[dekeyser_edouard_1876]]'s Oostende marriage act of 9 May 1946, read as an image,\nwhich describes his bride as divorced from Benoni Joseph Rossel.\n\nThat is the whole of him. The act names him to establish that Leontine was free to marry,\nnot to say anything about him, so there are no dates, no places and no parents — and\nnothing here justifies inventing any. Neither the wedding nor the divorce is dated in it,\nwhich is why his entry below carries neither.\n\nHe is at the far edge of this tree: the first husband of the second wife of a man who\nmarried into the family. No line of descent runs through him, and none ever will.\nFRONTIER — the Schreel–Rossel marriage and divorce acts, both West-Vlaanderen civil\nregistration, which would date the marriage and give his parents."});
