FamilyTree.person({"id":"sabbe_willem_1530","name":"Willem Sabbe","dates":"~1530 Harelbeke (Bavikhove) – 1581 Wielsbeke (Ooigem)","confidence":"sup","surname":"Sabbe","family":"sabbe","born":"~1530 Harelbeke (Bavikhove)","order":"1530","died":"1581 Wielsbeke (Ooigem)","occupation":"landbouwer (farmer)","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"sabbe_petrus_1504","spouses":[{"id":"demeulemeester_magdalena","name":"Magdalena Demeulemeester","detail":"m. ~1555"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Source detail: Geneanet isavdw (Sosa 27040)\n\nGrandfather of Petrus Sabbe (d.1652); farmer around Harelbeke/Wielsbeke (the Sabbe family's cradle, before the line moved to Oostkamp). Father Petrus Sabbe (1504-1557)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"schalandrijn_octavia_1886","name":"Octavia Maria Schalandrijn","dates":"b. 30 Apr 1886 Bredene","confidence":"doc","surname":"Schalandrijn","family":"schalandrijn","born":"30 Apr 1886 Bredene","order":"1886-04-30","line":"van-iseghem","father":"schalandryn_ludovicus","mother":"standaert_mathilde","spouses":[{"id":"devriendt_eugenius_1882","name":"Eugenius Alphonsius Devriendt","detail":"m. Oostende, 10 Nov 1906"}],"source":"gverdievel (Guy Verdievel); Marriage act nr. 258 — Eugenius Alphonsius Devriendt × Octavia Maria Schalandrijn, Oostende, 10 November 1906; Birth act nr. 116 — Octavia Maria Schalandrijn, Bredene, certificate dated 2 May 1886","note":"Born in the coastal village of Bredene; mother of Adrienne Devriendt.\n\nCORRECTED (2026-07-26): birth date corrected from 1886-05-02 to 1886-04-30. The date\nheld here was the certificate/registration date, not the birth date. The Bredene birth\nact itself (nr. 116, S21), read as an image, says she was born \"eergisteren de\ndertigsten April\" (the day before yesterday, the thirtieth of April) against an act\ndate of 2 May 1886; the 1906 marriage act (nr. 258, S20), read separately, independently\ngives the same 30 April date. See docs/research-log.md §48 for the retraction (§46\ncovers a source-id collision from the same pass).\n\nGRAFTED (2026-07-26): parents identified from the same 1906 Oostende marriage act,\nread as an image — father Ludovicus Schalandryn (werkman, resident at Oostende), mother\nMathilde Standaert (already deceased by 1906). See [[schalandryn_ludovicus]] and\n[[standaert_mathilde]] for what the acts do and do not support about them beyond this."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"schalandryn_ludovicus","name":"Ludovicus Franciscus Schalandryn","dates":"","confidence":"doc","surname":"Schalandryn","family":"schalandryn","occupation":"werkman (labourer)","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"standaert_mathilde","name":"Mathilde Standaert"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 258 — Eugenius Alphonsius Devriendt × Octavia Maria Schalandrijn, Oostende, 10 November 1906; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Named in his daughter Octavia's 1906 Oostende marriage act (nr. 258, S20), read as an\nimage, as father of the bride: \"Ludovicus Schalandrijn\", werkman, resident at Oostende\n(\"alhier wonende\"), present and consenting. The act signs him \"L. Schalandryn\"; his\ndaughter's own record spells the surname Schalandrijn, so the family name appears both\nways in the same generation and this record follows the act's own spelling of him.\n\nFRONTIER — leads from the vrijwilligersrab civil-registration indexes (Huwelijken and\nGeboorten), none read at image level, so none of the following is recorded as fact\nhere:\n\n- birth: Oudenburg, 29 January 1842 (act of 31 January 1842, nr. 14), naming his\n  parents as Ferdinandus Faustinus Schalandryn x Isabella Wallecan;\n- marriage to Mathilde Standaert: Oudenburg, 17 February 1871, act 17;\n- death: Oostende, 15 November 1916, per an Open Archives memorial card (fwk:a60b0372);\n- one generation further back, also index-only: Ferdinandus Faustinus Schalandryn's\n  parents Jacobus Schalandryn x Anna Devisschere, and Isabella Wallecan's parents\n  Henricus Wallecan x Joanna Vantornhoudt;\n- at least seven siblings of Octavia appear in the Geboorten index (rab-bs-geboorten) —\n  none are entered as records here.\n\nEach needs the underlying act image read before it becomes a fact; none is graftable\non the index alone (verification pass, 2026-07-26)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"scherrens_judoca_1617","name":"Judoca Scherrens","dates":"1617 – 1683","confidence":"sup","surname":"Scherrens","family":"scherrens","born":"1617","order":"1617","died":"1683","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"id":"devriese_michael_1615","name":"Michaël De Vriese"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links; kathrynann","note":"FRONTIER — wife of Michaël De Vriese (b. ~1615). Among the deepest roots in the tree; her parents not yet recovered."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"schoolmeesters_josina","name":"Josina Schoolmeesters","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Schoolmeesters","family":"schoolmeesters","sex":"f","occupation":"landbouwster (farmer)","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"vrebos_henricus","name":"Henricus Franciscus Vrebos"}],"source":"Civil marriage acts for the Bossin/Swaelens/Vrebos family of Kraainem, 1884-1901 (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Named as mother of the groom in her son [[vrebos_petrus_1856]]'s 1901 marriage act — Kraainem,\n30 May 1901 — resident Kraainem, *landbouwster*, so still living when her son remarried.\nThe act gives her no age or dates, so this record has none.\n\nFRONTIER: her marriage to [[vrebos_henricus]], and her own birth."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"schreel_leontine_1890","name":"Leontine Schreel","dates":"b. 11 Jan 1890 Aartrijke","confidence":"doc","surname":"Schreel","family":"schreel","sex":"f","born":"11 Jan 1890 Aartrijke","order":"1890-01-11","line":"de-keyser","spouses":[{"id":"rossel_benoni","name":"Benoni Joseph Rossel"},{"id":"dekeyser_edouard_1876","name":"Édouard Dekeyser","detail":"m. Oostende, 9 May 1946"}],"source":"FamilySearch","note":"Second wife of [[dekeyser_edouard_1876]], married at Oostende on 9 May 1946. `doc`, because\nthe act itself was read as an image and states her birth date, her birthplace and\nher own earlier marriage.\n\nShe had been married before, to [[rossel_benoni]], and was divorced from him when she\nmarried Édouard — the same act says so. That marriage is recorded as a marriage,\nlisted first because it was the earlier one; the act gives no date for either the\nwedding or the divorce, so neither is recorded. FRONTIER — the Schreel–Rossel marriage\nand divorce acts, which would date both and give his parents.\n\nShe is a step-relation, not blood: no line of descent here runs through her."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"senesael_anna","name":"Anna Theresia Senesael","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Senesael","family":"senesael","line":"devriendt","spouses":[{"id":"daneel_philippus","name":"Philippus Daneel"}],"source":"wernero (Werner Osaer)","note":"FRONTIER above — mother of Joanna Theresia Daneel (1808)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"smessaert_franciscus","name":"Franciscus Leopoldus Smessaert","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Smessaert","family":"smessaert","line":"devriendt","spouses":[{"id":"morree_anna","name":"Anna Francisca Morree"}],"source":"Marriage act — Franciscus Léopoldus Smessaert × Anna Francisca Morbeé, Brugge, 16 August 1851","note":"STRONG LEAD, NOT GRAFTED (July 2026). A Brugge marriage act of 16 August 1851 ([[S12]])\nrecords a **Franciscus Léopoldus Smessaert** marrying an **Anna Francisca Morbeé**, and\nnames both sets of parents: Paulus Smessaert x Isabella Claeys for him, Petrus Josephus\nMorbeé x Joanna De Clerck for her.\n\nThree things fit: the groom's triple name is distinctive and matches exactly, the bride's\nforenames match exactly, and a marriage in 1851 sits right for a son born at Oostende in\n1857. Brugge and Oostende are neighbours.\n\nOne thing does not: the bride is **Morbeé**, and this tree calls her **Morree**. That is a\ndisagreement, not a silence, and it is the only surname either of these two records has.\nEverything else here — both of them have no dates, no places and no source of their own —\ncomes from the wernero tree, so there is nothing independent to break the tie with. Under\nthe two-identifier rule this is a lead, and it stays one: no parents have been grafted.\n\nDECISIVE RECORD: [[smessaert_joannes_1857]]'s Oostende birth act of 12 January 1857, which would give\nhis mother's surname as the registrar wrote it. If it says Morbeé, this act is ours and\nfour new ancestors come with it; if it says Morree, the couple above are somebody else's."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"smessaert_georgius_1894","name":"Georgius Antonius Julianus Smessaert","dates":"b. 11 Oct 1894 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Smessaert","family":"smessaert","born":"11 Oct 1894 Oostende","order":"1894-10-11","line":"devriendt","father":"smessaert_joannes_1857","mother":"ramon_eugenia_1860","spouses":[{"id":"devos_joanna_1896","name":"Joanna Paula Devos","detail":"m. Oostende, 26 Apr 1919"}],"source":"wernero (Werner Osaer)","note":"Married Joanna Paula Devos in 1919; his daughter Yvonne (b.1914) was legitimized by that marriage."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"smessaert_joannes_1857","name":"Joannes Franciscus Smessaert","dates":"12 Jan 1857 Oostende – before 1919 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Smessaert","family":"smessaert","born":"12 Jan 1857 Oostende","order":"1857-01-12","died":"before 1919 Oostende","occupation":"werkman (labourer)","line":"devriendt","father":"smessaert_franciscus","mother":"morree_anna","spouses":[{"id":"ramon_eugenia_1860","name":"Eugenia Mathildis Ramon (1882)","detail":"m. Oostende, 4 Jan 1882"}],"source":"wernero (Werner Osaer)","note":"A labourer; son of Franciscus Leopoldus Smessaert & Anna Francisca Morree; 13+ children, many dying in infancy."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"smessaert_yvonne_1914","name":"Yvonne Smessaert","dates":"b. 11 Oct 1914 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Smessaert","family":"smessaert","born":"11 Oct 1914 Oostende","order":"1914-10-11","line":"devriendt","father":"smessaert_georgius_1894","mother":"devos_joanna_1896","spouses":[{"id":"devriendt_marcel_1914","name":"Marcel Devriendt","detail":"m. Stene, 16 Oct 1937"}],"source":"wernero (Werner Osaer)","note":"Born before her parents wed and legitimized by their 1919 marriage; married Marcel Devriendt in 1937. Born 11 October — the same day-and-month as her father's birthday."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"standaert_mathilde","name":"Mathilde Standaert","dates":"","confidence":"doc","surname":"Standaert","family":"standaert","occupation":"huishoudster (housekeeper)","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"schalandryn_ludovicus","name":"Ludovicus Franciscus Schalandryn"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 258 — Eugenius Alphonsius Devriendt × Octavia Maria Schalandrijn, Oostende, 10 November 1906; Birth act nr. 116 — Octavia Maria Schalandrijn, Bredene, certificate dated 2 May 1886; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Named as mother of the bride in her daughter Octavia's 1906 Oostende marriage act (nr.\n258, S20), read as an image — \"overleden\" (deceased) by that date, no date given there.\nThe Bredene birth act (nr. 116, 1886, S21), also read as an image, names her as the\ndeclarant's wife, age 42, occupation \"huishoudster\", \"geboortig van Brugge\" (native of\nBruges) — a birthplace stated directly by the act, though the act gives no birth date\nfor her, only her age.\n\nFRONTIER — her age of 42 in the 1886 act implies a birth around 1844, but that is a\nderivation from an age, not a birth date, and is not recorded as one. The\nvrijwilligersrab Geboorten index carries an unread entry giving Brugge, 17 March 1844 —\nconsistent with the derived year, but not read at image level, so not graftable. Her\nown parents, also index-only and unread: Petrus Standaert x Anna Deckers.\n\nEach needs the underlying act image read before it becomes a fact (verification pass,\n2026-07-26)."});
