FamilyTree.person({"id":"steijaert_livinus","name":"Livinus Bernardus Steijaert","dates":"b. ~1787","confidence":"sup","surname":"Steijaert","family":"steijaert","sex":"m","born":"~1787","order":"1787","occupation":"veldwachter","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"vermeeren_maria_1787","name":"Maria Theresia Vermeeren"}],"source":"Hontenisse death act nr. 31, 30 March 1814 — Maria Theresia Vermeeren","note":"Husband of [[vermeeren_maria_1787]], who died at Hontenisse in 1814. The death act gives\nhis age as 27 — hence `~1787` — and his trade as *veldwachter*, the village constable.\n\nThat is everything the act says about him: no birthplace, no parents, no death. A\n*veldwachter* was an appointed municipal officer, so the Hontenisse commune records would\nknow more about him than the parish registers will."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"stekelorum_agatha","name":"Agatha Stekelorum","dates":"d. 1855 Roksem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Stekelorum","family":"stekelorum","died":"1855 Roksem","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"stekelorum_pieter","mother":"denijs_helena","spouses":[{"id":"perquy_joannes","name":"Joannes Perquy"}],"source":"stefanieschil; Death act nr. 27 — Agatha Stekelorum, Roksem, 24 May 1855","note":"Grandmother of Henricus Josephus Bostyn on the Perquy side. Her parents Pieter Stekelorum × Helena Denijs.\n\nCORROBORATED (2026-07-26). Her own death act — Roksem nr. 27, 24 May 1855\n([[agatha-roksem-1855-death-agatha-stekelorum]]) — independently confirms both parents and\nher husband Joannes Perquy, from an archive index that does not derive from the\ntree-stefanieschil member tree that first supplied them. It is the only AGATHA act pairing\nPieter Stekelorum with Helena Denijs in the whole index; see [[stekelorum_pieter]] for the\ncheck against two near-collisions."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"stekelorum_pieter","name":"Pieter Stekelorum","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Stekelorum","family":"stekelorum","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"id":"denijs_helena","name":"Helena Denijs"}],"source":"stefanieschil; Death act nr. 27 — Agatha Stekelorum, Roksem, 24 May 1855","note":"FRONTIER above — great-great-grandfather of Elodia Bostyn on the Perquy line. Dates not yet recovered (late-1700s Westkerke area).\n\nCITATION REPAIRED (2026-07-26), replacing the §52 downgrade. His daughter\n[[stekelorum_agatha]]'s death act — Roksem nr. 27, 24 May 1855\n([[agatha-roksem-1855-death-agatha-stekelorum]]) — names him as her father, alongside\n[[denijs_helena]] as her mother and Joannes Perquy as her husband: four of this tree's\npeople in one document, corroborating the tree-stefanieschil claim from a source that does\nnot derive from it. CONFIDENCE STAYS `sup`: AGATHA serves this act only as an \"analyse van\nakte\" (index transcription — remark \"SCAN 586 GSU\", the scan itself not opened).\n\nTHE ONLY ACT. It is the only act in AGATHA's whole 13.4-million-act index that names a\nPieter Stekelorum and a Helena Denijs together, in any spelling — checked against all 37\nacts naming a \"Pieter Stekelorum\". Two near-collisions were tested and refuted: act\nOVWVL_00197046, a Pieter Stekelorum at Jabbeke, is the surviving partner of Joanna\nFrancisca Verplancke — no Denijs anywhere in the act; and act OVWVL_00345955, Varsenare\n1797, pairs a Helena **Deschacht**, widow of Stephanus Denys, with a husband named\n**Joannes** Stekelorum — a different forename, and a former husband's surname rather than\nher own. Neither touches the Roksem 1855 identification."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"stmartin_alicia","name":"Alicia Mathildis St Martin","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"St Martin","family":"stmartin","sex":"f","line":"vanstechelman","spouses":[{"id":"vanstechelman_henricus_1877","name":"Henricus Emilius Vanstechelman"}],"source":"België, West-Vlaanderen, burgerlijke stand, 1582-1950","note":"Named as the wife of [[vanstechelman_henricus_1877]] in his Oostende death registration of\n17 January 1941. That entry is the whole of what is known of her.\n\n`sup`, not `doc`: the registration is an index entry and the act image has not been\nread. FRONTIER — the act itself, and a Vanstechelman–St Martin marriage at Oostende."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"stockman_joannes_1646","name":"Joannes Stockman","dates":"~1646 – 1696","confidence":"sup","surname":"Stockman","family":"stockman","born":"~1646","order":"1646","died":"1696","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"dellaert_guillielma_1650","name":"Guillielma (Willemijne) Dellaert"}],"source":"paulderidder","note":"Father of Livina Stockman (~1688–1744), who married Joannes Bundervoet (~1682) — so a\ndirect ancestor through her sons Christoffel and Pieter.\n\nFrom the paulderidder ancestry chart of his grandson Pieter Bundervoet, which gives the\ncouple as Joannes Stockman (~1646–1696) × Guillielma \"Willemijne\" Dellaert (1650–1694).\nLivina's record carried no parents at all before this.\n\nFRONTIER: his own parents, and the Stockman–Dellaert marriage, in the Evergem registers\naround 1670."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"stockman_livina_1688","name":"Livina Stockman","dates":"~1688 – 1744 Evergem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Stockman","family":"stockman","born":"~1688","order":"1688","died":"1744 Evergem","line":"bundervoet","father":"stockman_joannes_1646","mother":"dellaert_guillielma_1650","spouses":[{"id":"bundervoet_joannes_1682","name":"Joannes Bundervoet"}],"source":"paulderidder; glorieuxp","note":"Source detail: Geneanet trees glorieuxp & paulderidder (both give her as c.1688-1744)\n\nJoannes Bundervoet's FIRST wife and mother of Christoffel (1709) and Pieter (1727). She died in 1744; Joannes then remarried Livina (Joanna) De Wilde ~1745 — the remarriage confirmed independently by the glorieuxp and paulderidder trees, and consistent with the chronology (Christoffel's 1709 birth predates the De Wilde marriage). Several other trees wrongly list Christoffel's mother as De Wilde."});
