FamilyTree.person({"id":"thumas_etienne_1802","name":"Etienne Thumas","dates":"26 Dec 1802 Grez-Doiceau – 18 Oct 1812 Grez-Doiceau","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","sex":"m","born":"26 Dec 1802 Grez-Doiceau","order":"1802-12-26","died":"18 Oct 1812 Grez-Doiceau","line":"thumas","father":"thumas_georges_1772","mother":"quinart_marie_1780","source":"Death act of Etienne Thumas, Grez-Doiceau, 18 October 1812; Netradyle — Grez-Doiceau, actes de naissance (tab_naiss.php)","note":"Son of [[thumas_georges_1772]] and [[quinart_marie_1780]], and so a brother of [[thumas_georges_1804]].\n\nHe is known from his own Grez-Doiceau death act of 18 October 1812, which names both his\nparents ([[S13]]). That act is the reason his mother's marriage is corroborated at all.\n\nNo age was read off the death act: it is indexed under the death and has not been read as\nan image, so it has not settled how old he died.\n\nBIRTH DATE ADDED (2026-07-27): [[netradyle-grez-naissances]] independently indexes his\nbirth as **THUMAS Georges Étienne, 26 December 1802**, father Georges Lambert, mother\nKinart Marie Catherine — the same couple held here, so this is his own birth act, not a\nnew person. Two identifiers agree: both parents' names, matching exactly, and the double\nforename (Georges Étienne / Étienne) intact across both this act and his 1812 death act.\nDying in October 1812 at not quite ten years old is chronologically clean against this\nbirth. `identify.py` did not itself flag this as the same person when this record was\nfirst written — this record then carried no birth date at all for it to compare, an\nobservation about the tool's reach rather than a complaint. `sup`: an index row, no\nregister image read."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"thumas_francois","name":"François Thumas","dates":"b. 1930–1939","confidence":"fam","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","born":"1930–1939","order":"1930","line":"thumas","father":"thumas_jean_1907","mother":"crabbe_marie","spouses":[{"id":"vandenhoeck_juliette_1937","name":"Juliette Vandenhoeck"}],"source":"The family itself","note":"Named by the family. His father is almost certainly Jean Thumas (1907–1995), who stayed in Kraainem — and Jean’s wife was Marie Louise Crabbé, so she is François’s mother. This father-link falls inside the 100-year privacy window and is the only remaining inference. Everything above it is documented: Jean → J.B. Georgius (1876) → Georges Carolus Josephus (1836) → the Grez-Doiceau Thumas trunk back to 1656."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"thumas_georges_1744","name":"Georges Thumas","dates":"14 Mar 1744 Grez-Doiceau – 20 Nov 1808 Grez-Doiceau","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","born":"14 Mar 1744 Grez-Doiceau","order":"1744-03-14","died":"20 Nov 1808 Grez-Doiceau","occupation":"menuisier (schrijnwerker / carpenter)","line":"thumas","father":"thumas_jean_1701","mother":"leclercq_marie_1710","spouses":[{"id":"noel_marie_1751","name":"Marie Catherine Noël","detail":"m. Grez-Doiceau, 3 Jan 1771"}],"source":"België, Brabant, burgerlijke stand, 1582-1950; Death act nr. 58 — George Thumas, Grez-Doiceau, 20 November 1808 (read on AGATHA); Death act of George Thumas, Grez-Doiceau, 20 November 1808; m2155","note":"The first of FOUR consecutive carpenter (menuisier) generations of Thumas in Grez-Doiceau. Recorded as a godfather (1771) and marriage witness (1775).\n\nCORROBORATED (July 2026) by his own death act — Grez-Doiceau, 20 November 1808, the date\nthis record already held, to the day. The act names his father as Lambert Thumas, his\nmother as Marie Leclercq and his wife as Marie Catherine Noël, so it confirms three links\nat once: [[thumas_jean_1701]], [[leclercq_marie_1710]] and the marriage to [[noel_marie_1751]], all of which\nstood on the m2155 tree alone until now.\n\nA NEAR-MISS WORTH KEEPING. Before the Thumas harvest was complete, the corpus offered a\ndifferent man for this record and scored him STRONG: *Martin Joseph* Thumas, who died at\nGrez-Doiceau on 15 February 1808 — same surname, same parish, same year, three agreeing\nidentifiers. He was rejected because the given names are different men and the days do\nnot match, and that rejection was right; the true act only appeared once more of the\nsurname had been harvested. The lesson is the one the charter states: surname plus place\nplus year is three agreements and still not an identification.\n\nACT READ (July 2026). His own death act — Grez-Doiceau, akte nr. 58, registered 21 November\n1808 and stating the death as the **20th** — has been read at the archive and saved\n([[george-thumas-1808-death-grez-doiceau]]). It confirms the death date exactly, gives his\ntrade as *menuisier*, the word this record already carried, and names his father, mother and\nwife: [[thumas_jean_1701]], [[leclercq_marie_1710]] and [[noel_marie_1751]]. Three links off a member tree and\nonto a civil act.\n\n**A conflict, left open.** The act says he was **60**, which puts his birth around 1747–48;\nthis record says **14 March 1744**, which would make him 64. The birth date is unchanged,\nbecause an age in a death act is hearsay — reported here by a 32-year-old day-labourer — and\nroutinely a few years out, while a stated date is at least a claim about a particular record.\nNeither is documented. The Grez-Doiceau baptisms for 1744 and 1747–48 would settle it.\n\nTHE AGE CONFLICT IS NOT SETTLED BY FAMILYSEARCH — and the reason matters. Its index of this\nfamily gives his birth as **1748**, which looks at first like independent support for the\n1808 act's \"age 60\" against this record's 1744. It is not independent: FamilySearch is\nindexing *that same act*, and 1748 is simply 1808 minus 60. Two sources agreeing are not two\nsources when one is computed from the other.\n\nWhat does bear on it is the family's own shape. His parents married at Wavre on\n**23 February 1743**, and FamilySearch holds a sister, **Catherine Josephe Thumas**, born\n**1745** to the same Lambert Thumas × Marie Leclercq and buried at Grez-Doiceau on 22 February\n1823. A first son in March 1744, thirteen months after the wedding, then a daughter in 1745,\nis an ordinary sequence. A first son in 1748, five years after the wedding and three years\nafter his sister, is less ordinary. That leans towards the 1744 this record already holds,\nwithout proving it.\n\nStill unresolved, and the record that would resolve it is his baptism: Grez-Doiceau parish\nregister, 1744 and 1747–48. Not indexed by name in either archive, so it needs the register\nimages read page by page — or FamilySearch's full-text search over them.\n\nDOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.\nNothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the\nevidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own\nDemogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or\nits image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"thumas_georges_1772","name":"Georges Lambert Thumas","dates":"17 Feb 1772 Grez-Doiceau – 22 Jan 1863 Grez-Doiceau","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","born":"17 Feb 1772 Grez-Doiceau","order":"1772-02-17","died":"22 Jan 1863 Grez-Doiceau","occupation":"menuisier (carpenter)","line":"thumas","father":"thumas_georges_1744","mother":"noel_marie_1751","spouses":[{"id":"quinart_marie_1780","name":"Marie Anne Catherine Quinart (Kinart)","detail":"m. Grez-Doiceau, 9 Feb 1801"}],"source":"Extract from the Grez-Doiceau death register — Georges Thumas, d. 12 January 1864 (issued 28 September 1868 as a marriage annex); Geneanet; Netradyle — Grez-Doiceau, actes de naissance (tab_naiss.php)","note":"Second of the four carpenter generations; had ten children and lived to age 90.\n\nCHECKED AND REJECTED (July 2026) — the corpus's best match for this record is not him.\nIt offers *Lambert Thumas*, who died at **Brussels on 28 February 1801**, and scores it 46\nbits on surname, place of origin (Grez-Doiceau), a mother and a spouse. Ours died at\nGrez-Doiceau in **1863**, sixty-two years later.\n\nWhat produced the score is worth naming, because it will recur: the agreement on \"mother\"\nand \"spouse\" is on FORENAMES only. That man's mother was Marie Joseph **Docq** and his wife\nMarie Catherine **Becquevort**; ours are Marie Catherine **Noël** and Marie Anne Catherine\n**Quinart**. Two women called Marie Catherine in one Walloon village is no evidence at all,\nand the surnames — the part that would have been evidence — disagree outright.\n\nA high score with a dead man's date sixty years out is the shape of a coincidence, not a\nfind. Left ungrafted and uncited.\n\nACT READ (2026-07-26): named, with [[quinart_marie_1780]], as a parent of the deceased in his son\n[[thumas_georges_1804]]'s death-act extract (S23) — *fils de Lambert Georges Thumas et de Marie\nCatherine Quinart, **décédés***.\n\nThis is the **first documentary evidence for this record at all**; it had rested entirely on\nGeneanet. It does not give his dates, but it does place him: he was dead by 28 September\n1868, which is consistent with the 1863 death held here, and it puts his fatherhood of\nGeorges on an act of civil registration rather than on a tree.\n\nNote the name order. This record and Geneanet call him *Georges Lambert*; the extract writes\n*Lambert Georges*, and AGATHA's Grez-Doiceau acts write him both ways and sometimes simply\n*Lambert*. The forms are recorded as variants, not resolved — his own acts would settle it.\n\nConfidence stays `sup`: nothing here documents his own birth, marriage or death, only that he\nwas his son's father and dead by 1868.\n\nCORROBORATED, INDEX-LEVEL (2026-07-27): [[netradyle-grez-naissances]] independently\nindexes his birth as **17 February 1772** at Grez — matching this record's day-level date\nexactly, with none of the 1-2 day drift seen elsewhere in this venue — naming his own\nparents as Georges Thumas and Marie Catherine Noël, and their marriage as 3 January 1771,\nnine months before. This is the first evidence for this generation from a source other\nthan Geneanet.\n\nCONFLICT, RECORDED NOT RESOLVED (2026-07-27): the same venue indexes his own marriage to\n[[quinart_marie_1780]] as **2 April 1799**, two years before the 9 February 1801 this record carries\nfrom Geneanet — a two-year gap, not the 1-2 day slippage seen on birth dates elsewhere in\nthis pass. Neither figure is a register image; this is one unauthenticated 2006 index\nagainst one member tree, and nothing here decides between them. It narrows, without\nclosing, the argument [[thumas_georges_1804]]'s own §49 note makes about his birth year — see that\nrecord."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"thumas_georges_1804","name":"Georges Thumas","dates":"24 Jan 1804 Grez-Doiceau – 12 Jan 1864 Grez-Doiceau","confidence":"doc","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","born":"24 Jan 1804 Grez-Doiceau","order":"1804-01-24","died":"12 Jan 1864 Grez-Doiceau","occupation":"menuisier (carpenter)","line":"thumas","father":"thumas_georges_1772","mother":"quinart_marie_1780","spouses":[{"id":"joostens_marie_1810","name":"Marie Catharina Joostens","detail":"m. Grez-Doiceau, 17 Feb 1835"}],"source":"Extract from the Grez-Doiceau death register — Georges Thumas, d. 12 January 1864 (issued 28 September 1868 as a marriage annex); Death act nr. 35 — Marie Catherine Joostens, Grez-Doiceau, 10 June 1857 (read on AGATHA); Kraainem marriage act nr. 2, 20 June 1872 — Thumas × Bossin (read on AGATHA); Marriage act — Georges Carolus Josephus Thumas × Antonia Bossin, Kraainem, 20 June 1872; Geneanet; Netradyle — Grez-Doiceau, actes de naissance (tab_naiss.php)","note":"Third of the four carpenter generations. Civil records give his birth as 24 Jan 1804 (earlier trees said 1805).\n\nCORROBORATED (July 2026) as a father, by his son's Kraainem marriage act of 20 June 1872,\nwhich names the bridegroom's parents as Georges Thumas and Maria Catharina Joostens — this\ncouple. He appears again in his wife's 1857 death act ([[S9]]) as her surviving husband.\n\nACT READ (July 2026): named as the bridegroom's father in the Kraainem act of 20 June 1872,\nwith [[joostens_marie_1810]] as the mother — the same couple his wife's 1857 death act shows.\n\nAGE CONFLICT (July 2026), recorded and left open. His wife's death act of 10 June 1857\nnames him as her surviving husband — *Georges Thumas, menuisier of Grez-Doiceau*, the trade\nthis record already carries, so the identification is not in doubt. But it gives his age as\n**63**, which puts his birth around 1793–94. This record says **24 January 1804**, which\nwould have made him 53.\n\nTen years is too wide to be the usual slippage, and the same act gets his wife's age right —\n47, agreeing with her recorded 1810. So one of the two is wrong and it is not obvious which:\nthe 1804 date has never been documented, and the 63 was spoken by whoever reported the death.\n\nNothing changed. FRONTIER: the Grez-Doiceau baptisms for 1793–94 and for 1804, and his own\n1864 death act, which would state an age to compare.\n\nREFINED (2026-07-26) — **the parent link does decide something after all, and the earlier\nnote here missed it.** It compared only his father's *birth* year, 1772, and concluded that\nfatherhood at 22 or at 32 is equally ordinary. But [[thumas_georges_1772]] married\n[[quinart_marie_1780]] on **9 February 1801**. A son born in 1793–94 would arrive *seven years before\nhis parents' marriage*; a son born in January 1804 arrives three years after it, which is\nunremarkable. That does not prove 1804 — births before a marriage happen, and this couple's\nmarriage date itself rests on Geneanet and is only `sup` — but it moves the weight decidedly\nonto 1804 and away from the 63.\n\nIt also matters *whose* age the 1857 act was reporting. The figure it got right, 47, was the\n**deceased's**: the person the act exists to record, checked against her own papers. The 63\nwas the age of a **surviving spouse**, stated in passing by whoever came to report the death.\nThose are not equally reliable numbers, and the act getting one right says little about the\nother.\n\nVENUES CLOSED (2026-07-26), so this is not a frontier to re-walk at AGATHA:\n- **his 1864 death act** — Grez-Doiceau deaths are indexed nearly completely for 1860 (49\n  acts) and then only in a trickle: about two to four a year for 1861–1874. No Georges Thumas\n  is among them. All eighteen Thumas appearances in Grez-Doiceau death acts of 1860–1880 are\n  *Charles Julien Thumas as* **Belanghebbende** — a commune official who turns up in dozens of\n  acts, and a standing trap for any match made on surname and place alone.\n- **his 1804 birth act** — AGATHA's Grez-Doiceau birth acts cover **1813 and 1814 only** (57\n  acts, all of them in those two years). 1804 is not in the index at all.\n\nWhat is left is the register images themselves — FamilySearch's Brabant-wallon civil\nregistration for 1804, and the parish registers for 1793–94.\n\nACT READ (2026-07-26) — **his own death act, at last, and it was hiding in a marriage\nregister.** An extract from the Grez-Doiceau death registers (S23), read as a register image,\nstates that *le douze janvier mil huit cent soixante quatre* Georges Thumas died at\nGrez-Doiceau, **veuf de Marie Catherine Joostens**, **fils de Lambert Georges Thumas et de\nMarie Catherine Quinart, décédés**.\n\nThree independent identifiers agree at once, and not one of them is a forename: both parents\nby name, and the wife by name. That matters here, because Georges Thumas is the commonest\nname in this commune's registers.\n\n**It documents two things this record had been carrying on a member tree's word.** The death\ndate, 12 January 1864, is now from civil registration. And the parent link to\n[[thumas_georges_1772]] and [[quinart_marie_1780]] — never documented before — is now on an act.\n\n**It does not settle the age conflict.** The extract gives no age and no birth date, so the\nten years between the recorded 1804 and the *63* of the 1857 act stand exactly where §49 left\nthem.\n\nThe extract was **délivré sur papier libre pour cause d'indigence constatée** — issued free\nbecause the family was certified too poor to pay for the paper.\n\nFRONTIER: it was drawn up on 28 September 1868 *for a marriage*, which means **a child of\nthis couple married at Grez-Doiceau around then**. This tree knows only [[thumas_georges_1836]], who\nmarried at Kraainem in 1872. The 1868 marriage sits in the same volume, near image 221, and\nshould name a sibling.\n\nThat marriage — [[thumas_georges_1843]] to [[deridder_sophie]], 7 October 1868 — is now\nidentified (S25) but the act itself remains VENUE CLOSED (2026-07-27): Open Archives holds\nzero Huwelijk or Geboorte acts for Grez-Doiceau at all, only Overlijden, so it cannot be\nreached by harvest; FamilySearch and AGATHA both came back `blocked` (expired session), not\n`miss`, this pass. See [[thumas_georges_1843]] and [[deridder_sophie]].\n\nCORROBORATED, INDEX-LEVEL (2026-07-27): [[netradyle-grez-naissances]] independently\nindexes his birth as **25 January 1804** — one day off the 24 January held here, the same\norder of slippage seen across every date this venue supplies — with father Georges and\nmother `KINAR Anne Catherine`, agreeing with [[thumas_georges_1772]] and [[quinart_marie_1780]]. A second\nindex compiler, independent of both Geneanet and FamilySearch, now agrees on the year and\nthe day is within the venue's own documented drift.\n\nNEGATIVE, SCOPED (2026-07-27) — checked, and it does **not** reopen §49. The same table\nindexes no Thumas birth at Grez between 1783 and 1797 at all (its earliest rows: 17 Sep\n1797, 24 Aug 1799, 10 Apr 1800), which could look like it counts against a 1793/94 birth.\nIt does not: Belgian civil registration in the French-annexed departments only began\naround 1796-97, exactly where this table's own coverage starts, so a civil-acts\ndépouillement holding nothing before that date is what the historical boundary predicts,\nwhether or not a 1793/94 birth happened — a birth that early would sit in a parish\nbaptismal register, a different kind of record entirely, not a civil one this venue could\never show. **§49 stays open exactly as it was.**\n\nA CONFLICT THAT DOES BEAR ON §49 (2026-07-27), recorded fully on [[thumas_georges_1772]] and\n[[quinart_marie_1780]] rather than here: his parents' own marriage is independently indexed at\nnetradyle as **2 April 1799**, two years earlier than the 9 February 1801 this record's\n§49 argument leans on. Under 1799 rather than 1801, the gap between the parents' marriage\nand a hypothetical 1793/94 birth narrows from roughly seven years to roughly five to six.\nThe direction of the §49 argument is unchanged — 1804 still sits comfortably after the\nmarriage, while 1793/94 would still precede it — only its size narrows by two years."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"thumas_georges_1836","name":"Georges Carolus Josephus Thumas","dates":"15 Sep 1836 Grez-Doiceau – 26 Oct 1922 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","born":"15 Sep 1836 Grez-Doiceau","order":"1836-09-15","died":"26 Oct 1922 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","occupation":"landbouwer & herbergier (farmer & innkeeper)","line":"thumas","father":"thumas_georges_1804","mother":"joostens_marie_1810","spouses":[{"id":"bossin_antonia_1849","name":"Antoina Bossin","detail":"m. Kraainem, 20 Jun 1872"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 4 — Jan Baptist Coppens × Joanna Catharina Seraphina Thumas, Kraainem, 27 July 1892; Marriage act nr. 4 — Franciscus Coenraets × Henrica Thumas, Kraainem, 15 April 1899; Marriage act nr. 3 — Ludovicus Bossin × Maria Isabella Helena Thumas, Kraainem, 10 April 1900; The children of Georges Thumas x Marie Catherine Joostens at Grez-Doiceau, 1835-1868; Kraainem marriage act nr. 2, 20 June 1872 — Thumas × Bossin (read on AGATHA); Marriage act — Georges Carolus Josephus Thumas × Antonia Bossin, Kraainem, 20 June 1872; Kraainem marriage act nr. 2, 3 February 1902 — Thumas × Vandenbemden; Geneanet; Netradyle — Grez-Doiceau, actes de naissance (tab_naiss.php)","note":"The migration generation: born in the Thumas heartland of Grez-Doiceau, he broke the four-generation carpentry tradition to become a farmer and innkeeper, moving north to Kraainem and then Sint-Stevens-Woluwe — founding the Kraainem Thumas family. Widowed of Antoina Bossin (d. 1894), he later partnered Maria Dehoux.\n\nDOCUMENTED (July 2026) as the bridegroom's father in the Kraainem marriage act of 3 February 1902 (akte nr. 2, [[S5]]), living at Kraainem, with\nhis trade given as *landbouwer en herbergier* — exactly the occupation this record already\ncarried, which is itself a check that this is the same man. The act fixes him as the\nfather of [[thumas_joannes_1876]] and the husband of [[bossin_antonia_1849]].\n\nHis own marriage act — Kraainem, 20 June 1872, naming his parents as Georges Thumas and\nMaria Catharina Joostens — is held in the harvested corpus and not yet read on AGATHA.\n\nALSO DOCUMENTED (July 2026) by his own marriage act — Kraainem, 20 June 1872 — the one\nthis record's `detail` already dated. It names him as the bridegroom, born at Grez-Doiceau,\nson of **Georges Thumas** and **Maria Catharina Joostens**, so it proves the links to\n[[thumas_georges_1804]] and [[joostens_marie_1810]] as well as the marriage to [[bossin_antonia_1849]].\n\nACT READ (July 2026). His own 1872 marriage act gives his birth as 15 September 1836 at\nGrez-Doiceau — as held — and his trade then as *fabrieksgast*, a factory hand. Thirty years\nlater, in his son's 1902 act, he is a *landbouwer en herbergier*. One man, two stages of a\nlife; the occupation field keeps the later one because that is how the family is remembered,\nand this note keeps the earlier.\n\nFRONTIER CLOSED, AND THEN SOME (2026-07-26). The 1899 Kraainem act naming Henrica was opened,\nand searching the surname pair *Thumas Bossin* found two more like it. **Three daughters, all\nfrom acts naming this couple as the bride's parents:**\n\n- [[thumas_joanna_1873]], b. Kraainem 21 March 1873, m. Jan Baptist Coppens there 27 July 1892 (S26)\n- [[thumas_henrica_1878]], b. Kraainem 24 June 1878, m. Franciscus Coenraets there 15 April 1899 (S27)\n- [[thumas_maria_1880]], b. Sint-Stevens-Woluwe 18 August 1880, m. Ludovicus Bossin there 10 April 1900 (S28)\n\nWith [[thumas_joannes_1876]], who married at Kraainem in 1902, that is four children — and the acts\ntrack his own life alongside them. He is a *fabriekbediende* in 1892 and a *herbergier* by\n1899, which is the move into the inn this record already described. The 1892 act has\n[[bossin_antonia_1849]] alive and keeping house; the 1899 and 1900 acts give her death date exactly.\n\nSTILL OPEN — **a fifth child, probably a son.** A witness at the 1900 wedding is *Georgius\nThumas, 24, of Kraainem, fabriekwerker*, and a *Georgius Thumas* witnesses at the 1902 wedding\ntoo. Born about 1875–76, in this couple's commune, standing at two of their children's\nweddings. He is almost certainly their son and he is **not grafted**, because a witness entry\ngives no parents and this family has already produced two brothers called Georges one\ngeneration up.\n\nFOUR SIBLINGS (2026-07-26), from FamilySearch's index of the Grez-Doiceau civil registers\n(S25), searched by both parents at once: [[thumas_marie_1835]] declared 11 August 1835,\n[[thumas_georges_1843]] 31 March 1843, [[thumas_jean_1845]] 20 August 1845, and [[thumas_charles_1850]], born\n1850 and dead at Grez-Doiceau on 9 April 1851.\n\n**His own record is what makes them safe.** His declaration sits in the same series on 16\nSeptember 1836, one day after the 15 September 1836 birth read from his 1872 act at the\narchive. A child already documented, inside the sequence, with the same parents and commune,\nis worth more than any name-matching at the edges of it.\n\n**A warning for every later pass: he had a brother also called Georges.** He is *Georges\nCharles Joseph*, born 1836, married at Kraainem in 1872. [[thumas_georges_1843]] is *Georges\nJoseph*, born 1843, married at Grez-Doiceau in 1868. Same parents, same surname, both\n\"Georges Thumas\" to a careless index. They are not to be merged.\n\nDOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.\nNothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the\nevidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own\nDemogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or\nits image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step.\n\nFORENAME LEFT OPEN, NOT MERGED (2026-07-27): [[netradyle-grez-naissances]] independently\nindexes a birth on his exact date with his exact parents — 15 September 1836, father\nGeorges, mother `JOUSTEN Marie Catherine` — but the child is entered as **THUMAS Grégoire\nCharles Joseph**, not Georges Charles Joseph. The identity is accepted: same event, same\nparents, no rival birth indexed at Grez in 1836, and his own 1872 Kraainem marriage act —\nread as an IMAGE — already gives *Georges Carolus Josephus* with these same parents. The\nforename itself is NOT PROVEN: two index-level sources disagree and neither is an image,\nand `data/forenames.json` folds no Georges/Grégoire pair — checked directly, and correctly\nkept apart, since Grégoire is independently attested in this same family (Lambert Grégoire\nin the 1799 marriage index above; a Grégoire Joseph born 1812) and so is not an implausible\nreading in its own right. Following the §54 precedent: the recorded forename stands as it\nis, and this is named as a frontier, not decided."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"thumas_georges_1843","name":"Georges Joseph Thumas","dates":"b. 1843 Grez-Doiceau","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","born":"1843 Grez-Doiceau","order":"1843","line":"thumas","father":"thumas_georges_1804","mother":"joostens_marie_1810","spouses":[{"id":"deridder_sophie","name":"Sophie Miranda Deridder","detail":"m. Grez-Doiceau, 7 Oct 1868"}],"source":"The children of Georges Thumas x Marie Catherine Joostens at Grez-Doiceau, 1835-1868; Netradyle — Grez-Doiceau, actes de mariage (tab_mari.php); Netradyle — Grez-Doiceau, actes de naissance (tab_naiss.php)","note":"Younger brother of [[thumas_georges_1836]], and **the reason his father's death act survives at\nall**. He married **Sophie Miranda Deridder** at Grez-Doiceau on **7 October 1868**, with\nbanns on 20 and 27 September. Because his father was dead, the commune drew up an extract of\n[[thumas_georges_1804]]'s 1864 death act on **28 September 1868** and bound it into the marriage\nvolume — that extract is [[S23]], the document that finally put his father's death date and\nhis grandparents' names onto civil registration. This wedding is why it exists.\n\nHis own birth was declared at Grez-Doiceau on **31 March 1843**; the birth itself is a day or\ntwo earlier, which is why it sits in `raw`.\n\n**Do not merge him with his brother.** [[thumas_georges_1836]] is *Georges Charles Joseph*, born 1836,\nmarried at Kraainem in 1872. This is *Georges Joseph*, born 1843, married at Grez-Doiceau in\n1868. Two sons of one couple, both called Georges, seven years apart — exactly the confusion\nthis project's rules exist to catch.\n\n`sup`: index rows only, no register image read.\n\nFRONTIER: the 1868 marriage act, which would give his trade, his exact birth and his wife's\nparents.\n\nCORROBORATED, SECOND INDEX (2026-07-27): [[netradyle-grez-mariages]] independently indexes\nthe marriage — \"row 50, 08/10/1868 THUMAS Georges & DERRIDER Sophie\" — a second, unrelated\ncompiler agreeing with S25 that this wedding happened at Grez-Doiceau in October 1868. Its\ndate, 8 October, is one day off the 7 October held here from S25; ordinary drift, not a\nconflict, and this venue's marriage detail pages carry no parents, ages or trade in any\ncase, so this can only corroborate the event, never supply what the FRONTIER above is\nstill asking for.\n\nVENUE CLOSED (2026-07-27): the target act was checked against the local corpus directly.\nOpen Archives holds **zero** Huwelijk or Geboorte acts for Grez-Doiceau at all — every one\nof its mentions there is an Overlijden — so neither the commune's own index nor\n`harvest.py` can reach this marriage by any route; a bulk or targeted pull would be\nwasted. FamilySearch (the exact film and image are already known, from S23's own volume)\nand AGATHA both came back `blocked` this pass — an expired/logged-out session, not a\n`miss` — so this remains the single highest-value open target on the Thumas line, waiting\non a session rather than on more searching.\n\nNEGATIVE, SCOPED (2026-07-27): his own birth is absent from\n[[netradyle-grez-naissances]]'s Thumas-surname Grez-Doiceau births table — 134 rows,\nfully paged, no `&pg=2` truncation trap — while four of his siblings appear in the same\ntable (Marie Thérèse Stéphanie 1835, the 1836 child, Jean Baptiste Zénon 1845, Charles\nEugène 1850). The only 1843 row at all is Rosalie Céline, 14 May. Read as a coverage gap\nin one 2006 volunteer dépouillement, not evidence of a birth elsewhere: his existence and\n1868 marriage already rest on S23 (a register **image**) and S25 (FamilySearch's\nindependent index)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"thumas_henrica_1878","name":"Henrica Thumas","dates":"b. 24 Jun 1878 Kraainem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","sex":"f","born":"24 Jun 1878 Kraainem","order":"1878-06-24","line":"thumas","father":"thumas_georges_1836","mother":"bossin_antonia_1849","spouses":[{"id":"coenraets_franciscus_1872","name":"Franciscus Coenraets","detail":"m. Kraainem, 15 Apr 1899"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 4 — Franciscus Coenraets × Henrica Thumas, Kraainem, 15 April 1899; Rijksarchief AGATHA — Belgian State Archives search robot","note":"Daughter of [[thumas_georges_1836]] and [[bossin_antonia_1849]], and so a sister of [[thumas_joannes_1876]] — an aunt of the\nThumas line that runs down to Dorien.\n\nFound in AGATHA's index while searching for her parents' own 1872 marriage: a **Kraainem\nmarriage of 15 April 1899** in which she is the bride and her parents are given as Georgius\nCarolus Josephus Thumas and Antonia Bossin.\n\nACT OPENED (2026-07-26) — the frontier this record named is closed. Kraainem act nr. 4 of 15\nApril 1899 (S27) gives her birth as **Kraainem, 24 June 1878**, her occupation as *zonder\nberoep*, and her husband as **[[coenraets_franciscus_1872]]**, a *brouwersgast* of Kraainem born at\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe in 1872, son of a shopkeeper of the same name and of [[godts_anna]], who had\ndied in 1875.\n\nThe act also states her mother's death exactly — Kraainem, **7 November 1894** — where\n[[bossin_antonia_1849]]'s own record had carried only the year.\n\nShe is one of at least three sisters: [[thumas_joanna_1873]] married in 1892 and [[thumas_maria_1880]] in\n1900, both at Kraainem, both from acts naming the same two parents."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"thumas_jean_1701","name":"Jean Lambert Thumas","dates":"26 Sep 1701 Grez-Doiceau – 3 Mar 1776 Grez-Doiceau","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","born":"26 Sep 1701 Grez-Doiceau","order":"1701-09-26","died":"3 Mar 1776 Grez-Doiceau","occupation":"marguillier & greffier (church warden / parish clerk)","line":"thumas","father":"thumas_antoine_1656","mother":"daix_dieudonnee_1665","spouses":[{"id":"leclercq_marie_1710","name":"Marie Jacqueline Leclercq","detail":"m. Wavre, 23 Feb 1743"}],"source":"Death act nr. 58 — George Thumas, Grez-Doiceau, 20 November 1808 (read on AGATHA); Death act of George Thumas, Grez-Doiceau, 20 November 1808; m2155","note":"CORROBORATED (July 2026) as a father. His son Georges's death act (Grez-Doiceau, 20\nNovember 1808) names the dead man's father as *Lambert Thumas* and his mother as Marie\nLeclercq — the pairing this record already asserts, now on a civil act rather than on the\nm2155 tree alone. The act gives the short form of his name, without the *Jean*.\n\nChurch warden and parish clerk of Grez-Doiceau. Our line descends from his SECOND marriage, to Marie Jacqueline Leclercq (Wavre, 1743) — their son Georges (1744) continues the line. His first wife was Marie Catherine Crèvecœur (m. 1727, d. 1742).\n\nACT READ (July 2026): named as *Lambert Thumas of Grez*, father of the deceased, in his son\nGeorge's 1808 Grez-Doiceau death act — with [[leclercq_marie_1710]] as the mother. The couple and the\nparentage are now on a civil act.\n\nDOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.\nNothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the\nevidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own\nDemogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or\nits image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"thumas_jean_1845","name":"Jean Baptiste Zénon Thumas","dates":"b. 1845 Grez-Doiceau","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","born":"1845 Grez-Doiceau","order":"1845","line":"thumas","father":"thumas_georges_1804","mother":"joostens_marie_1810","source":"The children of Georges Thumas x Marie Catherine Joostens at Grez-Doiceau, 1835-1868; Netradyle — Grez-Doiceau, actes de naissance (tab_naiss.php)","note":"Younger brother of [[thumas_georges_1836]]. His birth was declared at Grez-Doiceau on **20 August\n1845** (S25), between his brother [[thumas_georges_1843]] in 1843 and [[thumas_charles_1850]] in 1850.\n\n`raw` rather than a date: the index gives the declaration, not the birth.\n\n`sup`: an index row, no register image read.\n\nFRONTIER: his birth act, and whether he lived to marry — nothing is known of him after 1845.\n*Zénon* is an unusual enough forename to search on its own, which is worth trying before the\ncommon ones.\n\nCORROBORATED, INDEX-LEVEL (2026-07-27): [[netradyle-grez-naissances]] independently\nindexes him as **19 August 1845** — one day off the 20 August declaration held here (S25),\nthe same order of drift documented across this venue — with father Georges and mother\n`JOSTENS Marie Catherine`. Two independent index compilers now agree on the rare tripartite\nforename and both parents. The same row gives her origin commune as Woluwe-Saint-Pierre,\nwhich conflicts with the Woluwe-Saint-Lambert on [[joostens_marie_1810]]'s own death act; the\ndisagreement is recorded there, not resolved here."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"thumas_jean_1907","name":"Jean Thumas","dates":"23 Oct 1907 Kraainem – 22 Mar 1995 Kraainem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","born":"23 Oct 1907 Kraainem","order":"1907-10-23","died":"22 Mar 1995 Kraainem","line":"thumas","father":"thumas_joannes_1876","mother":"vandenbemden_joanna_1882","spouses":[{"id":"crabbe_marie","name":"Marie Louise Crabbé"}],"source":"jswaelens","note":"DOCUMENTED (b. 23 Oct 1907, d. 22 Mar 1995, both in Kraainem; Geneanet, marcelcroon). He lived his whole life in Kraainem and is the strongly-supported grandfather of Thiery. The ONE remaining sealed link is Jean → François (Thiery’s father), whose 20th-century birth is behind the 100-year civil-registration privacy wall."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"thumas_joanna_1873","name":"Joanna Catharina Seraphina Thumas","dates":"b. 21 Mar 1873 Kraainem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","sex":"f","born":"21 Mar 1873 Kraainem","order":"1873-03-21","line":"thumas","father":"thumas_georges_1836","mother":"bossin_antonia_1849","spouses":[{"id":"coppens_jan_1870","name":"Jan Baptist Coppens","detail":"m. Kraainem, 27 Jul 1892"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 4 — Jan Baptist Coppens × Joanna Catharina Seraphina Thumas, Kraainem, 27 July 1892","note":"Eldest known child of [[thumas_georges_1836]] and [[bossin_antonia_1849]] — born at **Kraainem on 21 March 1873**,\nnine months after her parents married there in June 1872, and so the first of the Kraainem\ngeneration.\n\nHer marriage act (Kraainem nr. 4, 27 July 1892, S26) gives her *zonder beroep* and names both\nparents: her father a *fabriekbediende*, her mother [[bossin_antonia_1849]] still living and keeping house.\nHer mother would be dead two years later.\n\nShe married **Jan Baptist Coppens**, a mason of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe.\n\n`sup`: AGATHA's transcription of the act, complete as it reads, but the register image has not\nbeen pulled."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"thumas_joannes_1876","name":"Joannes Baptista Georgius Thumas","dates":"26 Sep 1876 Kraainem – 23 Mar 1944 Brussel","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","born":"26 Sep 1876 Kraainem","order":"1876-09-26","died":"23 Mar 1944 Brussel","occupation":"fabriekwerker & gemeenteschepen (factory worker & alderman)","line":"thumas","father":"thumas_georges_1836","mother":"bossin_antonia_1849","spouses":[{"id":"vandenbemden_joanna_1882","name":"Joanna Vandenbemden","detail":"m. Kraainem, 3 Feb 1902"}],"source":"Kraainem marriage act nr. 2, 3 February 1902 — Thumas × Vandenbemden; marcelcroon (Marcel Croon); jswaelens","note":"Son of Georges Carolus Josephus and Antoina Bossin. A factory worker who also served as a schepen (municipal alderman) in Kraainem. Married Joanna Vandenbemden in Kraainem on 3 Feb 1902.\n\nDOCUMENTED (July 2026) by the Kraainem marriage act of 3 February 1902 (akte nr. 2, [[S5]]), where he is the bridegroom. It gives his birth at\nKraainem on 26 September 1876 and his trade as *fabriekwerker*, both as held here, and\nnames his parents outright — Georgius Carolus Josephus Thumas and Antonia Bossin. He was\nliving at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe when he married. The alderman's office in his occupation\nfield came from elsewhere and is not in this act.\n\nDOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.\nNothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the\nevidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own\nDemogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or\nits image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"thumas_maria_1880","name":"Maria Isabella Helena Thumas","dates":"b. 18 Aug 1880 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","sex":"f","born":"18 Aug 1880 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1880-08-18","line":"thumas","father":"thumas_georges_1836","mother":"bossin_antonia_1849","spouses":[{"id":"bossin_ludovicus_1879","name":"Ludovicus Bossin","detail":"m. Kraainem, 10 Apr 1900"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 3 — Ludovicus Bossin × Maria Isabella Helena Thumas, Kraainem, 10 April 1900; Civil registration acts for the Bossin family of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, Kraainem and Zaventem (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Daughter of [[thumas_georges_1836]] and [[bossin_antonia_1849]], born at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe on 18 August 1880**\n— the family had moved on from Kraainem, where her sisters were born, and her birth was\ndeclared on the 26th, which is the entry AGATHA carries separately under her mother's name.\n\nAt nineteen she was a *dienstmeid*, a housemaid, living at Kraainem. She married **Ludovicus\nBossin**, a polisher of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, on **10 April 1900** (Kraainem act nr. 3, S28).\nHer mother had been dead five years by then; the act records it.\n\n**RESOLVED — her husband's surname is not her mother's family.** [[bossin_ludovicus_1879]]'s\nown father's 1858 marriage act now names his parents as Judocus Bossin and Maria Desmedt,\nnot [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] and [[peremans_joanna_1824]] (her mother [[bossin_antonia_1849]]'s parents). See his\nrecord for the finding.\n\n**CORROBORATED (2026-07-27) by her own birth act, held in the harvested corpus (S33).**\nIt independently confirms both her parents by exact age and birthplace: her father,\n[[thumas_georges_1836]], aged 43, born Grez-Doiceau; her mother, [[bossin_antonia_1849]], aged 31, born\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe. The family is spelled **Thomas** on this act — both parents and her\nown entry — where her 1900 marriage act (S28) and her son's 1901 birth act both spell it\n**Thumas**. One family, an orthographic variant inside one transcription batch, not two.\n\n**A first known son (2026-07-27):** [[bossin_karel_1901]], born Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 27\nFebruary 1901, confirmed against her own held birth of 18 August 1880 (she is aged 20 on\nhis birth act, her August birthday not yet due).\n\n`sup`: an act analysis, not the register image."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"thumas_marie_1835","name":"Marie Thérèse Stéphanie Thumas","dates":"b. 1835 Grez-Doiceau","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","sex":"f","born":"1835 Grez-Doiceau","order":"1835","line":"thumas","father":"thumas_georges_1804","mother":"joostens_marie_1810","source":"The children of Georges Thumas x Marie Catherine Joostens at Grez-Doiceau, 1835-1868","note":"Eldest known child of [[thumas_georges_1804]] and [[joostens_marie_1810]], and an elder sister of\n[[thumas_georges_1836]]. Her birth was declared at Grez-Doiceau on **11 August 1835** (S25), under six\nmonths after her parents married there on 17 February 1835.\n\n`raw` rather than a date because the index gives the **declaration**, not the birth.\n\n`sup`: an index row, no register image read. `sex` is recorded from the forenames *only*\nbecause the register itself declines them in the feminine and the index marks the row so —\nnot inferred from how the name reads.\n\nFRONTIER: her birth act, and whether she lived to marry. Nothing is known of her after 1835."});
