FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanacker_joanna_1775","name":"Joanna Coleta Van Acker","dates":"16 Jan 1775 Lokeren – 12 Jul 1821 Lokeren","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Acker","family":"vanacker","born":"16 Jan 1775 Lokeren","order":"1775-01-16","died":"12 Jul 1821 Lokeren","line":"paelinck","spouses":[{"id":"paelinck_jan_1771","name":"Jan Baptist Paelinck","detail":"m. 1795"}],"source":"stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck)","note":"From Lokeren; her marriage (1795) brought the line into the Lokeren/Waasland area. Confirmed mother of Joannes Franciscus (1809). Her own parents are not in the stefpaelinck tree — a frontier."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780","name":"Antoine Joseph Albert Vanalderweireldt","dates":"9 May 1780 Diksmuide – Jul 1808 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vanalderweireldt","family":"vanalderweireldt","born":"9 May 1780 Diksmuide","order":"1780-05-09","died":"Jul 1808 Diksmuide","occupation":"werkman (labourer)","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"wyllie_brigitte_1779","name":"Brigitte Josephine Joanna Wyllie","detail":"m. Diksmuide, 8 Jun 1803"}],"source":"bartvanhooren (Bart Vanhooren); West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Died young, at 28, only months after the birth of his son Carolus.\n\nTHE MARRIAGE ACT REACHED (2026-07-27) — Diksmuide, 8 June 1803 (19 Prairial XI, the\nRepublican-calendar conversion checked by computation), act nr. 14, RAB ID 84989\n(`data/artifacts/vanalderweireldt-wyllie-1803-marriage-diksmuide.md`). The act image itself\nis FamilySearch film 1166236, image 962, ark `3:1:33SQ-GGKY-9C7D` — 403 unauthenticated, a\none-request retry once a session exists — so everything here is a volunteer INDEX/Detail\ntranscription, `sup` throughout, never `doc`. It gives his birth as 09/05/1780, matching\nthis record exactly (the first identifier), age 23, *werkman*, and names both his own\nparents and [[wyllie_brigitte_1779]]'s in the same document. **His own death act** — Diksmuide,\nact nr. 97, RAB ID 2299984 — independently gives his age as 28 and birthplace Diksmuide,\nconsistent with the same birth date: the second identifier. No rival Vanalderweireldt\ncouple was found in the area (a Bernard Carol Vanalderweireldt × Regina Papegay, d. 1820,\nis a different family, checked and set aside).\n\nTHE DEATH DAY RETRACTED (2026-07-27). This record held 21 July 1808 as a day-level death\ndate. That value is the death act's **Certificate Date** column — the day the death was\n*registered* — not a stated day of death; the act's own Date column is blank. No two of the\nthree transcriptions that give a day for his death agree with each other: **6 July 1808**\n(his widow's 1818 remarriage act, Previous-Partners table —\n`data/artifacts/looten-wyllie-1818-marriage-diksmuide.md`), **16 July 1808** (his son\n[[vanalderweireldt_petrus_1803]]'s 1828 marriage act) and **21 July 1808** (the certificate date, this\ndeath act — `data/artifacts/vanalderweireldt-antoine-1808-death-diksmuide.md`). July 1808 is\nsolid across all three; the day is not, so the day-level precision is withdrawn and only the\nmonth is held. What would settle it: the death act's own register image (FamilySearch film\n4794755, 403 unauthenticated) or either son's 1828 marriage act image.\n\nFOUR PARENTS NAMED, NONE GRAFTED. The 1803 act names his parents **Vanaldeweireldt Jacques\nIgnace × Verhaeghe Isabella Claire**, both said to have been born at Langemark (his mother\nat Diksmuide). The document was reached and read; the generation above it is still a\nfrontier, not a link — the same standard this pass applied throughout. The mother, Isabella\nClaire/Clara Verhaeghe, leans toward acceptance: named identically across **three**\nindependent acts (this one, his own 1808 death act, and the 1857 death act of a probable\nsister below), with no rival family found. The father does not clear the same bar: he is\n**Jacques Ignace** here, **François** on the 1808 death act, and **Jacobus Ignatius** on the\n1857 act — the same man beyond real doubt, but no two of the three readings of his forename\nagree. No father/mother is set on this record.\n\nA PROBABLE ELDER SISTER, NOT GRAFTED. **Maria Joanna Vanalderweireldt**, died Diksmuide act\n211, certificate 30 September 1857, aged 82y 8m 28d, born Diksmuide, father Jacobus\nIgnatius, mother Isabella Clara Verhaeghe — a third act naming that parent pair. Working\nback from the certificate date, 82y 8m 28d before 30 September 1857 lands on 2 January 1775\nalmost exactly (checked by computation) — about 5.3 years before this record's own birth, a\nplausible elder sister. But she cannot be linked as a sibling while the parents themselves\nare only a frontier, and her own date is back-computed from a certificate date, carrying the\nsame registration lag documented above — so this stays \"about 1775-01-02\", a named frontier\nin prose, not a person file.\n\nTWO MORE SONS FOUND WITH [[vanalderweireldt_carolus_1808]] (2026-07-27). [[vanalderweireldt_petrus_1803]], born **three\ndays** after this couple's own wedding — 11 June 1803 (22 Prairial XI) against the 8 June\nwedding, checked by computation both ways and read as the ordinary \"married to legitimate a\nchild already due\" pattern rather than a transcription slip; and [[vanalderweireldt_jean]], who died\nin infancy in January 1805. Full detail, spouse and sources on each of their own records.\n\nTWO FRONTIERS SCOPED AND LEFT OPEN. No death act for **Jacobus Ignatius Vanalderweireldt**\nor **Isabella Clara Verhaeghe** was found in the Diksmuide death index under any spelling\ntried — they most plausibly died before civil registration began, i.e. they sit in the\nparish registers. And the Diksmuide **birth** index for 1796–1815 is a blind window of\nexactly the same shape already documented for the Vincke family a generation later: it\ncarries a bare father surname, no forename and no mother at all, so this generation's\nsibship cannot be fixed from the birth side — only from the marriage and death acts above."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanalderweireldt_carolus_1808","name":"Carolus Ludovicus Vanalderweireldt","dates":"11 Mar 1808 Diksmuide – 14 Aug 1853 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vanalderweireldt","family":"vanalderweireldt","born":"11 Mar 1808 Diksmuide","order":"1808-03-11","died":"14 Aug 1853 Diksmuide","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780","mother":"wyllie_brigitte_1779","spouses":[{"id":"dutreeuw_eugenia_1808","name":"Eugenia Henrica Dutreeuw","detail":"m. Diksmuide, 4 Jun 1828"}],"source":"bartvanhooren (Bart Vanhooren); West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Born the same year his father died — his father Antoine died in July 1808, about four months after Carolus's birth.\n\nHIS OWN 1828 MARRIAGE ACT RESTATES HIS PARENTS (2026-07-27) — Diksmuide, 4 June 1828, act\nnr. 106, RAB ID 85449, microfilm 1166239 (VANALDEWEIRELDT Carolus Ludovicus × DUTREEUW\nEugenia Henrica, son of VANALDEWEIRELDT Antonius × WYLLIE Brigitta) — a second, independent\ncivil act on the same parent pair, 25 years after [[vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780]] and [[wyllie_brigitte_1779]]'s\nown wedding. It also gives both parents' death dates: father 21 July 1808 (the Certificate\nDate column of his death act, now understood to be a registration date rather than the day\nitself — see [[vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780]]) and mother 8 November 1824 (matching this couple's held\nvalue for [[wyllie_brigitte_1779]] to the day). SPELLING TRAP: this act writes the surname\nVANALDEWEIRELDT — no R after -ALD- — so it is invisible to a `naam=Vanalderweireldt` query\nand surfaced only via the mother's surname Wyllie and the bride's surname Dutreeuw.\n\nHIS OWN BIRTH REGISTRATION CORROBORATES THE HELD DATE (2026-07-27). The Diksmuide birth\nindex carries a bare row \"VANALDERWEIRELDT Charles, certificate 12/03/1808\" with no parents\nattached — part of the same 1796–1815 blind window noted on [[vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780]]'s record, so\nit cannot by itself prove the link — but its certificate date sits one day after this\nrecord's held birth of 11 March 1808, the ordinary declaration lag, and the 1828 marriage\nact above independently states the same 11 March 1808. Two acts agree; the held date is\nunchanged."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanalderweireldt_jean","name":"Jean Antoine Vanalderweireldt","dates":"d. 30 Jan 1805 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vanalderweireldt","family":"vanalderweireldt","died":"30 Jan 1805 Diksmuide","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780","mother":"wyllie_brigitte_1779","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Died in infancy, Diksmuide, act nr. 31, certificate 30 January 1805, RAB ID 2300267 — a\nsingle civil death act naming both parents, [[vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780]] × [[wyllie_brigitte_1779]], in\nfull. A third son alongside [[vanalderweireldt_carolus_1808]] and [[vanalderweireldt_petrus_1803]]. Volunteer\nINDEX/Detail transcription (`rab-bs-overlijdens`), `sup`, never `doc`."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845","name":"Ludovica Maria Vanalderweireldt","dates":"23 Nov 1845 Diksmuide – 1914","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vanalderweireldt","family":"vanalderweireldt","born":"23 Nov 1845 Diksmuide","order":"1845-11-23","died":"1914","occupation":"kantwerkster (lacemaker)","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vanalderweireldt_carolus_1808","mother":"dutreeuw_eugenia_1808","spouses":[{"id":"vincke_lucien_1840","name":"Lucien Julianus Vincke","detail":"m. Diksmuide, 24 May 1865"}],"source":"bartvanhooren (Bart Vanhooren); West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; Marriage act nr. 40 — Caesar Antonius Bocklandt x Florence Amelie Vincke, Diksmuide, 11 February 1893; Diksmuide (West-Vlaanderen) civil registers on FamilySearch — image group #004833210: marriages, births, deaths and certificates 1876-1890, 1269 browsable images; Marriage act nr. 212 — Eduardus Ludovicus Rudolphus Vanyseghem x Emma Celesta Vincke, Oostende, 28 September 1907 (register image)","note":"Daughter of Carolus Vanalderweireldt & Eugenia Dutreeuw; mother of Emma Celesta Vincke\n(1880–1974), and of at least seven more children.\n\n**NAMED AS MOTHER IN A REGISTER IMAGE FOR THE FIRST TIME (2026-07-27), DOC-GRADE.**\n[[vincke_emma_1880]]'s own birth act, read as the register image itself\n([[fs-diksmuide-civil-registers-film-004833210]],\n`data/artifacts/emma-vincke-1880-birth-act-image.md`), names her mother and gives, **for\nthe first time anywhere in this tree**, her occupation: ***kantwerkster*** (lacemaker).\nHer surname was re-cropped at 6× zoom in three passes to settle a prior \"not\nletter-by-letter certain\" caveat: the **R after `-ALD-`** is clearly present — ruling out\nthe `VANDERWEIRELT` no-R variant that hid records elsewhere in this family — and the\nfinal cluster reads **`-eldt`**, tighter than the artifact's own original reading. Her\nstated age, \"vyf en dertig\" (35), is one year above the 34y2m she would have completed\nagainst this record's held birth of 23 November 1845 — **not treated as a contradiction**:\nthe identical +1 offset recurs independently on her alone in a wholly separate 1888\ndocument, her son [[vincke_alfons_1865]]'s marriage act (43 stated vs 42 completed) — the same\nperson showing the same offset twice, in two acts eight years apart, is a\nbirth-year-subtraction convention, not two independent errors. This record's own\nconfidence stays `sup`, since her own birth is still index-only — the `doc` grade attaches\nto this specific parent-naming, read off a primary image.\n\n**ALSO NAMED MOTHER-OF-THE-BRIDE IN THE 1907 MARRIAGE ACT, DOC-GRADE.** Emma's own 1907\nOostende marriage act ([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]],\n`data/artifacts/vaniseghem-vincke-1907-marriage-oostende.md`) names her again, *\"zonder\nberoep\"* (no occupation stated there — a later-life change from *kantwerkster*, flagged\nrather than treated as a contradiction) — consenting not in person but by a separate act\npassed at Diksmuide on 8 September 1907, since she did not travel to Oostende. This\nconfirms she was alive in September 1907, consistent with this record's held death year of\n1914, and is a second, independent primary-image corroboration of the parent link, in a\ndifferent register from the birth act, 27 years apart.\n\nSEVEN MORE CHILDREN GRAFTED (research-log §64), from a province-wide sweep of the\nvrijwilligersrab Geboorten index (`rab-bs-geboorten`) for Diksmuide, each act naming both\nparents in full: [[vincke_charles_1871]] (b. 1871), [[vincke_romanie_1873]] (b. 1873),\n[[vincke_irma_1874]] (b. 1874), [[vincke_camilla_1876]] (b. 1876), [[vincke_eugene_1877]] (b. 1877),\n[[vincke_emma_1880]] (b. 1880, already held) and [[vincke_jerome_1886]] (b. 1886, aged 40.8 at his\nbirth — the upper end of childbearing but not implausible). See [[vincke_lucien_1840]]'s record\nfor the act numbers and the two independent filters that found no rival couple.\n\nAn EIGHTH CHILD, [[vincke_florence_1869]] (b. Diksmuide 1869), is grafted from her own 1893\nmarriage act rather than a birth act — see [[vincke_lucien_1840]]'s record for why. This joins\nthe couple's line to the De Keyser/Bocklandt branch of this tree (objective 3).\n\nTHE BLIND WINDOW BROKEN (research-log §67, 2026-07-27). FOUR MORE CHILDREN GRAFTED, via\ntheir own later marriage and death acts rather than a birth act: [[vincke_theophil_1866]]\n(b. 1866, m. Valerie Bolle 1893, d. Oostende 1922), [[vincke_bellarmin_1867]] (b. 1867, d.\nDiksmuide 1872, an infant), [[vincke_karolus_1870]] (b. 1870, d. Diksmuide 1871, an infant,\nwhose name was reused for [[vincke_charles_1871]] four months later) and [[vincke_alfons_1865]]\n(b. 1865, just outside this window, m. Eugenia Vandecappelle 1888). TWELVE\nGRANDCHILDREN follow, contingent on those two marriages — six through Theophil ×\nValerie Bolle, six through Alfons × Eugenia Vandecappelle — see [[vincke_lucien_1840]]'s record\nfor each one and the act numbers.\n\nTWO EXCLUDED: \"Medard Edmond Vincke\" (1866) is a different Vincke woman's child, settled\nby his own death act; \"Elodie Vincke\" (1870) belongs to a separate Diksmuide Vincke line\n(parents Richard Aloïs Vincke × Eugenie Dekeyrel per her own 1894 marriage act) and is not\nthe same person as this couple's own [[vincke_romanie_1873]] (\"Romanie Elodie\"). FIVE STILL\nNOT PROVEN — Emil Fidèle, Gustave Camil, Florida Juliana, Arthur Carolus, Cyrille Camil —\nremain a named frontier, not a link; see [[vincke_lucien_1840]]'s record for the scope of what\nwas searched and came back negative, and for the act-spacing argument used only to\nexclude, never to include."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanalderweireldt_petrus_1803","name":"Petrus Antonius Vanalderweireldt","dates":"11 Jun 1803 Diksmuide – 7 Jan 1869 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vanalderweireldt","family":"vanalderweireldt","born":"11 Jun 1803 Diksmuide","order":"1803-06-11","died":"7 Jan 1869 Diksmuide","occupation":"timmerman (carpenter)","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780","mother":"wyllie_brigitte_1779","spouses":[{"id":"bouckaert_marie_1799","name":"Marie Theresia Bouckaert","detail":"m. Diksmuide, 20 Apr 1828"}],"source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780]] × [[wyllie_brigitte_1779]], born 11 June 1803 (22 Prairial XI, the\nRepublican-calendar conversion checked by computation) at Diksmuide — **three days after\nhis parents' own 8 June wedding**. Checked rather than assumed to be a transcription slip:\n8 June plus three days is 11 June exactly, and this reads as the ordinary pattern of a\ncouple marrying to legitimate a child already on the way, not an error.\n\nParentage rests on two independent civil acts, both naming Antonius (Josephus) × Brigitta\nWyllie in full: his own marriage, Diksmuide 20 April 1828, act nr. 76, RAB ID 85443, to\n[[bouckaert_marie_1799]]; and his own death, Diksmuide act nr. 4, certificate 7 January\n1869, RAB ID 2292938. Both are volunteer INDEX/Detail transcriptions (`rab-bs-huwelijken`,\n`rab-bs-overlijdens`), `sup`, never `doc`.\n\nHis own children are visible in the same death index — sons Bernardus Franciscus (died\n1842) and Emilius Jacobus (died 1846) — with further descendants marrying in 1854, 1858\nand 1862. Noted here as a frontier for objective 2, not pursued this pass."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanalledewerelt_jacoba_1630","name":"Jacoba Van Alledewerelt","dates":"~1630 – 1675","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Alledewerelt","family":"vanalledewerelt","born":"~1630","order":"1630","died":"1675","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"id":"vanmaele_joannes_1641","name":"Joannes Van Maele","detail":"m. Beernem, 19 Jul 1664"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"FRONTIER above — grandmother of Francisca Van Maele."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanbergen_joannes_1815","name":"Joannes Franciscus Van Bergen","dates":"1815 – 1898","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Bergen","family":"vanbergen","born":"1815","order":"1815","died":"1898","occupation":"metser (mason)","line":"de-keyser","spouses":[{"id":"vermandel_ida_1825","name":"Ida Vermandel"}],"source":"Death act nr. 123 — Ida Vermandel, Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen), died 21 June 1865 (register image); Marriage act, 18 May 1882, Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen) — Petrus Vermorgen × Paulina Van Den Berghe (register image); Death act nr. 721 — Maria Louisa Vanbergen, Oostende, 23 November 1888; wete1998 (Erik Bekaert) — Hamme (O-Vl) specialist","note":"Maternal grandfather of Louise Bocklandt — father of Maria Louisa Van Bergen (1842). Of Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen).\n\nCORROBORATED (2026-07-26) by two register images and one index, none of which derive from\nthe `tree-wete1998` tree this record had rested on alone. His wife [[vermandel_ida_1825]]'s\n**1865 Hamme death act** names him by his full name as her husband, living at Hamme. His\ndaughter [[vandenberghe_paulina_1849]]'s **1882 Hamme marriage act** has him present in person,\nconsenting, **sixty-five years old** and a *metser*. And his daughter\n[[vanbergen_marielouise_1842]]'s 1888 Oostende death act gives him the same trade at Hamme.\n\nTwo things follow. The trade is now recorded, from three sources agreeing. And sixty-five\nin May 1882 puts his birth about 1817, which the held `1815` survives but is not confirmed\nby — so the year stays as it was, and it is worth knowing it comes from a member tree and\nnot from an act.\n\n`sup`, not `doc`, and deliberately: the two images prove he existed, married, worked as a\nmason and was alive at Hamme in 1865 and 1882. Neither gives his birth, his death or his\nparents, which are the three things this record still asserts on a tree's word. See\ndocs/research-log.md §52 for why that distinction is kept rather than rounded up.\n\nFRONTIER — his death, held as 1898. The 1882 act proves he was alive that May, so the\nwindow is 1882–1898 and the register is mapped: Hamme deaths 1894–1900 is FamilySearch\nDGS **004835775**. His marriage to Ida is the higher-value act, since it would name all\nfour of their parents; on her birthplace it should be sought at **Zelzate** (Huwelijken\n1821–1860, DGS 004670484) before Waasmunster or Hamme."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanbergen_marielouise_1842","name":"Marie-Louise Van Bergen","dates":"1842 Waasmunster – 22 Nov 1888 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Bergen","family":"vanbergen","born":"1842 Waasmunster","order":"1842","died":"22 Nov 1888 Oostende","occupation":"werkvrouw","line":"de-keyser","father":"vanbergen_joannes_1815","mother":"vermandel_ida_1825","spouses":[{"id":"bocklandt_edouard_1839","name":"Édouard Bocklandt"}],"source":"wete1998 (Erik Bekaert) — Hamme (O-Vl) specialist; Death act nr. 721 — Maria Louisa Vanbergen, Oostende, 23 November 1888","note":"Mother of Louise Marie Bocklandt (1877, Hamme O-Vl). Full name Maria Louisa Van Bergen,\n1842-1888. Her parents were Joannes Franciscus Van Bergen (1815-1898) × Ida Vermandel\n(1825-1865).\n\nCITATION REPAIRED (2026-07-26), replacing the §52 downgrade. Her own death act — Oostende\nnr. 721, 23 November 1888 ([[agatha-oostende-1888-death-maria-louisa-vanbergen]]) — names\nher father **Joannes Franciscus Vanbergen**, living at Hamme, *metser*, her mother **Ida\nVermandel**, \"overleden te Hamme\", and her partner **Eduardus Bocklandt**. CONFIDENCE STAYS\n`sup`: AGATHA serves this act only as an \"analyse van akte\" (index transcription), not the\nregister image.\n\nA BIRTHPLACE CORRECTION. The act states her *geboorteplaats* as **Waasmunster**, not Hamme.\nThe family prose elsewhere says Hamme throughout, but that was her father's residence at\nthe time of her death, not her own birth commune. Her own birth act, and her parents' own\nmarriage, therefore belong in the **Waasmunster** registers rather than Hamme's;\n[[vermandel_ida_1825]]'s record carries the same pointer, and is high on the research queue.\n\nDeath date and act date differ by one day: she died 22 November 1888, the act was drawn up\n23 November — ordinary Belgian declare-the-day-after practice, not a conflict.\n\nOccupation *werkvrouw* is from this 1888 act, at Oostende; the 1880 Hamme death act of her\nson Ludovicus ([[fs-hamme-1880-death-ludovicus-bocklandt]]) calls her *spinster*, aged 39,\neight years earlier — the field keeps the later trade, this note keeps the earlier one.\n\nA SISTER (2026-07-26): [[vandenberghe_paulina_1849]], born at Hamme about 1849, whose own 1882\nmarriage act names the same parents — and dates their mother's death to the day that\n[[vermandel_ida_1825]]'s own death act gives independently. Two more probable siblings, Josephus\n(b. 1852) and Henricus (b. 1861), are named as frontiers on their mother's record and are\nnot grafted: they rest on a name index and their acts have not been read."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanbogaert_alphonsus","name":"Alphonsus Van Bogaert","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Bogaert","family":"vanbogaert","sex":"m","line":"paelinck","father":"vanbogaert_carolus_1819","mother":"martinet_maria_1838","spouses":[{"id":"moerloos_rosalia","name":"Rosalia Moerloos","detail":"m. Sint-Niklaas, 7 Apr 1909"}],"source":"Marriage act — Alphonsus Van Bogaert × Rosalia Moerloos, Sint-Niklaas, 7 April 1909","note":"Son of [[vanbogaert_carolus_1819]] and [[martinet_maria_1838]], and so a brother of [[vanbogaert_maria_1861]] — an uncle of\nLéonie Paelinck.\n\nFrom his own Sint-Niklaas marriage act of 7 April 1909, which names both his parents and his\nbride, **Rosalia Moerloos**, daughter of Vitalis Moerloos and Nathalia Van Acker.\n\nNo dates of his own: the act is indexed under the marriage and has not been read as an image.\nFRONTIER — reading it would give both spouses' ages and therefore his birth year, and his\nwife's family are three more people the act already names."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanbogaert_carolus_1819","name":"Carolus Ludovicus Van Bogaert","dates":"2 Feb 1819 Nieuwkerken-Waas – 2 Jun 1892 Sint-Niklaas","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Bogaert","family":"vanbogaert","born":"2 Feb 1819 Nieuwkerken-Waas","order":"1819-02-02","died":"2 Jun 1892 Sint-Niklaas","occupation":"arbeider (labourer)","line":"paelinck","spouses":[{"id":"martinet_maria_1838","name":"Maria Ludovica Martinet","detail":"m. Nieuwkerken-Waas, 1 Feb 1860"}],"source":"Marriage act — Alphonsus Van Bogaert × Rosalia Moerloos, Sint-Niklaas, 7 April 1909; stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck)","note":"A labourer; father of Maria Magdalena Van Bogaert by his wife Maria Ludovica Martinet (1838–1911).\n\nCORROBORATED FROM A CIVIL ACT (July 2026). He and [[martinet_maria_1838]] are named together as the\nbridegroom's parents in the Sint-Niklaas marriage act of 7 April 1909 ([[S18]]) — seventeen\nyears after his own death, which is ordinary: an act names the parents whether living or not.\n\nThe act also reveals a son, [[vanbogaert_alphonsus]], who was not in this tree and is a brother of\n[[vanbogaert_maria_1861]]."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanbogaert_maria_1861","name":"Maria Magdalena Van Bogaert","dates":"25 Jul 1861 Nieuwkerken-Waas – 31 Dec 1928 Sint-Niklaas","confidence":"doc","surname":"Van Bogaert","family":"vanbogaert","born":"25 Jul 1861 Nieuwkerken-Waas","order":"1861-07-25","died":"31 Dec 1928 Sint-Niklaas","occupation":"huishoudster (housekeeper)","line":"paelinck","father":"vanbogaert_carolus_1819","mother":"martinet_maria_1838","spouses":[{"id":"paelinck_eduardus_1858","name":"Eduardus Paelinck","detail":"m. Sint-Niklaas, 17 Nov 1888"}],"source":"Birth registration nr. 997 — Philomena Leonia Paelinck, Sint-Niklaas, 31 October 1901; Birth act of Philomena Leonia Paelinck, Sint-Niklaas, 31 October 1901; stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck)","note":"Widowed young — her first husband Ludovicus Brion died in 1887 — then remarried Eduardus Paelinck in 1888. Buried at Begraafplaats Tereken, Sint-Niklaas. Daughter of Carolus Van Bogaert & Maria Martinet.\n\nCORROBORATED (July 2026) as a mother: named in her daughter Léonie's Sint-Niklaas birth\nact of 31 October 1901, alongside [[paelinck_eduardus_1858]].\n\nCONFIRMED BY A CIVIL RECORD (July 2026): named as the mother on her daughter's Sint-Niklaas\nbirth registration of 31 October 1901 ([[S16]]), alongside [[paelinck_eduardus_1858]].\n\nREGISTER PAGE READ (July 2026): named in her daughter's 1901 Sint-Niklaas birth act as\n*Maria Magdalena Van Bogaert*, **huishoudster** — an occupation this record did not carry."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vancraenenbroeck_anna","name":"Anna Van Craenenbroeck","dates":"","confidence":"fam","surname":"Van Craenenbroeck","family":"vancraenenbroeck","died":"","line":"janssens","spouses":[{"id":"janssens_rene","name":"René Janssens"}],"source":"cisken — the Zaventem Van Craenenbroeck trunk; The family itself","note":"Van Craenenbroeck is, in Zaventem, essentially ONE extended family, and it is richly documented — back to a 1721 marriage in Zaventem, and through the 1800s in neighbouring Sterrebeek, Wezembeek-Oppem and Kraainem. FAMILY LOCATED (Geneanet, July 2026): the modern Zaventem trunk (Geneanet tree 'cisken' + the Zaventem Kerkhoflaan cemetery index) centres on Antonius Josephus Van Craenenbroeck (1872 Sterrebeek – 1936 Zaventem) × Anna Maria Meeus (1877–1957) — Antonius himself a son of Amandus Franciscus Van Craenenbroeck (1835–1914) × Paulina Mommaerts (1838–1909), so this family is now documented back to the 1830s — with a sibling set born in Zaventem 1902–1918: Amandus Franciscus Henricus (1902–1977, m. Maria Balcaen 1929), Paul Gustaaf (1904–1988, m. Joanna Smolders 1928), Melania Leonia (1906), Joannes Arthur (1908–1982, m. Roza Van Opstal), Maurice Louis Willem (1913–1991) and Bertha Rosalia (1918). Anna — Chris & Eric's mother, born ~1930s in Zaventem, the witloof-farming milieu — fits this family almost certainly (rare surname + exact village + occupation region) and is most plausibly a GRANDDAUGHTER of Antonius, i.e. a daughter of one of those ~1928–29-married couples (Paul Gustaaf × Smolders or Amandus × Balcaen are the leading candidates). BUT the specific parent is NOT yet documented — the 'cisken' tree stops just above Anna's generation — so it is left OPEN, not grafted (no father/mother set here). To confirm which sibling is her parent: (1) Anna's own death notice / memorial card (she died recently in the Zaventem/Leuven area — likely names her parents and siblings); (2) her grave in the Zaventem Kerkhoflaan index; or (3) the owner of the 'cisken' Geneanet tree, a relative who very likely holds Anna's generation privately. Any one of these closes the link."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vandecappelle_eugenia","name":"Eugenia Maria Vandecappelle","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vandecappelle","family":"vandecappelle","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"vincke_alfons_1865","name":"Alfons Luciaan Vincke","detail":"m. Diksmuide, 19 Sep 1888"}],"source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; Memorial card — Eugenia Maria Vandecappelle, partner Alfons Luciaan Vincke","note":"Wife of [[vincke_alfons_1865]]. Named on their marriage act — Diksmuide, 19 September 1888,\nact nr. 149 (`rab-bs-huwelijken`) — and independently on a Familiekunde Vlaanderen\nWestkust memorial card (`fwk-eugenia-vandecappelle`,\n`fwk:f5704ac2-7b0f-1f02-6cfe-1829d47b9e7a`), which names the same couple. Index only, not\nthe register image, hence `sup`. Her own birth, death and parents are not in the\nreachable pages."});
