FamilyTree.person({"id":"vandenbemden_adela_1884","name":"Adela Vandenbemden","dates":"b. 25 Dec 1884 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vandenbemden","family":"vandenbemden","born":"25 Dec 1884 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1884-12-25","line":"thumas","father":"vandenbemden_henricus_1849","mother":"coekelberghs_maria_1848","source":"Civil birth acts naming both parents, for couples already in the tree (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Named as the child in a civil birth act at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1884-12-25**, which gives both\nparents — [[vandenbemden_henricus_1849]] and [[coekelberghs_maria_1848]] — and so places this person in the tree by the act\nrather than by a name. The father is aged 35, born at **Everberg**; the mother is aged 36, born at\n**Bertem** — both matching this couple's own recorded birthplaces exactly.\n\nThe act is held in the harvested corpus and reached through Open Archives:\nhttps://www.openarchieven.nl/abl:9e7d100e-ec98-d2c1-fecd-01cfee6ef581\n\nA rival same-name candidate was checked and ruled out: an Adela Vandenbemden remarries as a\nwidow at Kraainem in 1889, already too old to be this infant — a different, older, same-named\nwoman.\n\n`sup`: an indexed act, not the register image. **No `sex` is recorded**, because the harvested\nmention carries only the relation role and never a sex, and this project does not read a sex off a\nforename."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vandenbemden_felix_1876","name":"Felix Van den Bemden","dates":"b. 10 Sep 1876 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van den Bemden","family":"vandenbemden","born":"10 Sep 1876 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1876-09-10","occupation":"schaliedekker (roofer)","line":"thumas","father":"vandenbemden_henricus_1849","mother":"coekelberghs_maria_1848","spouses":[{"id":"coenraets_amelia_1876","name":"Amelia Coenraets","detail":"m. Kraainem, 8 Feb 1897"}],"source":"Civil birth acts naming both parents, for couples already in the tree (harvested corpus, July 2026); Marriage act — Felix Van den Bemden × Amelia Coenraets, Kraainem, 8 February 1897","note":"Named as the child in a civil birth act at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1876-09-10**, which gives both\nparents — [[vandenbemden_henricus_1849]] and [[coekelberghs_maria_1848]] — and so places this person in the tree by the act rather than\nby a name.\n\nThe act is held in the harvested corpus and reached through Open Archives:\nhttps://www.openarchieven.nl/abl:63fd8c85-b6a4-9f2a-9297-11b8a296d9ed\n\nDOUBLE-ATTESTED (2026-07-26) by his own marriage act, Kraainem, 8 February 1897, to\n[[coenraets_amelia_1876]] — read twenty-one years after the birth act, in an unrelated register, it\nindependently repeats his birth to the day and the place, and names his father with the same\ndeath date and place this tree already holds, **Henricus August Vandenbemden, deceased Kraainem\n12/08/1889**, and his mother **Maria Theresia Coekelberghs**, *herbergierster*. It also gives his\nown occupation, *schaliedekker*.\n\n`sup`: indexed acts, not the register images. **No `sex` is recorded on the birth act**, because\nthe harvested mention carries only the relation role and never a sex, and this project does not\nread a sex off a forename."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vandenbemden_henricus_1849","name":"Henricus Augustinus Vandenbemden","dates":"19 Aug 1849 Everberg – 12 Aug 1889 Kraainem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vandenbemden","family":"vandenbemden","born":"19 Aug 1849 Everberg","order":"1849-08-19","died":"12 Aug 1889 Kraainem","occupation":"dienstbode (servant)","line":"thumas","father":"vandenbemden_jan","mother":"langes_elisabeth","spouses":[{"id":"coekelberghs_maria_1848","name":"Maria Theresia Coekelberghs","detail":"m. Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 24 Apr 1873"}],"source":"Kraainem marriage act nr. 2, 3 February 1902 — Thumas × Vandenbemden; Sint-Stevens-Woluwe marriage act nr. 6, 24 April 1873 — Van den Bemden × Coekelberghs; Kraainem marriage act nr. 16, 6 November 1903 — Van Esch × Coekelberghs, her remarriage; Geneanet","note":"Source detail: Geneanet; daughter Joanna's 1902 Kraainem marriage act\n\nBorn in Everberg; married Maria Theresia Coekelberghs in 1873; died young (1889) at Kraainem. Named in daughter Joanna's 1902 marriage act.\n\nCORRECTED (July 2026). This record gave his death place as Sint-Stevens-Woluwe.\nthe Kraainem marriage act of 3 February 1902 (akte nr. 2, [[S5]]), which names him as the bride's late father, states **Kraainem** — with the death\ndate, 12 August 1889, agreeing exactly. The same man, the wrong commune; the place is now\nas the act has it. He had died thirteen years before his daughter married.\n\nGRAFTED and CORRECTED (2026-07-26): his own marriage act — **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 6,\n24 April 1873** — names his parents. This record carried them as a Geneanet claim flagged\n*to verify*: \"Joannes Baptista Vandenbemden × Agatha Langa\". The act gives\n[[vandenbemden_jan]] and [[langes_elisabeth]] — so the father was roughly right, the mother\nwas **Elisabeth Agatha**, not Agatha, and the surname was **Langes**, not Langa. The\nGeneanet reading is retired. The act also gives his trade at twenty-three, *dienstbode*,\nand the commune the marriage was passed in.\n\nTwo identifiers carry it beyond the surname: his birth, Everberg 19 August 1849, agreeing\nwith this record to the day, and the marriage date 24 April 1873, likewise. His death —\nKraainem, 12 August 1889 — is then confirmed a *third* time by his widow's 1903 remarriage\nact, which names him as her late husband with that date and that commune.\n\nOnly his mother is recorded as present and consenting. His father is a bare name with no\nresidence, no trade and no consent, which is the register's usual shape for a parent\nalready dead; nothing is recorded from that silence beyond noting it on\n[[vandenbemden_jan]].\n\nDOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, for the same reason as [[coekelberghs_maria_1848]]:\nevery act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis and none of them has a scan. See\ndocs/research-log.md §51.\n\nRESOLVED (2026-07-26): all seven further Sint-Stevens-Woluwe births the held corpus names for\nthis couple, 1873–1886, are now recorded — [[vandenbemden_lodewijk_1873]], [[vandenbemden_victor_1874]],\n[[vandenbemden_felix_1876]], [[vandenbemden_karel_1878]], [[vandenbemden_jan_1880]], [[vandenbemden_adela_1884]] and\n[[vandenbemden_julius_1886]] — each by an act naming both parents' exact birthplaces (father Everberg,\nmother Bertem), matching this couple's own recorded birthplaces. Felix and Jan are additionally\ndouble-attested by their own Kraainem marriage acts (1897 and 1900), which independently repeat\ntheir births and this couple's death and occupation facts twenty years on.\n\nAn eighth candidate, *Appolonia* (b. Sint-Stevens-Woluwe 1877-01-28), was checked and\n**REJECTED**: the act names a different couple, Willem Edouard Vandenbemden x Maria Anna\nVandenhoven — see the frontier on [[vandenbemden_jan]] for that rival family, a lead for a\nbrother rather than a graft here. The record this tree briefly carried for that child,\n`data/people/appolonia_vandenbemd77.md`, has been removed."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vandenbemden_jan","name":"Jan Baptist Van den Bemden","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van den Bemden","family":"vandenbemden","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"langes_elisabeth","name":"Elisabeth Agatha Langes"}],"source":"Sint-Stevens-Woluwe marriage act nr. 6, 24 April 1873 — Van den Bemden × Coekelberghs","note":"Father of the groom in his son [[vandenbemden_henricus_1849]]'s marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 6,\n24 April 1873.\n\n**What the act does not say about him is the informative part.** His wife\n[[langes_elisabeth]] is given a residence, a trade and the words *present and consenting*;\nhe is given a name and nothing else — no commune, no occupation, no consent. That is the\nregister's usual shape for a parent already dead, and it is why this record carries no\ndeath entry at all rather than a `raw` note claiming he was alive: a bare name is not a\nstatement either way, and inventing \"alive on 24 April 1873\" from silence would be exactly\nthe guess the grammar has no syntax for.\n\nHe confirms — and corrects — an unverified Geneanet claim this tree had been carrying on\nhis son's record, which named him *Joannes Baptista Vandenbemden*. The act's own spelling\nis *Jan Baptist Van den Bemden*, and it is followed here.\n\n`sup`: an AGATHA act analysis, not the register image.\n\nFRONTIER — his own marriage to Elisabeth Agatha Langes, which the Everberg or Kortenberg\nregisters should hold for roughly 1840–1849 and which would name his parents; and his\ndeath, which on the reading above falls before April 1873. Two Van den Bemden witnesses\nstood at his son's wedding — *Lodewijk*, 40, daglooner of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, and\n*Willem*, 26, landbouwer of Schaarbeek — and one of them is likely his son or his brother.\nNeither is grafted: the act states no kinship for either.\n\nFRONTIER — **Willem Edouard Vandenbemden**, a second Everberg-born Vandenbemden of much the same\nage, living in the same commune as [[vandenbemden_henricus_1849]], and a strong lead for a brother — but not\ngrafted. A Sint-Stevens-Woluwe birth act of 28 January 1877 names him as the declaring father: 28\nyears old, born at Everberg, *daglooner*, married to Maria Anna Vandenhoven, born at Kraainem\n(https://www.openarchieven.nl/abl:2c0d71d9-be5c-fa20-000f-fd03a9ac2403). That act was briefly\nmisread as [[vandenbemden_henricus_1849]]'s own child, Appolonia — see the correction on his record. The same\ncouple recurs as parents of a further child, Frans Vandenbemden (b. Kraainem 1872-09-28), in\nFrans's own 1897 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe marriage act, which also gives Willem Edouard's death:\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe, 20 March 1891\n(https://www.openarchieven.nl/abl:caefee09-568f-04b7-f115-22d4b7730684). Not grafted: the 1877\nact states no kinship between Willem Edouard and [[vandenbemden_henricus_1849]], and a shared birthplace\n(Everberg) and a shared decade of birth is one identifier, not the two this project requires\nbefore a link is made. Neither act names Willem Edouard's own parents, so there is not yet a way\nto test the \"brother\" reading directly."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vandenbemden_jan_1880","name":"Jan Van den Bemden","dates":"b. 9 Aug 1880 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van den Bemden","family":"vandenbemden","born":"9 Aug 1880 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1880-08-09","occupation":"fabriekwerker (factory worker)","line":"thumas","father":"vandenbemden_henricus_1849","mother":"coekelberghs_maria_1848","spouses":[{"id":"feyaerts_elisabeth_1878","name":"Elisabeth Leonia Feyaerts","detail":"m. Kraainem, 17 Sep 1900"}],"source":"Civil birth acts naming both parents, for couples already in the tree (harvested corpus, July 2026); Marriage act — Joannes (Jan) Vandenbemden × Elisabeth Leonia Feyaerts, Kraainem, 17 September 1900","note":"Named as the child in a civil birth act at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1880-08-09**, which gives both\nparents — [[vandenbemden_henricus_1849]] and [[coekelberghs_maria_1848]] — and so places this person in the tree by the act rather than\nby a name.\n\nThe act is held in the harvested corpus and reached through Open Archives:\nhttps://www.openarchieven.nl/abl:1623c443-8ba1-0bc1-d501-27c4bf99b573\n\nDOUBLE-ATTESTED (2026-07-26) by his own marriage act, Kraainem, 17 September 1900 (as *Joannes\nVandenbemden*), to [[feyaerts_elisabeth_1878]] — it independently repeats his birth to the day and\nthe place, and names his father with the same death date and place this tree already holds,\n**Henricus August Vandenbemden, deceased Kraainem 12/08/1889**, and his mother **Maria Theresia\nCoekelberghs**, *herbergierster*. It also gives his own occupation, *fabriekwerker*.\n\n`sup`: indexed acts, not the register images. **No `sex` is recorded on the birth act**, because\nthe harvested mention carries only the relation role and never a sex, and this project does not\nread a sex off a forename."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vandenbemden_joanna_1882","name":"Joanna Vandenbemden","dates":"15 Jun 1882 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe – 29 Apr 1948 Kraainem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vandenbemden","family":"vandenbemden","born":"15 Jun 1882 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1882-06-15","died":"29 Apr 1948 Kraainem","occupation":"naaister (seamstress)","line":"thumas","father":"vandenbemden_henricus_1849","mother":"coekelberghs_maria_1848","spouses":[{"id":"thumas_joannes_1876","name":"J.B. Georgius Thumas","detail":"m. Kraainem, 3 Feb 1902"}],"source":"Kraainem marriage act nr. 2, 3 February 1902 — Thumas × Vandenbemden; jswaelens","note":"Source detail: Geneanet (jswaelens); her 1902 Kraainem marriage act\n\nA seamstress; married J.B. Georgius Thumas in Kraainem in 1902. Her parents are named in that marriage act. Several of her children died in infancy.\n\nDOCUMENTED (July 2026) by the Kraainem marriage act of 3 February 1902 (akte nr. 2, [[S5]]), where she is the bride: born at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe\non 15 June 1882, living at Kraainem, *naaister* — the occupation already held here,\nconfirmed word for word — and daughter of Henricus Augustinus Vandenbemden and Maria\nTheresia Coekelberghs.\n\nDOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.\nNothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the\nevidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own\nDemogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or\nits image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vandenbemden_julius_1886","name":"Julius Vandenbemden","dates":"b. 17 May 1886 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vandenbemden","family":"vandenbemden","born":"17 May 1886 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1886-05-17","line":"thumas","father":"vandenbemden_henricus_1849","mother":"coekelberghs_maria_1848","source":"Civil birth acts naming both parents, for couples already in the tree (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Named as the child in a civil birth act at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1886-05-17**, which gives both\nparents — [[vandenbemden_henricus_1849]] and [[coekelberghs_maria_1848]] — and so places this person in the tree by the act rather than\nby a name.\n\nThe act is held in the harvested corpus and reached through Open Archives:\nhttps://www.openarchieven.nl/abl:51809fc3-2aad-95d3-4ab7-add9c04a74c9\n\n`sup`: an indexed act, not the register image. **No `sex` is recorded**, because the harvested\nmention carries only the relation role and never a sex, and this project does not read a sex\noff a forename."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vandenbemden_karel_1878","name":"Karel Borromeus Vandenbemden","dates":"b. 23 Aug 1878 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vandenbemden","family":"vandenbemden","born":"23 Aug 1878 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1878-08-23","line":"thumas","father":"vandenbemden_henricus_1849","mother":"coekelberghs_maria_1848","source":"Civil birth acts naming both parents, for couples already in the tree (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Named as the child in a civil birth act at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1878-08-23**, which gives both\nparents — [[vandenbemden_henricus_1849]] and [[coekelberghs_maria_1848]] — and so places this person in the tree by the act rather than\nby a name.\n\nThe act is held in the harvested corpus and reached through Open Archives:\nhttps://www.openarchieven.nl/abl:778eb9b2-ea98-cc5a-14b3-c4a9d265efa5\n\n`sup`: an indexed act, not the register image. **No `sex` is recorded**, because the harvested\nmention carries only the relation role and never a sex, and this project does not read a sex\noff a forename."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vandenbemden_lodewijk_1873","name":"Lodewijk Vandenbemden","dates":"b. 4 Jul 1873 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vandenbemden","family":"vandenbemden","born":"4 Jul 1873 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1873-07-04","line":"thumas","father":"vandenbemden_henricus_1849","mother":"coekelberghs_maria_1848","source":"Civil birth acts naming both parents, for couples already in the tree (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Named as the child in a civil birth act at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1873-07-04**, which gives both\nparents — [[vandenbemden_henricus_1849]] and [[coekelberghs_maria_1848]] — and so places this person in the tree by the act\nrather than by a name. The father is aged 23, born at **Everberg**; the mother is aged 24, born\nat **Bertem** — both birthplaces matching this couple's own recorded birthplaces exactly, which is\nwhat carries the link beyond the shared surname.\n\nThe act is held in the harvested corpus and reached through Open Archives:\nhttps://www.openarchieven.nl/abl:ad55a6f4-dfa8-2e61-fb92-d8bb1b562366\n\nLodewijk was born **ten weeks after his parents' wedding** — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 24 April 1873,\nto this birth on 4 July 1873. That is a fact about the two dates already in the record; no\nconclusion is drawn from it here.\n\n`sup`: an indexed act, not the register image. **No `sex` is recorded**, because the harvested\nmention carries only the relation role and never a sex, and this project does not read a sex\noff a forename."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vandenbemden_victor_1874","name":"Victor Van den Bemden","dates":"b. 18 Dec 1874 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van den Bemden","family":"vandenbemden","born":"18 Dec 1874 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1874-12-18","line":"thumas","father":"vandenbemden_henricus_1849","mother":"coekelberghs_maria_1848","source":"Civil birth acts naming both parents, for couples already in the tree (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Named as the child in a civil birth act at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1874-12-18**, which gives both\nparents — [[vandenbemden_henricus_1849]] and [[coekelberghs_maria_1848]] — and so places this person in the tree by the act\nrather than by a name. The father is aged 25, born at **Everberg**; the mother is aged 26, born at\n**Bertem** — both matching this couple's own recorded birthplaces exactly.\n\nThe act is held in the harvested corpus and reached through Open Archives:\nhttps://www.openarchieven.nl/abl:be7d371f-9949-fa85-0483-d43f287c93f3\n\nA rival same-name candidate was checked and ruled out: a different Victor Vandenbemden, son of\nAndre Vandenbemden x Catherine Pauline Cammaerts, marries at Tervuren in 1894 and again in 1919 —\na different family, not this child grown up.\n\n`sup`: an indexed act, not the register image. **No `sex` is recorded**, because the harvested\nmention carries only the relation role and never a sex, and this project does not read a sex off a\nforename."});
