FamilyTree.person({"id":"vandervarent_joannes","name":"Joannes van der Varent","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"van der Varent","family":"vandervarent","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"goossens_anna","name":"Anna Catharina Goossens"}],"source":"Marriage of Petrus van der Varent x Maria Josephina Peremans, Zaventem, 5 November 1840","note":"Named as a parent of the groom in his son [[vandervarent_petrus_1813]]'s marriage registration —\nZaventem, 5 November 1840 (S29). Nothing else: the entry gives him no age, no trade, no\nresidence and no dates, and none is invented here.\n\nFRONTIER: his marriage to [[goossens_anna]], which the Zaventem registers should hold for roughly\n1805–1813."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vandervarent_petrus_1813","name":"Petrús van der Varent","dates":"b. ~1813","confidence":"sup","surname":"van der Varent","family":"vandervarent","sex":"m","born":"~1813","order":"1813","line":"thumas","father":"vandervarent_joannes","mother":"goossens_anna","spouses":[{"id":"peremans_maria","name":"Maria Josephina Peremans","detail":"m. Zaventem, 5 Nov 1840"}],"source":"Marriage of Petrus van der Varent x Maria Josephina Peremans, Zaventem, 5 November 1840","note":"Married [[peremans_maria]] at Zaventem on **5 November 1840** (S29), which makes him\n[[peremans_joanna_1824]]'s brother-in-law and [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]]'s, six years before that wedding.\n\nHe was **27** at the marriage, which is where the *about 1813* comes from — an age, converted\nto an approximate year and marked as approximate, not promoted to a birth date.\n\nSon of [[vandervarent_joannes]] and [[goossens_anna]].\n\nThe record gives no place of birth, no trade and no residence, so this record has none.\n\n`sup`: an indexed registration, the act itself unread.\n\nNOT PROVEN, a frontier only (2026-07-27): a **Petrus Van Der Varen**, 35, stands witness\nat [[peremans_joannes_1820]]'s Zaventem marriage on 21 August 1848 (S34) — plausibly this\nman, since 35 in 1848 implies ~1813, matching the ~1813 already held here, but adding no\nmore precision than that. The act states no relation, and the surname is spelled\ndifferently (*Van Der Varen* against this record's *van der Varent*). Surname, place and\na plausible age are exactly the pattern that produced false positives elsewhere this\nrun — one identifier's worth, not two, so this is recorded as a lead and not linked."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vandewalle_carolus_1638","name":"Carolus Vandewalle","dates":"3 Feb 1638 Oostkamp – 19 Jan 1702","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vandewalle","family":"vandewalle","born":"3 Feb 1638 Oostkamp","order":"1638-02-03","died":"19 Jan 1702","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"vandewalle_petrus","mother":"vanhoutte_francisca_1594","spouses":[{"id":"rups_maria_1642","name":"Maria Rups","detail":"m. Oostkamp, 17 May 1662"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Grandfather of Barbara De Baecke (via daughter Maria Magdalena Vandewalle). Born out of wedlock (marked 'illegitime'). Married Maria Rups 1662."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vandewalle_cornelius","name":"Cornelius Vandewalle","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vandewalle","family":"vandewalle","sex":"m","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"id":"vanrenterghem_maria_1610","name":"Maria Van Renterghem"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Earlier husband of [[vanrenterghem_maria_1610]], who afterwards married [[rups_michael]]\n— our line runs through that second marriage, via their daughter [[rups_maria_1642]].\n\nA Vandewalle marrying into this family is not a coincidence worth ignoring: the\nVandewalles appear again a generation on, when Maria Rups married\n[[vandewalle_carolus_1638]] at Oostkamp in 1662. FRONTIER — whether Cornelius and\nCarolus are of the same family. Nothing here establishes it, and the surname alone\nis not evidence."});
