FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanesch_henricus_1836","name":"Henricus Van Esch","dates":"b. 23 Nov 1836 Bertem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Esch","family":"vanesch","born":"23 Nov 1836 Bertem","order":"1836-11-23","occupation":"herbergier (innkeeper)","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"coekelberghs_maria_1848","name":"Maria Theresia Coekelberghs","detail":"m. Kraainem, 6 Nov 1903"}],"source":"Kraainem marriage act nr. 16, 6 November 1903 — Van Esch × Coekelberghs, her remarriage","note":"[[coekelberghs_maria_1848]]'s second husband, married at Kraainem on 6 November 1903 (act nr. 16) —\nfourteen years after she was widowed of [[vandenbemden_henricus_1849]], and he a widower himself.\n\nBorn at Bertem on 23 November 1836, which is her own birth commune, and an *herbergier* at\nZaventem, which is her own trade: she is recorded as *herbergierster* on her daughter's\n1902 marriage act. Two innkeepers from the same village, marrying in their sixties.\n\nHe marries into this tree rather than descending in it: nothing here claims a blood\nrelation, and he is recorded because the act that names him is the same act that gives\n[[coekelberghs_joannes_1809]] and [[haesaerts_anna_1810]] their death dates.\n\n`sup`: an AGATHA act analysis (Demogen project huvlb20), not the register image. Beware the\nOpen Archives mirror of this act — its rendered HTML gives all three death dates one day\nearlier than both its own API record and the AGATHA page.\n\nFRONTIER — his first marriage and his parents, neither read. A widower of Bertem born in\n1836 should have both a first marriage and a first wife's death in the Bertem or Zaventem\nregisters."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vangindertaelen_joanna_1825","name":"Joanna Catharina Van Gindertaelen","dates":"b. ~1825","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Gindertaelen","family":"vangindertaelen","sex":"f","born":"~1825","order":"1825","occupation":"arbeidster (labourer)","line":"thumas","father":"vangindertaelen_joannes","mother":"huenaerts_anna","spouses":[{"id":"peremans_joannes_1820","name":"Joannes Baptista Peremans","detail":"m. Zaventem, 21 Aug 1848"}],"source":"Marriage act — Joannes Baptista Peremans x Joanna Catharina Van Gindertaelen, Zaventem, 21 August 1848","note":"Married [[peremans_joannes_1820]] at **Zaventem on 21 August 1848** (S34), which makes her\n[[peremans_joanna_1824]]'s sister-in-law. She was **23**, an *arbeidster*, and the act states she\ncould not write — twenty-three in August 1848 gives the *about 1825* birth year here, an\nage converted to a year and marked approximate, not a date the act itself gives.\n\nDaughter of [[vangindertaelen_joannes]] and [[huenaerts_anna]], both named in the act with their\nroles labelled — present and consenting — so there is no identity question here, only the\nordinary absence of a birth date, birthplace or trade for the parents beyond what the act\ngives.\n\n`sup`: an index-level AGATHA/Demogen act analysis, the register image unread.\n\nFRONTIER: her own birth act at Zaventem around 1825, and any children of this marriage."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vangindertaelen_joannes","name":"Joannes Franciscus Van Gindertaelen","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Gindertaelen","family":"vangindertaelen","sex":"m","occupation":"arbeider (labourer)","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"huenaerts_anna","name":"Anna Catharina Huenaerts"}],"source":"Marriage act — Joannes Baptista Peremans x Joanna Catharina Van Gindertaelen, Zaventem, 21 August 1848","note":"Named in his daughter [[vangindertaelen_joanna_1825]]'s marriage act — Zaventem, 21 August 1848\n(S34) — as *arbeider* of Zaventem, present and consenting. The act gives him no age and\nno dates, so this record has none.\n\nFRONTIER: his marriage to [[huenaerts_anna]], which the Zaventem registers should hold for\nroughly 1815–1825."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanhecke_catharina_1620","name":"Catharina van Hecke","dates":"~1620 – ~1670","confidence":"sup","surname":"van Hecke","family":"vanhecke","sex":"f","born":"~1620","order":"1620","died":"~1670","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"bundervoet_livinus_1600","name":"Livinus Bundervoet"}],"source":"paulderidder","note":"Second wife of [[bundervoet_livinus_1600]], and so a step-mother to [[bundervoet_segerius_1615]] rather\nthan an ancestor of this tree.\n\nWORTH NOTING, NOT CLAIMED: Livinus's son Segerius married [[vanhecke_joanna_1610]] (~1610), and\nLivinus himself married this Catharina van Hecke (~1620) — two van Hecke women marrying father\nand son. In a parish the size of Evergem that suggests one van Hecke family and possibly two\nsisters, but nothing read so far states any relationship between them, so none is recorded."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanhecke_joanna_1610","name":"Joanna (Janneken) van Hecke","dates":"~1610 – 1678","confidence":"sup","surname":"van Hecke","family":"vanhecke","born":"~1610","order":"1610","died":"1678","line":"bundervoet","father":"vanhecke_willem_1580","spouses":[{"id":"bundervoet_segerius_1615","name":"Segerius Bundervoet"}],"source":"paulderidder; glorieuxp","note":"Wife of Segerius Bundervoet and mother of Joannes Bundervoet (~1637).\n\nCORRECTED (July 2026): this record said \"her own parents not recorded here\". The\npaulderidder chart gives her father as Willem van Hecke (~1580), now linked; her mother\nappears there only as \"?\", so that side stays open."});
