FamilyTree.person({"id":"vaniseghem_arthur_1874","name":"Arthur Leopoldus Joannes Van Iseghem","dates":"b. 17 Mar 1874 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Iseghem","family":"vaniseghem","sex":"m","born":"17 Mar 1874 Oostende","order":"1874-03-17","occupation":"boodschapper (messenger)","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vaniseghem_joannes_1852","mother":"janssen_hermanie_1853","spouses":[{"name":"Elodia Joanna Schellynck","detail":"m. Oostende, 29 Jun 1901"},{"name":"Judith Maria Debbaut","detail":"m. Oostende, 22 Feb 1936"}],"source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] and [[janssen_hermanie_1853]] — one of eight children the vrijwilligersrab\nindexes give this couple; see [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] for the full sibship and the identifier that\ngrounds it (a province-wide sweep found nine different men recorded identically as\n\"Joannes Vaniseghem\", so it is the parent PAIR, not the father's name alone, that carries\nthis record).\n\nBorn Oostende, birth act nr. 140, RAB ID 1486295 (Birth Date column, not Certificate\nDate). His own first marriage act — Oostende, 29 June 1901, act nr. 147, RAB ID 666102 —\nindependently restates his birth as 17/03/1874 Oostende, an exact match and a second\nidentifier beyond the parent pair; he is recorded there as *boodschapper*, *ongehuwd*.\nMarried Elodia Joanna Schellynck (b. 20/08/1876 Oostende, d/o Petrus Constantinus\nSchellynck x Maria Coleta Vigne — not a record here).\n\n**A SECOND MARRIAGE, not a ninth child.** Oostende, 22 February 1936, act nr. 40, RAB ID\n711795, names a groom \"VANISEGHEM Arthur Leopoldus\" marrying Judith Maria Debbaut; its\nPrevious Partners table names Schellynck Elodia Joanna, the 1901 bride, which is what\nidentifies this as the same man remarrying rather than a distinct sibling. This venue's\nPrevious Partners table elsewhere in this family names only spouses who had already died\n(e.g. [[janssen_josephus_1820]]'s remarried widow), consistent with Elodia having died before\n1936, though no death act for her was found in this pass — not asserted as fact, only as\nthe ordinary reading of the table. Index rows throughout, no register image read, so\nconfidence stays `sup`."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vaniseghem_augustus_1875","name":"Augustus Joannes Judocus Van Iseghem","dates":"13 Aug 1875 Oostende – 4 Jan 1876 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Iseghem","family":"vaniseghem","sex":"m","born":"13 Aug 1875 Oostende","order":"1875-08-13","died":"4 Jan 1876 Oostende","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vaniseghem_joannes_1852","mother":"janssen_hermanie_1853","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] and [[janssen_hermanie_1853]] — one of eight children the vrijwilligersrab\nindexes give this couple; see [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] for the full sibship and the identifier\nthat grounds it.\n\nDied in infancy. Born Oostende, birth act nr. 417, RAB ID 1486298 (Birth Date column).\nDied Oostende, act nr. 6, RAB ID 263907, Sex M, age given as **4 months 22 days** —\nchecked by computation: 13 August 1875 plus 4 months 22 days lands on 4 January 1876\nexactly, cross-locking the death act to the birth act arithmetically, a second,\nindependent identifier beyond the parent pair. Both Date and Certificate Date columns\nagree on the death act (04/01/1876)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vaniseghem_camillus_1905","name":"Camillus Gustavus Van Iseghem","dates":"25 Apr 1905 Oostende – 29 Nov 1905 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Iseghem","family":"vaniseghem","sex":"m","born":"25 Apr 1905 Oostende","order":"1905-04-25","died":"29 Nov 1905 Oostende","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vaniseghem_eduardus_1880","mother":"vincke_emma_1880","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] and [[vincke_emma_1880]], and [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]]'s brother — found\nincidentally while sweeping the birth index for rows naming Emma Celesta Vincke as\nmother (Oostende act nr. 501, `rab-bs-geboorten`). Not itemised on this couple's own\nrecords before now: he has no marriage act in this sweep, unlike his five older siblings\n[[vaniseghem_flavie_1898]], [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1901]], [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]], [[vaniseghem_valentina_1909]] and [[vaniseghem_maria_1913]] — he\ndied in infancy, below.\n\n**HIS OWN DEATH ACT FOUND (2026-07-27), NOT \"no death act for either brother\" as first\nframed** — he was mistakenly described in an earlier search as \"a sixth child not in the\ntree\"; he was already held here. What is new is his death: Oostende, 29 November 1905\n(Certificate Date 30/11/1905, a one-day offset), act nr. 810, RAB ID 500127. Sex M. The\nDetail's own Birth Date field reads 25/04/1905, matching this record's birth date exactly\n— **a second, independent identifier**, so this birth date is no longer single-sourced.\nHe lived about seven months, dying at Aartshertoginnestraat 20.\n\nThe mother is written **\"VINCKE Emma Coleta\"** on this act, against \"Emma Celesta\" on her\nown 1907 marriage act and elsewhere in this tree. `data/forenames.json` folds\n\"celesta\"~\"celestina\"/\"celestine\", but not \"coleta\"/\"colette\" — this pair is not covered\nby that table. The identity does not depend on the fold: the father's rare full name\n(\"Eduardus Ludovicus Rudolphus Van Iseghem\") plus the exact birth-date match already give\ntwo identifiers. Recorded as a variant, not resolved into `forenames.json`.\n\n**Both parents are recorded \"Ongehuwd\" (unmarried), aged 25** — [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] (b.\n29/11/1880) turning 25 on the very day of this death, [[vincke_emma_1880]] (b. 23/01/1880)\nalready 25 — consistent with the couple's own 1907 marriage two years later, not a\ncontradiction. This **dates the relationship to at least 1905**, bearing on the open\nlegitimation frontier on [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]]'s record (born Lens 1903) and [[vaniseghem_flavie_1898]]'s\n(born Diksmuide 1898, under the surname Vincke) — see those records.\n\nA second son of the same forenames, [[vaniseghem_camillus_1911]], was born six years later,\nin 1911 — his own fate is still open; no death act for him has been found in this venue."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vaniseghem_camillus_1911","name":"Camillus Henricus Eduardus Van Iseghem","dates":"b. 6 Jan 1911 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Iseghem","family":"vaniseghem","born":"6 Jan 1911 Oostende","order":"1911-01-06","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vaniseghem_eduardus_1880","mother":"vincke_emma_1880","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] and [[vincke_emma_1880]], and [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]]'s brother — found\nincidentally while sweeping the birth index for rows naming Emma Celesta Vincke as\nmother (Oostende act nr. 14, `rab-bs-geboorten`). Not itemised on this couple's own\nrecords before now: he has no marriage act in this sweep, unlike his five siblings\n[[vaniseghem_flavie_1898]], [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1901]], [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]], [[vaniseghem_valentina_1909]] and [[vaniseghem_maria_1913]], so his\nown birth row is the only evidence for him.\n\n**NOT INDEPENDENTLY RE-CHECKED.** This birth date was read off the same index whose\n\"Date\" and \"Certificate Date\" columns are confirmed elsewhere in this family to be\nconflated (see `rab-bs-overlijdens`'s note, and the corrections on [[vincke_irma_1874]] and\n[[vincke_jerome_1886]], and on Albert Joseph Vincke, not itself a record here — see\n[[vincke_emma_1880]]'s frontier note). No second act or memorial card has confirmed this\ndate, so treat it as unverified until a second source is read. He shares\nhis first two forenames with an elder brother, [[vaniseghem_camillus_1905]], born six years\nearlier — a second such reuse in this family is plausible (the pattern is already\ndocumented twice over on [[vincke_theophil_1866]]'s own children).\n\n**UPDATE (2026-07-27):** [[vaniseghem_camillus_1905]]'s own death act has since been found\n(Oostende, 29 November 1905, age about seven months) — see his record. That resolves his\nfate but not this one's: **no death act for Camillus Henricus has been found** in this\nvenue's transcribed window, so whether the reuse of \"Camillus\" followed a death in this\ncase too remains open, not asserted."});
