FamilyTree.person({"id":"vaniseghem_eduardus_1880","name":"Eduardus Ludovicus Rudolphus Van Iseghem","dates":"29 Nov 1880 Oostende – 27 Jun 1945 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Iseghem","family":"vaniseghem","born":"29 Nov 1880 Oostende","order":"1880-11-29","died":"27 Jun 1945 Oostende","occupation":"werkman (labourer)","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vaniseghem_joannes_1852","mother":"janssen_hermanie_1853","spouses":[{"id":"vincke_emma_1880","name":"Emma Celesta Vincke","detail":"m. Oostende, 28 Sep 1907"}],"source":"Memorial card — Emma Celesta Vincke, d. Oostende 6 October 1974; gverdievel (Guy Verdievel); West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; Marriage act nr. 212 — Eduardus Ludovicus Rudolphus Vanyseghem x Emma Celesta Vincke, Oostende, 28 September 1907 (register image)","note":"Around 1903 the family was living in Lens, northern France (son Joannes was born there); father of at least seven children.\n\nCORROBORATED (July 2026) as a husband: named as the partner on [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s\nmemorial-card record. She died in 1974, nearly thirty years after him, and the card still\nnames him — which is how a widow's card usually reads, and it confirms the marriage from a\nsource outside the trees.\n\nFOUR MORE CHILDREN GRAFTED (research-log §64), from a sweep of the vrijwilligersrab\nHuwelijken index (`rab-bs-huwelijken`): [[vaniseghem_flavie_1898]] (m. Stene 1920), [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1901]]\n(m. Oostende 1927), [[vaniseghem_valentina_1909]] (m. Stene 1931) and [[vaniseghem_maria_1913]] (m. Stene 1935) —\neach act naming both parents identically to this record, alongside [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]] himself,\nwhose own 1928 marriage act turned up in the same sweep (see his record). None of the four\nacts gives a birth date, so none is recorded on these children. Three in-laws named only\nby the act — Desire Camille Gunst, Petrus Theodorus Carolus Joye, Joseph Louis Zwaenepoel\n— are left for a later pass rather than entered as records now.\n\n**BIRTH PLACE AND OWN CITATION SUPPLIED (2026-07-27).** His own birth row — Oostende, act\nnr. 763, RAB ID 1486308, FamilySearch waypoint QZ9J-GG1 — reads Birth Date 29/11/1880\n(the Birth Date column itself, not the Certificate Date, which is blank on this row),\nmatching this record to the day and giving `birth.place` for the first time. It is one of\neight rows this couple has in this index — see [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] for the full sibship and\nthe parent-pair identifier that grounds all eight, six new siblings ([[vaniseghem_arthur_1874]],\n[[vaniseghem_augustus_1875]], [[vaniseghem_leontius]], [[vaniseghem_gustavus_1878]], [[vaniseghem_joannes_1883]], [[vaniseghem_ludovicus_1888]],\n[[vaniseghem_joannes_1891]]) now on file.\n\n**[[vaniseghem_camillus_1905]], already held as a child of this marriage — not a new find —\nnow also has a death act on his own record (2026-07-27); see that record.**\n\n**HIS OWN MARRIAGE ACT READ AS A REGISTER IMAGE (2026-07-27), DOC-GRADE.** The 1907\nOostende act itself ([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]],\n`data/artifacts/vaniseghem-vincke-1907-marriage-oostende.md`) confirms his birth to the\nday (Oostende, 29 November 1880), gives his occupation for the first time as ***werkman***\n(labourer, the new occupation field above), and states he produced his militia\ncertificate. His parents [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] and [[janssen_hermanie_1853]] are both present and\nconsenting and both signed. Banns were published at Oostende on Sunday 8 September 1907;\nthe officer was Ernestus Van Glabbeke, schepen gedelegeerden; and the act carries **no\nmarginal annotation of any kind** — no divorce note, no later correction. This is an\nindependent primary source, 26 years apart from his father's 1933 death act, for the same\n[[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] × [[janssen_hermanie_1853]] parent link.\n\nNEW FRONTIER, NOT LINKED (2026-07-27). The same act names a witness, **Eugenius De Roo**,\n40, *kleermaker*, of Oostende, stated as *\"oom van den echtgenoot\"* — an uncle of the\ngroom — implying a sibling of one of his parents, [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] or [[janssen_hermanie_1853]],\nmarried a De Roo, or a De Roo/Deroo married into one of those families directly. No\nperson record, label or prior search anywhere in this tree mentions \"De Roo\". Not linked;\nrecorded as a named frontier only."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vaniseghem_eduardus_1901","name":"Eduardus Van Iseghem","dates":"b. 2 Nov 1901 Oostende","confidence":"doc","surname":"Van Iseghem","family":"vaniseghem","sex":"m","born":"2 Nov 1901 Oostende","order":"1901-11-02","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vaniseghem_eduardus_1880","mother":"vincke_emma_1880","spouses":[{"id":"gunst_angela","name":"Angela Coralia Gunst","detail":"m. Oostende, 15 Jan 1927"}],"source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; Marriage act nr. 212 — Eduardus Ludovicus Rudolphus Vanyseghem x Emma Celesta Vincke, Oostende, 28 September 1907 (register image)","note":"Son of [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] and [[vincke_emma_1880]], and [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]]'s brother — named for their\nfather. His own marriage act — Oostende nr. 10, 15 January 1927 (vrijwilligersrab\nHuwelijken index, `rab-bs-huwelijken`) — names his parents in full as Eduardus Van Iseghem\nx Emma Celesta Vincke, matching this couple exactly; one of five such acts spanning\n1920-1935 that all converge on the identical parent-name pair. He married **Angela\nCoralia Gunst**. This 1927 act of his own is index only, not a register image. The\nmarriage act does not give his own birth date.\n\n**Birth date (2026-07-27).** A birth-index sweep for rows naming [[vincke_emma_1880]] as mother\nturned up his own row: Oostende act nr. 1469, 2 November 1901 (`rab-bs-geboorten`). That\nreading was not independently re-checked against a second act, and this same index's\n\"Date\"/\"Certificate Date\" columns are confirmed elsewhere in this family to be conflated\n(see `rab-bs-overlijdens`'s note and the corrections on [[vincke_irma_1874]] and\n[[vincke_jerome_1886]]) — recorded with that caveat rather than left out, since the row cites a\nspecific act number.\n\n**THE CAVEAT IS RESOLVED (2026-07-27) — RECORD UPGRADED `sup` → `doc`.** His parents' own\n1907 marriage act, read as a register image\n([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]],\n`data/artifacts/vaniseghem-vincke-1907-marriage-oostende.md`), carries a legitimation\nclause naming him directly: \"voor hunne wettige zoons: Eduardus Vanyseghem, geboren te\nOostende den tweeden November negentien honderd en een\" — 2 November 1901, Oostende,\nexactly the date above. This is a wholly independent doc-grade primary source — a\ndifferent register and clerk from the birth-index row — so the earlier caveat no longer\napplies. It also newly establishes that he was born nearly six years before his parents'\nmarriage and was legitimized by it, the same mechanism as his sister [[vaniseghem_flavie_1898]] and\nbrother [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]], named in the same clause."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vaniseghem_flavie_1898","name":"Flavie Eulalie Van Iseghem","dates":"b. 26 Mar 1898 Diksmuide","confidence":"doc","surname":"Van Iseghem","family":"vaniseghem","sex":"f","born":"26 Mar 1898 Diksmuide","order":"1898-03-26","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vaniseghem_eduardus_1880","mother":"vincke_emma_1880","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; Marriage act nr. 212 — Eduardus Ludovicus Rudolphus Vanyseghem x Emma Celesta Vincke, Oostende, 28 September 1907 (register image)","note":"Daughter of [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] and [[vincke_emma_1880]], and [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]]'s sister. Her own\nmarriage act — Stene nr. 21, 22 May 1920 (vrijwilligersrab Huwelijken index,\n`rab-bs-huwelijken`) — names her parents in full as Eduardus Van Iseghem x Emma Celesta\nVincke, matching this couple exactly; one of five such acts spanning 1920-1935 that all\nconverge on the identical parent-name pair. That reading was index only, not the register\nimage; her parentage from it alone stayed `sup`.\n\nFRONTIER — her husband. The same index names him **Desire Camille Gunst**, but he has no\nrecord of his own here: this pass is naming [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] and [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s children,\nnot their in-laws, so his own record is left for objective 2's next pass rather than\nentered now.\n\nRESOLVED (2026-07-27) — BIRTH DATE AND PLACE SUPPLIED, RECORD UPGRADED `sup` → `doc`. The\nopen frontier below — a birth nine years before her parents' 1907 marriage — is answered\ndirectly by the marriage act's own legitimation clause, read as a register image\n([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]],\n`data/artifacts/vaniseghem-vincke-1907-marriage-oostende.md`): \"voor hunne wettige\ndochter: Flavie-Eulalie Vincke, geboren te Dixmude den zes en twintigsten Maart achttien\nhonderd acht en negentig\" — their legitimate daughter, born Diksmuide 26 March 1898. The\ntie to the birth-index row below is by forename pair, day, month and year and commune —\n**not** by act reference, since the 1907 act cites no birth act number for her. This is a\nlegitimation of a child already born, the same mechanism as [[dekeyser_edouard_1876]]'s marriage\nelsewhere in this tree, not an unrecorded earlier union.\n\nThe birth-index sweep that first found her (incidental to an unrelated 1866-1870\nblind-window pass): \"VINCKE Flavie Eulalie\", b. Diksmuide 26 March 1898 act nr. 21, father\nNN NN, mother VINCKE Emma Celesta — registered under her mother's surname, exactly as the\n1907 act itself also enters her (her two younger brothers are already entered there as\nVanyseghem/Van Yseghem). A second such row, \"VINCKE Albert Joseph\" (b. Diksmuide 9\nDecember 1899 act nr. 84, d. Diksmuide 26 March 1900), is **not** named in the\nlegitimation clause — see [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s record for why that stays unproven and\nunlinked."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vaniseghem_gustavus_1878","name":"Gustavus Leopoldus Van Iseghem","dates":"b. 5 Jan 1878 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Iseghem","family":"vaniseghem","born":"5 Jan 1878 Oostende","order":"1878-01-05","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vaniseghem_joannes_1852","mother":"janssen_hermanie_1853","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] and [[janssen_hermanie_1853]] — one of eight children the vrijwilligersrab\nindexes give this couple; see [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] for the full sibship and the identifier\nthat grounds it.\n\nBorn Oostende, birth act nr. 13, RAB ID 1486318 (Birth Date column). **No second act has\nbeen found for him** — no marriage, no death in this venue's transcribed window — so this\ndate is single-sourced, unlike six of his seven siblings, and is recorded with that\ncaveat rather than upgraded past `sup`. The hypothesis that he is the unnamed infant\n(\"Sn\") who died at Oostende 18/11/1878, ten months after this birth, was tested and\nrejected — see [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]]'s record for the reasoning. See that same record for the\nfour open alternatives on his own fate (death after 1939; death at Stene before 1915;\ndeath outside West-Vlaanderen; or an unmatched name-form)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vaniseghem_joannes_1819","name":"Joannes Josephus Van Iseghem","dates":"19 Mar 1819 Oostende – 6 Nov 1861 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Iseghem","family":"vaniseghem","born":"19 Mar 1819 Oostende","order":"1819-03-19","died":"6 Nov 1861 Oostende","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vaniseghem_judocus_1787","mother":"engelsen_victoria_1791","spouses":[{"id":"gautiert_anna_1819","name":"Anna Maria Gautiert","detail":"m. Oostende, 24 Mar 1847"}],"source":"gverdievel (Guy Verdievel); West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Died young at 42, a year after his wife Anna Maria Gautiert — their son Joannes (1852) was orphaned in childhood.\n\n**RE-CONFIRMED (2026-07-27)** by his son [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]]'s own 1872 marriage act (Oostende,\nact nr. 93, RAB ID 582203), which independently restates his death as 06/11/1861 Oostende\n— an exact match to this record, from a document outside the tree-gverdievel line this\nrecord otherwise rests on alone."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vaniseghem_joannes_1852","name":"Joannes Van Iseghem","dates":"25 Sep 1852 Oostende – 13 Nov 1933 Stene","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Iseghem","family":"vaniseghem","born":"25 Sep 1852 Oostende","order":"1852-09-25","died":"13 Nov 1933 Stene","occupation":"herbergier (innkeeper)","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vaniseghem_joannes_1819","mother":"gautiert_anna_1819","spouses":[{"id":"janssen_hermanie_1853","name":"Hermanie Ludovica Janssen","detail":"m. Oostende, 23 Aug 1872"}],"source":"gverdievel (Guy Verdievel); West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; Marriage act nr. 212 — Eduardus Ludovicus Rudolphus Vanyseghem x Emma Celesta Vincke, Oostende, 28 September 1907 (register image)","note":"Lived to 81; born in the city of Oostende but died in neighbouring rural Stene, where the family had settled.\n\n**THE IDENTIFIER FOR THIS WHOLE SIBSHIP (2026-07-27).** \"Joannes Vaniseghem\" is not, by\nitself, a name that picks out one man in this venue: grouping every VANISEGHEM Joannes\nfather row in the province-wide birth index by the named mother turns up **at least nine\ndifferent men recorded identically as \"Joannes Vaniseghem\"**, each paired with a different\nwife — Piesens Sophia, Werbrouck Barbara, Dekegelaere Philippina, Demeyer Maria, Carette\nVirginia, Lycke Isabelle, Vanhaecke Justine/Christina, and this record's own Hermanie\n(Hermania/Hermina) Ludovica Janssen. The father's forename alone is therefore not an\nidentifier here — **the pair, both parents' full names written in full, is the\ntwo-identifier minimum**, and it holds for the eight birth rows below: no row anywhere in\nthe province pairs \"Joannes\" with any mother but Hermania/Hermina Ludovica Janssen.\n\n**HIS OWN MARRIAGE ACT** — Oostende, 23 August 1872, act nr. 93, RAB ID 582203, microfilm\n4794599 — names both spouses in full and gives both their birth dates exactly as already\nheld (groom 25/09/1852, bride 05/07/1853 — see [[janssen_hermanie_1853]]), where previously\nboth rested on the single Geneanet tree `tree-gverdievel` alone. It also names all four\nparents — VANISEGHEM Joannes Josephus x GAUTIERT Anna Maria, and JANSSEN Josephus Joannes\nx HUYGHEBAERT Appolonia Joanna — matching this tree's held [[vaniseghem_joannes_1819]] x\n[[gautiert_anna_1819]] and [[janssen_josephus_1820]] x [[huyghebaert_appolonia_1830]] exactly, and gives\nthe previous generation's own deaths (see those four records), independently\nre-confirming dates a separate pass recorded the same day.\n\n**HIS OWN DEATH ACT** — Stene, 13 November 1933, act nr. 40, RAB ID 2184011 — is the only\nsource in this tree stating the [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] → [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] link **in a civil act's\nown words**: the Detail's own Birth Date field (25/09/1852, Oostende) matches this record\nto the day, and the two comparants are family, each stating their own relation —\n\"VANISEGHEM Eduard, 50, boodschapper, Stene, *zoon*\" and \"VANISEGHEM Joannes, 30,\nwerkman, Stene, *kleinzoon*\". The son is [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] (whose 1901 brother's own\nmarriage act separately gives him the same trade, *boodschapper*); the grandson, aged 30\nin 1933, fits [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]] (b. 11/05/1903) almost exactly — a second, previously\nunclaimed corroboration of the three-generation chain, alongside the stated one. Eduard's\ndeclared age, 50, is stated two years light — he turned 53 sixteen days after this act —\na declarant's rounded age, flagged rather than smoothed over. Widowerhood is stated to\n\"JANSSEN Hermania Ludovica\" in the Previous Partners table, matching [[janssen_hermanie_1853]].\nHis own birth act (Oostende, act nr 763 — see [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]]) is a fourth Van Iseghem\nsibling generation removed and is not this act; both remain index rows, not images, so\nconfidence stays `sup`.\n\n**A THIRD, INDEPENDENT PRIMARY SOURCE FOR THE SAME LINK (2026-07-27), DOC-GRADE.** His son\n[[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]]'s own 1907 marriage act, read as a register image\n([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]],\n`data/artifacts/vaniseghem-vincke-1907-marriage-oostende.md`), names him present and\nconsenting, and gives his occupation for the first time as ***herbergier*** (innkeeper,\nthe new occupation field above). This is 26 years earlier than his own 1933 death act\nabove, and a different register from both it and his birth act — a third, wholly\nindependent primary attestation of the same [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] × [[janssen_hermanie_1853]] →\n[[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] link. This record's own vital dates remain index-only, so confidence stays\n`sup`.\n\n**EIGHT CHILDREN with [[janssen_hermanie_1853]], all from the RAB birth index and cross-filed\nfrom her own record too, so no ninth exists on either side:** [[vaniseghem_arthur_1874]] (17/03/1874),\n[[vaniseghem_augustus_1875]] (13/08/1875, d. in infancy), [[vaniseghem_leontius]] (registered 1876, no birth\ndate recovered), [[vaniseghem_gustavus_1878]] (05/01/1878), [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] (29/11/1880, already held),\n[[vaniseghem_joannes_1883]] (21/03/1883, d. in infancy), [[vaniseghem_ludovicus_1888]] (20/02/1888, d. in\ninfancy) and [[vaniseghem_joannes_1891]] (16/05/1891). Filtering the province-wide index separately\nby father-name and by [[janssen_hermanie_1853]]'s own surname returns the identical eight RAB\nIDs {1486295, 1486298, 1486308, 1486318, 1486324, 1486325, 1486336, 2042291} — no rival\ncouple, no ninth child from either filter. Three further spellings (Vaniseghem, Van\nYseghem, Vaniseghen) were tried against the sibship: \"Vaniseghem\" returned the identical\n1568 rows as \"Van Iseghem\" (byte counts differ only by the echoed search string);\n\"Van Yseghem\" is a genuinely different key (25 rows, none this family); \"Vaniseghen\"\nreturns zero. **Not independently verified**: whether \"Vaniseghem\" and two-word\n\"Van Iseghem\" are byte-for-byte identical could not be checked, because only the\none-word capture was kept in scratch — recorded as unconfirmed, not as proven.\n\n**TWO UNNAMED INFANT DEATHS, NOT GRAFTED — no name, no id, no file (CLAUDE.md rule 5).**\nOostende, 18/11/1878, act nr. 626, RAB ID 264403: Sex M, born Oostende, Christinastraat\n72, no age given; father comparant \"VANISEGHEM Joannes, 26, Werkman … vader\" and mother\n25 — both ages consistent with this couple in 1878. And Oostende, 06/11/1879, act nr.\n570, RAB ID 266409: Detail entirely blank. Both are transcribed with \"Sn\" (no forename)\nin the Deceased field. **\"Sn\" is a name-position code, not a sex marker** — the codes\ncompound (\"VANISEGHEM Sn Vr\", \"DEVLOO Sn Ml\"), so Sn means registered without a forename\nand Ml/Vr (manlijk/vrouwelijk) carry the sex separately; the venue's own Vocabularium does\nnot define the code, this is read off the corpus itself. Of 71 such rows scanned\nprovince-wide across the Van Iseghem and Janssen result sets, only **33 reproduce** on a\nsecond read; the other 38 could not be reproduced and are not claimed. Not one of the 33\nnames a Partner and most name both parents — the signature of a newborn registration, not\nan adult's. Recorded as **\"unnamed child\"**, not \"stillborn\": the death Detail form has no\n\"Stillborn\" field at all (only the birth form does), so that distinction needs the\nregister image, not this index. The hypothesis that the 1878 row is [[vaniseghem_gustavus_1878]] dying\nat ten months is **rejected**: every other child of this couple who died after being\nnamed appears in this index *under that name* (see [[vaniseghem_augustus_1875]], [[vaniseghem_joannes_1883]],\n[[vaniseghem_ludovicus_1888]] below), so the venue's own demonstrated convention is that a named child\nis transcribed by name — \"Sn\" is consistent only with a child never named.\n\n**TWO STILL OPEN — [[vaniseghem_leontius]] and [[vaniseghem_gustavus_1878]] have no death and no marriage in\nthis venue.** Scope actually covered: Oostende deaths 1800–1939; Stene carries only 2 rows\nfor this surname in the whole file (1933, 1936), too thin to confirm or refute a death\nthere before 1915; marriages 1872–1936; both parent-side filters run each time. Four\nalternatives remain open, none closed: death after 1939; death at Stene before 1915;\ndeath outside West-Vlaanderen entirely — this family demonstrably moved, since\n[[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]]'s son [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]] was born at Lens, France; or an unmatched name-form.\n\n**\"No unrecorded daughter\" is narrowed, not established.** \"Hermania Ludovica\" appears\nexactly 5 times in the province-wide marriage file — once as a bride, four times as\n\"Mother of the Groom\", never as \"Mother of the Bride\". That is a real finding, but it\noverreaches to call it a closed enumeration: this couple is shown above to have had at\nleast one child (perhaps two) die before ever being named — exactly what a marriage\nsweep cannot catch. Recorded as **\"no unrecorded daughter who lived to marry within this\nvenue's window\"**, not as \"ruled out\".\n\n**A curiosity, explicitly weightless.** [[janssen_hermanie_1853]] died 13/11/1926 and this\nrecord 13/11/1933 — seven years to the day. A frequency check across all 1,521 dated rows\nin the relevant result sets shows 13/11 occurring 7 times, in line with the base rate for\nother day/month pairs (9–12 occurrences each). Genuine, but not evidence of anything —\nrecorded so a later pass does not mistake coincidence for a fact."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vaniseghem_joannes_1883","name":"Joannes Arthur Eduardus Van Iseghem","dates":"21 Mar 1883 Oostende – 4 Sep 1883 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Iseghem","family":"vaniseghem","sex":"m","born":"21 Mar 1883 Oostende","order":"1883-03-21","died":"4 Sep 1883 Oostende","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vaniseghem_joannes_1852","mother":"janssen_hermanie_1853","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] and [[janssen_hermanie_1853]] — one of eight children the vrijwilligersrab\nindexes give this couple; see [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] for the full sibship and the identifier\nthat grounds it. Not to be confused with two other sons of this couple also named\nJoannes: [[vaniseghem_joannes_1891]] (his younger brother) and their father [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] himself.\n\nDied in infancy. Born Oostende, birth act nr. 232, RAB ID 1486324 (Birth Date column).\nDied Oostende, act nr. 429, RAB ID 267970, Sex M — the death act's own Detail Birth Date\nfield independently restates 21/03/1883, an exact match to the birth act and a second,\nindependent identifier beyond the parent pair. Both Date and Certificate Date columns\nagree on the death act (04/09/1883)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vaniseghem_joannes_1891","name":"Joannes Arthur Leopoldus Van Iseghem","dates":"b. 16 May 1891 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Iseghem","family":"vaniseghem","sex":"m","born":"16 May 1891 Oostende","order":"1891-05-16","occupation":"barbier (barber)","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vaniseghem_joannes_1852","mother":"janssen_hermanie_1853","spouses":[{"name":"Bertha Martha Coenye","detail":"m. Oostende, 29 Nov 1911"}],"source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] and [[janssen_hermanie_1853]] — one of eight children the vrijwilligersrab\nindexes give this couple; see [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] for the full sibship and the identifier\nthat grounds it. Not to be confused with his elder brother [[vaniseghem_joannes_1883]] or their\nfather [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]], also both named Joannes.\n\nBorn Oostende, birth act nr. 415, RAB ID 1486325 (Birth Date column). His own marriage\nact — Oostende, 29 November 1911, act nr. 293, RAB ID 666909 — independently restates\nhis birth as 16/05/1891 Oostende, an exact match and a second identifier beyond the\nparent pair; he is recorded there as *barbier*, *ongehuwd*. Married Bertha Martha Coenye\n(b. 30/07/1890 Oostende, d/o Leopoldus Franciscus Coenye, *visser*, x Helena Coleta\nVanderheyde — not a record here). Index rows throughout, no register image read, so\nconfidence stays `sup`."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vaniseghem_joannes_1903","name":"Joannes Van Iseghem","dates":"11 May 1903 Lens (Fr) – 5 May 1969 Oostende","confidence":"doc","surname":"Van Iseghem","family":"vaniseghem","born":"11 May 1903 Lens (Fr)","order":"1903-05-11","died":"5 May 1969 Oostende","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vaniseghem_eduardus_1880","mother":"vincke_emma_1880","spouses":[{"id":"devriendt_adrienne_1908","name":"Adrienne Margaretha Devriendt","detail":"m. Stene, 24 Mar 1928"}],"source":"Memorial card — Joannes Vaniseghem, d. Oostende 5 May 1969; bartvanhooren (Bart Vanhooren); gverdievel (Guy Verdievel); West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; Marriage act nr. 212 — Eduardus Ludovicus Rudolphus Vanyseghem x Emma Celesta Vincke, Oostende, 28 September 1907 (register image)","note":"Born in the French coal-mining town of Lens, where his Oostende family had emigrated for work; the family later returned to Belgium. Died six days short of his 66th birthday.\n\nCORROBORATED (July 2026) by a Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust memorial-card record:\nborn **Lens** 11 May 1903, died Oostende 5 May 1969, partner Adrienne Devriendt. The\nbirthplace is the striking part — an Oostende family with a son born at Lens — and the\ncard gives it independently of the trees, which is the strongest single reason to believe\nthis is the same man. This record notes Lens as being in France; the card says only\n\"Lens\" — which Lens was not settled by the card, but is settled below by his parents' own\n1907 marriage act.\n\nMARRIAGE DATED (2026-07-27): his own marriage act — Stene nr. 6, 24 March 1928\n(vrijwilligersrab Huwelijken index, `rab-bs-huwelijken`) — names his parents in full as\nEduardus Van Iseghem × Emma Celesta Vincke, matching this tree's existing\n[[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] × [[vincke_emma_1880]] exactly, and the bride's parents as Devriendt Eugenius\nAlphonsius × Schalandryn Octavia Maria, matching [[devriendt_eugenius_1882]] × [[schalandrijn_octavia_1886]]\nexactly. Both couples were already held in this tree as his and Adrienne's parents; this\nact corroborates an already-fully-linked marriage and supplies the date and place that\nwere previously missing from both records, not a new tree collapse.\n\nFRONTIER — an unexplained gap of over four years. His held birth, 11 May 1903 at Lens,\nprecedes his parents' held marriage, 28 September 1907, by more than four years. Either\nan earlier, unregistered union or a later legitimation would explain it — this tree\nalready carries the second pattern elsewhere (see [[dekeyser_edouard_1876]]'s marriage to Louise\nBocklandt, which legitimized two children already born). Left open; neither date is\naltered here.\n\n**A second data point for the same pattern (2026-07-27).** A birth-index sweep for rows\nnaming [[vincke_emma_1880]] as mother, incidental to an unrelated blind-window pass, turned up\ntwo more births registered to her alone before the 1907 marriage, father NN NN: \"VINCKE\nFlavie Eulalie\" (b. 1898, matching [[vaniseghem_flavie_1898]]'s rare forename pair) and \"VINCKE Albert\nJoseph\" (b. 1899, d. 1900). If either was legitimized by the 1907 marriage, that would be\nthe same mechanism that would explain this record's own Lens-1903 gap. **NOT PROVEN,\nnot grafted** — it needs the marriage act's own legitimation field read (see\n[[vaniseghem_flavie_1898]]'s record for the exact query handle). Recorded here as the same open\nquestion, not resolved by it.\n\n**A third data point (2026-07-27).** [[vaniseghem_camillus_1905]]'s own death act (Oostende,\n29/11/1905) records both his parents as \"Ongehuwd\", aged 25 — i.e. still unmarried in\nlate 1905, two years before their actual wedding. This independently dates the\nrelationship to at least 1905, sitting between the 1898/1899 Vincke-surnamed births above\nand this record's own 1903 Lens birth. It strengthens the pattern without proving the\nlegitimation hypothesis: the marriage act's own legitimation field still has not been\nread.\n\n**RESOLVED (2026-07-27) — RECORD UPGRADED `sup` → `doc`.** The parents' own 1907 marriage\nact, read as a register image ([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]],\n`data/artifacts/vaniseghem-vincke-1907-marriage-oostende.md`), carries a legitimation\nclause naming him directly: \"en Joannes Van Yseghem, geboren te Lens, in Frankryk, den\nelfden Mei negentien honderd en drie\" — 11 May 1903, **Lens, in France**, in the\nregister's own words. This settles both open questions on this record at once: which Lens\n(the act states it explicitly), and the four-year gap before the parents' marriage — this\nis a **legitimation of a child already born**, the same mechanism as [[dekeyser_edouard_1876]]'s\nmarriage elsewhere in this tree, not an unrecorded earlier union. His siblings\n[[vaniseghem_flavie_1898]] and [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1901]] are named in the identical clause on the identical\nterms; see their records.\n\n**A CHILD NOT IN THE TREE, NOT GRAFTED (2026-07-27).** A death-index sweep turned up \"VAN\nISEGHEM Roger Bernard\", Stene, 27/02/1929, act nr. 10, RAB ID 2148819 — father \"VAN\nISEGHEM Joannes\", mother \"DEVRIENDT Adrienne Margaretha\", both written in full, matching\nthis couple exactly and sitting eleven months after their 24/03/1928 marriage. Two\nidentifiers (both parents' full names) are present, but **no Detail view was fetched for\nthis row** — no sex, no birth date, no age — so nothing beyond his existence and\nparentage can be stated, and no record is created. What would settle it: the Detail page,\nGET `/en/node/172` on RAB ID 2148819. He would predate [[vaniseghem_rosette]], [[vaniseghem_diane]] and\n[[vaniseghem_edi]] if confirmed."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vaniseghem_judocus_1787","name":"Judocus Franciscus Van Iseghem","dates":"19 Nov 1787 Oostende – 19 Apr 1832 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Iseghem","family":"vaniseghem","born":"19 Nov 1787 Oostende","order":"1787-11-19","died":"19 Apr 1832 Oostende","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"engelsen_victoria_1791","name":"Victoria Eugenia Engelsen","detail":"m. Oostende, 25 Mar 1810"}],"source":"gverdievel (Guy Verdievel)","note":"Married during the French Imperial period, when Oostende was annexed to France; died at 44.\n\nCHECKED AND REJECTED (July 2026). The corpus's best candidate for this record scores 33\nbits and is not him: an **Aalst** death act of 11 March 1869 for Josephus Hippolytus Van\nIseghem, whose father is *Constantinus Franciscus* Van Iseghem.\n\nThree things kill it. Our Judocus died at Oostende in **1832**, so he cannot be a named\nfather in an 1869 act. The forename is Constantinus Franciscus, not Judocus Franciscus —\nthe *Franciscus* they share is the commonest middle name in these registers. And Aalst is\nin Oost-Vlaanderen, sixty miles from the Oostende family this record belongs to.\n\nWhat produced the score was the surname plus that shared *Franciscus* plus a child's name.\nVan Iseghem is not rare enough in Oost-Vlaanderen for that to mean anything. Left ungrafted\nand uncited."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vaniseghem_leontius","name":"Leontius Josephus Van Iseghem","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Iseghem","family":"vaniseghem","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vaniseghem_joannes_1852","mother":"janssen_hermanie_1853","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] and [[janssen_hermanie_1853]] — one of eight children the vrijwilligersrab\nindexes give this couple; see [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] for the full sibship and the identifier\nthat grounds it. He sits chronologically between siblings born August 1875 and January\n1878.\n\nRegistered at Oostende, act nr. 541, RAB ID 2042291, microfilm 4794210 — both parents\nnamed in full. **No birth date is recorded.** The row's Birth Date column is empty; only\na Certificate Date of 24/10/1876 is given, and this venue's registration lag is not known\nto run same-day (a lone Certificate Date has been shown elsewhere in this family, and in\nthis same pass, to be a declaration date rather than the birth), so not even a\n\"born before 24/10/1876\" bound is recorded here — only that his birth was registered on\nor shortly before that date. Born Oostende (the place is on the row; the date is not).\n\nNo death and no marriage act for him has been found in this venue — see [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]]'s\nrecord for the four open alternatives that apply equally to [[vaniseghem_gustavus_1878]]."});
