FamilyTree.person({"id":"vannieuwenhuyse_petrus_1649","name":"Petrus Van Nieuwenhuyse","dates":"7 Mar 1649 Oostkamp – 1701","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Nieuwenhuyse","family":"vannieuwenhuyse","born":"7 Mar 1649 Oostkamp","order":"1649-03-07","died":"1701","occupation":"schepen van Oostkamp (alderman)","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"vannieuwenhuyse_marinus_1620","mother":"govaert_cornelia_1625","spouses":[{"id":"monballiu_jacoba_1651","name":"Jacoba Monballiu","detail":"m. Oostkamp, 23 Jul 1673"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links; Oostkamp Sint-Pietersbanden parish register: baptisms 26 Jun 1630 - 14 Apr 1652 (and marriages 9 Aug 1631 - 14 Apr 1652), AGATHA digitised item 513_9000_000_00774","note":"Source detail: Geneanet isavdw; birth act agatha.arch.be scan 513_9000_000_00774 (Sosa 3382)\n\nFather of Anna Van Nieuwenhuyse (1676). Served as a schepen (alderman/magistrate) of Oostkamp. Parents Marinus Van Nieuwenhuyse (~1620-1666) x Cornelia Govaert (~1625-1653).\n\nTHE REFERENCE IS REAL, BUT STILL NOT `doc` (2026-07-26). §52 downgraded this record because\nthe \"scan 513_9000_000_00774\" citation could not be checked against anything real. It now\ncan be: `/nl/search/genealogie/35229` on AGATHA resolves to exactly that item —\n[[agatha-oostkamp-doopregister-1630-1652]], the **Oostkamp Sint-Pietersbanden parish\nregister, Doopakten 26 June 1630 – 14 April 1652** — and a 7 March 1649 baptism falls\ninside its span. That does not restore `doc`, for three reasons: (1) the reference names a\n**volume**, not a page or an act — it says where to look, not what was read; (2) the images\nrequire an AGATHA login this project's browser session does not have — logged **blocked**,\nnot **miss**; and (3) it is a register of **baptisms**, so a date read there would be a\nbaptism date, and this record's `birth: 1649-03-07` field would need relabelling, not just\nsourcing.\n\nTHREE NAMED FRONTIERS, from the same pass. First, his **1673 marriage** is mapped the same\nway: `/nl/search/genealogie/35236` = AGATHA item 513_9000_000_00777, from scan 0_0660,\ncovering 5 July 1673 – 30 April 1702 — the volume holding his 23 July 1673 wedding to\n[[monballiu_jacoba_1651]]. Second, the **Oostkamp baptisms of 1652–1673** — which would carry\nhis siblings and his own earliest children — are marked by AGATHA itself as *\"Niet\nbeschikbaar — hiaten in de originele registers en op de microfilms\"* (not available — gaps\nin the original registers and on the microfilms): a hole in the source, not in the search.\nThird, **Begrafenisakten Oostkamp 1662** lists a *Marinus Van Nieuwenhuyse* as *\"Partner van\nde overledene\"* — which does not sit with this tree's own ~1653 death for\n[[govaert_cornelia_1625]], his mother. No act id has been read for that entry, so it stays a\nfrontier rather than a correction: it may be a second Marinus, a mis-transcribed date, or a\nreal conflict with her death year."});
