FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanstechelman_andreas_1698","name":"Andreas Andries Vanstechelman","dates":"1 Mar 1698 Woumen – before 1748","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vanstechelman","family":"vanstechelman","born":"1 Mar 1698 Woumen","order":"1698-03-01","died":"before 1748","line":"vanstechelman","father":"vanstechelman_andreas_1667","mother":"pluvier_elisabeth","spouses":[{"id":"boxoens_maria","name":"Maria Anna Theresia Boxoens"}],"source":"stechec (Christian Vanstechelman)","note":"Of Woumen; eight children including Silvester (1740)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanstechelman_augusta_1882","name":"Augusta Vanstechelman","dates":"14 Mar 1882 Mariakerke – 4 Oct 1922 Mariakerke","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vanstechelman","family":"vanstechelman","born":"14 Mar 1882 Mariakerke","order":"1882-03-14","died":"4 Oct 1922 Mariakerke","line":"vanstechelman","father":"vanstechelman_petrus_1854","mother":"wagebaert_clementia_1853","spouses":[{"id":"bundervoet_petrus_1879","name":"Petrus Bundervoet"}],"source":"België, West-Vlaanderen, burgerlijke stand, 1582-1950; Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust memorial card — Augusta Vanstechelman, d. Mariakerke 4 Oct 1922; stechec (Christian Vanstechelman)","note":"One of fifteen siblings; her marriage to Petrus Bundervoet is the Vanstechelman–Bundervoet junction.\n\nCORROBORATED (July 2026). A Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust memorial-card record\ngives birth 14 March 1882 at Mariakerke, death 4 October 1922 at Mariakerke, and spouse\nPetrus Bundervoet — every field as held here, where before this rested on the stechec\ntree alone. Found by harvesting the surname from Open Archives, not by searching for her.\n\nStays `sup`: an index transcription of a card, not an image read.\n\nCORROBORATED FROM CIVIL REGISTRATION (July 2026), not only from a memorial card. Her\nparents [[vanstechelman_petrus_1854]] and [[wagebaert_clementia_1853]] appear together as the parents on three of\nher siblings' Oostende acts ([[fs-wvl-bs]]) — a couple attested repeatedly in the registers\nrather than asserted once by a tree.\n\nThree of her siblings surface in West-Flemish civil registration, each in an act naming\nboth parents — which is what corroborates the parentage:\n\n- **Henricus Emilius Vanstechelman**, b. 1877, died Oostende 17 January 1941, married\n  Alicia Mathildis St Martin;\n- **Leontius Ivo Vanstechelman**, married at Oostende 20 August 1922 to Lucia Amelia Maene;\n- **Paula Mathilde Vanstechelman**, married at Oostende 11 May 1924 to Alberic Luciaan Delrue.\n\nAll three now have records — [[vanstechelman_henricus_1877]], [[vanstechelman_leontius]] and [[vanstechelman_paula]] — at `sup`,\nciting the acts that name them. They were briefly left as a frontier on the grounds that no\nimage had been read, which was the wrong test: adding a person a document names as somebody's\nchild is transcription, not identification, and the rule about two independent identifiers\nguards the second thing. A civil act naming both parents is stronger evidence than the member\ntrees several people here were added from.\n\nHow they were found is worth recording: searching the mother's surname. Vanstechelman is\ncommon at Oostende, Wagebaert is not, so querying the rare maternal name isolates this one\nhousehold out of the parish."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanstechelman_felix_1800","name":"Felix Guillielmus Vanstechelman","dates":"13 Feb 1800 Zevekote – 9 Nov 1869 Mariakerke","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vanstechelman","family":"vanstechelman","born":"13 Feb 1800 Zevekote","order":"1800-02-13","died":"9 Nov 1869 Mariakerke","occupation":"herbergier (innkeeper)","line":"vanstechelman","father":"vanstechelman_pieter_1770","mother":"vanhille_carolina_1773","spouses":[{"id":"vandenbroucke_sophia_1815","name":"Sophia Van den Broucke","detail":"m. Mariakerke, 19 Dec 1844"}],"source":"stechec (Christian Vanstechelman)","note":"An innkeeper who moved the family from inland Zevekote to the coastal village of Mariakerke, near Oostende. Our line is via his 2nd wife, Sophia Van den Broucke."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanstechelman_henricus_1877","name":"Henricus Emilius Vanstechelman","dates":"1877 – 17 Jan 1941 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vanstechelman","family":"vanstechelman","sex":"m","born":"1877","order":"1877","died":"17 Jan 1941 Oostende","line":"vanstechelman","father":"vanstechelman_petrus_1854","mother":"wagebaert_clementia_1853","spouses":[{"id":"stmartin_alicia","name":"Alicia Mathildis St Martin"}],"source":"België, West-Vlaanderen, burgerlijke stand, 1582-1950","note":"Elder brother of [[vanstechelman_augusta_1882]], and so a brother-in-law of Petrus Franciscus Bundervoet.\n\nFrom his own Oostende death registration of 17 January 1941, which names his parents as\nPetrus Jacobus and Clemencia Sophia Wagebaert and his wife as Alicia Mathildis St Martin.\nThe birth year of 1877 is the one the death act implies rather than a stated date, so it is\nrecorded as a bare year.\n\nThe act is an index entry and has not been read as an image, which is why this stays `sup`.\nHis wife has no record of her own yet."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanstechelman_leontius","name":"Leontius Ivo Vanstechelman","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vanstechelman","family":"vanstechelman","sex":"m","line":"vanstechelman","father":"vanstechelman_petrus_1854","mother":"wagebaert_clementia_1853","spouses":[{"id":"maene_lucia","name":"Lucia Amelia Maene","detail":"m. Oostende, 20 Aug 1922"}],"source":"België, West-Vlaanderen, burgerlijke stand, 1582-1950","note":"Brother of [[vanstechelman_augusta_1882]], named in his own Oostende marriage registration of 20 August 1922,\nwhich gives his parents as Petrus Jacobus and Clementia Sophia Wagebaert and his bride as\nLucia Amelia Maene.\n\nNo dates of his own: the marriage act is indexed under the event, not his birth, and nothing\nelse has been read for him. FRONTIER — his birth act at Mariakerke or Oostende would give\nthem, and the marriage act itself, read rather than indexed, would give both spouses' ages\nand his wife's parents."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanstechelman_paula","name":"Paula Mathilde Vanstechelman","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vanstechelman","family":"vanstechelman","sex":"f","line":"vanstechelman","father":"vanstechelman_petrus_1854","mother":"wagebaert_clementia_1853","spouses":[{"id":"delrue_alberic","name":"Alberic Luciaan Delrue","detail":"m. Oostende, 11 May 1924"}],"source":"België, West-Vlaanderen, burgerlijke stand, 1582-1950","note":"Sister of [[vanstechelman_augusta_1882]], named in her own Oostende marriage registration of 11 May 1924, which\ngives her parents as Petrus Jacobus and Clemence Wagebaert — the mother's name shortened\nthere, as it is in several of these acts — and her husband as Alberic Luciaan Delrue.\n\nNo dates of her own yet; the act is indexed under the marriage. FRONTIER: her birth act, and\nthe marriage act read rather than indexed."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanstechelman_petrus_1854","name":"Petrus Jacobus Vanstechelman","dates":"28 Feb 1854 Mariakerke – 26 Nov 1927 Mariakerke","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vanstechelman","family":"vanstechelman","born":"28 Feb 1854 Mariakerke","order":"1854-02-28","died":"26 Nov 1927 Mariakerke","occupation":"metser (mason)","line":"vanstechelman","father":"vanstechelman_felix_1800","mother":"vandenbroucke_sophia_1815","spouses":[{"id":"wagebaert_clementia_1853","name":"Clementia Sophia Wagebaert","detail":"m. Mariakerke, 21 Jan 1875"}],"source":"België, West-Vlaanderen, burgerlijke stand, 1582-1950; stechec (Christian Vanstechelman)","note":"A mason who fathered fifteen children (including Augusta); he and his wife both died in 1927.\n\nCORROBORATED (July 2026): named as the father — *Petrus Jacobus*, sometimes without the\nsurname repeated — on three Oostende civil acts of his children, beside Clementia Sophia\nWagebaert ([[fs-wvl-bs]])."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanstechelman_pieter_1770","name":"Pieter Jacobus Vanstechelman","dates":"12 May 1770 Zevekote – 28 Sep 1827 Zevekote","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vanstechelman","family":"vanstechelman","born":"12 May 1770 Zevekote","order":"1770-05-12","died":"28 Sep 1827 Zevekote","line":"vanstechelman","father":"vanstechelman_silvester_1740","mother":"casteleyn_angela_1741","spouses":[{"id":"vanhille_carolina_1773","name":"Carolina Van Hille"}],"source":"stechec (Christian Vanstechelman)","note":"Of Zevekote; first wife Carolina Van Hille (our line, eight children incl. Felix); remarried Anna Osaer in 1810."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vanstechelman_silvester_1740","name":"Silvester Engelbertus Vanstechelman","dates":"21 Jan 1740 Woumen – 22 Oct 1809 Zevekote","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vanstechelman","family":"vanstechelman","born":"21 Jan 1740 Woumen","order":"1740-01-21","died":"22 Oct 1809 Zevekote","line":"vanstechelman","father":"vanstechelman_andreas_1698","mother":"boxoens_maria","spouses":[{"id":"casteleyn_angela_1741","name":"Angela Jacoba Casteleyn"}],"source":"stechec (Christian Vanstechelman)","note":"Married three times and fathered about fourteen children; the generation that settled the family in Zevekote. Our line runs through his 2nd wife, Angela Casteleyn."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vantyghem_nn","name":"NN Vantyghem","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vantyghem","family":"vantyghem","sex":"f","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"huyghebaert_augustinus_1824","name":"Augustinus Desiderius Huyghebaert","detail":"m. Zandvoorde, 23 Nov 1859"}],"source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Wife of [[huyghebaert_augustinus_1824]], married Zandvoorde 23 November 1859, act nr. 62\n(RAB 361339). Only her family name is recorded in the index."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"verbrugghe_joanna_1655","name":"Joanna (Janneken) Verbrugghe","dates":"~1655 – 1704","confidence":"sup","surname":"Verbrugghe","family":"verbrugghe","born":"~1655","order":"1655","died":"1704","line":"bundervoet","father":"verbrugghe_nicolas","spouses":[{"id":"bundervoet_joannes_1637","name":"Joannes Bundervoet"}],"source":"paulderidder; glorieuxp","note":"Mother of Joannes Bundervoet (~1682).\n\nCORRECTED (July 2026): this record said \"her own parents not recorded here\". They are —\nthe paulderidder ancestry chart names her father as Nicolas Verbrugghe, now linked. Her\nmother is shown there only as \"?\", so that side is still open.\n\nNote the near-miss: this tree holds another Joanna Verbrugghe, who died at Hontenisse in\n1734, married Petrus van Huffel, and was a daughter of Gerard Verbrugge x Anna de Cock.\nShe is a different woman. A Geneanet URL without an occurrence number lands on her\nfirst, so anyone re-checking this line should follow the link from Joannes Bundervoet's\nprofile rather than searching the name."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"verbrugghe_nicolas","name":"Nicolas Verbrugghe","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Verbrugghe","family":"verbrugghe","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"name":"(wife unrecorded)"}],"source":"paulderidder","note":"Father of Joanna (Janneken) Verbrugghe (~1655–1704), and so a direct ancestor through\nher son Joannes Bundervoet (~1682).\n\nNamed as her father in the paulderidder tree's ancestry chart; the tree gives him no\ndates at all and no wife, which is why this record carries none either. Joanna's\nrecord previously said her parents were \"not recorded here\" — they were, and this\ncorrects that.\n\nFRONTIER: everything about him. Evergem parish registers for a Verbrugghe–? marriage\nin the 1640s–50s would be the first place to look, since a daughter born ~1655 puts\nthe marriage a little before it."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"verelst_joanna","name":"Joanna Theresia Ver Elst","dates":"d. 19 Dec 1843 Zaventem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Ver Elst","family":"verelst","died":"19 Dec 1843 Zaventem","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"peremans_egidius","name":"Egidius Peremans"}],"source":"Zaventem marriage act nr. 1, 24 February 1846 — Bossin × Peremans; Marriage act — Joannes Baptista Peremans x Joanna Catharina Van Gindertaelen, Zaventem, 21 August 1848","note":"Mother of the bride in her daughter [[peremans_joanna_1824]]'s marriage act — Zaventem, act nr. 1,\n24 February 1846 (S19), read as an image. She was dead by then, at Zaventem on 19 December\n1843, six years after her husband [[peremans_egidius]] and barely two years before her\ndaughter married.\n\nThe act gives her no age and no occupation, so this record has neither.\n\nThe surname is written *Ver Elst* on the act, in two words. Verelst and Van Elst are the\nusual Brabant forms, and her own acts will show which the family wrote.\n\nFRONTIER — her 1843 Zaventem death act, which should give her age and her parents. Note\nthat her daughter declared to the 1846 act, with her witnesses, that she had never known\nher grandparents nor where they died: this generation was not reachable through the\nfamily's own memory in 1846, and it will have to come from the registers.\n\nDOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.\nNothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the\nevidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own\nDemogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or\nits image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step.\n\nCORROBORATED (2026-07-27): a fifth child, [[peremans_joannes_1820]], names her again as his\nmother in his own 1848 Zaventem marriage act (S34) — dead, at Zaventem, on **19 December\n1843**, an exact day-level match to the date held here since S19. The two transcriptions\nare of two different registers, drawn 2.5 years apart, so an identical day-level date\nrepeated across both is strong corroboration rather than coincidence. This is also what\nanchors [[peremans_joannes_1820]] as her son: see his own record for the reasoning."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"verkouille_cornelia_1836","name":"Cornelia Coleta Verkouille","dates":"11 Oct 1836 Oostende – 6 Apr 1910 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Verkouille","family":"verkouille","born":"11 Oct 1836 Oostende","order":"1836-10-11","died":"6 Apr 1910 Oostende","occupation":"werkster (charwoman)","line":"devriendt","father":"verkouille_livinus","mother":"malfait_maria","spouses":[{"id":"ramon_carolus_1835","name":"Carolus Ludovicus Ramon","detail":"m. Oostende, 14 Sep 1859"}],"source":"Geneanet","note":"Daughter of Livinus Verkouille & Maria Malfait; widowed in 1883 when her fisherman husband was lost at sea, she outlived him by 27 years."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"verkouille_livinus","name":"Livinus Hermanus Verkouille","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Verkouille","family":"verkouille","line":"devriendt","spouses":[{"id":"malfait_maria","name":"Maria Lodewijka Malfait"}],"source":"wernero (Werner Osaer)"});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vermandel_ida_1825","name":"Ida Vermandel","dates":"1825 Zelzate – 21 Jun 1865 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)","confidence":"doc","surname":"Vermandel","family":"vermandel","born":"1825 Zelzate","order":"1825","died":"21 Jun 1865 Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)","occupation":"arbeidster (labourer)","line":"de-keyser","spouses":[{"id":"vanbergen_joannes_1815","name":"Joannes Franciscus Van Bergen"}],"source":"Death act nr. 123 — Ida Vermandel, Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen), died 21 June 1865 (register image); Marriage act, 18 May 1882, Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen) — Petrus Vermorgen × Paulina Van Den Berghe (register image); wete1998 (Erik Bekaert) — Hamme (O-Vl) specialist; Death act nr. 721 — Maria Louisa Vanbergen, Oostende, 23 November 1888","note":"Maternal grandmother of Louise Bocklandt; wife of Joannes Franciscus Van Bergen.\n\nACT READ (2026-07-26) — **Hamme death act nr. 123, 1865**, read as the register image. She\nhad been in this tree with a bare year at each end and no place at all. The act gives:\n\n> …dat gisteren, den een en twintigsten Juny, om half negen uren 's avonds, **Ida\n> Vermandel**, oud negen en dertig jaren, *arbeidster*, **geboortig van Zeltzaete**,\n> wonende te Hamme, **huisvrouw van Joannes Franciscus Van Bergen**, dochter van nog\n> levende […] Vermandel en van […] Verplancken, overleden is in het burgerhospitael…\n\nShe died on **21 June 1865** at Hamme, in the town hospital on the Marktplein, aged\nthirty-nine and working as a labourer. Two identifiers carry the identification and neither\nis her name: the commune, which [[vanbergen_marielouise_1842]]'s 1888 Oostende death act independently\ngives as where Ida died, and her husband's full name, matching [[vanbergen_joannes_1815]] exactly.\n*Ida Vermandel* is in any case close to unique — the only other in the whole Open Archives\nindex is a 1949 death in France.\n\n**Her birthplace is Zelzate, not Waasmunster**, and that needs stating carefully, because\n§56 had just moved this family's assumed origin from Hamme to Waasmunster on her daughter's\nevidence. Both are true and they are two different people: Marie-Louise was born at\nWaasmunster in 1842, Ida at Zelzate around 1825. Zelzate is not in the Waasland at all — it\nis on the Dutch border north of Gent. Her own birth act and her parents are therefore in\nthe **Zelzate** registers, and the marriage could be in any of three communes.\n\nHer age, thirty-nine in June 1865, puts her birth between June 1825 and June 1826. The held\n`1825` survives that without being confirmed by it, so the year stays as it was.\n\nFRONTIER — **her parents are named in this act and are deliberately not recorded.** It says\nthey were *nog levende*, still living, in June 1865, which is itself a search constraint.\nBut the forenames do not survive magnification: the father's is a looped capital followed\nby *-rimus*, where P, F and S are all plausible against the same clerk's *Petrus* and\n*Franciscus* elsewhere on the page, and the mother's renders as something between\n*Josephina* and *Delphina*. The surnames are legible — **Vermandel** and **Verplancken**.\nA forename read at the edge of legibility is exactly the guess this project has no syntax\nfor, so nothing is written. Her Zelzate birth act settles both, and the Zelzate registers\nare mapped: `fs-zelzate-civil-registers-1796-1870`, with a ten-year table covering\n1802–1870 (DGS 005089047) that turns it into a single lookup.\n\nFRONTIER — two more probable children, index-level only and not grafted: **Josephus**\n(b. 1852, m. Clementina Van Buyten at Hamme 1911, d. Hamme 27 October 1927) and **Henricus**\n(b. 1861, d. Hamme 2 May 1919), both indexed with this mother and a father *Franciscus*.\nTheir own acts have not been read. [[vandenberghe_paulina_1849]] stood in exactly that position until\nher 1882 act was opened, which is the argument for opening theirs."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vermeeren_maria_1787","name":"Maria Theresia Vermeeren","dates":"~1787 Assenede – 30 Mar 1814 Hontenisse","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vermeeren","family":"vermeeren","sex":"f","born":"~1787 Assenede","order":"1787","died":"30 Mar 1814 Hontenisse","line":"bundervoet","father":"vermeire_carolus","mother":"bundervoet_petronella_1754","spouses":[{"id":"steijaert_livinus","name":"Livinus Bernardus Steijaert"}],"source":"Hontenisse death act nr. 31, 30 March 1814 — Maria Theresia Vermeeren","note":"Granddaughter of [[bundervoet_petrus_1727]] through her mother\n[[bundervoet_petronella_1754]], and so a blood relative of Renée and Léon under\nobjective 2 — the furthest this branch is yet documented across the Dutch border.\n\nHer death act at Hontenisse, in Zeeuws-Vlaanderen, on **30 March 1814** gives her age as\n27 and her birthplace as **Assenede**, names her parents as Karel Vermeeren and Petronella\nBundervoet, and gives her husband [[steijaert_livinus]], a *veldwachter* — a village\nconstable — also aged 27.\n\n**The birth year is derived from a stated age, so it is approximate.** \"27 jaar\" in March\n1814 puts her birth in 1786 or 1787 and the record says `~1787` rather than picking one.\nHer parents married at Assenede in 1781, which is consistent and is the second identifier\nthat ties this act to that couple rather than to another Petronella Bundervoet.\n\nThe act has a scan at the Zeeuws Archief that has not been read; it would give the day of\nher birth or at least the exact age, and where the couple were living."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vermeersch_margaretha","name":"Margaretha Vermeersch","dates":"d. 1645","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vermeersch","family":"vermeersch","died":"1645","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"id":"willems_laurentius","name":"Laurentius Willems","detail":"m. Wingene, 18 Oct 1612"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"FRONTIER above — grandmother of Joannes Van Maele."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vermeire_carolus","name":"Carolus Vermeire","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vermeire","family":"vermeire","sex":"m","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"bundervoet_petronella_1754","name":"Petronella Bundervoet","detail":"m. Assenede, 1781"}],"source":"Assenede marriage 1781 — Carolus Vermeire × Petronella Bundervoet; Hontenisse death act nr. 31, 30 March 1814 — Maria Theresia Vermeeren","note":"Married [[bundervoet_petronella_1754]] at Assenede in 1781. Their daughter\n[[vermeeren_maria_1787]] died across the border at Hontenisse in 1814.\n\n**His surname is written two ways by the two sources that name him** — *Vermeire* in the\nAssenede marriage index, *Vermeeren* in the Dutch death act of 1814, where he appears as\n\"Karel Vermeeren\". The Flemish form is kept here because that is what the register of his\nown marriage gives; the Dutch act is a clerk in another country writing down a name\nreported to him. Neither is corrected into the other and no third form is invented.\n\nNothing else is stated about him: no birth, no death, no trade. The Assenede marriage act\nwould give his age and his parents."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vermorgen_petrus","name":"Petrus Vermorgen","dates":"","confidence":"doc","surname":"Vermorgen","family":"vermorgen","line":"de-keyser","spouses":[{"id":"vandenberghe_paulina_1849","name":"Paulina Van Den Berghe","detail":"m. Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen), 18 May 1882"}],"source":"Marriage act, 18 May 1882, Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen) — Petrus Vermorgen × Paulina Van Den Berghe (register image)","note":"Married [[vandenberghe_paulina_1849]] at Hamme on 18 May 1882. He is here because she is: the act\nthat made her a graftable daughter of [[vanbergen_joannes_1815]] and [[vermandel_ida_1825]] is his\nmarriage act too, and a person named in this tree gets a record rather than living as a\nstring in someone else's prose.\n\nNothing else about him is recorded, because the pass that read this act was reading the\nbride's half of it. His age, his trade, his birthplace and his parents are all on the same\nimage and simply have not been transcribed yet.\n\nFRONTIER — the rest of this act. It is `fs-hamme-1882-marriage-vermorgen-vandenberghe`,\nFamilySearch film 004833291 item 1, image 249, and re-reading the groom's half would fill\nthis record in one visit and probably add his parents as well."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"verniers_petronella_1661","name":"Petronella Verniers","dates":"26 Sep 1661 Destelbergen – 16 Feb 1709 Destelbergen","confidence":"sup","surname":"Verniers","family":"verniers","born":"26 Sep 1661 Destelbergen","order":"1661-09-26","died":"16 Feb 1709 Destelbergen","line":"paelinck","spouses":[{"id":"paelinck_ludovicus_1660","name":"Ludovicus Paelinck","detail":"m. Lochristi, Feb 1681"}],"source":"stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck)","note":"Lived her whole documented life in Destelbergen; wife of Ludovicus Paelinck and mother of Adrianus (1690)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"verstraeten_ludovicus","name":"Ludovicus Verstraeten","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Verstraeten","family":"verstraeten","sex":"m","occupation":"landbouwer (farmer)","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"torfs_rosalia","name":"Rosalia Torfs"}],"source":"Civil marriage acts for the Bossin/Swaelens/Vrebos family of Kraainem, 1884-1901 (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Named as father of the bride in his daughter [[verstraeten_maria_1867]]'s marriage act — Werchter,\n18 January 1896 — *landbouwer*. The act gives him no age and no dates, so this record has\nnone.\n\nFRONTIER: his marriage to [[torfs_rosalia]], which the Werchter registers should hold for\nroughly 1855–1866."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"verstraeten_maria_1867","name":"Maria Catharina Verstraeten","dates":"b. 7 Mar 1867 Werchter","confidence":"sup","surname":"Verstraeten","family":"verstraeten","sex":"f","born":"7 Mar 1867 Werchter","order":"1867-03-07","occupation":"naaister (seamstress)","line":"thumas","father":"verstraeten_ludovicus","mother":"torfs_rosalia","spouses":[{"id":"bossin_joannes_1866","name":"Joannes Franciscus Bossin","detail":"m. Werchter, 18 Jan 1896"}],"source":"Civil marriage acts for the Bossin/Swaelens/Vrebos family of Kraainem, 1884-1901 (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Married [[bossin_joannes_1866]] at **Werchter on 18 January 1896**. Born **Werchter,\n7 March 1867**, a *naaister*. Her parents are named in the act — **Ludovicus\nVerstraeten**, landbouwer, and **Rosalia Torfs**, landbouwster, both of Werchter — see\n[[verstraeten_ludovicus]] and [[torfs_rosalia]].\n\n`sup`: an index-level AGATHA/Demogen act analysis, no register image read.\n\nFRONTIER: her own birth act at Werchter, and any children of this marriage."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vervaeck_antonius","name":"Antonius Joannes Vervaeck","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vervaeck","family":"vervaeck","sex":"m","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"bundervoet_livina_1760","name":"Livina Maria Bundervoet","detail":"m. Assenede, 1788"}],"source":"Assenede marriage 1788 — Antonius Joannes Vervaeck × Livina Maria Bundervoet","note":"Married [[bundervoet_livina_1760]] at Assenede in 1788. She died there in 1831.\n\nHe exists on one line of the Assenede marriage index and nothing more is stated — no\nbirth, no death, no trade, and none of them is guessed. The act itself would give his age\nand his parents, and whether the couple had children, which is the open question: they\nmarried in 1788 and she lived to 1831, so a household of some size should be findable in\nthe Assenede registers under objective 2."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_alfons_1865","name":"Alfons Luciaan Vincke","dates":"b. 13 Sep 1865 Diksmuide","confidence":"doc","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"13 Sep 1865 Diksmuide","order":"1865-09-13","occupation":"ijzersmit (blacksmith)","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_lucien_1840","mother":"vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845","spouses":[{"id":"vandecappelle_eugenia","name":"Eugenia Maria Vandecappelle","detail":"m. Diksmuide, 19 Sep 1888"}],"source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; Memorial card — Alfons Luciaan Vincke, partner Eugenia Maria Vandecappelle; Marriage act nr. 212 — Eduardus Ludovicus Rudolphus Vanyseghem x Emma Celesta Vincke, Oostende, 28 September 1907 (register image)","note":"Son of [[vincke_lucien_1840]] and [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]], and [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s brother — found\none year **outside** the 1866-1870 blind window this pass was sent to close, while\nsweeping the marriage index for the window's children. His own birth, Diksmuide 1865 act\nnr. 202, falls just before it: the couple married 24 May 1865, so this is barely four\nmonths on.\n\nHis marriage — Diksmuide, 19 September 1888, act nr. 149 (`rab-bs-huwelijken`) — gives\nhim born Diksmuide 13 September 1865, age 23, *ijzersmit*, and names his parents in full\nas Vincke Lucianus Julianus (48, metser) × Vanalderweireldt Ludovica Maria (43,\nkantwerkster) — matching this couple exactly and matching birth act nr. 202 to the day.\nIndependently corroborated from the local corpus, not the same register: a Familiekunde\nVlaanderen Westkust memorial card (`fwk-alfons-vincke`,\n`fwk:bb261d5b-e241-84c8-0c3c-860a943cca23`) gives his birth as 13 September 1865 and names\nthe same spouse, Eugenia Vandecappelle.\n\n**Flagged plainly, not smoothed over:** he was born 3 months 20 days after his parents'\n24 May 1865 wedding — conception preceding the marriage by roughly five months, which is\nsometimes the reason for the marriage rather than a contradiction of it. Neither date is\nadjusted.\n\nHis own birth act and 1888 marriage act remain index only, not the register image.\n\n**THE SIBLING LINK ITSELF UPGRADED TO `doc` (2026-07-27).** His sister [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s\nown 1907 marriage act, read as a register image\n([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]],\n`data/artifacts/vaniseghem-vincke-1907-marriage-oostende.md`), carries him as a witness,\nin the register's own words: *\"Alphonsus Vincke, oud twee en veertig jaren, stoofmaker,\nbroeder der echtgenoote\"* — 42 years old, stoofmaker, **brother of the bride**. Two\nidentifiers agree in this one primary image: his stated age matches his held birth date\nto the exact day (he turned 42 fifteen days before the 28 September 1907 act), and the act\n**states the sibling relationship directly**, rather than it being inferred only from the\nseparately-held parent records that grafted him here at `sup` (research-log §67). His\noccupation there, *stoofmaker*, differs from *ijzersmit* on his own 1888 marriage act — a\nplausible 19-year career change, flagged rather than treated as a contradiction. His own\nbirth act is still unread as an image, so only the sibling identification itself carries\n`doc`."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_andre_1901","name":"Andre Jerome Vincke","dates":"b. 3 Jul 1901 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"3 Jul 1901 Diksmuide","order":"1901-07-03","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_alfons_1865","mother":"vandecappelle_eugenia","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vincke_alfons_1865]] and [[vandecappelle_eugenia]] — the last of six children the\ncouple's own birth-index entries surface (Diksmuide act nr. 51, `rab-bs-geboorten`),\ncontingent on their parent link being accepted. No death act found in the reachable\npages. Index only, not the register image, hence `sup`."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_antonius","name":"Antonius Vincke","dates":"b. 1770–1779","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"1770–1779","order":"1770","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"peperstraete_anne","name":"Anne Therese Peperstraete","detail":"m. Westvleteren, 9 May 1797"}],"source":"bartvanhooren (Bart Vanhooren)","note":"Married at Westvleteren in 1797; father of Engel Antonius Vincke."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_bellarmin_1867","name":"Bellarmin Eugène Vincke","dates":"1867 Diksmuide – 5 Sep 1872 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"1867 Diksmuide","order":"1867","died":"5 Sep 1872 Diksmuide","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_lucien_1840","mother":"vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vincke_lucien_1840]] and [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]], and [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s brother — one of\nfour children recovered from the couple's **1866-1870 blind window**, where the Diksmuide\nbirth index gives only the bare father surname VINCKE, no forename and no mother (his own\nbirth row is Diksmuide 1867 nr. 245). His parentage instead comes from his death, not his\nbirth: he died at Diksmuide 5 September 1872, act nr. 188 (`rab-bs-overlijdens`, indexed\nas *Bellarmin Eugenius*), which names both parents in full — Vincke Lucianus Julianus ×\nVanalderweireldt Ludovica Maria — an infant of about five, dead before he could ever have\nmarried and so unreachable through any marriage-act route. Index only, not the register\nimage, hence `sup`.\n\nThe death index is what broke this wall: it reaches children who never lived to marry,\nwhich a marriage-act sweep by construction cannot."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_camilla_1876","name":"Camilla Celina Vincke","dates":"20 Apr 1876 Diksmuide – 10 Dec 1876 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"20 Apr 1876 Diksmuide","order":"1876-04-20","died":"10 Dec 1876 Diksmuide","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_lucien_1840","mother":"vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Daughter of [[vincke_lucien_1840]] and [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]], and [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s sister. Her\nbirth — Diksmuide act nr. 84, 20 April 1876 — is one of seven Diksmuide rows in the\nvrijwilligersrab Geboorten index (`rab-bs-geboorten`) naming both parents in full as\nVincke Lucien Julianus x Vanalderweireldt Ludovica Maria (mother aged 30.4). A\nprovince-wide sweep of the same index, filtered separately by father's forename and by\nmother's surname, returns the identical seven rows — no rival couple. Index only, not the\nregister image, hence `sup`.\n\nDied in infancy, Diksmuide act nr. 246, 10 December 1876, at about eight months\n(`rab-bs-overlijdens`), naming both parents again. Both date columns on this act agree —\nunlike her siblings [[vincke_irma_1874]] and [[vincke_jerome_1886]], whose proposed dates needed\ncorrecting for the Date-vs-Certificate-Date conflation this index shares with\n`rab-bs-geboorten` — so 10 December stands without adjustment."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_camille_1895","name":"Camille Cyrille Vincke","dates":"21 Apr 1895 Diksmuide – 10 Nov 1918 Brugge","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"21 Apr 1895 Diksmuide","order":"1895-04-21","died":"10 Nov 1918 Brugge","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_alfons_1865","mother":"vandecappelle_eugenia","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vincke_alfons_1865]] and [[vandecappelle_eugenia]] — one of six children the couple's\nown birth-index entries surface (Diksmuide act nr. 27, `rab-bs-geboorten`), contingent on\ntheir parent link being accepted. Died at Brugge, act nr. 1728 (`rab-bs-overlijdens`),\nwhich names his parents a second time — Alphonse Lucien Vincke × Vandecappelle Eugenie\nMaria — corroborating the parent link independently of his birth registration.\n\n**Distinguish from a namesake left unresolved elsewhere.** This is *not* the blind-window\nchild \"Cyrille Camil\" (Diksmuide birth act 1870 nr. 69) — that child, one generation up,\nis still a NOT PROVEN frontier on [[vincke_lucien_1840]]'s own record; this Camille Cyrille is\na grandchild, born 1895, twenty-five years later. Index only, not the register image,\nhence `sup`."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_charles_1871","name":"Charles Louis Vincke","dates":"b. 30 Dec 1871 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"30 Dec 1871 Diksmuide","order":"1871-12-30","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_lucien_1840","mother":"vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vincke_lucien_1840]] and [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]], and [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s brother. His birth\n— Diksmuide act nr. 277, 30 December 1871 — is one of seven Diksmuide rows in the\nvrijwilligersrab Geboorten index (`rab-bs-geboorten`) naming both parents in full as\nVincke Lucien Julianus x Vanalderweireldt Ludovica Maria, matching this couple exactly:\nthe couple married 24 May 1865, so this is 6.6 years on. A province-wide sweep of the\nsame index, filtered separately by the father's forename pair and by the mother's rare\nsurname, returns the identical seven rows — no rival couple. Index only, not the register\nimage, hence `sup`.\n\n**Name reuse.** An elder brother, [[vincke_karolus_1870]] (\"Karolus Louis Vincke\", one of the\n1866-1870 blind-window children recovered via his own death act), died at Diksmuide 9\nSeptember 1871, just under four months before Charles Louis was born — the ordinary\npattern of a name given again after an infant of the same name had died."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_eduardus_1905","name":"Eduardus Hieronymus Vincke","dates":"b. 27 Sep 1905 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"27 Sep 1905 Oostende","order":"1905-09-27","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_theophil_1866","mother":"bolle_valerie","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vincke_theophil_1866]] and [[bolle_valerie]] — the last of six children the couple's\nown birth-index entries surface, contingent on their parent link being accepted. Born at\n**Oostende**, act nr. 1184, rather than Diksmuide like his five older siblings: the\nfamily had moved there by 1905, which is also where [[vincke_theophil_1866]] himself died in\n1922. No death act found in the reachable pages. Index only, not the register image,\nhence `sup`."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_emma_1880","name":"Emma Celesta Vincke","dates":"23 Jan 1880 Diksmuide – 6 Oct 1974 Oostende","confidence":"doc","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"23 Jan 1880 Diksmuide","order":"1880-01-23","died":"6 Oct 1974 Oostende","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_lucien_1840","mother":"vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845","spouses":[{"id":"vaniseghem_eduardus_1880","name":"Eduardus Van Iseghem","detail":"m. Oostende, 28 Sep 1907"}],"source":"Memorial card — Emma Celesta Vincke, d. Oostende 6 October 1974; gverdievel (Guy Verdievel); Birth act nr. 14 — Emma Celesta Vincke, Diksmuide, 24 January 1880 (AGATHA act analysis); West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; Diksmuide (West-Vlaanderen) civil registers on FamilySearch — image group #004833210: marriages, births, deaths and certificates 1876-1890, 1269 browsable images; Marriage act nr. 212 — Eduardus Ludovicus Rudolphus Vanyseghem x Emma Celesta Vincke, Oostende, 28 September 1907 (register image)","note":"Lived to 94 — the longest-lived in this cluster — outliving her husband by nearly 30 years. Daughter of Lucien Vincke & Ludovica Vanalderweireldt.\n\nCORROBORATED (July 2026). A Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust memorial-card record gives\nher birth at Diksmuide on 23 January 1880, her death at Oostende on 6 October 1974, and\nher partner as Eduard Van Iseghem — every field as held here, and the marriage to\n[[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] with it. She had rested on the gverdievel tree alone.\n\nHer birth act is Diksmuide **akte nr. 14, act date 24 January 1880**, child *Emma Celesta\nVincke*, born Diksmuide 23 January 1880 — one day before the act date, the ordinary gap\nbetween a birth and its declaration — naming her parents [[vincke_lucien_1840]] ×\n[[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]]. The act id is GEWVL_GEBWVL_01583386. Its AGATHA index transcription\nis held as `data/artifacts/emma-vincke-1880-birth-diksmuide.md`\n([[agatha-diksmuide-1880-birth-emma-vincke]]) and **stays `sup`** — see below for why.\n\n**THE REGISTER IMAGE READ (2026-07-27) — UPGRADES THIS RECORD `sup` → `doc`.** FamilySearch\nimage group **004833210**, image **392 of 1269**, ark `3:1:33SQ-GPD9-32V`\n([[fs-diksmuide-civil-registers-film-004833210]]) is the register page itself, held as\n`data/artifacts/emma-vincke-1880-birth-act-image.md`. It supersedes the AGATHA index\ntranscription above, which is kept alongside it rather than discarded — one is the primary\nact, the other its independent index precursor, and both remain useful. Two identifiers\nare now read directly off the image: birth date + place (23 January 1880, Diksmuide) and\nboth parents' full names, Lucien Julianus Vincke × Ludovica Maria Vanalderweireldt.\n\n**New facts the image gives that no index held:** the birth hour, **3 a.m.**; the\naddress — the father's own dwelling on the **Kleinendyk**, Diksmuide; the father's trade\nin the register's own hand, ***metsersdiender*** (the tree held \"metserdiener\" from a\nmember tree — the act writes it with the linking -s-; see [[vincke_lucien_1840]]); and\n[[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]]'s occupation, ***kantwerkster*** (lacemaker), not previously held\nanywhere. The declaring officer was **Edmond Paret**, schepen.\n\n**Two objections were raised against the match, and both are defeated — recorded, not\nsmoothed over.** First: both parents' stated ages are one year high — 40 and 35, where\nthey were 39y10m and 34y2m by this tree's held birth dates. The identical +1 offset\nrecurs on [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]] alone in a wholly separate document, her 1888 Alfons Vincke\nmarriage act (43 stated vs 42 completed, where Lucien's own age there is uninformative\nbecause his birthday had already passed) — one person showing the same offset twice, in\ntwo acts eight years and one register apart, is a birth-year-subtraction convention (the\nage reached *during* that year, not the age completed at declaration), not two independent\nerrors, and it does not unseat either held birth date. Second: the mother's surname was\nflagged as not letter-by-letter certain on first read. Re-cropped at 6× zoom in three\npasses: the **R after `-ALD-`** is clearly present — ruling out the `VANDERWEIRELT`\nno-R variant that hid records elsewhere in this family — and the final cluster reads\n**`-eldt`**, tighter than the artifact's own original caveat (corrected there too).\n\n**The venue fact, now confirmed logged in, not merely index-derived.** AGATHA (as user\n`shbunder`) publishes **no scan link at all** for its West-Vlaanderen birth project — every\n`<a>` on act GEWVL_GEBWVL_01583386 was tested for image/scan/mirador/iiif, zero matches —\nso the earlier finding that the act's own page carries no route to the image is structural,\nnot a session artifact. And AGATHA's own remark on the act, **\"SCAN 392 GSU\"**, is exactly\nFamilySearch's frame 392 on film 004833210 — the bridge AGATHA itself does not publish.\n\nCORROBORATED INDEPENDENTLY by her own marriage act — Oostende, 28 September 1907, act nr.\n212 (RAB ID 668717, FamilySearch film 004166052 image i=138) — which names her parents the\nsame way, Vincke Lucien Julianus × Vanalderweireldt Ludovica Maria. First read from the\nvrijwilligersrab Huwelijken index (`rab-bs-huwelijken`), where it was real corroboration —\na different commune, register and volunteer batch from the birth-act transcription — but\n**not independent of AGATHA in its birth-side pairing**: the vrijwilligersrab BIRTH row for\nthis same act shares AGATHA's own hidden act id, 1583386 (GEWVL_GEBWVL_01583386), the same\nRijksarchief volunteer transcription seen twice, not a second source. **Now also read as\nthe register image itself** ([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]],\n`data/artifacts/vaniseghem-vincke-1907-marriage-oostende.md`), doc-grade and genuinely\nindependent of the birth-act image — different register, date and clerk — confirming the\nsame parent names and her birth date and place to the day.\n\nFOUR MORE CHILDREN GRAFTED (research-log §64), from the same Huwelijken sweep:\n[[vaniseghem_flavie_1898]] (m. Stene 1920), [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1901]] (m. Oostende 1927), [[vaniseghem_valentina_1909]]\n(m. Stene 1931) and [[vaniseghem_maria_1913]] (m. Stene 1935) — each act naming both parents\nidentically to this record, alongside [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]] himself, whose own 1928 marriage act\nturned up in the same sweep (see his record).\n\nTWO MORE CHILDREN, WITH A CAVEAT (2026-07-27): a birth-index sweep for rows naming this\nrecord as mother turned up two more Oostende children of [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] × this record —\n[[vaniseghem_camillus_1905]] (b. 25 April 1905, act nr. 501) and [[vaniseghem_camillus_1911]]\n(b. 6 January 1911, act nr. 14) — and birth dates for three already-held children,\n[[vaniseghem_eduardus_1901]] (2 November 1901), [[vaniseghem_valentina_1909]] (23 March 1909) and [[vaniseghem_maria_1913]]\n(22 January 1913). [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1901]]'s date is no longer uncorroborated: the 1907 marriage\nact's own legitimation clause, below, independently confirms it. [[vaniseghem_valentina_1909]] and\n[[vaniseghem_maria_1913]]'s dates remain not independently re-checked against a second act.\n\nTHE LEGITIMATION CLAUSE READ (2026-07-27) — RESOLVES THE TWO-BIRTHS-BEFORE-MARRIAGE\nFRONTIER, IN PART. The 1907\nmarriage act's own legitimation clause ([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]])\nnames exactly three children as this couple's legitimate issue: [[vaniseghem_flavie_1898]] (b.\nDiksmuide 26 March 1898), [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1901]] (b. Oostende 2 November 1901) and [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]]\n(b. Lens, France, 11 May 1903) — see each record. \"VINCKE Flavie Eulalie\" of 26 March 1898\nis [[vaniseghem_flavie_1898]] herself, tied by forename pair, day, month, year and commune, not by act\nreference (the 1907 act cites no birth act number). \"VINCKE Albert Joseph\" (b. 9 December\n1899, d. 26 March 1900) is **named by neither the legitimation clause nor any other act**:\nthe clause names three children and no others, and both his death and\n[[vaniseghem_camillus_1905]]'s (d. 1905) predate the 1907 wedding, the ordinary reason a\nlegitimation passes over an already-dead infant. The act is silent on him, not contrary —\nhis paternity **stays unproven and unlinked**; see [[vincke_romanie_1873]] for a separate,\nexplicitly-speculative lead this same act raised and did not settle."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_engel_1807","name":"Engel Antonius Vincke","dates":"b. 17 Feb 1807 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"17 Feb 1807 Diksmuide","order":"1807-02-17","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_antonius","mother":"peperstraete_anne","spouses":[{"id":"leynseele_virginia_1818","name":"Virginia Coleta Leynseele"}],"source":"bartvanhooren (Bart Vanhooren)","note":"Of Diksmuide; married twice — our line runs through his 2nd wife, Virginia Leynseele (their son Lucien, 1840)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_eugene_1877","name":"Eugène Lucien Vincke","dates":"23 Jul 1877 Diksmuide – 4 Apr 1902 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"23 Jul 1877 Diksmuide","order":"1877-07-23","died":"4 Apr 1902 Diksmuide","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_lucien_1840","mother":"vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vincke_lucien_1840]] and [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]], and [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s brother. His birth\n— Diksmuide act nr. 169, 23 July 1877 — is one of seven Diksmuide rows in the\nvrijwilligersrab Geboorten index (`rab-bs-geboorten`) naming both parents in full as\nVincke Lucien Julianus x Vanalderweireldt Ludovica Maria (mother aged 31.7). A\nprovince-wide sweep of the same index, filtered separately by father's forename and by\nmother's surname, returns the identical seven rows — no rival couple. Index only, not the\nregister image, hence `sup`.\n\nDied at Diksmuide, act nr. 24, 4 April 1902, aged 24 (`rab-bs-overlijdens`; mother\nwritten Vanalderweireldt Louise Maria there). Both date columns on this act agree —\nunlike his siblings [[vincke_irma_1874]] and [[vincke_jerome_1886]], whose proposed dates needed\ncorrecting for the Date-vs-Certificate-Date conflation this index shares with\n`rab-bs-geboorten` — so 4 April stands without adjustment."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_florence_1869","name":"Florence Amelie Vincke","dates":"b. 1869 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","sex":"f","born":"1869 Diksmuide","order":"1869","occupation":"kantwerkster (lace-maker)","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_lucien_1840","mother":"vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845","spouses":[{"id":"bocklandt_caesar_1867","name":"Caesar Antonius Bocklandt","detail":"m. Diksmuide, 11 Feb 1893"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 40 — Caesar Antonius Bocklandt x Florence Amelie Vincke, Diksmuide, 11 February 1893; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Daughter of [[vincke_lucien_1840]] and [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]], and [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s eldest known\nsister. **Her parentage comes from her own 1893 MARRIAGE act, not her birth act.** The\nDiksmuide birth index for 1866-1870 records only a bare father surname, no forename and no\nmother at all (`rab-bs-geboorten`) — so her own birth row, Diksmuide act nr. 87 of 1869,\ndoes not name her parents. The marriage act — Diksmuide nr. 40, 11 February 1893\n([[agatha-diksmuide-1893-marriage-bocklandt-vincke]]) — names her born at Diksmuide\n22 April 1869, *kantwerkster*, daughter of Lucien Julianus Vincke and Ludovica Maria\nVanalderweireldt, and married **Caesar Antonius Bocklandt** (b. Hamme 2 Jul 1867,\n*koordedraaier*), son of [[bocklandt_edouard_1839]] and [[vanbergen_marielouise_1842]]. AGATHA serves this\nact only as an \"analyse van akte\" (index transcription), not the register image, hence\n`sup`.\n\nThis is the link the tree had already recorded but not acted on: the 1893 act sat on\n[[bocklandt_caesar_1867]]'s own record naming the bride's parents by name only — one\nidentifier, short of a graft — and Florence Amelie had no record of her own to graft onto.\nWith her own record now written, the parents match [[vincke_lucien_1840]] x [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]]\nby full name, and a province-wide sweep of the Diksmuide birth index found no rival\ncouple. This joins the Van Iseghem and De Keyser/Bocklandt branches of this tree (objective\n3) — research-log §64."});
