FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_irma_1874","name":"Irma Maria Vincke","dates":"1 Nov 1874 Diksmuide – 25 Apr 1875 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"1 Nov 1874 Diksmuide","order":"1874-11-01","died":"25 Apr 1875 Diksmuide","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_lucien_1840","mother":"vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Daughter of [[vincke_lucien_1840]] and [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]], and [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s sister. Her\nbirth — Diksmuide act nr. 236, 1 November 1874 — is one of seven Diksmuide rows in the\nvrijwilligersrab Geboorten index (`rab-bs-geboorten`) naming both parents in full as\nVincke Lucien Julianus x Vanalderweireldt Ludovica Maria (mother aged 28.9). A\nprovince-wide sweep of the same index, filtered separately by father's forename and by\nmother's surname, returns the identical seven rows — no rival couple. Index only, not the\nregister image, hence `sup`.\n\nDied in infancy, Diksmuide act nr. 86, 25 April 1875, at about six months\n(`rab-bs-overlijdens`), naming both parents again. **CORRECTED on entry**: the death\nindex's \"Certificate Date\" column reads 26 April; the \"Date\" column, which is the death\nitself, reads 25 April. This is the same Date-vs-Certificate-Date conflation already\ndocumented on `rab-bs-geboorten`'s note for the births index, now confirmed to affect the\ndeaths index too — the note there has been updated accordingly. 25 April is recorded\nhere, not 26."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_jerome_1886","name":"Jerome Maurice Vincke","dates":"22 Sep 1886 Diksmuide – 13 Jan 1889 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"22 Sep 1886 Diksmuide","order":"1886-09-22","died":"13 Jan 1889 Diksmuide","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_lucien_1840","mother":"vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vincke_lucien_1840]] and [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]], and [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s brother — the\nyoungest known child of the couple. His birth — Diksmuide act nr. 167, 22 September 1886\n— is one of seven Diksmuide rows in the vrijwilligersrab Geboorten index\n(`rab-bs-geboorten`) naming both parents in full as Vincke Lucien Julianus x\nVanalderweireldt Ludovica Maria. His mother was 40.8 at his birth — the upper end of\nchildbearing but not implausible, and the 6.6-year gap since [[vincke_emma_1880]] (1880) is\nconsistent with unrecorded infant losses in the couple's 1866-1870 blind window (see\n[[vincke_lucien_1840]]'s record). A province-wide sweep of the same index, filtered separately\nby father's forename and by mother's surname, returns the identical seven rows — no rival\ncouple. Index only, not the register image, hence `sup`.\n\nDied at Diksmuide, act nr. 5, 13 January 1889, aged two (`rab-bs-overlijdens`), naming\nboth parents again. **CORRECTED on entry**: the death index's \"Certificate Date\" column\nreads 14 January; the \"Date\" column, which is the death itself, reads 13 January — the\nsame Date-vs-Certificate-Date conflation already documented on `rab-bs-geboorten`'s note\nfor the births index, now confirmed to affect the deaths index too. 13 January is\nrecorded here, not 14."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_juliette_1889","name":"Juliette Gabrielle Camilla Vincke","dates":"b. 11 May 1889 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"11 May 1889 Diksmuide","order":"1889-05-11","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_alfons_1865","mother":"vandecappelle_eugenia","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Daughter of [[vincke_alfons_1865]] and [[vandecappelle_eugenia]] — one of six children the\ncouple's own birth-index entries surface (Diksmuide act nr. 66, `rab-bs-geboorten`),\ncontingent on their parent link being accepted. No death act found in the reachable\npages. Index only, not the register image, hence `sup`."});
