FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_karolus_1870","name":"Karolus Louis Vincke","dates":"1870 Diksmuide – 9 Sep 1871 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"1870 Diksmuide","order":"1870","died":"9 Sep 1871 Diksmuide","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_lucien_1840","mother":"vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vincke_lucien_1840]] and [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]], and [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s brother — one of\nfour children recovered from the couple's **1866-1870 blind window**, where the Diksmuide\nbirth index gives only the bare father surname VINCKE, no forename and no mother (his own\nbirth row is Diksmuide 1870 nr. 247). His parentage instead comes from his death: he died\nat Diksmuide 9 September 1871, act nr. 189 (`rab-bs-overlijdens`, indexed as *Carolus\nLudovicus*), naming both parents in full — Vincke Lucien Julien × Vanalderweireldt\nLudovica Maria — an infant who died before he could ever have married. Index only, not\nthe register image, hence `sup`.\n\n**Name reuse.** [[vincke_charles_1871]] (\"Charles Louis Vincke\") was born to the same couple\njust under four months later, 30 December 1871 — the ordinary pattern of a name given to\na new child after an infant of the same name had died."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_leopold_1895","name":"Leopold Maurice Vincke","dates":"21 Feb 1895 Diksmuide – 9 May 1895 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"21 Feb 1895 Diksmuide","order":"1895-02-21","died":"9 May 1895 Diksmuide","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_theophil_1866","mother":"bolle_valerie","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vincke_theophil_1866]] and [[bolle_valerie]] — one of six children the couple's own\nbirth-index entries surface (Diksmuide act nr. 11, `rab-bs-geboorten`), contingent on\ntheir parent link being accepted. Died in infancy, aged about eleven weeks (Diksmuide act\nnr. 44, `rab-bs-overlijdens`). Index only, not the register image, hence `sup`.\n\n**Name reuse.** A second son, [[vincke_leopold_1900]], was given the same name five\nyears later and also died in infancy — two distinct children, not a transcription\nduplicate; see his record."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_leopold_1900","name":"Leopold Maurice Vincke","dates":"27 Jan 1900 Diksmuide – 17 Feb 1900 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"27 Jan 1900 Diksmuide","order":"1900-01-27","died":"17 Feb 1900 Diksmuide","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_theophil_1866","mother":"bolle_valerie","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vincke_theophil_1866]] and [[bolle_valerie]] — one of six children the couple's own\nbirth-index entries surface (Diksmuide act nr. 11, `rab-bs-geboorten`), contingent on\ntheir parent link being accepted. Died in infancy, aged about three weeks (Diksmuide act\nnr. 26, `rab-bs-overlijdens`). Index only, not the register image, hence `sup`.\n\n**Name reuse, not a duplicate.** An elder brother, [[vincke_leopold_1895]], was born\nunder the identical name five years earlier and also died in infancy. Two distinct\nchildren given the same name after the first died — the ordinary pattern already\nrecorded elsewhere in this family (see [[vincke_karolus_1870]]/[[vincke_charles_1871]]) — not a\ntranscription artefact of one child counted twice."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_louisa_1894","name":"Louisa Camilla Vincke","dates":"24 Mar 1894 Diksmuide – 18 Jun 1894 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"24 Mar 1894 Diksmuide","order":"1894-03-24","died":"18 Jun 1894 Diksmuide","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_alfons_1865","mother":"vandecappelle_eugenia","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Daughter of [[vincke_alfons_1865]] and [[vandecappelle_eugenia]] — one of six children the\ncouple's own birth-index entries surface (Diksmuide act nr. 35, `rab-bs-geboorten`),\ncontingent on their parent link being accepted. Died in infancy, aged about three months\n(Diksmuide act nr. 51, `rab-bs-overlijdens`). Index only, not the register image, hence\n`sup`."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_lucien_1840","name":"Lucien Julianus Vincke","dates":"b. 26 Mar 1840 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"26 Mar 1840 Diksmuide","order":"1840-03-26","occupation":"metsersdiender (mason's assistant)","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_engel_1807","mother":"leynseele_virginia_1818","spouses":[{"id":"vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845","name":"Ludovica Maria Vanalderweireldt","detail":"m. Diksmuide, 24 May 1865"}],"source":"bartvanhooren (Bart Vanhooren); West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; Marriage act nr. 40 — Caesar Antonius Bocklandt x Florence Amelie Vincke, Diksmuide, 11 February 1893; Diksmuide (West-Vlaanderen) civil registers on FamilySearch — image group #004833210: marriages, births, deaths and certificates 1876-1890, 1269 browsable images; Marriage act nr. 212 — Eduardus Ludovicus Rudolphus Vanyseghem x Emma Celesta Vincke, Oostende, 28 September 1907 (register image)","note":"A mason's assistant; son of Engel Antonius Vincke & Virginia Leynseele.\n\n**NAMED AS FATHER IN A REGISTER IMAGE FOR THE FIRST TIME (2026-07-27), DOC-GRADE.**\n[[vincke_emma_1880]]'s own birth act, read as the register image itself\n([[fs-diksmuide-civil-registers-film-004833210]],\n`data/artifacts/emma-vincke-1880-birth-act-image.md`), names him father, occupation\nwritten in the register's own hand as ***metsersdiender*** — the linking -s- this record's\noccupation field now carries, corrected from \"metserdiener\" as held from a member tree.\nHis stated age, \"veertig\" (40), is one year above the 39y10m he would have completed\nagainst this record's held birth of 26 March 1840 — **not treated as a contradiction**:\nthe identical +1 offset recurs, independently, on his wife [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]] alone in a\nwholly separate 1888 document (43 stated vs 42 completed) — one person showing the same\noffset twice, in two acts eight years and one register apart, is a birth-year-subtraction\nconvention, not two independent errors, and it unseats neither held birth date. This\nrecord's own confidence stays `sup`, since his own birth is still index-only — the `doc`\ngrade attaches to this specific parent-naming, read off a primary image.\n\n**ALSO NAMED FATHER-OF-THE-BRIDE IN THE 1907 MARRIAGE ACT, DOC-GRADE.** Emma's own 1907\nOostende marriage act ([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]],\n`data/artifacts/vaniseghem-vincke-1907-marriage-oostende.md`) names him again, present and\nconsenting: *\"Lucien Julianus, werkman\"* — a plain labourer, a further occupation change\nfrom *metsersdiender* (1880) and *metser* (Alfons's 1888 marriage act), flagged as a\nplausible career shift over 27 years rather than a contradiction. This is a second,\nindependent primary-image corroboration of the parent link, in a different register from\nthe birth act, 27 years apart.\n\nSEVEN MORE CHILDREN GRAFTED (research-log §64), from a province-wide sweep of the\nvrijwilligersrab Geboorten index (`rab-bs-geboorten`) for Diksmuide, each act naming both\nparents in full as Vincke Lucien Julianus x Vanalderweireldt Ludovica Maria: [[vincke_charles_1871]]\n(b. 30 Dec 1871), [[vincke_romanie_1873]] (b. 7 Oct 1873 — one capture spells the father \"Lucien\nJulien\", a forename variant, not a rival father), [[vincke_irma_1874]] (b. 1 Nov 1874),\n[[vincke_camilla_1876]] (b. 20 Apr 1876), [[vincke_eugene_1877]] (b. 23 Jul 1877), [[vincke_emma_1880]]\n(b. 23 Jan 1880, already held) and [[vincke_jerome_1886]] (b. 22 Sep 1886). Filtering the same\nindex separately by father's forename and by mother's rare surname returns the identical\nset — no rival couple. This closes the enumeration for Diksmuide **1871 onward**.\n\nAn EIGHTH CHILD, [[vincke_florence_1869]] (b. Diksmuide 1869), is grafted separately from her\nown 1893 marriage act ([[agatha-diksmuide-1893-marriage-bocklandt-vincke]]), not from a\nbirth act: Diksmuide's 1866-1870 birth rows carry only a bare father surname, no forename\nand no mother, so parentage cannot be read from the index in that window. Her marriage\nalso joins this couple's line to the De Keyser/Bocklandt branch (objective 3).\n\nTHE 1866-1870 BLIND WINDOW, BROKEN (research-log §67, 2026-07-27). Diksmuide births in\nthose years name no parents in the index at all — but the couple's children's own LATER\nacts do, the same route that recovered Florence Amelie. Two further routes closed most of\nit: each blind-window child's own marriage act, and — crucially, because it reaches\nchildren who died before ever marrying — each one's own death act.\n\nFOUR MORE CHILDREN GRAFTED: [[vincke_theophil_1866]] (b. 1866, m. Valerie Bolle 1893, d.\nOostende 1922 — via his own marriage AND death acts, 29 years apart, full parent-name\nagreement on both, plus a rival Theophile Achille Vincke of Diksmuide ruled out by\nparents/spouse/death year), [[vincke_bellarmin_1867]] (b. 1867, d. Diksmuide 1872, an infant —\nvia his death act only, since he never married), [[vincke_karolus_1870]] (b. 1870, d.\nDiksmuide 1871, an infant, whose name was then reused for [[vincke_charles_1871]] four months\nlater — via his death act only) and [[vincke_alfons_1865]] (b. 1865, one year OUTSIDE this\nwindow but found by the same marriage-index sweep, m. Eugenia Vandecappelle 1888,\ncorroborated independently by a Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust memorial card — born 3\nmonths 20 days after this couple's own wedding, flagged and not smoothed over).\n\nTWELVE GRANDCHILDREN, contingent on the two links above: six children of\n[[vincke_theophil_1866]] × [[bolle_valerie]] — [[vincke_marie_1894]] (1894-1895),\n[[vincke_leopold_1895]] (1895, an infant death), [[vincke_marie_1896]] (1896),\n[[vincke_madeleine_1898]] (1898-1898, an infant death), [[vincke_leopold_1900]]\n(1900-1900, the same name reused after the first died) and [[vincke_eduardus_1905]]\n(b. Oostende 1905, after the family moved there) — and six of [[vincke_alfons_1865]] ×\n[[vandecappelle_eugenia]]: [[vincke_juliette_1889]] (1889),\n[[vincke_georges_1890]] (1890), [[vincke_karel_1892]] (1892), [[vincke_louisa_1894]]\n(1894-1894, an infant death), [[vincke_camille_1895]] (b. 1895, d. Brugge 1918, his own\ndeath act naming his parents a second time) and [[vincke_andre_1901]] (1901).\n\nTWO EXCLUDED, deliberately not grafted. \"Medard Edmond Vincke\" (blind-window birth 1866\nnr. 214) is a different Vincke woman's child: his own death act (Diksmuide 1866 nr. 274)\nnames father NN NN, mother Vincke Philomena Helena. \"Elodie Vincke\" (blind-window birth\n1870 nr. 16) belongs to a separate, prolific Diksmuide Vincke line: her own 1894 marriage\nact names her parents as Richard Aloïs Vincke × Eugenie Dekeyrel, not this couple — a\nbirth-year wobble (1870 vs 1871) on the index is immaterial, since under either year the\nparents are not ours. This clan holds two different women named Elodie: this record's\nown [[vincke_romanie_1873]] (\"Romanie Elodie\", act 206/1873, parents named in full) is not the\nsame person as the excluded 1870 Elodie above — exactly the near-miss class CLAUDE.md's\nrule 1 exists for.\n\nFIVE STILL NOT PROVEN, a named frontier rather than a link: **Emil Fidèle** (1867 nr.\n256), **Gustave Camil** (1867 nr. 266), **Florida Juliana** (1869 nr. 74), **Arthur\nCarolus** (1870 nr. 88) and **Cyrille Camil** (1870 nr. 69) are bare VINCKE-only rows with\nno parent-naming act found for any of them, in either the marriage or the death index.\nScope actually covered, so the wall stays re-openable rather than closed: the whole\nWest-Flemish marriage index (all communes, all years, Vincke + Vyncke, eight spellings of\nthe mother's surname); the whole West-Flemish death index (Vincke, 2212 rows — Florida\nreturns zero province-wide); Open Archives Belgium-wide, twelve forename queries, 75\nrecords. Diksmuide itself carries 26 Vincke-touching marriages 1880-1910 and 124 death\nrows 1798-1910 — the commune **is** covered; these five are absent from it, not hidden\nbehind it. What would settle them is the register image behind the `SCAN nnn GSU`\nreference on the AGATHA side, or a FamilySearch session on the vrijwilligersrab arks — not\na further index sweep. A NEW LEAD, NOT AN IDENTIFIER (2026-07-27): a witness at\n[[vincke_emma_1880]]'s 1907 marriage, Constantinus Degraeve, is stated in the act as *\"zwager\nder echtgenoote\"* — brother-in-law of the bride — implying a Vincke sister of hers married\na Degraeve, possibly one of the five above, possibly [[vincke_romanie_1873]] (the one daughter\nof this couple with no further record of her own). See [[vincke_romanie_1873]]'s record: this\nis recorded as pure surname-coincidence speculation, not linked to anyone.\n\nAlso ambiguous: a Nieuwkerke marriage of \"VINCKE Cyrille Camille\" ×\n\"REUBRECHT Valerie Eugenie\" (act nr. 4) is blank in every Detail field and two corpus\nmemorial cards confirm the couple existed (d. 22/05/1937) but name no parents — it neither\nconfirms nor refutes a link to Cyrille Camil above.\n\nAN ARGUMENT, USED ONLY TO EXCLUDE, NEVER TO INCLUDE. Diksmuide birth acts are\nstrictly date-ordered (77 act-number/date pairs checked 1871-1910, zero violations), so\nact-number spacing against a known birth rate can flag an implausible gap. The birth rate\nis not constant, though — it declines from ~0.73-0.81 acts/day in the early 1870s to\n~0.2-0.3 by 1900-1910 — and recomputed with the conservative in-period rate (~0.75), the\ngap around the 1870 acts comes out to roughly 212-237 days, still under the ~270-300-day\nfloor a second full-term birth needs. This spacing argument is corroboration only, and it\nis never grounds for a graft (CLAUDE.md rule 1): it agrees with the independent exclusion\nof Medard Edmond above (~48 days' spacing, plausible only as a different mother's child,\nwhich his own death act already settles), and it does **not** close the excluded Elodie\nabove (~282 days, borderline) — that case is settled by her own marriage act, a document,\nnot by this arithmetic."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_madeleine_1898","name":"Madeleine Marie Vincke","dates":"5 May 1898 Diksmuide – 29 Jun 1898 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"5 May 1898 Diksmuide","order":"1898-05-05","died":"29 Jun 1898 Diksmuide","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_theophil_1866","mother":"bolle_valerie","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Daughter of [[vincke_theophil_1866]] and [[bolle_valerie]] — one of six children the couple's\nown birth-index entries surface (Diksmuide act nr. 40, `rab-bs-geboorten`), contingent on\ntheir parent link being accepted. Died in infancy, aged about eight weeks (Diksmuide act\nnr. 47, `rab-bs-overlijdens`). Index only, not the register image, hence `sup`."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_marie_1894","name":"Marie Sophie Vincke","dates":"24 Feb 1894 Diksmuide – 12 Oct 1895 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"24 Feb 1894 Diksmuide","order":"1894-02-24","died":"12 Oct 1895 Diksmuide","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_theophil_1866","mother":"bolle_valerie","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Daughter of [[vincke_theophil_1866]] and [[bolle_valerie]] — one of six children the couple's\nown birth-index entries surface (Diksmuide act nr. 23, `rab-bs-geboorten`), contingent on\ntheir parent link being accepted. Died in infancy, aged about twenty months (Diksmuide\nact nr. 96, `rab-bs-overlijdens`). Index only, not the register image, hence `sup`."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_marie_1896","name":"Marie Louise Vincke","dates":"b. 9 Sep 1896 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"9 Sep 1896 Diksmuide","order":"1896-09-09","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_theophil_1866","mother":"bolle_valerie","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Daughter of [[vincke_theophil_1866]] and [[bolle_valerie]] — one of six children the couple's\nown birth-index entries surface (Diksmuide act nr. 72, `rab-bs-geboorten`), contingent on\ntheir parent link being accepted. No death act found in the reachable pages. Index only,\nnot the register image, hence `sup`."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_romanie_1873","name":"Romanie Elodie Vincke","dates":"b. 7 Oct 1873 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"7 Oct 1873 Diksmuide","order":"1873-10-07","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_lucien_1840","mother":"vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845","source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Geboorten (birth index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; Marriage act nr. 212 — Eduardus Ludovicus Rudolphus Vanyseghem x Emma Celesta Vincke, Oostende, 28 September 1907 (register image)","note":"Daughter of [[vincke_lucien_1840]] and [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]], and [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s sister. Her\nbirth — Diksmuide act nr. 206, 7 October 1873 — is one of seven Diksmuide rows in the\nvrijwilligersrab Geboorten index (`rab-bs-geboorten`) naming both parents as Vincke Lucien\nJulianus x Vanalderweireldt Ludovica Maria. Index only, not the register image, hence\n`sup`.\n\n**One capture of this act renders the father as \"Lucien Julien\" rather than \"Lucien\nJulianus\"** — every other act in this cluster, and his own record, give him the latter.\nAccepted here as a French/Latin variant of the same forename, not a different father:\nthe mother's rarer full name, the commune and the chronology (she was 27.9) all agree,\nthere is no evidence of Ludovica having any other husband, and the same province-wide\nsweep that closes off a rival couple for her siblings found none here either. The variant\nis flagged, not concealed.\n\nFormerly a frontier on [[vincke_lucien_1840]]'s own record (\"a probable second daughter, not\ngrafted\"); resolved here (research-log §64).\n\nNEW FRONTIER, NOT LINKED (2026-07-27). [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s own 1907 marriage act, read as a\nregister image ([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]]), carries a witness\n**Constantinus Degraeve**, 36, *aardewerker*, of Diksmuide, stated in the register's own\nwords as *\"zwager der echtgenoote\"* — brother-in-law of the bride — implying an\n**unrecorded Vincke sister married a Degraeve**. No person record, label or prior search\nanywhere in this tree mentions \"Degraeve.\" This record is the only Vincke daughter of\n[[vincke_lucien_1840]] × [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]] known to have survived to adulthood with no\nfurther record of her own (no marriage, no death) — but that is **pure surname-coincidence\nspeculation, not an identifier**, and it is recorded here as exactly that: not a link, not\nan inference, a bare coincidence noted so a later pass does not rediscover it and\noverclaim. What would settle it: Constantinus Degraeve's own marriage act, or a Diksmuide\nor Oostende marriage pairing a Vincke bride to a Degraeve groom. See [[vincke_lucien_1840]]'s\nown record for the five Vincke children still unaccounted for, any of whom this witness\nline could equally point to."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vincke_theophil_1866","name":"Theophil Henri Vincke","dates":"23 Jul 1866 Diksmuide – 22 Apr 1922 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vincke","family":"vincke","born":"23 Jul 1866 Diksmuide","order":"1866-07-23","died":"22 Apr 1922 Oostende","occupation":"schoenmaker (shoemaker)","line":"van-iseghem","father":"vincke_lucien_1840","mother":"vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845","spouses":[{"id":"bolle_valerie","name":"Valerie Marie Pharaïlde Bolle","detail":"m. Diksmuide, 13 Dec 1893"}],"source":"West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Son of [[vincke_lucien_1840]] and [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]], and [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s brother — one of\nfour children this pass recovers from the couple's **1866-1870 blind window**: the\nDiksmuide birth index there gives only the bare father surname VINCKE, no forename, no\nmother, and a birth date recorded as `YYYY/00/00`. His own birth act (Diksmuide 1866 nr.\n175) is one of those bare rows, so his parentage comes from his own marriage, 29 years\nlater, not from his birth act.\n\nHis marriage — Diksmuide, 13 December 1893, act nr. 239 (`rab-bs-huwelijken`) — gives him\nborn Diksmuide 23 July 1866 (matching act nr. 175 exactly), age 27, *schoenmaker*, and\nnames his parents as Vincke Lucien Julien (53, metser) × Vanderweirelt Louise Marie (48,\nkantwerkster). His own death — Oostende, 22 April 1922, act nr. 280\n(`rab-bs-overlijdens`) — repeats the parent names (Vincke Lucien Julien × Vanalderweireldt\nLouise Maria) 29 years later, in a different register and commune, and separately names\nhis surviving spouse, Bolle Valerie Maria, matching the 1893 bride exactly. Full\nparent-name agreement across two independent registers 29 years apart, plus the\ndeath act's own spouse cross-check, is what carries the graft.\n\n**The mother's surname on the 1893 act reads VANDERWEIRELT — the \"-AL-\" dropped — which is\nwhy this row is invisible to a query for Vanalderweireldt.** Accepted as the same woman:\nthis pass's own marriage-index sweep queried eight spellings of the surname\n(Vanalderweireldt, Vanalderweirelt, Vanderweirelt, Vanderweireldt, Alderweireldt,\nVanaldeweireldt, Vanalderwerelt, Vandeweireldt) precisely because the family name is\ntranscribed inconsistently across acts, and `Louise`/`Ludovica` is a documented forename\nfold — `data/forenames.json`'s `f` block groups `ludovica`, `lodewijka` and `louise`\ntogether, sex-split so the fold can never cross into a male form.\n\n**A rival, ruled out, is the reason this needed care.** A second Diksmuide man,\n*Theophile Achille Vincke*, son of Adolf Vincke × Celina Maria Vandenberghe, married\nDelaleeuwe Eugenia in 1903 and died at Diksmuide in 1959\n(`fwk:e427e82c-0ce3-5a43-afac-4eea747ce86a`) — same forename pair, same surname, same\ncommune. Distinguished by parents, spouse and death year: name and surname alone would\nhave been dangerous here.\n\nIndex only, not the register image, hence `sup`."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vogels_amelia","name":"Amelia Vogels","dates":"","confidence":"doc","surname":"Vogels","family":"vogels","sex":"f","occupation":"landbouwster (farmer)","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"guns_joannes","name":"Joannes Franciscus Guns"}],"source":"Civil marriage acts for the Bossin/Swaelens/Vrebos family of Kraainem, 1884-1901 (harvested corpus, July 2026); Marriage act nr. 6 — Henricus Bossin x Maria Catharina Guns, Kraainem, 23 November 1887 (register image)","note":"Named as mother of the bride in her daughter [[guns_maria_1864]]'s marriage act — Kraainem, 23\nNovember 1887 — resident Sterrebeek, *landbouwster*. The act gives her no age and no\ndates, so this record has none.\n\n**UPGRADED TO `doc` (2026-07-27)** — the register image was read, confirming her present\nin person and consenting alongside [[guns_joannes]], not just an AGATHA/Demogen index row.\n\nFRONTIER: her marriage to [[guns_joannes]], which the Sterrebeek/Vossem registers should hold\nfor roughly 1855–1864."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vrebos_henricus","name":"Henricus Franciscus Vrebos","dates":"d. 18 Dec 1871 Kraainem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vrebos","family":"vrebos","sex":"m","died":"18 Dec 1871 Kraainem","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"schoolmeesters_josina","name":"Josina Schoolmeesters"}],"source":"Civil marriage acts for the Bossin/Swaelens/Vrebos family of Kraainem, 1884-1901 (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Named as father of the groom, already dead, in his son [[vrebos_petrus_1856]]'s 1901 marriage\nact — Kraainem, 30 May 1901 — which gives his death as **Kraainem, 18 December 1871**.\nThe act gives him no age, occupation or birth date, so this record has none.\n\nFRONTIER: his marriage to [[schoolmeesters_josina]], and his own birth."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vrebos_petrus_1856","name":"Petrus Vrebos","dates":"b. 30 May 1856 Kraainem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vrebos","family":"vrebos","sex":"m","born":"30 May 1856 Kraainem","order":"1856-05-30","occupation":"pleisteraar (plasterer)","line":"thumas","father":"vrebos_henricus","mother":"schoolmeesters_josina","spouses":[{"name":"Elisabeth Theresia Geuffens"},{"id":"bossin_ludovica_1853","name":"Ludovica Bossin","detail":"m. Kraainem, 30 May 1901"}],"source":"Civil marriage acts for the Bossin/Swaelens/Vrebos family of Kraainem, 1884-1901 (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Not previously in the tree. He married [[bossin_ludovica_1853]] — [[bossin_antonia_1849]]'s sister,\n[[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] and [[peremans_joanna_1824]]'s daughter — at **Kraainem on 30 May 1901**, her\nremarriage after the death of her first husband, [[swaelens_joannes_1858]] (Kraainem, 7 October 1898).\nBorn **Kraainem, 30 May 1856**, a *pleisteraar*, and himself a widower at the marriage:\nhis first wife, **Elisabeth Theresia Geuffens**, had died at Kraainem on 30 April 1900,\nbarely thirteen months before this act — named in it only as his deceased \"vorige\npartner\", with no birth date, age or parents given, so no record is made for her beyond\nthis note.\n\nHis parents are named in the act: **Henricus Franciscus Vrebos**, dead at Kraainem on 18\nDecember 1871, and **Josina Schoolmeesters**, landbouwster of Kraainem — see [[vrebos_henricus]]\nand [[schoolmeesters_josina]].\n\n`sup`: an index-level AGATHA/Demogen act analysis, no register image read.\n\nFRONTIER: his first marriage to Elisabeth Theresia Geuffens, and any children by either\nmarriage."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"vyveraert_nn","name":"NN Vyveraert","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vyveraert","family":"vyveraert","sex":"f","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"bundervoet_petrus_1560","name":"Petrus Bundervoet"}],"source":"paulderidder; glorieuxp","note":"Wife of [[bundervoet_petrus_1560]], the earliest recorded ancestor of the Bundervoet\nline. Her given name is not recorded — only the family name — so she is written the\nway [[vandenberghe_nn]] is, and for the same reason.\n\nHis record says he married twice; this is the only wife either tree names, and\nwhich of the two marriages it was is not stated. Whether [[bundervoet_livinus_1600]] is\nher son or the other wife's is therefore open, and the maternity is deliberately not\nrecorded. FRONTIER — an Evergem marriage act naming her."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"wagebaert_clementia_1853","name":"Clementia Sophia Wagebaert","dates":"1853 – 1927","confidence":"sup","surname":"Wagebaert","family":"wagebaert","born":"1853","order":"1853","died":"1927","line":"vanstechelman","father":"wagebaert_henricus","mother":"vandillen_angela","spouses":[{"id":"vanstechelman_petrus_1854","name":"Petrus Jacobus Vanstechelman","detail":"m. Mariakerke, 21 Jan 1875"}],"source":"België, West-Vlaanderen, burgerlijke stand, 1582-1950; stechec (Christian Vanstechelman)","note":"Wife of the mason Petrus Jacobus Vanstechelman; died in 1927, the same year as her husband.\n\nCORROBORATED (July 2026). She is named as the mother — as *Clementia Sophia Wagebaert*, and\nin one act as *Clemence* — on three Oostende civil acts of her children, alongside Petrus\nJacobus ([[fs-wvl-bs]]). Her own dates are still unrecorded here; the acts name her without\ngiving them."});
