FamilyTree.person({"id":"wittenheyns_barbara_1535","name":"Barbara Wittenheyns","dates":"b. ~1535","confidence":"sup","surname":"Wittenheyns","family":"wittenheyns","born":"~1535","order":"1535","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"wittenheyns_petrus_1500","mother":"tjonck_judoca_1510","spouses":[{"id":"vanrenterghem_guillielmus_1530","name":"Guillielmus Van Renterghem"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Mother of Judocus Van Renterghem. A Wittenheyns of Oostkamp — the same Oostkamp Wittenheyns family that also appears on our Vandewalle line (via Mattheus Wittenheyns ~1500), on a second independent branch."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"wittenheyns_joanna_1530","name":"Joanna Wittenheyns","dates":"b. ~1530","confidence":"sup","surname":"Wittenheyns","family":"wittenheyns","born":"~1530","order":"1530","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"wittenheyns_mattheus_1500","mother":"deruwe_maria_1500","spouses":[{"id":"vandewalle_simon_1530","name":"Simon Vandewalle"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Her marriage to Simon Vandewalle is named in a 1573 Oostkamp act ('Janneken Wittenheyns fa Matheus x Simon Vande Walle')."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"wittenheyns_mattheus_1500","name":"Mattheus Wittenheyns","dates":"~1500 – ~1546 Oostkamp","confidence":"sup","surname":"Wittenheyns","family":"wittenheyns","born":"~1500","order":"1500","died":"~1546 Oostkamp","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"id":"deruwe_maria_1500","name":"Maria De Ruwe"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"DEEPEST CONFIRMED ANCESTOR (with his wife). Called 'gheseyt Maraels'. Named with wife and children in the 1547 Bruges orphan register (weesregister St.-Jan). Born ~1500 — the reign of Charles V. No parents recorded."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"wittenheyns_petrus_1500","name":"Petrus Wittenheyns","dates":"~1500 – before 1575","confidence":"sup","surname":"Wittenheyns","family":"wittenheyns","born":"~1500","order":"1500","died":"before 1575","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"id":"tjonck_judoca_1510","name":"Judoca 't Jonck"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"DEEPEST-TIER ANCESTOR — born ~1500, Oostkamp. Father of Barbara Wittenheyns (~1535). The Wittenheyns of Oostkamp appear on two independent lines of ours (also\n[[wittenheyns_mattheus_1500]] ~1500, via the Vandewalle line); whether Petrus and Mattheus\nare brothers is not established. No parents recorded.\n\nCHECKED AND REJECTED (July 2026) — the duplicate detector flags Petrus and Mattheus as\npossibly one person, on a rare surname plus a birth year of about 1500. They are not.\nFour things separate them, and none is a spelling difference:\n\n- different given names — Mattheus and Petrus are not variants of one another;\n- different wives — Judoca 't Jonck here, Maria De Ruwe there;\n- different deaths — before 1575 here, about 1546 at Oostkamp there;\n- different children — Barbara (~1535) here; Mattheus's children are named with him in\n  the 1547 Bruges orphan register.\n\nTwo men of one uncommon surname, born about the same time in the same parish, is what a\npair of brothers or cousins looks like. The warning is expected to keep firing, because\nit is derived from surname and year alone; this note is the answer to it."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"wittock_rosalia_1820","name":"Rosalia Wittock","dates":"b. 15 Nov 1820 Belsele","confidence":"sup","surname":"Wittock","family":"wittock","born":"15 Nov 1820 Belsele","order":"1820-11-15","occupation":"huisvrouw (housewife)","line":"paelinck","spouses":[{"id":"paelinck_joannes_1809","name":"Joannes Franciscus Paelinck"}],"source":"stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck)","note":"Housewife; mother of six recorded children including Eduardus (1858)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"wolf_maria_1836","name":"Maria Wolf","dates":"b. 4 Apr 1836 Brussel","confidence":"sup","surname":"Wolf","family":"wolf","born":"4 Apr 1836 Brussel","order":"1836-04-04","occupation":"herbergierster (innkeeper)","line":"thumas","mother":"wolf_petronella","spouses":[{"id":"bossin_joannes_1834","name":"Joannes Baptista Bossin","detail":"m. Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 17 Jun 1858"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 3 — Ludovicus Bossin × Maria Isabella Helena Thumas, Kraainem, 10 April 1900; Civil registration acts for the Bossin family of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, Kraainem and Zaventem (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Mother of the groom in her son [[bossin_ludovicus_1879]]'s marriage act — Kraainem nr. 3, 10\nApril 1900 (S28). A *herbergierster* of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe: she kept an inn, as her son's\nnew father-in-law [[thumas_georges_1836]] did at Kraainem.\n\nWidowed since 1887 and running the house herself thirteen years later — the act gives her the\ntrade in her own right, not her husband's.\n\n**BIRTH DATED, AND A HARD CHILDHOOD NAMED (2026-07-27).** Her own marriage act — Sint-\nStevens-Woluwe nr. 4, **17 June 1858** (S33) — gives her birth as **4 April 1836,\nBrussel**, a *dienstmeyt*, and records her as a *verlaten kind* (abandoned child): she\ndeclared under oath that her mother's last residence was unknown to her and that she had\nnever known her, which her witnesses confirmed under oath. The act nonetheless names her\nmother formally, [[wolf_petronella]], a *dagloonster* — presumably from her own birth\nrecord rather than personal knowledge — and names no father for her at all. Both facts are\nrecorded as the act gives them, without resolving one into the other.\n\n**The couple's five further children, all read from acts naming this exact birthdate\nagainst her stated age, agreeing to the year in five of five:** 21 in 1857\n([[bossin_joannes_1857]]), 22 in 1859 ([[bossin_philippus_1859]]), 39 in 1876\n([[bossin_jan_1876]]), 46 in 1882 ([[bossin_frans_1882]]), and 43 on\n[[bossin_ludovicus_1879]]'s own 1879 birth act. See [[bossin_joannes_1834]] for the couple's fuller\nrecord, including a sixth child, [[bossin_guillielmus_1869]] (b. Kraainem 1869), known only from\nhis own 1896 marriage act, which also independently restates her husband's death.\n\n**Her surname is spelled five ways across these acts**: *Dewolf* (1857), *Wolf* (1859 and\nher own 1858 marriage), *Anna Maria De Wolf* (1876), *Wolf* again (1882), *Anna Maria\nDewolf* (her son [[bossin_jan_1876]]'s 1897 marriage, age 62) and *Maria Anna Dewolf*\n([[bossin_guillielmus_1869]]'s 1896 marriage) — one woman, several clerks, across more than forty\nyears of documents.\n\nHer own trade moves too: *dienstmeyt* at her 1858 marriage, *dagloonster* (1857),\nunstated (1859), *huishoudster* (1876, 1882, 1897), *herbergierster* in her own right by\n1900, after widowhood.\n\n*Wolf* is rare enough in this corner of Brabant to be searchable on its own, which is the\ncheap next move — as is [[wolf_petronella]]'s own record, which names no known husband at\nall."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"wolf_petronella","name":"Petronella Wolf","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Wolf","family":"wolf","occupation":"dagloonster (day labourer)","line":"thumas","source":"Civil registration acts for the Bossin family of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, Kraainem and Zaventem (harvested corpus, July 2026)","note":"Named as mother of the bride in her daughter [[wolf_maria_1836]]'s marriage act —\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 4, 17 June 1858 (S33), a *dagloonster*. No father is named for\nthe bride at all — the act records her as a *verlaten kind*, an abandoned child.\n\n**Named, but not known to her own daughter.** The same act has [[wolf_maria_1836]] declare\nunder oath that her mother's last residence was unknown to her and that she had never\nknown her, a declaration her witnesses confirmed under oath. Both facts stand as the act\ngives them: a name and a trade recorded formally, and a daughter who swears she never\nknew the woman. Neither is resolved into the other here.\n\nThe act gives no age, so this record carries no birth date.\n\nFRONTIER: whatever record named her to the 1858 clerk in the first place — a foundling\nregister or [[wolf_maria_1836]]'s own birth act — neither yet searched for."});
