FamilyTree.person({"id":"wyllie_brigitte_1779","name":"Brigitte Josephine Joanna Wyllie","dates":"1779 Diksmuide – 8 Nov 1824 Diksmuide","confidence":"sup","surname":"Wyllie","family":"wyllie","born":"1779 Diksmuide","order":"1779","died":"8 Nov 1824 Diksmuide","line":"van-iseghem","spouses":[{"id":"vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780","name":"Antoine Vanalderweireldt","detail":"m. Diksmuide, 8 Jun 1803"},{"id":"looten_francois_1785","name":"François Joseph Looten","detail":"m. Diksmuide, 25 Jun 1818"}],"source":"bartvanhooren (Bart Vanhooren); West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Huwelijken (marriage index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers; West-Vlaamse Burgerlijke Stand — Overlijdens (death index), Rijksarchief Brugge/Kortrijk volunteers","note":"Bore the Scottish-origin surname Wyllie in West-Flanders; widowed young in 1808, remarried\nin 1818 (below).\n\nBIRTH DATE OPEN, NOT RESOLVED EITHER WAY (2026-07-27). This record held 22 February 1779.\nTwo independent acts — her own 1803 marriage\n(`data/artifacts/vanalderweireldt-wyllie-1803-marriage-diksmuide.md`) and her 1818\nremarriage (`data/artifacts/looten-wyllie-1818-marriage-diksmuide.md`) — both instead\ntranscribe her birth as 22 October 1779, the day and month transposed against what was held.\nNeither reading satisfies both acts' own stated ages, checked by computation: born\n22/10/1779 gives age 23 at the 1803 wedding (the act says 24) but age 38 at the 1818 one\n(the act says 38, correct); born 22/02/1779 gives age 24 in 1803 (correct) but age 39 in\n1818 (the act says 38, wrong). Neither candidate is dropped in favour of the other — both\nare recorded here as competing — so the point date is reduced to the year both\ntranscriptions and the arithmetic agree on. An index-level self-reported age is not primary\nevidence either way, so even resolving this conflict would not reach `doc`; only her own\nbirth or baptismal record would.\n\nREMARRIED, FOUND WITHOUT LOOKING FOR IT (2026-07-27). Diksmuide, 25 June 1818, act nr. 82,\nRAB ID 85255, microfilm 1166237 (`data/artifacts/looten-wyllie-1818-marriage-diksmuide.md`)\n— she married [[looten_francois_1785]], a widow at 38. **What identifies this bride as this\nrecord is the act's own Previous-Partners table**, not the name agreeing alone: VANALDERWEIRELDT\n| Antoine | Diksmuide | 06/07/1808 — naming her first husband, his place and a third value\nfor his death day. Her parents are given identically to the 1803 act. The methodological\npoint worth keeping: a Vanalderweireldt-only search would never have found this marriage,\nbecause by 1818 she carries a different surname — it surfaced only because her own 1824\ndeath act still names Looten as her partner, and the search worked back from there. See\n[[looten_francois_1785]] for the marriage and the children.\n\nDEATH DATE CONFIRMED, NOT RETRACTED — A DELIBERATE CONTRAST (2026-07-27). Her own\ndeath-index row (Diksmuide act nr. 198, RAB ID 2298609, Certificate Date 10/11/1824, Date\ncolumn blank) has exactly the same blank-Date-column shape that cost [[vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780]] his\nday-level precision. Here it does not cost this record anything: both her sons'\nown 1828 marriage acts — [[vanalderweireldt_carolus_1808]]'s and [[vanalderweireldt_petrus_1803]]'s — independently state\nher decease as 8 November 1824, this record's held value, a two-day lag behind the\ncertificate date rather than a contradiction of it. Kept at day precision because two later,\nindependent civil acts agree — where Antoine's three sources did not agree with each other\nat all.\n\nFOUR MORE NAMES, NONE LINKED. Her own parents, as both acts name them: **Wyllie François\nAntoine × Deman** [forename open]. The father leans toward acceptance — named identically\nin the 1803 and 1818 acts, and corroborated by an exact death date and place (30 September\n1811, Diksmuide) given on the 1818 act. Her mother's forename is not settled: the 1803 act\nwrites \"Deman Brigitte\", the 1818 act \"Deman Catharine\", and her own death-index row renders\nher fully as \"Deman Catherine Bregite\" — read together, this looks like a compound name\nsplit differently by different clerks (the same pattern runs through this whole cluster:\nIsabella Claire/Clara, this record's own Josephine Joanna, Antoine's Joseph Albert), not a\ncontradiction. No single forename is asserted, and neither parent is linked, per the same\nstandard applied on [[vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780]]'s record.\n\nTWO MORE GENERATIONS, NAMED AND LEFT OPEN. Her mother's own parents, from her mother's 1801\ndeath act (Diksmuide act nr. 48, certificate 1 January 1801): Jean Deman × Marie Jeanne\nD'Hondt. Her father's own parents, from his 1811 death act (Diksmuide act nr. 175,\ncertificate 2 October 1811): Pierre Jacques Wyllie × Marie Barbe Lengs — the same act\nrecording that he remarried Colette Prudence Minne in 1807, after her mother's death. All\nfour sit one generation beyond an already-open parent generation, on one index row each, and\nD'Hondt is common enough in this region to carry real rival risk — the same caution §66\napplied to the Huyghebaert grandparents. Not created as person files, per CLAUDE.md rule 4."});
